window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5501,"title":"Chapter 5501: Chapter 5500: No Longer So Passive!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Sensing, it turned out, was not so simple in a place like this.","When Noah had asked Seo-yeon about dying Causes, his daughter had closed her eyes upon the golden sands and reached out with the gift that had once felt Chernobyl grieving across an entire Observable Existence. And after a long moment, her small brows had furrowed.","\"I can barely feel... something, Aba. But it’s all murky. Veiled! \" She had opened her eyes with visible frustration. \" It’s like listening for a song underwater. This place is too heavy and too old. I think... I think I need to adapt to it first.\"","So Noah had not pushed.","He had simply lifted her onto the wide handle of his golden throne, and there she sat now with her legs crossed and her eyes closed, mirrored light drifting faintly off her small frame as she sensed and adapted and sensed again, hour after hour as their island of dream-sand drifted across the storming dark of THE Krazhor-Nul.","And while his daughter listened for dying songs... Noah decided to work.","For his mind had been circling THE Tide That Owes Nothing ever since Straif settled into it. The Foundation returned three thousand to twenty thousandfold on what was given, and its Sharpened Returns honed every boon toward what served him most! The math of it was almost embarrassing. Giving was the single most profitable act in his entire arsenal, and yet he had been treating it passively, waiting for moments of gifting to arise on their own!","Why wait?! Why not manufacture generosity at scale?","Farming. Blacksmithing. Crafting! If he produced treasures with his own hands and gifted them to his own people, the Tide would answer every single gift, and its Sharpened Returns would answer with things he could then gift again or wield himself! And the ultimate goal glimmered clearly at the end of that chain: to place items in the hands of his people that let them express the power of True Lifeforms, even if they themselves could not yet become True!","If they could not yet be True... he would forge them Trueness they could wear.","\" Infiniverse ,\" Noah said as he rose from his throne. \" Handle the farming. Herbs and Ores...\"","\" Gladly, Master!\" Her manifestation smiled.","THE Infiniverse itself was vast and filled with thousands of Realms filled with farmland. Osmontian Source Infinite Herbs would simply need to be ushered and matured!","And Noah conjured his forge.","HUUM!","It rose out of the dream-sands before him, an ancient friend from some time ago given new grandeur, an anvil the size of a hill set beside a furnace whose mouth burned with churning Osmontian Source Infinity, cerulean flames wrapped around a core of his own Intent as chimneys of black stone vented sparks of pure blue into the storm! Racks of gleaming tools framed it. Quenching pools of liquid starlight steamed beside it!","He named it as he looked upon it.","THE Quintessential Osmontian Forge!","Then THE True Human Emperor rolled his shoulders, took up a great hammer from the racks, and got to work!","His hands reached out across the passing dark of THE Krazhor-Nul as they flew, plucking everything their island crossed! Ancient trees of petrified silver from the fossil valleys. Stones veined with the third unnamed essense of the storm-rain. Ores that THE Infiniverse condensed from their passage, chunks of fallen star-matter, boughs of obsidian wood harvested carefully and far from any cursed fruit. All of it flowed into the furnace’s cerulean mouth as Noah infused every raw material of this Dimension with rivers of his Osmontian Source Infinity and the seamless weight of his Intent!","CLANG! CLANG! CLANG!","The hammer rose and fell as the storm above seemed to keep rhythm.","Metal that had never known shape learned it beneath his hands as blades stretched out upon the anvil, glowing blue-gold before plunging into starlight pools with screams of steam. Armor plates curved into being like the petals of iron flowers. Spearheads. Shields. Gauntlets and greaves and helms, each one drinking his Osmontian Source Infinity, each one carrying a whisper of his Intent folded a thousand times into its grain, and he deemed this new class of creations with a craftsman’s simple pride!","Advanced Apeiron Armaments!","THE Infiniverse worked beside him through it all, her hands feeding the furnace as she infused ores and materials from her many realms as well, with her humming softly while she passed her Master his materials!","And upon the throne’s handle, Seo-yeon sensed on with closed eyes as Emotive kept watch over her and their surroundings both, though it had to be said that Emotive’s watching kept drifting, again and again, to the forge itself, where Noah had shed his upper robes and worked the hammer with his muscular frame gleaming under cerulean sparks, and her manic eyes gleamed right back with unhidden appreciation as she sighed happily at every strike!","Time passed.","And after some time, dozens of weapons and full-body armors lay arranged across the golden sands in gleaming rows, and the prompts settled over his craft.","|Cataloguing your session’s finest works among the Advanced Apeiron Armaments.|","|THE Apeiron Warblade: forged from petrified silver and star-matter, its edge carries your infused Intent as it cleaves through defenses of weak THE Fifth Scale as through parchment...|","|THE Apeiron Aegis: a full-body armor plated from treated obsidian wood, drinking one-third of all force that strikes it into its own reinforcement...|","|THE Stormrain Piercer: a spear quenched in the essense of this Dimension’s rain, its thrusts briefly ignoring the distinction between body and Source...|","Noah nodded as he surveyed the rows!","Fine works. Genuinely fine, worthy of arming Emperors of lesser eras! And every single one of them was, to his true purpose, merely seed-stock.","He gathered an armful of the finest pieces, and turned, and began gifting them to Emotive.","\" For you.\"","\"For me? !\" Emotive lit up like a detonation as she accepted blade after blade, armor after armor, hugging the entire pile to her chest with her manic eyes shining! She had the Amaranthine Heart seated in Noah’s own chest and power enough to disorient True Lifeforms, and she cradled the gifted armaments as if each one was the first present anyone had ever given her! \" Mine! All mine, from your own hands!\"","And above them, existence buzzed and seethed.","The air over the forge trembled as reality folded around acts of pure giving, gifts made with one’s own labor and gifted with no expectation of return, and THE Tide That Owes Nothing triggered!","WAA!","From the seething point above, light condensed.","It poured downward in two streams of blinding radiance as the storm itself bent around their descent, and within the light, two shapes formed! The first was a full-body armor, plated in scales of deep abyssal blue that shifted like a living tide, its helm crowned with a circlet-motif that pulsed in rhythm with some vast unseen heart.","The second was a bow, taller than a man, its limbs carved from some pale gleaming material that Noah’s Sight could not source to any known Dimension, its string a single taut thread of golden light!","And both of them burned with Egoic Intents!","Actual Egoic Intents, faint and simple but seamless, \"I am\" declarations woven into forged matter as the two armaments descended onto the golden sands.","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has answered your session of crafting and giving.|","| First: THE Tidebound Apeiron of the Sunken Sovereign . A full-body armor of unfathomable origins, its materials drawn from a unique Dimension of Existence whose oceans predate the Scales, forged in conjunction with terrifying authorities that have elevated it beyond all mortal craft to become a True Egoic Armament. It carries its own simple Egoic Intent. Any lifeform bearing any Intent whatsoever may don it, and while worn, it grants the defenses of a weak True Lifeform, the armor’s own Trueness standing in for what the wearer lacks...|","| Second: THE Goldenstring Longbow of the First Dawn . A True Egoic Armament of equally unfathomable make, its pale limbs harvested from that same unique Dimension and strung with condensed authority. Any lifeform with any Intent may draw it, and every loosed arrow expresses the offensive power of a weak True Lifeform, the bow’s Egoic Intent supplying the Trueness behind each shot...|","|A Fourth Scale being wearing the first and drawing the second could stand upon a battlefield of True Lifeforms and not immediately die .|","...!","Noah gazed at the two True Egoic Armaments grandly as he lifted the Tidebound Apeiron in one hand and the Goldenstring Longbow in the other, feeling their simple, loyal little Intents hum against his own, and he nodded slowly.","He set both aside with care, and then turned back to the gleaming rows upon the sands, and began giving Emotive the remaining ones! Blade after blade into her delighted arms as the air seethed again! Armor after armor as existence folded and the Tide triggered once more, and again, boons condensing above the drifting island in slow succession as Noah’s hands kept giving and giving!","And through it all, his mind ran the glorious math forward.","He would forge, and gift, and the Tide would answer. And piece by piece, session by session, he would fill THE Infiniverse’s armories with True Egoic Armaments until every single one of his core people, every core human under his crown who lacked the weavings to become True themselves, could don Trueness like a coat and draw Trueness like a bowstring!","They could survive. They could stand in places that would have unraveled them! They could get the chance to see a place like this Dimension with their own eyes.","Above the golden island, existence seethed yet again!"]},{"number":5502,"title":"Chapter 5502: Chapter 5501: Human!","paragraphs":["The forge sang on, and the golden island was no longer quiet.","CLANG! CLANG!","Noah’s hammer rose and fell upon the anvil as fresh Advanced Apeiron Armaments cooled in gleaming rows, and all around him, across the drifting dream-sands, dozens of his closest people walked beneath the storming skies of THE Krazhor-Nul.","His Mother was here. Henry was here. Barbatos, Adelaide, Sigrid, Riya, Naldine, Titano, The Emperor Penguin, Kazuhiko, Erikson, Lich Ra’Zan, Khor, Amser, The Dora Shath’yar...dozens of the people drawn out from the safety of THE Infiniverse and standing upon the sands of his Dimension, and every single one of them was adorned in THE Tidebound Apeiron!","The abyssal-blue armors had transformed upon each wearer, thinning and reshaping until they lay like a layer of their own clothing, Amelia’s flowing into the trim of her emerald gown, Henry’s settling as a blue-gold mantle across his shoulders, Barbatos wearing hers like a duelist’s coat as the Emperor Penguin’s armor had simply become a small regal breastplate that he polished with one flipper!","And with the simple Egoic Intents of their armaments humming, the lethal ambient density of THE Krazhor-Nul broke around them like water around stones as they gazed at the wonders of this place with open awe!","The storm of raining authorities. The distant fossil ranges. The million-mile tree far behind them. His people drank it all in, and Noah watched them drink it in as his hammer kept its rhythm.","And then, as they crossed into a new region...they sensed a cluster of lifeforms!","Ahead, the dark geography gave way to a vast basin wrapped in mist and slow-turning storms, and stretched over all of it like a soap-bubble of solid law was a dimensional forcefield, a boundary of layered weavings that pressed back against their approach with a simple, ancient demand. Only a True Lifeform could cross.","Noah’s Trueness answered without being asked, and the boundary parted around the golden island like a curtain!","And within...","\" Whoa ...\" Seo-yeon whispered.","Within was a hidden paradise. Rolling plains of luminous silver-green grass spread beneath the mist as groves of colossal blue-leafed trees rose like towers, and moving through this greenery, grazing upon it in slow contented herds...were massive lifeforms!","They were like archaic dinosaurs. Colossal long-necked beasts whose hides shimmered with plated opal scales, their backs ridged with crystalline sails that caught the storm-light. Horned quadrupeds the size of hills with manes of drifting silver flame. Massive shelled grazers whose shells spiraled like the horns of legends, gentle-eyed and slow, tearing up whole trees and chewing them with the placid rhythm of creatures who had never once needed to hurry. They were herbivores, every one of them, eating the surrounding greenery in peace.","And each of them...had their Sources vibrantly at THE Fourth Scale of Existence!","| Designation: THE Mistgrove Behemoths of THE Krazhor-Nul . They are natal inhabitants of this Dimension, protected within grazing sanctuaries such as this one, and every member of the herd carries a natal intent related to herbivores, expressions of placidity, growth, and endless grazing woven into their Sources from birth. They hold no aggression weavings whatsoever. They are, in the plainest terms, the fattened cattle of this Dimension.|","Noah’s eyes shined brightly!","He gazed upon their massive bodies, the mountainous slabs of muscle shifting beneath opal hides, the sheer tonnage of meat wandering placidly before him, Fourth Scale Sources marbled through every fiber of it, and a singular, profound, deeply human question rose through the mind of THE True Human Emperor.","How... would the bodies of these creatures taste?!","He set down his hammer.","What followed was conducted in respectful silence. Noah’s hand extended as his authority reached across the plains and plucked one of the massive beasts from the edge of the herd, a horned grazer the size of a hill, its end delivered so swiftly and painlessly that the rest of the herd did not even pause their chewing! The golden island rose at his will, lifting high above the misted basin until the sanctuary spread below them like a painting, and there, in the high quiet above a paradise, Noah rolled up his sleeves.","From his many actualized Civilizations, The Civilization of Cooking was pulled out!","The weavings of a hundred thousand kitchens settled over his body as his stance changed, his hands changed, the entire manner of his existence changed, and THE True Human Emperor became a chef once more.","His blades moved first. The colossal beast was broken down with strokes of such precision that not a single fiber tore wrong, mountains of marbled crimson meat separating into their noble cuts as bones the size of towers were set aside. And then came the fire.","His Osmontian Source Infinity rose as the flames!","Cerulean fire bloomed across dozens of floating grill-stations as Noah cooked upon his own Infinity, the blue flames licking up around slabs of Fourth Scale meat, and through the fire itself he provided the spices, threads of his Intent folding into the flames as seasoning, notes of his Causes rendered into flavor, Harvest lending depth and Quintessence lending purity as the smoke that rose over the golden island turned fragrant enough to make many weep!","And the cuts that emerged...","Thick-cut ribs glazed in their own rendered Source, the meat pulling from the bone in tender crimson sheets that steamed with cerulean light! Rolled roasts, seared to a crust of gold and carved into medallions so marbled they glowed like stained glass.","Skewers of flame-mane flank, charred and dripping. Broths of tower-bone simmered until they shimmered like liquid pearl, and upon every plate, every cut burned faintly with Osmontian Source Infinity and the warm weight of his Intent, food that was also, in the truest sense, him!","|Each prepared meal of Mistgrove Behemoth provides +100 Osmontian Biomass to those consuming it, alongside an all-parameter elevation of their Source lasting several days, a strengthening of natal placidity within their weavings that steadies the mind against fear and madness, and a gentle deepening of the consumer’s affinity toward their own Intent. In plainer terms: this meal makes them stronger, calmer, braver, and truer.|","\"... Aba .\" Seo-yeon had drifted up beside the grills, and she was openly salivating, mirrored light flickering off her cheeks. \" Aba, is it ready?\"","\" Go ,\" Noah said, and the feast began!","His people fell upon the food with the joy of soldiers given a festival! Titano wept openly over the ribs. The Emperor Penguin claimed an entire loin roast and defended it with regal menace. Sigrid and Adelaide dueled with skewers, Kazuhiko ate in reverent silence, Lich Ra’Zan, who did not strictly need to eat, ate anyway, and Seo-yeon sat on the throne handle with a rib bigger than she was, absolutely destroying it.","And Noah stood back from the grills, and looked at his people, in this dangerous Dimension, and thought...","This...was what it meant to be human.","Because out here, in the vastness of existence, amid all the terrors and Scales and dying Causes and cursed lineages, a human wonders what their purpose is. What they were here for! It was a terrifying question to ever ponder, as one may search across eras and never once find the answer. But when they all came together like this, eating and laughing and simply being around each other beneath a storm that could kill Mesozoic Scale beings...the question quieted.","This was being human. Not the answer to the question, but the reason the question could be borne at all.","His gaze drifted across the feast, and paused.","In one corner of the golden island, away from the laughter...Emotive was bowing.","She was bowing toward the butler-like figure of Malphas, her head lowered deep as her hands pressed together before her. Malphas had served her once, in the era when Emotive played with the emotions of all her servants, when her cruelty had been a habit. She had done everything since to redeem herself.","But redemption in general was one thing as she had to do the other.","Malphas stood stiffly before her with a difficult expression fighting across his composed face, a servant’s discipline warring with emotions he was trying desperately not to show. But he did not walk away either, and Emotive did not rise until he had managed, stiffly, barely, a single nod.","Noah watched it all in silence.","Near the two of them, Heidrun strutted past! The lustrous goat, her fur now a stellar cascade of white-gold and blue, held her horned head at a magnificently arrogant angle as she surveyed the feast like a queen inspecting tribute, and then began to eat with a delicacy that fooled no one, as she was on her third plate, this fatty.","Noah looked at all of this.","And his thoughts turned.","His Osmontian Tongue, four Letters strong and hungry for more. The Infinite Tongue that had preceded it. The First Tongue, THE Primordial Tongue, all the grammars of power that existence had layered across the ages, and the directions his own Tongue could still grow!","Letters were carved from lived truth. And what truth had he lived more thoroughly than the one unfolding on these sands right now?","So he simply said it.","\"I AM...HUMAN.\"","HUUUM!","Waves of silent immensity permeated all around.","The fourth Letter rolled out over the golden island not as a simple, settled fact, and it wrapped around the feast like warmth around a hearth as his people’s laughter rang inside it, and Noah simply enjoyed this moment!","And at this time...","Above him, his Intent and his Osmontian Source Infinity began to gather!","Existence folded and formed glimmering singularities across the sky over the island, points of light blooming one after another as wonders began to descend toward him, and the familiar seethe of his Foundations moved beneath all of it with unusual force, THE Tide exerting itself tremendously, his whole Scale of Foundations flexing as if determined to guarantee an ecstatic result!","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has been triggered. You hunted, butchered, cooked, and served with your own hands, gifting a feast woven from your Civilizations, your Infinity, and your Intent to dozens of those dearest to you. The Tide has judged this compound act of giving among the purest it has yet answered, and your Foundations have exerted themselves in concert to sharpen the returns.|","|Boons delivered, and they seem to be Meats stemming from True Lifeforms.|","WAA!","The singularities opened, and the boons descended!","Slabs of meat drifted down through the storm-light, each one sealed in folds of glimmering preservation, and even wrapped, even inert, their presense pressed upon the island with the unmistakable seamless weight of Trueness!","|First: THE Coilflesh of the World-Serpent, three great cuts recovered through the weavings from the destroyed divided bodies of Ormarr Grimtunge. Each prepared meal grants between +3,000 and +5,000 Osmontian Biomass, alongside a lasting reinforcement of the consumer’s bindings and grip upon their own existence...|","|Second: THE Marbled Haunch of a Fallen Aurochs-Sovereign, a True Lifeform of a prior era whose remains the Tide sourced from the deep graves of this Dimension. Each meal grants between +5,000 and +8,000 Osmontian Biomass, and briefly allows any consumer to bear burdens far past their Scale without buckling...|","|Third, and finest: THE Pale Sirloin of an Unnamed True Grazer, its origin veiled even to me, its flesh humming with a placid natal intent so profound it borders on law. Each meal grants +10,000 Osmontian Biomass, and deepens the consumer’s Trueness itself by a sliver...|","...!","Noah looked upon the descending bounty with shining eyes as slabs of True Lifeform meat settled gently onto his grill-stations, ingredients that lifeforms of any era would wage wars over, delivered to a chef because he had fed his family well, and he began taking them all in with the reverent hands of a craftsman receiving sacred materials.","For this, too...was being human!"]},{"number":5503,"title":"Chapter 5503: Chapter 5502: Sensation!","paragraphs":["The feast roared on across the golden island, and beneath its laughter, Noah gave a silent command to THE Infiniverse to take the herd below. All of it!","She stepped off the edge of the drifting island and flew down.","Noah watched her descent as her cerulean-threaded form dove through the mists of the sanctuary, and then THE Infiniverse went to work in a manner only a Living Observable Existence could. Her authority spread out across the entire basin as she carved out this whole section of THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension, the silver-green plains, the towering blue groves, the placid herds of Mistgrove Behemoths mid-graze, even the ancient soils and the mist itself, all of it separating from the dark geography in one colossal, gentle excision. The dimensional forcefield collapsed as its paradise simply rose, an entire ecosystem lifting like a lily pulled whole from a pond!","And she pulled it into herself.","Her form bloomed with cerulean light as the carved sanctuary folded into her existence, realms within her opening to receive it, and the herds did not even panic, placid natal intents registering only that the sky had changed color and the grass was somehow sweeter. Within moments, an entire domain of THE Krazhor-Nul had been relocated into THE Infiniverse, and somewhere inside her.","And while she did so...Noah heard back from Ryaenara at this time.","He had already heard from THE Creature a little while ago, flat words crossing the dark to confirm he was safe, his portion of the Serpent collapsed into dust. And right now, threading faintly through the heavy weavings of this Dimension, Ryaenara’s voice arrived saying similar words!","\" Fucking finally, the threads connect. That serpent was a pain!\" Her voice carried its old looseness. \" Now listen, I cannot sense your location. Everything in this Dimension carries unknown restrictions, the weavings here are old and territorial, and if we drift too far apart, even messages like this one may not reach through anymore. So describe the regions you have recently crossed, landmarks, anything, and we will see about coming together again.\"","A pause, and then her voice dropped lower.","\" And one more thing. When I defeated his body, that snake looked at me with those crimson eyes and said, ominously, mind you, that they were coming for us. They. Not I. He has called for help, or he serves something that is now aware of us. Be careful.\"","Noah smiled slightly as he listened.","This was almost the exact same conversation he had held with THE Creature. The same inability to sense locations, the same request for landmarks, well, without the warning.","He proceeded to communicate back to Ryaenara, describing the million-mile obsidian tree, the fossil valleys, the bone sea’s direction, every landmark their golden island had crossed.","And while he did this, he looked at his feasting people, and made a decision.","\" Everyone ,\" Noah called out, and the laughter quieted as dozens of faces turned to him. \" Finish the feast inside THE Infiniverse. Take the remaining meats with you, take your time, and acclimate to the power settling in you. Your Sources are elevated and your armaments are new, so train with them, learn them, and grow fat and strong! When the time comes, if its safe, you can put the power to use. Otherwise...we may have to upgrade The Dungeons and Crucibles within to give you all a taste of Adversity...\"","...!","His words rang out and began to be followed by all.","He needed to get a better grasp of this Dimension and its dangers, and a feast, however joyous, was a gathering of everything he loved in one exposed place. His people withdrew in cheerful waves, Titano carrying three plates, the Emperor Penguin refusing to relinquish his roast, Amelia squeezing Noah’s hand once before stepping through, and soon the golden island held only those he left outside.","Seo-yeon, still sensing upon the throne’s handle. THE Infiniverse. And Emotive!","Their journey continued across the Dimension as the island flew on through the storming dark, and Noah lay back on his throne and closed his eyes.","His senses spread out.","He reached into the chaotic infinity raging through the skies of this place, pulling upon his Infinite Tongue to gather as much information as possible, and as the boundless currents poured their grammar through him, his thoughts moved.","THE Infinite Tongue. THE Primordial Tongue!","Both, at their heart, equated to depth of understanding, how deeply one understood Infinity, and how deeply one understood THE Primordial Source. Letters and weavings of those Tongues were simply understanding crystallized.","And Noah had walked further down both, fusing Infinity and Primordial Source together and integrating them so deeply into his existence that they had stopped being external concepts at all.","But he had done so through his Identity. Osmontian!","He could continue seeking and grasping the Letters and weavings of THE Primordial Tongue and THE Infinite Tongue directly, learning the old grammars as they were written. Or...he could continue expressing Infinity and THE Primordial Source through his identity, through the Osmontian Source Infinity that was both of them fused and claimed as his.","The answer...was fairly obvious.","Why learn a language as a foreigner when he had already built his own tongue atop its roots? Through his Osmontian Source Infinity, he unlocked more and more Trueness in conjunction with his Intent, and more True Appendages arose this way, the Eye, the Vigil, the Root, all of them grown from identity rather than granted by grammar. And for easy advancement, his Osmontian Biomass was the answer, of which he gained more of through his Osmontian Tongue and its Letters, through I AM’s perpetual assertion, through HUMAN’s gathering warmth, through the Tide answering his gifts.","Everything...was neatly connected! Identity fed the Tongue, the Tongue fed the Biomass, the Biomass fed the grades, the grades deepened the Trueness, and the Trueness grew new anatomy. He closed his eyes and smiled as he felt as much as he could, boundless chaotic strings of Infinity humming through his awareness alongside the deep prismatic obsidian currents of Primordial Source!","And threading between both of them, everywherein this Dimension...the third essence.","It had been prevalent all around since their hatching. In the storm-rain. In the stones he forged with. In the heavy air itself, a quiet third presence braided through the two authorities he knew best, and Noah turned the whole of his focus upon it now as its nature began, slowly, to be grasped by him!","It did not vibrate like Infinity. It did not flow like Primordial Source. It clung. It remembered. Every string of it hooked into other strings like a burr, like a debt, like a word spoken over a cradle that never stopped applying, and as his Osmontian Source Infinity traced its grammar, the prompts began to bloom.","|You have grasped the nature of the third essence.|","| Designation: THE Lingering Word. It is Curse Authority. Concentrated, ambient, and ancient past all framing, and its weavings trace directly back to Those Who Remain. This entire Dimension is saturated in it because this entire Dimension was judged in it. THE Lingering Word is the residue of the original curse spoken over THE Krazhor-Nul, the authority that collapsed the Steeds’ First Causes into terminal weavings and bound expiration into the blood of every Cursed Descendant. It has rained upon this place for ages beyond counting, and it does not fade, because a curse from Those Who Remain is not an event. It is a standing sentence, still being served.|","|Its properties, as I can measure them: it is a True authority of binding and decree. A wielder could brand outcomes onto existences, terminal weavings, guaranteed endings, decrees that ignore the gap between Scales entirely, for a curse does not fight its target’s power, it simply applies. The Marrowbane Fruit you carry is a condensed droplet of this very authority.|","|And its cost. THE Lingering Word is detrimental to the existence of any wielder. To speak in it is to hold it, and to hold it is to be marked by it, every use hooks its burrs into the wielder’s own weavings, and enough use will seed terminal threads into one’s own Cause. The Cursed Descendants did not merely inherit their curse. Their ancestors wielded this authority in their experiments, and it collected its fee.|","...!"]},{"number":5504,"title":"Chapter 5504: Chapter 5503: Sisyphus! I","paragraphs":["THE Lingering Word churned at the edges of his awareness, and Noah studied it the way a man studies a beautiful blade lying in poisoned oil.","A True authority of binding and decree. Sentences that ignored the gap between Scales entirely, endings that simply applied!","Every sentence spoken in it writes a small piece of the speaker’s own ending.","And he did not know how quickly he could be tainted.","Was it ten uses before the burrs seeded terminal threads into his Cause? A hundred? One? The Cursed Descendants themselves were the case study, and Noah had no intention of joining a study group whose members all had expiration dates. So he decided, calmly and finally, not to utilize it for now.","But there was another matter that had been quietly bothering him since the battle, and this one he could solve today.","The fusion.","When THE Quintessential Confluence had released, all his grades had settled back down a rank, and his Egoic Intent had fallen from its functional C-Rank back to its true D-Rank Ruis. And Noah had not liked it! For those brief moments of the battle, his Intent had erupted with the grandeur of Ananke, identity so dense it functioned as inevitability, and after tasting that...going without it felt like a handicap! Like a man who had stood at his full height once and was now asked to stoop.","Why stoop, when he had the wealth to stand?","\" Ruination. My Intent...elevate it to C-Rank.\"","|Elevating. 300,000 Osmontian Biomass spent as THE Egoic Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian rises from D-Rank, Ruis, to C-Rank, Straif. Your reserves settle at 163,000. And since you will ask next: elevation to B-Rank, Ngetal, will require 1,250,000 Osmontian Biomass.|","...!","HUUM!","The elevation flowed through him, and Noah closed his eyes to feel it properly!","His Intent rose through his existence like a tide claiming a shore it had always owned, and everything it touched changed! His Volume deepened first, the sheer breadth of what \"Osmontian\" contained expanding as his records and Causes and lived truths pressed outward into the new grade. His Output sharpened second, the force with which his identity expressed itself into existence gaining an edge that made the storm-winds bend subtly around the golden island! And his Trueness...his Trueness sang! The seam between what he claimed and what he was, already nonexistent, somehow grew more nonexistent, his \"I am\" settling into reality with a weight that made the ambient weavings of THE Krazhor-Nul shift respectfully around him.","At C-Rank Straif, unfused, his Intent already brushed Ananke grandeur. And fused, it would stand at B-Rank!","He breathed out slowly as satisfaction settled through his body, and then he turned to the matter that this elevation had really been preparing for.","\" Infiniverse.\"","Her manifestation approached across the golden sands, and Noah gestured to the space between them where their shared connection hummed, that unfathomably deep weave that was his Pantheon and her body and their bond all at once.","\" Shall we finish actualizing THE Quintessential Pantheon of THE Infiniverse? It is a Pantheonic Dimension, and it is also you. So we can officially designate you as your own Dimension. \" His eyes gleamed. \" Let us enact its rulings.\"","\"I was already finalizing this, Master.\"","Her reply came efficient and level, her expression composed as ever. She raised one hand, and between her fingers, threads of cerulean weavings began to weave!","\" THE Infiniverse, as a Dimension, is capable of enacting the Absolute Dimensional Ruling. I have written it as follows: only those bearing Osmontian Source Infinity, or those granted access, may enter. \" The threads locked into place with a sound like a vault door the size of existence closing.","\" Unless we encounter something that can shatter Dimensions completely, a True or Primeval Lifeform exceeding THE Sixth Scale, THE Seventh, or whatever stands equivalent to such heights, those within me are safe. That is the ruling. It is now absolute.\"","HUUM!","Noah felt it settle through the Pantheon, a weaving older in nature than walls, and his people within her became, in a single stroke, unreachable by many!","\" There is more ,\" THE Infiniverse continued. \" The completion of a Pantheon carries a lesser-known consequence. Civilizational Access, the access one holds to their own Way and its full utility, approaches 100% for all those who complete their Pantheons. Those upon Vakochev’s Scales will never reach 100% access unless they become True. It is the hidden ceiling of the Scales themselves.\"","\" At 100%, a True Lifeform gains the capability to steer their own power. \" Her voice remained level, but the weight in it rose. \" How one’s power progresses, which directions it grows, what shape the next advancement takes, these stop being matters of fortune and framework, and become matters of will. A True Lifeform with an enacted Pantheon and a forged Intent no longer discovers their path. They author it. You have been doing this instinctively for a while now.\"","Noah nodded slowly as the implications unfolded through him! Every being on the Scales climbed a ladder someone else had built. A completed True Lifeform built the ladder as they climbed it.","But not every True Lifeform lived outside of Scales of Existence.","\" And the second feature I have actualized so far,\" THE Infiniverse said . \"I studied your Estuary Eye, Master. I admired its principle. So I wrote a version of it into my Dimensional weavings. Wherever I am, THE Infiniverse now passively devours the surrounding Dimension I reside within. Its space, its ambient essense, its unclaimed weavings, all of it, drawn into me continuously, and with it...I grow larger and larger. Every moment we spend within THE Krazhor-Nul, I am quietly eating THE Krazhor-Nul.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone ever brighter!","A Living Observable Existence that grazed upon the very Dimensions she visited! He loved it for its elegance, growth without battle, expansion without exposure, his home swelling silently.","Before, she had to devour Folds or Wheels of Existence for expansion as since then, she grew rapidly without needing to. Even now, her growth continued as she didn’t particularly need to devour surrounding Dimensions. But if she could and proceeded to do so to elevate her growth even further, why not?"]},{"number":5505,"title":"Chapter 5505: Chapter 5504: Sisyphus! II","paragraphs":["The golden island drifted on through the storm, and for a while, Noah simply sat with his elevated Intent and his finalizing Pantheon and his thoughts.","Then he spoke to no one and to all of them.","\" There is an old myth I always think about. The myth of Sisyphus. \" His gaze rested on the raging horizon.","\"A king who offended the powers above him, and was sentenced to roll an immense boulder up a mountain. And every time he neared the peak, the boulder would roll back down, and he would descend, and begin again. Forever. That was the entire punishment. Not fire, not blades. Just effort, rendered meaningless, repeated without end.\"","Emotive had gone still beside him. THE Infiniverse listened without moving.","\" The lesson, as it was taught, was about futility. The cruelty of labor that arrives nowhere! And when I heard it while I was young, I pitied him. Endless hardship, endless struggle, a mountain that never stays climbed. What existence could be worse?\" Noah’s mouth curved faintly.","\" But when I think about hardship now. About adversity, and effort. I find I only want more and more of it. Show me the boulder! Show me the mountain! I have rolled my stone up through Scales and eras and domains, and every time it rolled back down, I picked it up heavier and climbed faster, and somewhere along the way, the climbing stopped being the punishment and became the point. I think, if I met Sisyphus now, I would not pity him. I would ask him what he learned on the ten thousandth climb that he missed on the first.\"","...!","He paused.","\" And at the same time...I feel like thinking this way puts my family, and everyone I love, in more and more danger.\"","...!","\"I want adversity to grow. I have built my entire existence to convert hardship into height! But this adversity is sometimes extremely terrifying, and it does not always aim at me. What will I do when, one day, an adversity comes that causes an irreversible death of those close to me? I chase after hardship so relentlessly.\" His voice stayed level which made it heavier.","\" Am I so selfish, to do this? To drag everything I love along the road to every storm I can find, because the storms make me grander?\"","He thought this out loud, openly, and THE Infiniverse and Emotive were somber as they listened, neither offering comfort. A distance away, Seo-yeon still sat with her eyes closed, sensing, her small frame wrapped in mirrored light, unaware that her Aba was speaking about her and many others.","Noah looked at her for a long moment.","\" This is another one of my human qualities, \" he said quietly. \" Selfishness. Every human expresses it. The wanting that does not stop to fully count its costs! I want to continue climbing higher and higher, and I am doing so knowing the dangers, knowing the peril, knowing exactly who stands behind me on the mountain. This is human. And it is one of the negative aspects of being human, so I will not pretend it is a virtue.\" His eyes sharpened!","\"I will simply be ready for the consequences when they come. I know what my existence is. I am playing with my life and the lives of many. So, to do my very best to ensure I do not fall...\"","He rose from the throne.","\"I shall enact the last Letter of THE Osmontian Tongue.\"","HUUM!","The last Letter!","Well, he could always change his mind later, it was his Tongue after all. But he wanted this to be the last Letter! For he had studied the First Tongue, the Infinite Tongue, THE Primordial Tongue across his climb, and all of them shared the same bloat, many Letters, especislly THE First Tongue, where most simply ended up being there, catalogued and unutilized, grammar for the sake of grammar!","His Tongue would not rot that way. Five Letters, consolidated hard around his core identity, and from that foundation...he would begin enacting Words. And then sentances.","It was definitely very sad not to reach that magical number 9, but he wouldn’t dwell on it.","A language did not grow grand by adding more alphabet. It grew grand by speaking!","\" For now, my last Letter of THE Osmontian Tongue shall be... \" Noah’s voice rolled out across the golden sands as his existence gathered itself. \" PROTAGONIST. I AM...THE PROTAGONIST!\"","HUUM!","He had this Civilization already, seated inside his Osmontian Pillar within his Scales of Existence! And as abstract as the identity was, it was pivotal, for what was a Protagonist?","Across every story humanity had ever told, barring the protagonists of extremely darker tales, the Protagonist and their people were safe! They werre not spared hardship, never spared hardship, but carried through it. The Protagonist faced the impossible battle and made the breakthrough at the final moment. The Protagonist’s family survived the siege. The story bent, subtly and constantly, toward their continuation.","It was the oldest architecture in Human storytelling, and Noah uttered this Letter wanting it to truly become part of his identity, so that his selfishness in seeking adversity...would not come one day to bite everything he loved.","The Letter carved itself into his backbone as existence checked the claim, weighing a being who had clawed up from a dying world through apocalypses and found the word fit!","|The Fifth Letter of THE Osmontian Tongue has been transcribed. PROTAGONIST. I will catalogue its boons.|","| First: THE Aura of THE Protagonist. Whenever you face adversity, this aura gathers around you, and it passively produces Osmontian Biomass proportional to the adversity being faced. A skirmish will trickle. A battle against something that should kill you will pour! It is a mechanization of the oldest pattern in Human stories, the protagonist who somehow makes their breakthrough in the middle of the battle that guaranteed their death. From this moment, the more impossible your circumstances, the faster your wealth grows...|","| Second: THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard. The Protagonist survives because the Protagonist reads the story. Upon any lifeform your gaze settles on, you may now perceive their Character Sheet: their designation, their driving motivations, their current disposition toward you, whether malice, neutrality, or favor, their level of danger to you rendered in plain terms, and the pertinent threads of their circumstance, debts, fears, and desires. Beings vastly exceeding your existence will return partial sheets, veiled in ?????, and beings actively concealing themselves may distort their entries. But against all others, you now walk into every room already holding the script.|","...!","Prompts of magisterial wonder bloomed.","Noah gazed at the terrifying capabilities detailed before him as the fifth Letter settled its weight through his existence, and he nodded slowly, and whispered calmly to himself.","\"I AM THE PROTAGONIST.\"","He said it silently, privately, because he wanted to convince himself! Because he knew there could be terrifying adversity on the horizon, adversity he himself had invited by fishing an unknown door out of the dark, and he wanted every tool possible to get past such adversity that he himself wanted...without ruining what he wanted to protect!","For he was THE True Human Emperor. He could be selfish. He could be loving! He could be brave, fearless, Quintessential, and so much more. But most of all, he needed himself and those around him to be safe, for one major human condition was death. And death...came for all humans.","Would he be any different?","In his grand existence, if he endlessly asked himself his purpose, and continued to enact his Scales, and climbed the ladder of existence rung after rung after rung, it was truly hard for him to die.","But could he ever call himself immortal? Or would that violate what it meant to be human, as even for him...there would be an end one day? Was that Osmontian? Was that part of his identity?","He kept these thoughts to himself and nobody else, and in the privacy of his own vast existence, he wondered... how existence would be without Noah Osmont in it.","\"...\"","He was met with heavy silence within himself.","Noah breathed out, and focused. He stopped thinking about what the end could be, for he was living in the now! And his now was infinitely grand, filled with aspirstions and goals, with so many things he wanted to explore and understand! For now, he wouldn’t think about his end. If there was ever an end.","It was such a human thing... that he may have not realized it."]},{"number":5506,"title":"Chapter 5506: Chapter 5505: Come! I","paragraphs":["<THE Creature>","Where did he end?","The question walked with him across the storming dark of THE Krazhor-Nul, as it had walked with him across every era since THE Wyld. His titanic body moved through the raging skies wrapped in obsidian flames, fossil ranges and drifting mountains sliding past beneath him, and the question turned itself over in his silence.","He was Existence. This was not philosophy, it was anatomy! His Pantheon took the shape of whatever surrounded him because whatever surrounded him was, in the deepest accounting, already his. The bone seas were him. The storm was him. The million-mile trees and the cursed rain and the ancient graves, all of it existence, and all of existence...him.","And yet.","Was the curse woven through this Dimension him? The curse clung to every string of this place, a sentence spoken by Those Who Remain, and when his flames passed through it, it did not feel like touching himself. It felt foreign! Like finding a scar on one’s back that one never remembered earning. And the statue, the inherited thing that rose when he called and stared where it pleased, was that him? It answered him. It was his. And yet every time it moved on its own, something in his ancient frame said borrowed, said debt!","Up to which point was it all him? And past which point did Existence become something foreign wearing his name?","He had no answer.","\" Hm ,\" THE Creature said to the storm, and kept walking.","And then he sensed it!","A grand aura of existence, far across the dark, old and vast and utterly still, the particular stillness of something mighty that had stopped being alive a very long time ago. His flat eyes narrowed as his path bent toward it, obsidian flames trailing behind his titanic strides, and the geography changed beneath him as he crossed, dark stone giving way to shores of rust-colored crystal, and then to the sea.","A vast red sea!","It stretched to every horizon beneath the storm, waters the deep arterial color of old blood, waves rolling slow and heavy as if the sea itself remembered grief. And upon those red waters, floating like a fallen mountain range...","Was a leg.","A single colossal severed leg, its pale flesh unrotted across what may have been ages, its scale so vast that clouds gathered around its heel, and the grandeur pouring off of it pressed upon the entire sea!","For this...was the limb of a Primeval One! A corpse-piece of one of existence’s apex beings, and even a piece of their body, even in death, was terrifying, its residual weavings humming with an authority that made the red waves kneel flat for miles around it!","And two figures were trying to eat it.","THE Creature’s gaze went cold as he took them in because he recognized something. Two True Lifeforms hovered above the colossal limb, golden radiance pouring off their frames as they worked siphoning weavings into the dead flesh, and they were struggling!","Sweat-light beaded off their golden brows as the Primeval limb’s residual grandeur fought their extraction at every thread, a dead thing still too proud to be drunk easily! And around each of them burned their natures plainly, one wreathed in the crimson storm of an elevated Ego of Ira, wrath refined across a True existence, the other wrapped in the towering golden pillar of an elevated Ego of Superbius, pride worn as law!","Gilded True Lifeforms.","His cold gaze held on them, and old detestation moved through his frame like a slow tide! He detested the entire structure of Gilded Ones. The harvesters! The golden civilization that had stood behind the reaping of First Causes from Observable Existences across many Ages, plucking the hearts of newborn domains while THE Primeval Ones stood behind them and blessed the harvest! He had planned, in the long ledger of his intentions, to one day gaze upon those Primeval Ones themselves, the ancient backers, the ones existence had somehow permitted to farm existence.","But Gilded True Lifeforms were a good place to start!","And there was also the limb. A Primeval One’s corpse-piece, dense with authority that even True Lifeforms strained to siphon, floating unclaimed upon a red sea. THE Creature could take that for himself!","He was honest with himself, as he was Existence and lying to himself was structurally embarrassing. His motivations here were self-serving! He knew exactly what he wanted to achieve. The detestation was real, the old grudge was real, but he was not here as an avenger of harvested Observable Existences. He was here because two things he disliked were holding one thing he wanted.","THE Creature stretched.","His titanic frame rolled its shoulders as obsidian flames climbed higher, and he measured the math plainly. One against two True Lifeforms, both Gilded, both elevated, both True, would be a challenge for him! A real one.","But he was born in Adversity, and he lived on Adversity!","So he went forward.","He did not announce himself. He did not offer pleasantries, or demands, or even a single word, for words were for negotiations and there was nothing here to negotiate! His obsidian flames began to rise in vast burning sheets as his stride lengthened across the red waves, and behind him, folding out of nothing, the titanic visage of the ancient statue bloomed, its faceless face staring down at the two golden figures with an immensity that made the sea shudder!","And already, silently, completely, before either Gilded True Lifeform had even turned around...","All of the surrounding existence had become his Pantheon!","The red sea was his. The storm above the limb was his! The rust-crystal shores and the kneeling waves and the very space the two harvesters floated in, all of it THE Pantheon of All Existence, and the two golden beings were no longer standing on a battlefield.","They were standing inside him in the most...significant way possible as at such a time...","THE Creature attacked!"]},{"number":5507,"title":"Chapter 5507: Chapter 5506: Come! II","paragraphs":["Existence closed its fist!","The red sea rose in colossal walls as the storm hammered down, space itself folding inward upon the two golden figures with the full weight of THE Pantheon of All Existence, THE MAW tearing open across the sky as THE Burden of Existence descended in the same breath, everything, all at once, the same overwhelming convergence that had crushed a portion of Ormarr Grimtunge into prismatic dust!","And it worked.","On one of them!","The Gilded True Lifeform wreathed in Ira was caught mid-turn as the Burden slammed him down into the red waves, his crimson wrath erupting against the folding sea as his golden frame buckled beneath eras of carried adversity, his scream tearing across the water!","But the other one...","The other one simply raised his gaze.","The Gilded True Lifeform wrapped in the golden pillar of Superbius looked up at the collapsing totality of Existence bearing down upon him, and his eyes were filled with nothing but pride! No alarm. No strain! Only the mild, bottomless offense of a being interrupted, and he raised one golden hand...","And swatted.","BOOOM!","A terrifying Ananke Intent smashed outward from that single gesture!","It did not push through THE Creature’s Pantheon. It overruled it! Inevitability of a caliber the Serpent had never dreamed of crashed against the folding existence and declared it unfolded, declared the seas flat, declared the intruder elsewhere, and THE Creature’s titanic frame was smashed backward across the red sea, his obsidian flames guttering as he tore a canyon through the arterial waves for hundreds of miles before his form arrested itself!","And when he looked at this being again...he truly looked.","His flat eyes read the golden figure hovering calm above the Primeval limb, and the accounting came back cold and clear! This being had far since escaped THE Mesozoic Scale. The Fifth Scale did not contain him! He stood upon the Sixth Scale equivalent, or even higher, the Scale the old records named THE Cenozoic Scale , the tier where Vakochev’s ladder grew thin!","And this entity seemed comfortable on it.","\" Hm ,\" said THE Creature, and rose, and attacked again!","He unleashed everything, just as he had against Ormarr! THE MAW split the sky and devoured the incoming golden weavings by the hundreds. THE Burden of Existence dropped again and again, eras of weight hammering down! The statue’s faceless immensity pressed upon the battlefield as the whole red sea churned as his Pantheon, fossil-crystal shores tearing free to orbit his advance, and THE Creature moved through his own convergence like a flaming obsidian titan, striking with the accumulated mass of everything that existed nearby!","And he was pressed back.","Pressed! Continuously, grindingly pushed back, the golden being meeting the totality of Existence with one hand while the pillar of Superbius around him burned brighter, and this entity seemed a level above even Ryaenara as his cold laughter finally rolled across the red sea!","\" Haha... ha. And who,\" the Gilded True Lifeform asked, golden eyes gleaming with genuine, unhurried amusement, \" do you think you are, to attack like this? No words. No declaration! You simply walked up to your betters and swung all of existence at us like a club. I have lived a very long time, dark thing, and I confess, the audacity is almost refreshing.\"","His hand pressed forward, and THE Creature learned what made this being’s oppression unique!","For the Ananke Intent of this Superbius Gilded One carried qualities other Intents could not even imagine! Ordinary inevitability declared outcomes upon targets. His inevitability declared outcomes upon the stage itself, his Intent woven through with Dimensional weavings, the deep grammar of Dimensions folded into every expression of his will! When he pressed, he did not merely press against THE Creature. He pressed against the space THE Creature occupied, against the weavings THE Creature’s Pantheon had claimed, and the surrounding existence simply tore apart beneath the declarations, reality shredding in golden lines because his pride had decided that where he pushed, nothing, not even the fabric of the Dimension, was permitted to push back!","It was Intent that had stopped negotiating with existence entirely!","THE Creature’s Pantheon claimed the surroundings, and the golden being’s Intent tore the claimed surroundings out from under him, ripping the stage apart faster than Existence could be it, and piece by piece, exchange by exchange, THE Creature was gradually getting bloody!","Obsidian flames sputtered around fresh wounds as his titanic frame absorbed blow after declaring blow, dark blood the color of deep space scattering across the red waves, and through all of it, THE Creature remained calm! He did not rage. He did not fear, for Existence had no fear! He simply fought, and bled, and thought, with the flat clarity that had carried him since before THE Wyld.","What should he do? He had hit an immovable wall as...should he call for help?","Normally, the question would not even rise. Normally, he would face everything himself, alone, as he had faced every era since his other half was brutalized before his eyes, for Existence needed nothing else! Existence bore all things alone. That was the architecture of him, the truth his appendages had grown from, the path he had built his entire long survival upon.","But...","Another exchange. Another golden declaration tearing through his claimed sea. Another wound opening across his titanic shoulder as he was pressed back another hundred miles!","He thought once more. He was not Existence alone.","The thought arrived quietly, in the middle of the blood and the pressure, and it did not feel like weakness. It felt, strangely, like an idea he had been refusing to finish for eras! He was Existence. And he was also THE Creature! And THE Creature was made up of many things, the flames, the flat words, the grudges and the graves, the memory of a slaughtered other half, the endless Adversity, and...","Connections. Connections were one of the things he was made of!","He had simply spent so long bearing everything alone that he had catalogued them as things he protected, and never once as things he could call!","And out of all his connections... Even if he called for Osmont, this anomaly could not cross this Dimension’s restricted weavings in time. Even Ryaenara, mighty as she was, could not sense his location through THE Krazhor-Nul’s ancient veils! Distance ruled them all here.","But he knew one person who was not ruled by distance.","One person who could always appear wherever he needed to appear...so long as he was called for! An old explorer of everywhere, who had A Way others could not imagine.","The golden being’s next declaration tore the sea apart beneath him, and THE Creature stood bloody at the heart of his own shredding Pantheon, facing powerful Gilded True Lifeforms upon a red sea at the bottom of a cursed Dimension...","And called out grandly!","\" Anaximander, come.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5508,"title":"Chapter 5508: Chapter 5507: The Explorer! I","paragraphs":["The Superbius Gilded True Lifeform struck again.","His terrifying Intent descended upon the bloodied titan as golden Dimensional weavings tore the red sea apart along its path, inevitability declaring THE Creature broken, the stage shredding beneath the declaration as the strike crossed the distance in a single fold of pride!","And then a figure appeared in front of THE Creature.","It was a humanoid visage. A scholar! An explorer! A man of unremarkable height in scholarly white robes, his hair tousled as if he had just walked out of a library and into a hurricane, his hands clasped calmly behind his back!","And shockingly...the descending Intent split!","The golden declaration of a Cenozoic-equivalent being forked around the newcomer like a river forced around a stone it could not acknowledge, tearing twin canyons through the sea on either side of him as it dispersed into the storm, as if the Intent itself simply could not hit the being that had just appeared!","THE Creature looked at this being, and sighed, and shook his head with open marvel.","Anaximander!","A supposedly normal human who had been studying the stars of a Lower Observable Existence, only to be visited paradoxically by THE Weavers, and from there...he had taken a step simply because he said he could...and appeared in space! He could not survive in space. But he simply deemed that he should, and so he did!","He held no authority. Not a single wisp of it, not then and not now! And yet this man had shouldered the burden of the Veil between the Living and the Dead, helping THE Creature carry it without even knowing what it was. He could do things because his existence made it so he could do them, and in that early era, others had not truly understood what they were looking at. Even THE Creature had not.","But the moment THE Creature grasped the weavings of a True Lifeform, of Identity and how it steered everything, how a lived claim made existence conform...his first thought had been Anaximander.","In all of existence, THE Creature truly could not say who had lived their way, based purely on their identity, making existence conform to what they believed...more than Anaximander!","And he appeared now, untouched, the terrifying Intent of a Superbius Gilded True Lifeform parting around him, likely because somewhere along his wandering road, the scholar had simply declared a commandment that his body could not be harmed by others.","THE Creature shook his head and nodded to him.","\"It has been some time, Anaximander.\"","...!","The explorer turned, and laughed!","\" Some time? It’s been over a year, big guy!\"","...!","A year?","Barely days had passed since THE Creature, Osmont, and Anaximander had parted, since they painted the skies of that Lower Observable Existence red-gold with the blood of a Gilded One and started this entire chain of events.","But for Anaximander, more than a year had passed? Just what dimensions had this man wandered into, to distort time so much?","There was no time to catch up.","Anaximander turned around to see the two grand True Lifeforms gazing over coldly, the Ira one risen bloodied from the waves, the Superbius one burning with golden offense, and the scholar whistled in open amazement as he looked them up and down like specimens.","\"Oh, wonderful. The two of you are True ,\" he said, nodding along to his own observation. \" Genuinely True, I can tell, it’s all very impressive. But...hm. Your Egos seem to conflict with your Trueness. Ira rages against what is, and Superbius insists on more than what is, and both of those are arguments with reality, aren’t they? That is quite paradoxical for beings whose whole foundation is being seamless with reality.\" He tilted his head, and said it plainly, like a diagnosis .","\"I don’t think...you are True at all.\"","...!","HUUM!","He said such simple words.","And yet in the next moment, the gazes of two True Lifeforms changed heavily! Shock bloomed first, then incredulity, and then from their golden bodies...their Intents began to leak! Wrath and pride flooded out of them in unraveling streams as if a hole had been poked in each of their existences, Trueness hemorrhaging into the storm, two seamless claims suddenly springing seams because a man with no authority had looked at them and disagreed!","Even THE Creature was alarmed!","His flat eyes swept the scholar and found nothing, no Intent, no working, no exertion of any framework existence had ever catalogued, just a man in white robes floating over a red sea, being right at people!","\" You may want to attack, big guy,\" Anaximander said casually, \"I can’t keep this up for too long!\"","...!","THE Creature shook his head once at the immensity of his friend.","And took a step!","He imposed himself upon two incredulous True Lifeforms in whose deepest weavings doubt had begun to bloom, doubt about the very claims their existences were built upon! And when there was doubt in something True...it was done for!","The battle that followed was brutal.","BOOM!","The Ira Gilded One erupted first as his True Appendage tore free of his back, THE Gauntlets of the Unspent Fury, colossal crimson gauntlets forged from every rage he had ever swallowed, and he met THE Creature’s charge head-on as their fists collided with a detonation that vaporized miles of the red sea! THE Creature took the blow across his jaw, dark blood scattering, and answered with THE Burden, slamming the wrathful titan down through the boiling waves as he followed him under, fists hammering down like falling eras!","The Superbius one moved a breath later, golden light screaming as his own Appendage bloomed, THE Crown of the Unbowed Summit, a floating diadem of golden Dimensional weavings that tore reality apart in halos around him, and his declarations rained down upon THE Creature’s back, shredding the claimed sea, ripping wounds across obsidian shoulders even as their Trueness kept leaking, kept bleeding, their every technique arriving thinner than the last!","CRACK!","THE Creature caught the Ira one’s gauntlet mid-swing and broke the arm behind it over his knee!","The wrathful being howled as THE MAW opened along the titan’s shoulder and bit the crimson Appendage in half, devouring fury mid-scream, and THE Creature spun through the golden declarations raining from above, taking two across the chest, bleeding, always bleeding, and not slowing at all, as he seized the Ira one by the skull and used a True Lifeform as a club to smash the descending Crown from the sky!","\"You...what did he DO?!\"","...!","And through all of it, both Gilded beings kept glancing hatefully at the scholar!"]},{"number":5509,"title":"Chapter 5509: Chapter 5508: The Explorer! II","paragraphs":["They kept glancing at the explorer who floated calmly beyond the battle with no authority around him whatsoever, doing, as far as any sense could detect, absolutely nothing.","And when they looked at him in their fury, they actually saw him wiping sweat from his forehead, dabbing at it with his sleeve like an academic in an overheated lecture hall, and they wanted to curse him! What was he so tired from when he was just floating there?!","...!","Their distraction cost them everything.","THE Creature’s Pantheon closed. The red sea folded upward in continental walls as the Burden descended one final time upon both leaking, doubting, hemorrhaging existences, and THE MAW opened wider than it had ever opened, wide as a horizon, and THE Creature drove both Gilded True Lifeforms into it with his own bleeding hands!","He devoured them!","Their bodies, their Appendages, their screaming and unraveling Intents, wrath and pride and every last golden thread of two True existences, all of it poured down into the burning dark of THE MAW as the sea finally, finally went still!","And THE Creature fell.","His titanic frame smashed into the calm red water and lay there, half-sunken, breathing heavily as obsidian flames flickered low across dozens of wounds, his existence groaning as it began to heal! Deep within him, the boons of devouring two powerful True Lifeforms churned through his foundations, wrath and pride and Trueness breaking down into raw existential wealth, his frame drinking it all as his grades creaked upward, and Existence, for once, simply floated on its back and processed.","\"...\"","Anaximander whistled and floated over.","The scholar drifted across the settling waves, and then his eyes blinked wide in wonder as he finally noticed the colossal pale limb floating in the distance, the severed leg with clouds around its heel!","\" Oh my. What Lifeform left such a limb behind?\"","His eyes sparkled with a pure, bottomless need to understand.","THE Creature breathed out heavily from the water, and waved one bleeding hand.","\" The limb of a Primeval One. You can have it. \" He said it flatly, easily.","\"I wouldn’t have even come close to getting it without your help.\"","...!","He said such words casually, handing away a treasure that a True Lifeform of the Sixth Scale had been bleeding themselves to siphon, for THE Creature had tremendous control over his greed!","Anaximander blinked at him. Then he laughed, loud and delighted, robes shaking.","\" What use have I for something so big? Come on, I’ll study it, maybe cook a bit of it, and then you can have it after.\" He settled cross-legged onto the air above the healing titan, grinning. \"It is great seeing you again, Old Friend. I only wish Osmont was here too, so we could all enjoy this properly! I have so many stories. I met so many interesting things! There was this dimension made entirely of arguments, and a creature that only existed on alternating days, and...\"","THE Creature calibrated his existence in the water below, and interrupted mildly.","\" Osmont is in this Dimension too. Just somewhere very far, as I can’t easily reach him.\"","At these words, Anaximander’s eyes lit up like twin stars!","\" Osmont is here too? Haha! \" The Explorer clapped his hands once. \" Then it should be easy for us all to get together. I can just take us to him.\"","...!","THE Creature’s eyes shone with brilliance as he looked up at Anaximander.","The restricted weavings of THE Krazhor-Nul. The veils that blinded even Ryaenara. The distances that severed messages! And this man, this authority-less scholar, stood on the air and offered to simply walk past all of it, because doors, and distances, and ancient Dimensional restrictions, were superstitions he had never subscribed to.","Right. He was Anaximander!","And between him and Osmont, THE Creature could truly not decide who was more of an anomaly. He shook his head as...","His aura began to surge upwards!","THE Creature lay half-sunken in the calm red sea as the digestion of two True Lifeforms truly began, and it was a heavy feast even for Existence! Wrath and pride broke down within THE MAW’s deep furnaces as two devoured Intents unwound into raw Trueness, two consumed Pantheons dissolved into dense existential wealth, and his obsidian flames climbed higher and higher off his healing frame as his aura swelled in slow, rising tides that made the storm above the sea circle like stirred water.","And while he digested, Anaximander drifted over to the limb.","The scholar floated up alongside the colossal severed leg of the Primeval One, craning his neck to take in its full scale, the pale unrotted flesh, the clouds gathered around its heel, the residual grandeur that kept the red waves flattened for miles, and he shook his head with unhidden marvel.","\" You know, after I left our Observable Existence, I crossed through multiple Dimensions ,\" he said, walking slowly along the air beside the limb as if strolling a museum hall . \"I just wanted to get away and explore! And in all the Dimensions I have been in, all of them, Primeval Lifeforms are deemed those at the top. The apex above apexes! You do not readily find a limb of one just...lying around.\" He gestured at it, delighted.","\"I heard stories of Dimensions that served as old battlefields, places where many Primeval and True Lifeforms died in ancient wars, and I was planning on making a trip to one eventually. But this will do...\"","He said such words casually.","THE Creature watched him from the water as the digestion churned on, and he couldn’t help but ask.","\" Your path is somewhat unique. What do you normally gain from something like this?\"","Anaximander smiled.","And then, shockingly, he came near the limb, the very limb that two Gilded True Lifeforms had been straining and sweating to siphon, whose residual grandeur had fought a Cenozoic-adjacent being thread by thread, and simply placed his hand on it!","His lack of aura, his lack of power, his lack of anything, seemingly did not cause the limb to even react! The dead flesh that had resisted True Lifeforms accepted the palm of a scholar with no authority the way a book accepts being opened, and Anaximander patted it fondly.","\" There is an old parable I heard in one of the many worlds I visited,\" he said. \" This one was about a two-thousand-year-old Taoist, and it went like this. A farmer lost his only horse, and his neighbors cried for his bad luck. The farmer simply asked, how do you know it is bad?\" His hand drifted along the pale flesh as he spoke.","\" The next day, the horse returned, and brought a dozen wild horses with it. The neighbors cheered for his good fortune. The farmer asked, how do you know it is good?\"","THE Creature listened from the red water, flames rising slowly.","\" Days later, the farmer’s son fell off one of the wild horses and broke his leg. The neighbors cried about the bad luck. The farmer asked, how do you know it is bad?\" Anaximander’s voice carried easily across the still sea.","\" And soon, the army arrived to draft all able-bodied young men for a war. But the son was skipped, because of his broken leg. And the neighbors rejoiced at his luck!\"","He turned back toward the healing titan, and his scholar’s eyes were bright.","\"The lesson in it was simple. All knowledge is temporary! You never know the full story when events happen. The horse leaving was the horses arriving. The broken leg was the saved life! True wisdom is accepting life as it comes, because the story is never finished when you judge it.\"","...!"]},{"number":5510,"title":"Chapter 5510: Chapter 5509: Giving! I","paragraphs":["He patted the Primeval limb once more.","\"So, what do I gain from something like this? Exactly that. I know things I have no control over will happen, big guy. They always do. Horses leave, and armies come. I cannot stop any of it.\" He shrugged, and there was nothing resigned in the gesture at all, only appetite.","\" So I just seek more and more knowledge, to just maybe understand those things when they happen...or get through them. Understanding the power of beings like Primeval Lifeforms is a good test of knowledge! And knowledge is the only thing I will ever need, while I prepare for whatever existence sends my way.\" He laughed at himself, waving a hand.","\" Haha, I talked too much, it’s been a while since I had company that talks back! I’ll be done with a preliminary look soon, and then I’ll see if I can take us to Osmont.\"","With these words, Anaximander focused.","He closed his eyes while touching the limb, his tousled head bowing slightly, a man with no authority quietly reading the corpse-flesh of an apex being like a text, and the red sea went very still around him.","And THE Creature, half-sunken and healing, thought about the story.","How do you know what is good or what is bad?","He turned the parable over in his flat, ancient way. His other half, brutalized before his eyes, the worst thing existence had ever done to him, and the reason he had carried every burden alone since. It was..Bad. Surely bad!","And yet that carrying had grown into THE Burden of Existence, the appendage that had crushed a Serpent and hammered Gilded True Lifeforms into THE MAW among many more. The statue, inherited and unwanted, foreign weight wearing his name. Bad? It had risen for him many now, and he still breathed! Even today, pressed bloody across a red sea by a Cenozoic-equivalent being, moments from a loss that would have ended eras of solitude, bad, plainly bad, and it had forced him to finally finish the weavings he had refused for so long, that connections were not only things he protected. And the finishing had brought Anaximander, and Anaximander was about to bring Osmont!","\"...\"","How do you know it is good or bad?","He didn’t.","Existence itself, and he could not judge his own story mid-telling.","\"Hm,\" THE Creature said quietly to the red water, and let the parable settle into his foundations.","Then he had to focus himself.","For eating the Intent and Pantheon of an Ananke Intent True Lifeform, alongside the Intent and Pantheon of an Egoic Intent True Lifeform, was truly a heavy feast! Wrath’s seamless pride and inevitability’s golden grammar poured through his deepest weavings as his own Intent drank and drank, and the accounting of the digestion ran clear before him. It should be enough to take him to Ananke as well.","Just barely!","Enough to carry Existence itself across the threshold of the second order, from I am...to I must be obeyed!","So he focused.","And like this, the red sea closed on the two of them.","A scholar in white robes with his eyes shut and his palm upon the limb of a dead apex being, reading! A titan of obsidian flame half-sunken in arterial waters, digesting two True existences toward inevitability! Neither of them speaking, neither of them moving, the storm turning in slow reverence overhead.","And around the two of them, unfathomable Trueness gathered in silent, invisible waves!","...!","---","<THE True Human Emperor>","Ever since he became THE True Human Emperor, Noah felt like he had become more...contemplative.","He thought about many things now, in the drifting quiets between eruptions, and he had come to understand that this was not idleness. It was work! For a True Lifeform advanced through Identity, and Identity was not a treasure one stumbled upon, it was a territory one surveyed. If he was not turning his own self over, examining its borders, questioning its choices, then he would not truly be advancing at all. Contemplation was cultivation now. The throne was also a training ground!","And after transcribing THE Protagonist, his last Letter, or perhaps his potential last Letter, his thoughts had circled back to a decision he had made without ever formally making it.","Why had he never made INFINITE one of the Letters of THE Osmontian Tongue?","He turned the question over honestly! Infinity was the root of him, the fireball skill book, the mana, the first Cause, the boundless rivers he traveled by. Surely it deserved a Letter? And yet every time he weighed it, it did not feel like it could stand entirely true! For he was not Infinity itself, he was Osmontian, and Infinity was one of the things his identity expressed. To carve INFINITE into his backbone felt like claiming a robe was the body! He wanted to stand for Infinity through his Osmontian identity, not beside it.","And the Source received no Letter for the same deeper reason. He had long since fused Source and Infinity into Osmontian Source Infinity, one thing, seamless, his! Declaring them as separate Letters felt like...seperation. Like undoing a marriage to honor the spouses individually!","Well. This was how he currently felt. He could always change his mind.","And as he was thinking all this, the chaotic tendrils of Infinity nearby had gathered to him.","They floated in like rivers finding their sea, wild currents of the storm bending down to the golden island and coiling around his seated figure, and Noah read them idly, the information they carried of where they had been, of the ancient territories they had raged across, of things that had passed through them in ages past! It was like listening to well-traveled elders gossip, and he had been at it for hours.","Then the surroundings fluctuated heavily!","Noah rose to attention in an instant, Intent gathering, wings a thought away, for something was folding space nearby and folding it close, and in this Dimension, arrivals were rarely gentle...!","WAP!","The air split, and THE Creature appeared!","The titanic figure landed upon the edge of the golden sands wrapped in his obsidian flames, freshly-healed wounds still tracing pale lines across his frame, his aura carrying a new density that Noah’s senses flagged immediately! And behind him, hanging in the storming sky...","Was a foot.","A colossal severed limb floated in space above the golden island, pale and unrotted and vast beyond framing, clouds gathered around its heel as its residual grandeur pressed the storm flat for miles, and standing before it, wiping his brow, was a man in white scholarly robes!","\"... Anaximander?\""]},{"number":5511,"title":"Chapter 5511: Chapter 5510: Giving! II","paragraphs":["Noah looked ahead with open surprise as THE Infiniverse and Emotive turned sharply, and even Seo-yeon’s eyes snapped open from her sensing, all of them taking in the entrants, and all of them especially staring at the floating limb!","Anaximander wiped his brows as if he were genuinely tired, and then he saw Noah, and his whole face lit up! He took a step, and appeared directly before the throne, and pulled Noah into a laughing bro hug, clapping his back.","\"It has been many months, my friend! You look good!\"","Noah shook his head as he returned the embrace and looked the explorer over.","He looked good? How the hell had this supposedly weak explorer made it to a Dimension this terrifying? And months had passed for him, when barely days had passed since they had parted over the red-gold skies of their Lower Observable Existence?","Existence was truly vast and full of terrors!","\"It has been a little while,\" Noah said, his mouth curving as his gaze slid past the scholar’s shoulder. \" How did you end up here with...that?\"","Even Noah could not keep his attention off the heart-shaking limb behind them! Anaximander turned to follow his gaze, and it was the titanic figure of THE Creature, floating over across the sands, who answered.","\"I called Anaximander over after facing two Gilded True Lifeforms I could not overcome,\" THE Creature said flatly. \" The limb of a Primeval One was the boon from it that they were trying to devour.\"","...!","Noah’s brows rose.","THE Creature had met something he could not overcome, and the solution...was Anaximander? So this monstrous explorer held enough power to go against True Lifeforms as well? Noah smiled at the idea, another impossible line quietly added to the ledger of his strangest friend, and at this moment, a small figure padded across the golden sands.","Seo-yeon came over to greet the newcomer, stopping before him with her hands clasped politely, mirrored light drifting off her shoulders.","\" Hello, Aba’s friend! I am Seo-yeon! \" She tilted her head at him, and her small brows furrowed with genuine puzzlement. \" You are as powerful as Aba and the big Creature? But I don’t sense any authority from you...\"","Anaximander knelt down to her height and shook her small hand with complete seriousness.","\" Hello, Seo-yeon. It is very nice to meet you.\" He smiled, and answered her puzzle simply. \" Sometimes you don’t need authority to be powerful. You just need to be yourself.\"","...!","Seo-yeon’s eyes shone as she heard this, the words settling into her somewhere deep, and Noah watched his daughter store the sentance away like a treasure.","But his own gaze had already drifted back, again, to the limb of the Primeval One.","THE Creature watched him watching it, and thought for a moment, and then spoke.","\" You can have...a piece of it, if you want. It is currently Anaximander’s, for him to study.\"","Noah shook his head slowly.","His eyes were shining brilliantly, for he was thinking about something else entirely, an idea assembling itself piece by piece behind the shine, and he voiced out calmly soon after.","\" Do you two trust me?\"","...!","Anaximander rose up from Seo-yeon’s height and blinked. He looked at THE Creature. THE Creature looked at him. The two of them nodded.","\" Then give me ownership of this entire limb.\"","...!","He said the words calmly!","And with how prized the thing floating before them was, a corpse-piece of an apex being that Sixth Scale existences had bled to siphon, anyone else hearing such words might break off relations on the spot and call him greedy! But Anaximander and THE Creature both only raised their brows, exchanged one more glance, and nodded lightly.","\" It’s yours, \" Anaximander said.","HUUM!","Noah’s figure rose from the throne at this.","For he was thinking about many things. About the utility and usage of something like THE Tide That Owes Nothing. About what things were considered his, or not his, in the deep accounting of existence! About what things he could give away, and what the act of giving truly required.","He had a daring idea he wanted to try.","He floated near the limb, and the pressure hit him like a wall. Even dead, even severed, the residual grandeur of a Primeval One pressed against his existence in slow crushing waves, and Noah could barely get near it, his newly-elevated C-Rank Intent flaring out grandly around his body as identity pushed back against the weight of an apex corpse! Endless blue bloomed beneath the colossal foot as his Osmontian Source Infinity formed a vast platform at its base, and Noah strained!","His body burned with effort as the platform groaned, and slowly, barely, the limb of a Primeval One began to move! Inch by trembling inch, he floated it forward, and through the strain he could feel it happening, some deep weaving of existence turning its pages, conditions of ownership being met one by one through the sweat of genuine effort, the thing becoming his not by word but by work!","And then, barely holding the limb aloft, Noah turned to Anaximander behind him, and spoke heavily through the strain.","\"I give freely and openly...this treasure of mine...to you.\"","HUUM!","Anaximander looked toward Noah as if wondering just what game his friend was playing. He just asked for it, and was now giving it back?","And as Noah did this, he raised his gaze above, and wondered.","Was his capability truly so busted? Would this even lead to anything? Could-","BOOOM!","Before his thoughts even finished, the skies above them tore open!","An aura bloomed through the tear, and it was heavy, tens of times heavier than the limb floating below it, pressing down upon the entire golden island as Noah looked up in astonishment, as Anaximander’s jaw actually dropped, as even THE Creature’s flat eyes widened, and through it all, booming prompts arrived!","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has been triggered.|","...!","Oh!","It was simply an idea he wanted to try! Simply...an idea!"]},{"number":5512,"title":"Chapter 5512: Chapter 5511: Predator and Prey! I","paragraphs":["Something immensely pristine and magisterial was emerging!","Noah looked up, and the Dimension itself was splitting apart! The heavy skies of THE Krazhor-Nul tore open along a widening seam as white and gold light pulsed outward for light years, waves of pristine radiance rolling across the storm and flattening it, and through the tear, condensing out of the light with unbearable slowness...was a limb!","It formed lengthwise, vast and pale and rounded, extending down through the split skies in a long thick column of white-gold flesh, and Noah stared up at its emerging shape with his astonishment slowly acquiring a very specific quality.","No way, right?","The limb kept extending! Long, cylindrical, rounded at its emerging tip, radiating apex grandeur across light years, and Noah, THE True Human Emperor, found himself tilting his head at the boon descending from his most sacred Foundation as a single unworthy thought refused to leave.","No. No way. The Tide wouldn’t!","And then hair erupted across it!","Pristine white hairs bloomed along the entire column in cascading waves, silken and radiant and flowing, and the shape resolved at last into what it had always been becoming, a tail!","A colossal severed tail of some Primeval being, its white-gold hairs drifting weightlessly across the torn sky, each strand humming with power, and Noah breathed out in relief.","But this was only the first.","Two more auras bloomed through the tear, and both of them exceeded the limb of the Primeval One floating below by at least tens of times. The whole golden island groaned under their arrival as Emotive grabbed Seo-yeon close, and the second emergence condensed into view.","It was a portion of a brain!","A vast hemisphere of white-gold cerebral matter, its folded surface glowing along every ridge and valley, a cerebral cortex of some apex existence with rivers of luminous thought-essense still flickering through its folds like trapped lightning, dead and yet dreaming, its presense pressing down with a weight that made Intent itself feel observed!","And lastly...came the bubble.","It emerged smallest of the three, a translucent sphere no larger than a palace, and it was undoubtedly the most astonishing and heart-shaking of them all! For within the bubble drifted cells. Ancient, colossal, slowly-turning cells of pure white-gold, each one a cathedral of primordial architecture, their membranes woven from layered lattices of proto-existence, their nuclei burning like compressed dawns! They were totipotent, the primeval root-cells from which anything could grow, flesh or organ or appendage or existence itself, undifferentiated and therefore unlimited, each one humming with the terrifying patience of matter that had not yet chosen what to become! Merely gazing at them, Noah’s Sight could perceive infinite branching futures folded inside every membrane, wings and eyes and hearts and things without names, all of them waiting, all of them possible!","And the moment all three finished forming, the prompts arrived.","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has answered the single greatest act of giving you have ever performed. You strained your existence to claim true ownership of a Primeval One’s limb, and gave it away freely in the same breath. The Sharpened Returns have reached across depths I cannot source, and I will catalogue what has emerged.|","| First: THE Blank Caudal of the Unwritten Primeval . A template tail-appendage of Primeval grade, unwritten by any Intent.|","| Second: THE Blank Cortex of the Unwritten Primeval. A template cerebral appendage of Primeval grade, likewise unwritten.|","| Third: THE Primeval Totipotent Cell Source. A preserved cluster of Primeval totipotent cells, the root-matter of apex existence itself, capable of becoming anything.|","|The formation of these three goes against existence itself. They are Primeval Appendages and Source bearing no Intent except a basal, enigmatic, and tyrannical Primeval Intent, and that Intent looks down upon everything. Upon this Dimension. Upon all of you. They acknowledge no claim and await no owner! If they are not locked down and taken into an existence within the next nanosecond, they will disappear across Dimensions and Time.|","...!","Noah roared out!","\" Catch the other two! They will disappear in a nanosecond if left alone!\"","He bellowed it in the span of an instant as his crown was already spinning, THE Infiniverse already dissolving into his chest, the fusion of THE Quintessential Confluence slamming through his body mid-flight as he shot upward toward the one he could not bear to lose, the most overwhelming of the three, the cluster of cells! And behind him, astonished and yet instant, THE Creature blurred toward the white-haired tail as Anaximander simply took a step and appeared before the cerebral cortex.","Noah arrived before the bubble of cells.","And their aura hit him like the contempt of a mountain range.","The cluster radiated terrific white-gold grandeur, power and arrogance woven into every turning membrane, a basal Primeval Intent gazing down upon the fused confluence of three True Lifeforms the way emperors gaze at petitioners, and the bubble was already thinning, already sliding sideways out of the grip of the present, Dimensions and Time opening around it like doors!","\" COME!\"","Noah bellowed as he unleashed everything!","His Intent erupted at its fused grandeur as his Osmontian Source Infinity poured out in continental tides, cerulean seas crashing around the bubble from every direction, and he barely, barely surrounded the cluster, his power straining against that tyrannical basal Intent like hands around a falling star! It was not enough to hold. He could feel it! The cells looked down upon his grip and were already leaving, and to actually obtain them, to take them into his existence, he would have to exert everything and then more than everything.","And through the strain, prompts buzzed in his mind.","|From your immense giving, you have also gained 5,000,000 Osmontian Biomass. Current reserves: 5,163,000.|","Five million!","The number landed, and Noah did not celebrate it, he spent it.","\" All facets of my existence, upgrade them to Rank C! And my Intent...\" His roar tore across the light-flooded sky as the cells strained against his seas! \" Take THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian to Rank B!\"","|Executing everything at once, Master. The required number of Osmontian Biomass will vary for different upgrades of your existence as your existence has been rapidly elevating from the surroundings and from the foods and products you have been consuming.|","...!"]},{"number":5513,"title":"Chapter 5513: Chapter 5512: Predator and Prey! II","paragraphs":["|Osmontian Source Infinity elevated to C-Rank, Straif, the Blackthorn, the grade of sharpness and consequence. Cost: 300,000.|","|Volume elevated to C-Rank. Output elevated to C-Rank. Trueness elevated to C-Rank.|","|The remaining Foundations, elevated through their grades to C-Rank, Straif: THE Unkneeling Crown. THE Mirror That Keeps. THE Hunger That Refines. THE Unmoved Verdict. THE Pure Trajectory. THE All-Drawing Stillness. THE Remembered Truth. And THE Sovereign Existence, your Ninth, whose imposition of your identity upon nearby existence now carries the Blackthorn’s edge. Cost: 1,960,000.|","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing, your Second Foundation, elevated to B-Rank, Ngetal, the Reed, the grade of reach and pervasion. Its returns now range from twenty thousand to one hundred thousandfold, and its Sharpened Returns have deepened into Woven Returns, boons that may now arrive already interlinked with your existing capabilities. Cost: 1,100,000.|","|And THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian, elevated from C-Rank, Straif, to B-Rank, Ngetal. Cost: 1,250,000. Within THE Quintessential Confluence, it now functions at A-Rank, Idho, the Yew, the grade of near-permanence and authority over endings.|","|Total expenditure: 4,760,000. Remaining reserves: 403,000. Every facet of your existence now stands at C-Rank or above, and your Intent stands within the peak.|","...!","The pressure of his existence began to change!","It was visible! Across the light-flooded sky, Noah’s fused frame erupted with the settling weight of an entire existence rising grades in a single breath, his hair blazing brighter as the lemniscate rings in his eyes multiplied, and around him, billowing prismatic cerulean seas of his A-Rank-functioning Intent surged outward and wrapped around the cluster of cells in layer after layer after layer!","And finally...there was some form of stability!","The tyrannical basal Intent of the cells pressed against his seas, and for the first time, the seas did not thin! The bubble’s sideways slide through Dimensions and Time slowed, and strained, and stopped, ancient arrogance meeting an identity that had just paid millions of Biomass for the right to disagree with it, and the two pressures ground against each other in silence above the golden island!","Noah reached his hand out to grasp them!","...!","---","<THE Recorder of Wilds>","Countless gigaparsecs from a golden island, upon a drifting cloud of solid gold, an old woman in white robes was having her tea.","The cloud floated placidly through the storming dark of THE Krazhor-Nul as its owner sat cross-legged at its center, a full tea set arranged before her upon a lacquered tray, steam curling gently from a cup so ancient its glaze had forgotten its original color.","Her long white hair was pinned loosely with a single wooden stick, her wrinkled face was folded into an expression of profound peace, and around her frame, the lethal ambient density of this Dimension, the pressure that killed non-True Lifeforms in minutes and made True ones wary...simply did not apply!","The rain of authorities parted around her cloud out of what could only be called respect.","She was Primeval.","And she was, at this moment, being interrupted mid-sip.","Far below her drifting cloud, a procession moved across the dark geography, and it was vast! More than twenty True Lifeforms traveled in loose formation across the storm, and more than half of them pressed upon existence with the weight of THE Cenozoic Scale, a gathering of apex beings. Among them coiled Ormarr Grimtunge, the great Serpent whole once more. Beneath them all, dragging the storm sideways with its ambient wrongness, walked a Steed. And at the very head of the procession, leading all of it, flew a woman in red robes.","The old woman set down her cup, leaned comfortably forward upon her cloud, and began to speak. To no one. To herself , in warm, hushed, marveling tones, as she always did, for she had been talking herself through the wilds of existence for longer than most Dimensions had held their shapes.","\" Here we see...a migration of tepid animals. Twenty and some, more than half of them Cenozoic. Now that is a rare sight. A colony this size only leaves the nest for a handful of reasons. Whatever could their reason be...\"","She settled in comfortably, the way one does before a long-awaited nature scene, and her voice echoed out with old, patient wonder.","\" Every animal has a part to play in the ecosystem of existence. Some are prey. Some are predators. And many, many more live somewhere in between, scavengers, followers, grazers, mimics, each one filling its little role in the great turning of things. It is easy to forget, watching the big ones stomp about, that the roles were never chosen. They simply grew into them. And here...here we have nearly the whole cast in a single frame.\"","She lifted a wrinkled finger toward the figure at the head of the procession.","\" There. At the front is...a predator.\"","The red-robed woman flew cold-faced through the storm, and her entire existence emanated bloodlust and brutality! Her crimson eyes stared dead ahead, unblinking, and around her frame the very weavings of the Dimension seemed to thin and part, not out of respect, as they did for the old woman’s cloud, but out of the simple instinct of things avoiding an edge.","She did not speak as she simply moved, and twenty True Lifeforms moved behind her!","\" This predator seems to be a proper one, too. Her weavings reveal she us...Lissana. Look at her. No wasted motion, no chatter, no play. She’s shaped like a blade because that is what her path made of her, killing, refined across a True existence until nothing else was left. Even the others keep just slightly behind her wake. They don’t do that out of respect. They do it the way small fish keep clear of a shark’s mouth, without ever quite thinking about it. She could thin this entire column before it agreed on a direction to run...\"","Her finger drifted back along the formation, and her old eyes creased with rich amusement.","\" And here, oh, here we have a much more common creature. The Serpent, Ormarr. His Trueness seems injured, and his position...it is not at the head, where a beast his size belongs, but tucked at her flank, held low, adjusting himself to her wake stroke by stroke.That makes him... a follower. A creature that seeks any path for himself, whichever one is nearest and strongest at the time, and today her path happens to be it. He’s been hurt somewhere, badly, and so he presses up against a bigger predator and performs harmlessness while he waits for his chance to matter again. Nature makes a great many of these. They survive wonderfully. They just never quite become anything.\"","...!"]},{"number":5514,"title":"Chapter 5514: Chapter 5513: Predator and Prey! III","paragraphs":["She chuckled into her sleeve, and swept her finger across the broader host.","\" As for the rest of the colony, followers too, but of a gentler sort. Followers of their own paths of advancement. The antlered one, the three-faced one, the stone hound at the rear, each of them walked their own long road to Trueness, and each of them is here because a keeper called and the rewards seemed worth the errand. Look at how loosely they fly. Boredom, in a war-column! Every one of them is idly wondering why so many were sent for so small a task, and every one of them expects to be home before their perch cools. That is the comfort of a herd that has never once been thinned. I’ve seen that comfort many times, in many magnificent gatherings.\" She sipped her tea. \"I rarely saw it twice in the same gathering.\"","Then she paused, and her voice turned musing, the idle wondering of a very old watcher turning a specimen over in her mind.","\" Though it does make one think, watching the Serpent groom himself against her shadow. These creatures call themselves True. Their whole existence rests on a seamless claim of I am. But if an animal fully and completely follows another, choosing nothing, steering nothing, simply attaching itself to whichever wake is strongest...is it truly true? Can a claim of I am survive a lifetime of I follow? Hm... \" She smiled into her cup.","\" Nature loves a paradox. She hides them in the strangest burrows.\"","Then her voice dropped, hushing into genuine reverence, and she turned her finger downward, to the thing beneath them all.","\" And there. Quietly now.\"","The Steed of Oblivion moved through the dark like a wound of Existence.","It was colossal beyond even this host combined, a mountainous quadruped whose hide had gone the gray of forgotten things, whose failing First Cause flickered through its frame in guttering terminal weavings like a city being unlit district by district, and around it for vast miles, existence simply dimmed.","Ambient essense thinned. The storm quieted! Even the cursed rain seemed reluctant to land upon it, and it walked with its great head hung low, chained at the throat, radiating an ambient field of dimensional suppression that made even the Cenozoic beings above it keep their distance!","\"A burden-bearer of the first broods ,\" the old woman breathed. \" Bred as a unique type of living Observable Existence when this Dimension was young and its makers still walked it. Look at what’s left of the poor thing. That guttering in its weavings is a First Cause ages deep into its dying. And that awful dimming around it, that used to be the very gift that carried riders between Dimensions, curdled now into a walking suppression that chokes every dimensional law that comes near. The keepers, those vile progeny thst are cursed, use them as weapons these days. Imagine finding one of the rarest songbirds in existence and deciding its best use is as a club.\" She sighed, long and old.","\"It is in constant pain. Every step. And it has been walking a very, very long time. What a painful existence. Almost makes one want to make a move and put such a thing out of its misery. Would that not ve simpler? Easier? But alas...I am only here at the behest of s friend and will not be involved on any other matters.\"","She refreshed her tea, unhurried, as the war-host crawled on below.","\"But...let’s take stock, shall we? A predator, unwrapped after ages in the drawer. A follower serpent hiding in her shadow, hoping her path will carry him somewhere. Twenty comfortable creatures on their own roads, too mighty to look behind themselves. And a dying burden-bearer dragged along as a siege engine, which The Jarls only ever unchain for prey they genuinely fear losing. Fear. A dying titan has been frightened into spending every treasure he owns at once, and not one of the treasures has thought to ask why...why exactly is such a sordid group of animals moving, and to where?\"","She was asking herself of their purpose!","And... that was when she sensed it!","BOOM!","Countless gigaparsecs away, blinding white-gold light erupted across the deep dark!","The old woman’s cup paused halfway to her lips! Her ancient eyes, eyes that had watched eras the way others watched seasons, widened by a full measure as the distant radiance pulsed across the Dimension, and the flavor of it reached her with unmistakable clarity. Pristine. Magisterial. Apex!","Weavings of a Primeval One!","\"... Oh ?\" she said.","But there shouldn’t be any of her kind in the immediate surroundings?","The old woman sipped her tea slowly, and looked back down at the procession, at the cold predator in red and the fawning Serpent and the twenty comfortable mighty.","They were all heading towards that same direction as after seeing that light, they became even faster!","\" Well now. It seems somwthing interesting is at play...\" She set down her cup and rose, white robes settling around her small frame as her golden cloud began to drift downward. \" I assumed this was a colony marching on prey. Easy pickings for a dying keeper’s larder. But that light out there...say differently.\"","Her cloud descended through the storm, closer and closer to the marching party, and her old eyes gleamed.","\"So the question flips over. Is this herd closing on a meal, or are those ahead the predators instead?\"","A small, ancient smile folded through her wrinkles as she loved to observe nature and how it unfolded.","With that, the old woman floated her golden cloud extremely close to the party of True Lifeforms, settling in barely above Ormarr’s own coils, near enough to see the crimson eyes of the predator in red staring dead ahead, near enough to catch the idle words of the comfortable mighty, near enough to hear the Steed’s labored breathing, her tea set clinking gently as she poured herself a fresh cup in the middle of their formation!","And not a single one of them, not the blade, not the Serpent, not twenty True Lifeforms, not even the dying Steed of Those Who Remain...","Could see or sense her at all!"]},{"number":5515,"title":"Chapter 5515: Chapter 5514: Predator and Prey! IV","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","His Intent stood at A-Rank, Idho, and Noah had never felt anything like it!","Within the fusion of THE Quintessential Confluence, THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian functioned at the grade of near-permanence and authority over endings, and its grandeur was something he couldnt fully understand just yet.","Identity so dense it functioned as inevitability. I am, spoken with such weight that existence stopped checking!","And yet...there was more.","He could feel it at the very edges of his Intent, a trembling, a readiness, as if the whole of his identity stood before a door it had only just discovered! His Intent almost felt like it was about to undergo another evolution, something past Ananke entirely. But it was like there was something missing. The door stood, and his Intent pressed against it, and it did not open! Maybe there was one more step. One more truth to live, one more claim to earn!","Either way, that trembling readiness allowed him to erupt with a terrifying immensity right now, and right now was what mattered!","\" COME!\"","Noah bellowed out as he pulled!","The cluster of Primeval Totipotent Cells strained against his billowing prismatic seas one final time, tyrannical basal Intent glaring down at him across the gap of Scales, and Noah simply refused it, his A-Rank-functioning Intent crashing over that ancient arrogance in wave after wave as he forcefully dragged the bubble out of its sideways slide and into his existence! The translucent sphere of white-gold cells flowed toward his chest, shrinking as it came, cathedral-cells folding down and down as his Osmontian Source Infinity wrapped them in layer upon layer of endless blue, and they sank into him!","Through his chest. Through his weavings! Down through the deep architecture of everything he was, Noah guiding them with gritted teeth into the very core of his Source, into the endless sea of blue at the heart of his existence where his Infinity churned without shore or floor, and there, in the deepest waters of himself...he anchored them down!","HUUM!","He felt their immense Primeval aura the whole way, contempt and grandeur pressing against his inner seas.","But the moment they finished entering his existence...the cells became still.","The tyrannical basal Intent quieted like a storm crossing into a temple, and his Intent and Osmontian Source Infinity began to flood into them, blue tides washing across white-gold membranes as the cluster settled at his core, slowly turning, slowly drinking, ancient totipotency meeting an identity that had paid everything for the right to hold it.","|You have successfully contained THE Primeval Totipotent Cell Source. It is anchored at the core of your Source, and it has ceased resisting. Your Trueness is now permeating across the cells, and due to their totipotent nature, they will not remain blank. Something wholly yours, carrying a profound Primeval origin, will emerge from them in time. I cannot yet model what.|","...!","Noah breathed out heavily as he felt things stabilizing within him, the two pressures at his core settling into a slow, watchful equilibrium, and he finally looked around.","And the sights around him were something!","THE Creature stood tall in the air a distance away, and his obsidian flames were rapidly rising in tempersture! They billowed hotter and brighter around his titanic frame with every breath, and the reason stuck out plainly behind him, a tail.","THE Blank Caudal of the Unwritten Primeval had rooted itself at the base of his spine, colossal and white-haired and drifting, and its pristine radiance was bleeding up through his flames as they changed, traces of white-gold threading through the obsidian fire like dawn invading a midnight.","And Anaximander...","Anaximander was clutching his head with both hands as if he had the headache of several lifetimes! The scholar hovered lopsided in the air, white robes askew, wincing as THE Blank Cortex of the Unwritten Primeval settled somewhere into his existence, and yet even through the wincing, his eyes were shining with pure amazement, and he looked over towards Noah with an expression that asked, louder than words, just how in all of existence did you DO that?!","Noah only smiled.","He felt no negative way at all towards THE Creature and Anaximander obtaining the other two boons. How could he? He wouldn’t have even gotten anything without them giving him the original limb freely, and in that screaming nanosecond, he would never have been able to lock all three down alone anyways. Two Primeval templates in the hands of his two strongest friends. The Tide had fed all of them, and Noah found that outcome...deeply Osmontian.","He let go of the fusion.","The Confluence released as his grades settled back down a rank, Ruination’s strings reweaving into the circlet upon his brow as THE Infiniverse stepped lightly out of his chest and appeared beside him, her composed eyes immediately turning inward, no doubt inspecting the new Primeval tenant anchored in her Master’s core! Noah rolled his shoulders as the quiet weight of one True Lifeform settled back over him, reserves at 403,000+, every facet at Straif or above, and a cluster of apex root-cells slowly turning in his deepest sea!","He was about to put his full focus on the cells inside him when...","\" Aba.\"","Seo-yeon’s voice cut across the golden sands, and it was frowning.","Noah turned. His daughter still sat upon the throne’s handle once more, but her eyes were open now, her small brows drawn together, mirrored light flickering unevenly off her shoulders as she stared out into the storming dark.","\" Aba, I can finally sense something. The heaviness went away for a moment when all that light happened, and now I can feel them clearly, but...\" Her frown deepened as she shook her small head. \"It does not make sense.\"","Noah crossed the sands to her in an instant, kneeling to her height as his voice came level.","\" What do you feel?\"","\"Two clusters.\" Seo-yeon’s hands rose, and she pointed in two entirely different directions across the dark geography, her fingers trembling faintly with the strain of holding both threads at once. \" Two clusters of pained, dying Causes. They hurt, Aba. They hurt so much, like Chernobyl hurt, but there are so potent, and they are in different directions, and...\" Her wide eyes lifted to her father’s face.","\" Both of them are coming towards us. Towards here. They are not wandering. They are coming...?\"","...!","Noah’s gaze turned heavy at these words!"]},{"number":5516,"title":"Chapter 5516: Chapter 5515: Existential Intermission- Lifeforms","paragraphs":["<Existential Intermission>","From the private records of THE Recorder of Wilds, kept across ages, read by no one.","—","I have been asked, exactly once in all my long wandering, what it is I actually do.","The asker was a mountain that had learned to speak, and I told it the truth. I study lifeforms and how they interact with space and time. That is all. Existence is a wilderness beyond any measuring, and wildernesses are made of the things that live in them, and someone ought to be writing it all down.","So. Today’s entry. Let us take stock of the great varieties, for my own amusement if nothing else.","—","Beginning with the Gilded Ones, since they insist on being noticed.","A Gilded Lifeform is what happens when a species decides that the self is a resource to be mined. Their entire civilization is built upon the Ego, amplified, refined, layered, and hammered into brilliance. Superbius, Ira, Invidia, Avaritia, all the grand flavors of self, worn like plumage. And I will say this clearly, because my records are honest even when the wilds are not. It actually works. Who would’ve thought?","A Gilded One’s amplified Ego is a genuine architecture of power, and the finest of them burn brighter than nearly anything on Vakochev’s Scales.","Their weakness is the same as their gift. An Ego amplified is an Ego exposed. I once watched a Gilded hierarch of the Superbius line refuse to retreat from a collapsing Dimension because retreating contradicted his self-image, and the Dimension closed over him like water over a dropped coin. All because he was trying his best to stay true to his pride. Magnificent. Foolish. The two are neighbors more often than not. I actually don’t like Gilded Lifeforms too much.","Then the Infinite Lifeforms, the children of boundlessness.","Where the Gilded mine the self, the Infinite mine the endless. Their Sources run on Infinity itself, that wild grammar of never-finishing, and it shapes them into creatures of escalation. An Infinite Lifeform does not ask what am I, it asks what more am I, and the answer never stops arriving. I have watched infant Infinite Ones lose fights they should have won because they were too busy growing mid-battle to bother defending, and I have watched elder Infinite Ones stack themselves upward through sheer accumulated more until Scales stopped describing them.","They too have Egos, and this is where matters become interesting, for an Infinite Ego does not amplify like a Gilded one. It compounds. Quietly. Endlessly. The most dangerous beings I have ever recorded were not the loud ones. They were Infinite Ones who had been compounding in silence for an age as many lean towards the calmer Egos.","Humility, Charity, Kindness...you know the ones.","The Source Lifeforms, next. The deep-rooted.","These draw their existence from THE Primordial Source, the oldest water in the oldest well, and it makes them dense in a way no other variety matches. A Source Lifeform of middling rank can often simply outlast a superior enemy, their weavings anchored so deep into the primordial that unraveling them is like trying to dig up a mountain’s roots with a spoon. They are slow to rise, slow to anger, slow to die. Patience, given a body.","And then...the Trueness.","Trueness is not a species. It is a threshold. Any of the varieties may cross it. A lifeform becomes True when its claim of I am goes seamless, when identity and existence stop being two things, and the moment that happens, the old categories elevate.","A Gilded One who crosses becomes a Gilded True Lifeform, their amplified Ego now welded to a seamless self, and these stand toe to toe with Source True Lifeforms, whose primordial density now carries a will that cannot be pried from it. I have watched exactly such a pair duel across a dead sea for six years, and I still could not tell you which variety is superior, only that the sea did not survive the question.","And apart even these, the True Infinite Lifeforms. Boundlessness made seamless. Compounding without ceiling, claimed without seam. I have recorded many in my ages. Some of them could match a Primeval Lifeform as...there are no absolutes in life.","There are Dimensions filled with entire Civilizations of one Lifeform that could sweep the floor with another.","There are Dimensions filled with monstrous Source True Lifeforms that even Primeval Lifeforms don’t wish to enter due to some ancient animosities.","Which brings me to my own kind.","Primeval Lifeforms are most time the apex across many Dimensions not because we are strongest, though we usually are, but because we are some of the earliest. Our weavings sit beneath the frameworks others climb. Scales, Tongues, Egos, all of it was built atop ground we were already standing on. This grants tremendous advantage and, I have come to believe, a tremendous laziness. My kind watches. Hoards. Grazes on Dimensions like fat cattle on endless grass. Very few of us are ever asked a hard question.","What is our purpose? To steer causes? To fight in major wars? Why...are we here?","Alas. Forget about any Existential Crises.","Then, we continue on with the ones that fit nowhere. My favorite entries in the Dimension of Existence I am currently visiting.","The Steeds. Living Observable Existences, bred as beasts by hands that predate my records, carrying First Causes the way other creatures carry hearts. No category holds them. They are Observable Existences that walk, and those here are dying, and that is a separate entry I have not yet had the stomach to finish.","But...this is one Dimension. There are many Dimensions as are there no Steeds that are not cursed? That move grandly even now?","There are THE Descendants of Those Who Remain, those whose blood is mixed with pure wonder as these fuckers...man oh man. Some are weak, some are powerful. But even the weak ones could do wonders.","And there are more. Oh, more. I have glimpsed things in the far folds that I have no shelf for. A lifeform that existed only as a debt passed between other lifeforms. A herd that was a single memory wearing ten thousand bodies. Something at the bottom of a drowned Dimension that I am fairly certain was a question, alive, and waiting to be asked. The Sealed One...eh, something that could be considered a big deal, and also not a big deal. It is all...relative.","There are a countless number of unique beings, scattered across Existence and its endless Dimensions. That is the true census, and it humbles every category I have ever drawn.","Existence is far too vast. Those within it are abundant beyond any recording.","Which is, of course, precisely why one records."]},{"number":5517,"title":"Chapter 5517: Chapter 5516: Marrow!","paragraphs":["Two dying Causes, coming towards them!","Noah’s expression was heavy as his mind turned through the possibilities. Why would this be happening? One possibility related to Ormarr, the Serpent had promised that they were coming. But the other...he couldn’t say for sure. Two clusters, two directions, both converging on their exact location as if the golden island had become a lodestone!","And he couldn’t even think about this in his usual terms of welcome Adversity, because this might be the type of adversity that was apocalyptic.","He was powerful. Every facet at Straif, an Intent at Ngetal, a Pantheon with absolute rulings! But he was not invincible, and the gap between those two words was where entire existences went to die. So he had to plan ahead thoroughly, and planning began with information.","He thought for a moment, and then knelt back down to his daughter’s height.","\" Seo-yeon. When you think about those two dying Causes coming over...how do they make you feel?\"","Seo-yeon’s small face scrunched up as she closed her eyes and reached back into the threads, her hands slowly rising to hover over her own chest as she felt them out.","\" The first one... \" Her voice went small. \" The first one feels bad, Aba. It hurts, but it’s a mean hurt. Like it’s been hurting so long that it turned into hating. It feels heavy and cruel and, and like it wants everything else to hurt too. Like a king who is angry at everyone.\" She shivered!","\" There are many little dying songs in that cluster, but they’re all chained to one big mean one.\"","Hatred and despotic emotions. A cluster of dying Causes chained to a cruel center! Noah’s eyes narrowed.","\" And the second?\"","\"The second one is... \" Seo-yeon’s brows unfurrowed, and her voice turned confused, almost wondering. \" The second one hurts just as much. Maybe more! It’s so old and so tired, Aba. But it doesn’t feel mean at all. It feels like...\"","She opened her eyes and looked up at her father with genuine puzzlement. \" It feels like hope? It’s dying and it’s hurting and it’s rushing here so fast, and the whole time it feels...hopeful.\"","...!","Hope?","Why would a cursed, dying thing be surging towards them with hope?!","Noah’s brows frowned deeply as a suspicion stirred! His gaze turned briefly inward, toward the fifth Letter newly carved into his backbone, and he questioned it directly. Had PROTAGONIST done something crazy again already?","He’d had to turn off the capabilities of the Protagonist once before, when it was simply doing too much, bending circumstances, summoning conveniences, dragging narrative weight toward him like a gravity well of plot! And now that he had transcribed it into a Letter of his very Tongue...was it already so effective that cursed things were being pulled across a Dimension towards him?","He sighed.","Well. If the Letter was going to act like this, then he would at least use it properly. Information first!","His gaze rose to THE Creature and Anaximander, who were drifting over towards the golden island, one trailing white-gold through his obsidian flames, the other still rubbing his temples, and Noah utilized the Letter of THE PROTAGONIST upon them.","|THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard has activated. Character Sheets are being compiled for the beings within your gaze.|","| Character Sheet: THE Creature, THE Great Ruler. Designation: Existence. True Lifeform, Intent transforming to Ananke, mid-digestion. Disposition toward you: genuine friendship. Danger to you: none by will, immense by association . Motivations: To rule, to bear what must be borne, to guard his bonds, and, newly formed, to understand the inherited thing that watches. Notable thread: a deep grief regarding a brutalized other half, carried since before THE Wyld, unhealed and unspoken. Notable thread: THE Burden he carries is older than his memory of receiving it, and its previous bearer is ?????. Notable thread: potential inheritor or Descendant. Notable thread: something is aware of this Regard, and is looking back. More information on Records may be possible...|","| Character Sheet: Anaximander, THE Explorer. Designation: ?????. Scale: inapplicable. Authority: none. Threat assessment: he is exactly as dangerous as he believes he needs to be. Disposition toward you: genuine friendship, wholly without agenda. Motivations: to know. Simply, bottomlessly, to know. Notable thread: his self-declared commandments number seven, of which you have witnessed two. Notable thread: his Undefined Life Line does not merely lack definition. Something appears to have erased it. More information on Records may be possible...|","...!","Prompts of majesty and wonder bloomed.","Noah looked at the two beings drifting toward him with open wonder as the Sheets settled through his mind! Something that looked back at his Regard! Commandments numbering seven! A Life Line not undefined but erased! Every answer his new capability delivered arrived carrying three fresh questions on its back, and these were his friends, beings whose favor toward him was written in absolute terms.","Now, if he could see the weavings of his enemies just like this...","It would be knowledge. Information! And information was the key for many, many things. Battles were won before they began by those who knew their opponent’s motivations, their fears, their desires, their price.","\" Osmont .\" THE Creature landed upon the golden sands, his changed flames settling, and his flat gaze studied Noah with something adjacent to curiosity as the tail behind him buzzed. \" How....did you do that, exactly?\"","Anaximander landed beside him, still wincing, and pointed at his own temple.","Noah only smiled as he shook his head!","\" Just a little trick. \" He turned toward the throne. \" But we do have to get going, as it seems we may have company soon. Let’s pack up and go.\"","He said these words as the vibrant gold platform buzzed beneath all of them, dream-sands humming with readiness as the forge folded itself away and the island prepared to move again! Anaximander sighed as he glanced back at the colossal pale limb of the Primeval One still floating in the storm-torn sky, the foot that had started this entire chain of events, and waved a hand at it.","\" I’ll have my hands full analyzing this cerebral cortex alone. Truly, it argues with me when I read it.\" He grinned over at Noah. \" As thanks, I think you can freely keep that limb.\"","...!","Anaximander said such words casually, gifting away a treasure that a Cenozoic being had bled for.","And Noah did not stand on ceremony! His Intent erupted out like a tyrannical blue sea, prismatic cerulean tides wrapping around the colossal limb as he dragged the entire thing across the sky and folded it inside THE Infiniverse, an apex corpse-piece settling into his home’s deep storage beside farms and forges and feasting halls.","His mind was already running through its uses. But for now...","For now, there was a choice to make.","They would not sit still. And they would not flee, either! He turned his gaze out across the storming dark, toward the direction of the second cluster, and decided. They would go towards the dying Cause that seemed to be filled with hope!","The hateful cluster was many Causes chained to one despotic center. But the hopeful one was rushing towards them with the feeling of hope, and hope was not the emotion of an enemy! Whatever it was, it likely wanted something from him rather than of him. If both clusters were converging on his position regardless, then the only real choice was which meeting he controlled. He would meet hope first, learn everything it knew, and face hatred afterwards with that knowledge in hand.","Information first. Always information first!","\" We move ,\" Noah declared as he rose onto the throne, Seo-yeon scooping herself onto its handle as Emotive bounced up beside him and THE Infiniverse took her place at the island’s edge!","Thereafter, THE Creature and Anaximander landed fully upon the platform, the titan’s white-gold-threaded flames folding calm as the scholar plopped down cross-legged near the throne, and the vibrant golden island of dream-sand buzzed with gathering power beneath all of them...","And shot out towards a certain direction!"]},{"number":5518,"title":"Chapter 5518: Chapter 5517: Existence and Anomalies! I","paragraphs":["The golden island tore across the storming dark of THE Krazhor-Nul, and upon it, THE Creature spoke calmly.","\" What are we running from, and what are we running to?\"","Noah’s mouth curved slightly from his throne as he answered plainly.","\" We are likely running away from one of those monstrous Cursed Steeds we learned about. It feels hateful and despotic. And we...are running towards another Cursed Steed! This one feels a bit...hopeful.\"","\"...\"","He said such words easily, and they were enough to make Anaximander smile and THE Creature frown!","For both of them instantly understood that something perilous was unfolding. Running from one dying Steed directly into another was not a plan any sane being would call safe.","Anaximander stroked his chin and spoke with calm honesty.","\"I would offer to simply carry everyone away, you know. \" His eyes drifted across the island, over Emotive and Seo-yeon and THE Infiniverse, and finally settled on Noah, and he winced slightly. \" But when I think about moving all of you, especially you, Osmont...your weight feels unfathomably heavy. It is not a matter of strength, I don’t carry things with strength. It is that whatever I carry comes with me, and what you are carrying would make traversal impossible. I would take a step and arrive nowhere at all.\"","Noah calmly listened, and nodded without any surprise.","He knew exactly what the scholar was sensing. He carried THE Infiniverse with him, and within her, countless deciillions of lives, thousands of realms, relocated sanctuaries, armories, farms, and now the limb of a Primeval One! Everything he had...was far too heavy. He was not a traveler anymore. He was an Existential nation that walked!","\" It’s okay,\" Noah said simply. \" It’s Adversity. We simply need to get through it.\"","The island flew on, and Noah’s gaze slid over to the cross-legged scholar with genuine curiosity.","\" Where have you been, by the way? For months to have passed?\"","\" Ah...\" Anaximander brightened immediately.","\" After we parted, I took a step to be far away. As far as I could manage, even, perhaps, toward those like me, if such things exist. And I appeared inside a Dimension filled with...well, they call themselves Superpowered Lifeforms.\"","...!","\" An entire society of extremely terrifying beings!\" Anaximander nodded seriously. \" They protect a cluster of Observable Existences within a vast Dimension from invasions and infiltrations, constantly, generation after generation, because their Dimension produces some type of Panacea that True Lifeforms across existence want badly. That place was...unique. Truly unique! I became friends with the protectors there. One of them, a Superpowered True Lifeform who could exert the weight of three Observable Existences with his body alone, mistakenly thought I was one of them, because I didn’t have any inherent authority either.\" He laughed at the memory.","Noah’s brows rose as he listened! A society of authority-less True Lifeforms guarding a treasure-Dimension? Existence truly was vast.","\" But he said something curious,\" Anaximander continued. \" He mentioned how across Existence, different Dimensions exist as some Dimensions hold natural treasures that invite the envy of others. Panaceas. Unique essenses. Rare weavings that form nowhere else! His Dimension was one of them, and so they had fought countless conflicts across the ages, Gilded True Lifeforms and Infinite True Lifeforms arriving in waves, wanting what they protected.\" He gestured loosely at the storming skies around them.","\"It rather reframes this place, doesn’t it? A Dimension is not merely a location. It is a body with organs worth stealing. I left a little after that, traveled around a bit, saw some truly strange corners, and then I went back to them, because their Dimension was the largest and most complex one I had found. I was there when THE Creature called me.\" He sighed then, and something troubled crossed his open face. \" I may actually need to go back soon...\"","He seemed weighed by something as he said it, a rare shadow on the perpetually delighted scholar!","But he shook his head and continued. \" But the other Dimensions I saw are...\"","And as Noah listened to Anaximander alongside the others with rapt attention...inside of his own Existence, many things were happening.","The cluster of Primeval Totipotent Cells anchored at the core of his Source had been drinking! Heavy inputs of himself flooded into them continuously, his Intent, his Osmontian Source Infinity, his Trueness, and somewhere in that deep blue sea, the drinking had crossed a threshold, for the cells seemed to have decided on exactly what to become.","They had read him. And his own Intent and identity had answered.","For what was THE Quintessential Osmontian, at his very root? A being who produced himself. Osmontian Biomass, generated endlessly, spent endlessly! And so his identity pressed its decision into the totipotent lattices, and the cells, capable of becoming anything, chose to become the thing that makes!","They moved!","The white-gold cluster dissolved from its anchoring and spread through him, flowing out of his Source’s deep sea and into his body, into his frame, into his bones! They poured through his skeleton like luminous rivers finding their channels, sinking into femur and spine and rib and skull, into the trabecular hollows where the oldest work of any body is done, and there they took form, cell by cathedral-cell, weaving themselves into the spongy architecture of his skeleton as they became...","Bone marrow!","Stellar blue-gold marrow bloomed through every bone of his existence, hematopoietic architecture rewritten at the Primeval grade, stem-lattices of white-gold threading through his skeletal core as the totipotent cells differentiated into an endless self-renewing engine, and the moment it finished anchoring...","Noah felt tremendous pain!","The marrow ignited! Cells began to be produced from it, the first generation of something entirely new, and they flowed outwards from his bones into the rest of his body, into blood and weaving and Source, and every single one of them burned going out, his whole frame lit from the inside by the agony of an existence being repopulated.","And alongside the pain...","BOOM!","A booming beat of his heart!","An utterly wild and fiendish aura erupted from Noah’s seated figure, ancient past all framing, and Anaximander stopped talking mid-sentance! THE Creature’s head turned sharply. Emotive and THE Infiniverse and even Seo-yeon all looked towards him at once, for the aura radiating off THE True Human Emperor in this moment did not feel like the composed weight of a crowned Osmontian.","It felt ancient. It felt...ever so slighty Primeval! Just tiny slivers of it!","|The Primeval Totipotent Cell Source has completed its differentiation. Designation: THE Primeval Osmontian Marrow. It is catalogued as a True Primeval Appendage of THE Osmontian, the first of its kind, an appendage grown not from your Trueness alone but from the fusion of your identity with apex Primeval root-matter.|","|Its function: it is a bone marrow, elevated terrifyingly. Seated through your entire skeleton, it now performs the deepest work of your body at the Primeval grade, producing THE Primeval Osmontian Cells, living cells carrying traces of Primeval weavings mixed inseparably with your Osmontian weavings. These cells proliferate across all parts of your existence. Your blood. Your flesh. Your Source. Your Intent’s expressions. Your very weavings! Everything you are will, over time, come to be built from cells that are part Primeval, and the fiendish ancientness you are currently radiating is the first generation announcing itself.|","| The rate of production of THE Primeval Osmontian Cells is fixed . However. It can be accelerated under one condition: whenever you are wounded by a malicious foreign authority. And should your existence be injured enough that you begin to bleed, the following will occur. You will continue to bleed for a few seconds, deliberately, as the marrow reads the wound. Production will accelerate. And you will enter THE Primeval Osmontian Berserker state, a battle-state in which your existence is momentarily elevated the more injured you become. Production, accelerated. Healing, accelerated. Power, Intent, Output, all of it, elevated in proportion to your wounds.|","...!","Noah felt the slow production beginning within him, the glorious Cells drifting out from his blue-gold marrow in steady generations, each one settling into his existence like a brick into a wall being quietly rebuilt from something older and grander! And as they proliferated...more prompts bloomed!","|A further consequence, and a considerable one. As THE Primeval Osmontian Cells proliferate and empower all facets of your existence, the intrinsic quality of every component rises, and elevation costs are gradually reducing across the board. Your Foundations. Your Osmontian Source Infinity. Your Volume, Output, and Trueness. All of them will grow cheaper to elevate as your cellular base grows more Primeval. And for the summit currently visible: elevation of THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian to A-Rank, Idho, currently stands at 15,000,000 Osmontian Biomass . The Cells will bring that number down, Master. Slowly.|","Fifteen million!","Noah gazed at these prompts, at the summit priced and the road toward it quietly discounting itself with every Cell his marrow breathed out, and silently, steadily, the fiendish aura of ancientness became more and more prevalent across his existence, settling into his body, his gaze, his presense, an old wildness taking up permanent residence beneath the composed surface of THE True Human Emperor.","And through it all, he simply continued listening to Anaximander, the golden island streaking through the storm as all of them discussed many things!"]},{"number":5519,"title":"Chapter 5519: Chapter 5518: Existence and Anomalies! II","paragraphs":["The golden island streaked across the storming dark, and upon it, Anaximander had gone quiet for a long moment.","Noah had just finished telling him more about the fate of their Observable Existence, the door they had all come from...gone. Taken into the hands of THE Sealed One.","The scholar exhaled slow. He shook his head, and then, being Anaximander, curiosity reasserted itself.","\"Ashes to ashes, dust to dust. I am glad you were able to save many. And I haven’t heard much about THE Sealed One in my travels. But I have heard extensively about two others, and if we are to speak of things worth fearing across Dimensions, these two came up at every campfire, in every society, in every tongue. THE Dimensional Eater. And Vakochev.\"","Noah’s brows rose.","Anaximander leaned forward. \" There exists a slime. A small, harmless-looking slime. It appears within unsuspecting Dimensions without warning, without wake, without any door anyone can find, and it simply...sits there. Wobbling. Doing nothing! And here is the terrible weavings every civilization has learned across the ages. If that slime survives within a Dimension for longer than a few days, that Dimension will likely be marked for death. And then, at some hour no one can predict, the whole of it, the space, the weavings, the lifeforms, the very dimensional laws, will be devoured.\"","\" The entire Dimension! Which is why, and I found this both tragic and extremely funny, slimes are hunted across nearly every established Dimension in existence. All slimes! Innocent ones, ordinary ones, little wobbling nothings that couldn’t devour a meal, exterminated on sight, because no lifeform who knows the story is willing to take the chance that the harmless one in front of them is THE one .\" He spread his hands.","\" An entire species made refugee by a single member’s reputation. The Superpowered folk had standing extermination patrols. I watched a powerful protector burn a puddle of slime the size of a teacup with enough power to crack half an Observable Existence, and when I asked him if that seemed excessive, he looked at me like I was the mad one.\"","\" And Vakochev ,\" Anaximander continued, his voice settling into genuine scholarly respect, \" is another matter entirely. From everything I gathered, he is one of the more powerful beings of this Era. Not a myth, not an ancient, a living power, current and active! And his Scales of Existence are not merely a ladder someone wrote down. They are a framework, a living structure covering many Observable Existences and Dimensions, vast areas of THE Infinite Carcosa, great stretches of THE Source Lands. Uncountable lifeforms are born, climb, and die entirely inside his architecture without ever learning a single other way to grow. \" He raised one finger.","\" Even some weaker True Lifeforms, beings who have formed their own Egoic Intent, who have crossed onto their own path and owe the Scales nothing...paradoxically continue to follow the structure of his Scales anyway. His framework remains paramount even after Trueness, for those who want it.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly at that!","And then, from the edge of the golden sands, the silent Creature spoke up.","\" Existence is vast.\"","His flat voice settled over the island, and everyone turned.","\" We are young by comparison. All of us. Histories have been unfolding long before us, and we are walking across their aftermaths and calling it exploration.\" His white-gold-threaded flames stirred slowly around his frame.","\" Apart from THE Sealed One...those for us to look out for are the Lineages connected to Those Who Remain. The Descendants of Those Who Remain. Those who are part of their Lineages...believe Existence is theirs. Not as ambition. As inheritance.\"","Noah listened closely, for THE Creature’s path was Existence itself!","\" We are in a Dimension that has Cursed Descendants. Broken ones. Dying ones. But there are many more Dimensions of normal Descendants, unbroken lineages, and they all hold unique and terrifying capabilities exceeding any True Lifeform.\" His flat gaze moved across all of them, unhurried.","\" And if I can give any advice...never take power as Absolute. The rankings you know, Infinite, Source, Gilded, True, they are catalogues, not walls. You might meet lifeforms who don’t fit in any of them, and they might have power exceeding all of them. \"","Then, dryly, without any change in his tone at all...","\"I mean, look at Osmont here. I envision him to be one of those anomalous Existences. Alongside you, Anaximander.\"","...!","Noah and Anaximander both shook their heads at these words immediately.","\"I am...just human, nothing more... \" Noah said.","\" And I am a very normal scholar, an explorer...\" Anaximander added, nodding seriously!","\" Hm ,\" said THE Creature.","Noah leaned back upon his throne as the conversation washed around him, thinking about everything that had been said.","A slime that ate Dimensions. A framework so grand the free still climbed it! Lineages who believed Existence was inherited property, and unbroken Descendants scattered across Dimensions with capabilities exceeding Trueness itself. Existence truly was vast and filled with far too many things, far too many powers, far too many histories still unfolding beneath every step they took!","But he...would move steadily on his own path.","His own way. His own Tongue, his own Scales! His Second Scale was being enacted even now, its Foundations all standing at Straif and above, and it almost seemed ready for the next stage, some threshold he could feel approaching. And beyond that, his curiosity burned in specific directions! His Causes. His Infinite Cause, seated in himself and THE Infiniverse and grown grander with her every devoured mouthful of this Dimension!","And the Steeds of Those Who Remain, dying carriers of First Causes, one of them rushing toward him at this very moment with hope in its failing weavings.","What gains could potentially be made there? What did a being who could seat Causes owe to creatures whose Causes were dying?","The golden island tore onward toward the hopeful dying thing, and THE True Human Emperor smiled slightly upon his throne! After a stretch of comfortable quiet, Noah began to speak again.","His voice was calm.","\"I wonder sometimes how far we should go on those we consider our enemies.\" His gaze rested on the raging horizon. \" THE Gilded Ones. Much of those who affected our Lower Observable Existence are either dead, or taken by THE Sealed One. So what remains of that grudge? Will we seek and kill all Gilded Ones, since we don’t like their nature? Those who are True? The Primeval Ones standing behind them?\" His fingers drummed once on the throne’s armrest.","\" When would the killing be enough? Or does one look at a certain point and say...it’s enough there? When is animosity enough, and when do you let go?\"","No one interrupted. Even Emotive was still.","\" Because as much as I love conflict, as a father, I start to think of all the countless who had nothing to do with the wars I waged with others...but I eradicated them all. And I have eradicated many. \" The words came flat and unflinching, a ledger read aloud.","\" Entire hierarchies. Entire Civilizations. Beings who were simply born into the wrong banner in the wrong era, standing in formations they never chose, and I unmade them alongside their masters without slowing down to sort one from the other.\"","He let that sit, and then continued.","\"I am currently distinguished as...THE True Human Emperor. And I have been thinking. I have been thinking about what I will do past THE Sealed One, and the Gilded and Infinite that he uses. About all those I have taken the lives of. I have been thinking some fairly crazy and grand thoughts, of how if I truly want to live by my identity, as THE True Human Emperor...should my gaze begin looking out across all of existence, to bring all those I deem Humans...under my fold?\"","...!","\" Every scattered branch of humanity across every Dimension and Observable Existence. Every people with that brief, burning, striving pattern I call Human, gathered beneath one crown.\" His eyes gleamed with something that was neither warmth nor coldness but both braided together.","\" Would this be me enacting conquest, as I have done before? Or salvation? I do know it will empower me. Every Human under my fold feeds the identity, and the identity feeds everything I am. So maybe the question is not about conquest or salvation but moreso...am I selfishly acting with my nature in mind, to do something grand...simply for the sake of my power?\"","He exhaled, and his mouth curved wryly.","\" Ah, I am talking a lot. I am just wrestling with the idea of what I will do across existence...for the sake of my identity. I don’t think I will sit still.\"","...!","The silence that followed was brief.","Because THE Creature answered, and his flat voice came down grand!","\" Existence is not idle.\"","His white-gold-threaded flames stirred as his gaze fixed on Noah.","\" Existence isn’t something to simply be gawked at while a countless many die...because there are no rulers. I have walked across eras of it. I have seen what fills the spaces where no one governs. Harvests. Hoards. Lineages who believe everything is theirs, feeding on those who cannot answer back.\" His voice did not rise, and that made it heavier.","\" As someone walking the path of Existence, I will tell you now that I seek to be a ruler. An Existential Ruler. A Great Ruler. Like Vakochev. So that I...can stand and declare how things should be.\"","...!","\"If I don’t like how Gilded Ones are, I will change it. If I don’t like how Source Lifeforms are, I will change it! Countless Lifeforms out there struggle and suffer because those who are good...have no capacity to be strong and take care of business. I have an immense dislike to many lifeforms who consider themselves good and pious...while doing nothing as their neighbors die and are oppressed. Goodness without power is a lament. I have heard enough laments.\" His flat eyes darkened with something old.","\"I wish to be in a position of power to ensure what happened to me doesn’t happen to anyone else. No half of anyone, brutalized while the other half watches. Not on any shore of Existence I rule.\"","Anaximander had gone completely still, listening with the focus of a scholar witnessing something worth recording forever!","\" The conquest you mention...seems to be alongside the same lines as what I wish to do. You, Osmont, wish to be a Ruler! \" THE Creature said it plainly.","\" Vakochev...is too passive. He made Scales based on Adversity. Sure. His Scales were good. They allowed me to get where I am! But that pain, that adversity...let it come to those who seek it. The innocent who simply want to live and die, why should they suffer alongside everyone else? Why should a farmer climb the same bleeding ladder as a conqueror, or be left to rot at its base?\" His flames pulsed once!","\" No. Vakochev’s Scales are too...general. New Scales are needed. New direction is needed.\"","And then, for the first time in the entire exchange, something moved through THE Creature’s expression!","\"I thought I may have been trying to enact my own vision alone. But it seems that you...have your own vision as well.\" He nodded once, slow and final. \" This is more than okay. You or me...we can see which one of our visions can be painted across Existence!\"","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with unfathomable brightness as he looked at THE Creature!","Two visions, spoken plainly over golden sands in a cursed Dimension! An Emperor of all Humans, and a Ruler of Existence itself! Not rivals, not yet, perhaps not ever, but two beings who had just discovered that neither of them intended to leave Existence as they found it, and an immense silence settled in this space as the golden island tore onward through the storm, carrying both of their futures toward a dying hope that nobody could say with surety...where it would end up."]},{"number":5520,"title":"Chapter 5520: Chapter 5519: No Chance!","paragraphs":["To lead. To rule!","Noah was already a leader and ruler, he already held the distinction of THE True Human Emperor as for him, it came naturally. His people, his crown, his fold, all of it had grown out of him the way branches grow from a trunk.","But now, he thought of the distinction of a Great Ruler.","Could he truly see himself returning to glorious Conquest and expanding his rule across...THE Source Lands? THE Infinite Carcosa? And even across Dimensions of Existence themselves?! Would this be his quickest route to power, every Human gathered beneath his identity feeding the Letter that fed everything else?","He was thinking such grand thoughts when...","HUUM!","\" Aba, the hateful cause is accelerating towards us!\"","Seo-yeon’s warning cut across the golden sands, and it came as a shock! For they had been moving at tremendous speeds in another direction entirely, streaking toward the hopeful dying Cause, and yet what she considered the hateful dying cluster was the one reaching them first!","Noah’s will surged as the golden platform accelerated further, his Ananke Intent flooding across every grain of dream-sand as the entire island took on a deep blue hue, a comet of gold and cerulean tearing through the storming dark of THE Krazhor-Nul.","Light years folded beneath them. The Ego of Humilitas wrapped them tighter than it ever had!","And it did not matter.","For behind them, pressing through the storm like the fingers of a closing hand, he and all the others could now sense a terrifying set of auras! Many auras! Heavy past framing, and gaining!","Noah sighed once.","Then he patted Seo-yeon gently on the head. \" You need to go back inside for now.\"","His daughter looked up at him, and she did not argue, for she could feel what was coming better than anyone! She nodded as mirrored light gathered around her small frame. \" Aba... be careful.\"","She folded away into THE Infiniverse!","Noah’s gaze turned to Emotive next, and he nodded once. Emotive pouted enormously, opened her mouth to protest, read his eyes, closed her mouth, and retreated into THE Infiniverse with her arms crossed the entire way down!","And in the next moment...existence congealed.","The storm around them thickened like cooling tar as the golden island’s tremendous speed began bleeding away for no reason Noah’s senses could name, space itself growing dense, resistant, wrong! He poured more Intent into their passage. The island surged. And then the concept of space seemingly became nullified entirely, for no matter how much further Noah pushed, no matter how many light years his will declared crossed...he found they were in the same space!","The horizon refused to approach. The distance refused to close! They flew, and they arrived nowhere, held inside a single stretch of storm like an insect in a trap.","|An extremely potent Ananke Intent has pervaded the surroundings. Its weavings mark it as belonging to a Source True Lifeform, and its declaration is simple: this space does not release what stands within it.|","...!","At these words, the faces of Noah, THE Creature, Anaximander, and THE Infiniverse all hardened as they gazed back!","And they saw...a group of utterly terrifying beings.","The storm behind them had filled with True Lifeforms! More than twenty of them spread in loose formation across the dark sky, over half pressing down with the weight of THE Cenozoic Scale, antlered and flamed and stone-hided apex existences whose idle comfort had sharpened into readiness! Among them coiled Ormarr Grimtunge, whole and massive, his crimson eyes gleaming with long-awaited delight.","Beside him flew a woman in red robes whose cold face and crimson gaze emanated nothing, absolutely nothing, except the promise of murder!","And behind them all...was a monstrous, cursed thing.","Noah’s eyes fixed upon it, and even his composed heart pressed heavier in his chest!","It was colossal beyond the entire party combined, a mountainous quadruped whose gray hide had gone the color of forgotten things, its titanic frame furrowed with fissures through which its failing First Cause guttered.","Chains of screaming crimson metal wrapped its throat. Its breath dragged like landslides! And its eyes...its eyes were vast pools of dying light filled with pain and hate and coldness all at once, the gaze of something that had been walking in agony for so long that agony had become its only remaining language, and beneath all of it, Noah could feel its dying Causes, and they were so heavy.","So heavy!","And then its ambient field touched them.","The Steed of Oblivion’s suppression rolled across the trapped island like a tide of gray silence, and for the first time in her existence, THE Infiniverse made a sound of pain!","It felt like...Pantheon compression! Noah felt his own Pantheon strain against his backbone as its realms refused to unfurl, thousands of skies pressing inward as if a hand had closed around his home, and the ambient Biomass tick that had fed him since their hatching simply...stopped! Within THE Infiniverse, nested Observable Existences groaned as her weavings cramped, and Ruination’s prompts arrived colder than they had ever been.","|The Steed’s ambient field is an architecture of dimensional sovereignty, designed by Those Who Remain to keep their mounts paramount above all other dimensional laws. Within its range, THE Quintessential Pantheon of THE Infiniverse cannot fully unfurl. THE Quintessential Confluence will function at reduced grades. The Absolute Dimensional Ruling holds for now, but the field is not attacking it. It is slowly denying it the right to exist. Everyone inside THE Infiniverse is safe at this moment. That statement has a time limit, and I do not yet know its length.|","...!","The coldest prompts she had ever delivered!","And through the gray pressure, the woman in red spoke. Exactly once. Her voice was quiet, toneless, and it landed across the trapped space like a blade being drawn from its sheath in a silent room.","\" Kneel, and most of you will be kept alive.\"","That was all. No threat performed, no power flared! Just a fact, stated by something shaped for killing, and the twenty True Lifeforms behind her settled into formation as though the outcome had already been filed!","And beside her, Ormarr Grimtunge finally had his moment!","The great Serpent uncoiled forward through the storm, rising high above the trapped golden island with his reassembled bulk gleaming, and his laughter rolled out rich and vindicated, a follower savoring the taste of overwhelming force at his back.","\" Hey now, look at this! Two of you have actually gathered back together! \" His crimson eyes swept from Noah to THE Creature, drinking in their hardened faces like fine wine. \" Haha, existence is being truly kind today! The seated fucker and the grave-walker, wrapped up in one net! Do you know what I had to endure because of you two? Do you know what it is to be a length of yourself short in front of your betters?!\" His coils flexed as his smile stretched wide and brutal!","\" No matter. No matter at all! It seems like...it is the end of the road for you all!\"","This vindictive fucker began to look at them with glee.","And in Noah’s eyes, at this exact moment...time seemingly stopped.","He stretched a moment of an instant into infinity!","His perception expanded through the frozen frame, the Serpent’s gloating suspended mid-syllable, the blade in red hanging motionless, the Steed’s guttering Causes flickering in place, and within that endless instant, THE True Human Emperor went to work! For a battle against this was not a battle.","THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard activated!","His gaze swept across Lissana, across Ormarr, across the host, across the Steed, and many others, and the Character Sheets bloomed!","| Character Sheet: Lissana. Designation: THE Edge That Was Forged . Source True Lifeform. Her Ananke Intent is the declaration currently sealing this space. Danger to you: extreme. In direct combat, she alone exceeds your current fused ceiling. Disposition: no malice, no favor, nothing. You are a task. Motivations: she was forged, literally, her existence refined across a True lifetime. Notable thread: she does not know why twenty were sent by Jarl Erling for this errand, and unexplained orders unsettle the only thing she trusts, her function. Notable thread: her deepest buried thread is a single question she has never been permitted to ask: what she is when there is nothing to kill? Notable thread: her orders are capture, not slaughter. THE Infiniverse is to be taken undamaged, and she has been told nothing about why. She dislikes fighting blind more than she dislikes anything in existence.|","| Character Sheet: Ormarr Grimtunge. True Lifeform. Danger to you: Moderate, and currently irrelevant, as he will not act before Lissana does. Disposition: hatred, humiliation, hunger for redress. Motivations: to restore his standing with Jarl Erling. Notable thread: he was commanded to secrecy. No other Jarl may learn of this errand, and Ormarr believes this secrecy is about his master’s pride. He has not asked himself what discovery would be worth hiding. Notable thread: he fears the blade in red far more than he fears you, and he fears one further thing above even her: being blamed if this errand fails. It cannot fail, be has to deliver!|","| Character Sheet: THE Steed of Oblivion. Designation: Ghrimhest, THE Fourth of the Second Brood . A living Observable Existence of the old broods, its First Cause in terminal collapse for ages beyond counting. Danger to you: absolute. There is no chance of victory against it. None. Its ambient sovereignty predates every framework you climb, its dying field grows stronger the longer you stand inside it, and even if all of you fight with everything, together, at your peaks...you cannot win! Its body does not need to strike you. Its existence alone is the strike. Motivations: none remain. Pain has replaced them all. Notable thread: it hates its handlers more than it hates its cargo. Notable thread: beneath the pain, its dying Causes are still listening. For what, it no longer remembers. Notable thread: ?????|","...!"]},{"number":5521,"title":"Chapter 5521: Chapter 5520: Buy Time!","paragraphs":["The stretched instant held, and within it, Noah finished his thoughts.","They came for THE Infiniverse! And it was under the command of Jarl Erling as it should relate or Observable Existences and causes as how did he know? Did this fucker Ormarr report back so thoroughly after his death?","But apart from this...","Winning was not possible.","Lissana alone exceeded even his fused ceiling. Twenty True Lifeforms stood behind her with more than half at Cenozoic. And beneath all of them walked a being whose existence was the strike, whose ambient field was slowly denying his home the right to exist. Even all of them together, at their peaks, could not win this.","But he did not need to win this.","Because far across the storming dark, a dying Cause filled with hope was still rushing toward him! If his suspicions about what approached held even half their weight...then what he needed was not victory.","What he needed was time!","And buying time from beings who held every advantage required only one currency. Doubt! He had read their Sheets as he knew many of their details.","So THE True Human Emperor decided, within a frozen instant, to become grander than he was.","’ Anaximander. Creature. Let me handle this for now. I am simply buying us time for now as something should be coming to balance the Scales...maybe.’","The mental messages left him as the instant collapsed, and time resumed!","Ormarr’s gloating laughter was still rolling across the trapped space. Lissana’s declaration still hung like a drawn blade! And Noah, cornered and outweighed beyond everything ...smiled slightly, and let go of every rein inside his marrow!","HUUM!","The aura of THE Primeval Osmontian Marrow erupted from him freely.","The fiendish ancientness he had kept settled beneath his composure poured outward in slow, heavy waves, stellar blue-gold pressure carrying that unmistakable flavor of the apex and the earliest, and it rolled across the formation of True Lifeforms like a scent from a deeper age!","The party’s loose formation...tightened.","The storm-antlered one’s head snapped up. The three-faced female’s gray flames dimmed to embers as her every face turned! The stone hound at the rear stopped looking backward!","And Noah floated forward alone and unhurried! Ahead of THE Creature and Anaximander, out past the edge of the golden sands, drifting into the open storm between his island and the blade in red as if the space between them belonged to him, as if her Ananke Intent sealing the region was a courtesy he was permitting, and he spoke with a lazy, unbothered cadence.","\" Lissana.\"","...!","The blade in red did not move, but her crimson eyes sharpened by a fraction, and behind her, Ormarr’s coils actually flinched.","\" That is your designation, is it not? A blade, an extremely sharp blade...used by Jarl Erling.\" Noah’s voice carried easily through the suppression field entirely unafraid!","\" And Ormarr fucking Grimtunge. Tell me, have you restored your standing with Jarl Erling yet, or is this errand your only chance to suck up? The only chance for you to prove yourself?\"","\"You...!\" Ormarr’s crimson eyes flared wide as his grand composure cracked down the middle! \" How do you know of...\"","\"I know a great many things.\" Noah’s smile did not widen.","And within his gaze, silently, THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard drank.","Every reaction fed it! Every flinch and flare peeled another layer, the Sheets deepening as he got more and more records, as suspicion and alarm loosened the weavings of the beings before him.","His eyes returned to Lissana, and his voice gentled into something almost curious. \" Such a gathering. Such expenditure! Do you know exactly what you were sent to do?\"","\"...\"","\" Do you know why you all were sent here? Why the Steed was woken for the first time in your service? Why your orders are capture, undamaged, when Jarl Erling has never once in his long dying cared whether merchandise arrived intact?\" Each question fell like a drop of ink into clear water!","\" You were told nothing. Have you asked yourself why he would hide and not come himself?\"","...!","Lissana’s crimson eyes narrowed!","It was the smallest motion, a fraction of a fraction.","\" Careful, all of you.\" Ormarr had recovered enough to talk.","\" He plays games. He talks and talks while...\"","\" While what, Ormarr?\" Noah turned to the Serpent lazily. \" Someone as afraid as you shouldn’t talk too much. I have already killed a part of you once.\"","WAA!","Noah spread his arms slightly, and invited them deeper.","His marrow’s aura deepened around him, ancient and fiendish and utterly unbothered, and behind him, as if summoned by the gesture, the white-gold threading through THE Creature’s obsidian flames burned brighter, and even Anaximander simply floated, unreadable.","\"I’ll make things even simpler. Sense my existence. Sense the existence of those behind me.\"","The trapped space went very quiet.","\" What does it smell like?\" Noah asked softly. \" What does it feel like?\"","Twenty True Lifeforms, against every tactical instinct they possessed...sensed!","They could not help it! The question was already inside them, and their ancient senses reached across the gap, and what came back was exactly what he knew it would be. Primeval weavings.","What they felt before. The white-gold light that had split this Dimension’s sky for light years, the bloom every one of them had sensed and raced toward, and it had come from HERE, from THESE beings!","\" You all felt the light. Your dying master pointed you at things backed by Primeval Ones and told you nothing. So I will ask the only question that matters...Will you all stake your lives to infuriate the Primeval Lifeforms sitting behind us...for the dying Jarl who could not even come here himself? How many years does that cursed fucker have left to live anyways? You all will be free soon enough...or are you waiting for his death to loot his corpse? Is this part of why you are in his service?\"","He pulled and pulled as much information as he could as he bullshitted!","The question detonated in silence!","Hesitation rolled through the formation like a slow wave.","For a long moment, the party Jarl Erling had built held its breath!","And then Lissana spoke.","Her voice came exactly as it had before and it cut through every seeded doubt!","\"I am only a blade.\"","Her crimson eyes rested on Noah, and there was nothing in them! No fear his aura could catch, no doubt his questions could water, no ambition his knowledge could leverage. Nothing but function!","\"I am pointed, and I strike. Nothing else matters.\"","...!","She barely moved her fingers.","It was less than a gesture! A whisper of motion at the end of one red sleeve, the kind of movement a being makes brushing away dust, and in the next moment, the space between them simply agreed with her!","Noah’s defenses were bypassed! The layered folds of his Osmontian Source Infinity, the passive refusals of THE Unmoved Verdict, the conforming pressure of THE Sovereign Existence, edge after edge after edge slid past all of them as if they were opinions and she was fact, and a huge gash tore open across Noah’s chest!","His flesh parted! And stellar crimson-blue-gold blood gushed out into the storm, blood that burned faintly with ancient light as it scattered across the trapped dark, and THE True Human Emperor’s body rocked backward through the suppression field with his presense split open for every watching eye!","And Lissana looked down coldly as she repeated herself...","\"I said, Kneel.\"","...!"]},{"number":5522,"title":"Chapter 5522: Chapter 5521: Fear and Doubt! I","paragraphs":["He floated in the trapped dark, split open, and he had never looked more like an Emperor.","The gash across his chest wept freely, and yet Noah’s body did not so much as sway! He hung in the storm with his crown gleaming and his shoulders level, dark bluish hair drifting in the pressure-winds of a Cenozoic enemy, and his blood...his blood did not fall.","It swirled!","Stellar crimson-blue-gold blood rose from his wound in slow, glorious ribbons, coiling around his figure like loyal serpents of burning light, each droplet threaded with Primeval Osmontian Cells that glimmered against the dark, and the sight of it silenced parts of the party that Lissana’s attack had been meant to embolden! For wounded things were supposed to diminish. Prey was supposed to shrink when cut!","And the crowned figure before them bled upward, wore his own blood as regalia, and gazed ahead with nothing on his face but calmness.","| You are facing tremendous adversity. THE Aura of THE Protagonist has been triggered, and it has been pouring since the space sealed. Twenty-one True Lifeforms and a burden-bearer whose existence is the strike, all arrayed against you alone. The Aura is drinking every drop of this impossibility. +100,000 Osmontian Biomass has been gained so far. The count climbs while you stand here.|","| You have been wounded by a malicious foreign authority. THE Primeval Osmontian Marrow has read the wound, and production of THE Primeval Osmontian Cells is accelerating. You are bleeding, and per its design, you will continue to bleed for these few seconds, deliberately, as the deeper condition engages.|","| THE Primeval Osmontian Berserker state has been triggered . Your existence now elevates the more injured you become. Production, accelerated. Healing, accelerated. Power, Intent, Output, all climbing in proportion to your wounds. She cut you to punctuate a command, Master. She has instead turned a key.|","...!","Prompts of majesty and wonder bloomed!","And his existence began to give off even grander waves of power! The fiendish ancient aura of the Marrow deepened around his bleeding frame, blue-gold pressure rolling out in slow tides that tasted older with every pulse, and the swirling ribbons of his blood burned brighter as the Berserker state fed on the very gash meant to humble him.","At this moment, three figures came to float beside him.","THE Creature drifted to his right, obsidian flames threaded with white-gold, his flat gaze fixed ahead. Anaximander settled at his left, robes drifting, unreadable.","And THE Infiniverse’s manifestation took her place at his shoulder, composed and cold-eyed even as her realms strained. All three of them stood against the pressure pressing from every direction, the Steed’s suppression grinding down on their weavings, Lissana’s sealed space coiled around them, twenty True Lifeforms arrayed beyond, and every one of them felt the strain, and not one of them showed it.","Yet even in such a precarious position, Noah seemed unbothered as he floated there and looked towards Lissana.","Him. Kneel?","He almost wanted to laugh! He literally could not do it even if he wanted to, as his very identity was that much against it. THE Unkneeling Crown was his First Foundation! No Ego hierarchy in existence could place him beneath it, and no command could bend knees that his own weavings refused to own! Her demand was not merely offensive. It was, for him specifically, structurally impossible!","So. How could he bullshit to gain more time?","He could always...keep talking.","And the more he withstood this adversity, the more Osmontian Biomass he gained from it! He had to do this, as there was very real danger here, danger that could end everything, and within him, THE Infiniverse had to be protected. Every second bought was a second closer to the hopeful thing racing across the dark!","So...","Noah, even while bleeding, gazed at Lissana and Ormarr and the others, and began to tell a story.","\"In a certain dimension, there was a king who ruled over a wealthy valley, protected by a massive stone dam that held back the roaring sea. He was a proud man, convinced that because he was king, nothing he built could ever fail.\"","\"...\"","The party stared! A story? The bleeding fucker was telling them a story?!","\" One morning, his chief architect rushed into the throne room, trembling with fear. ’My King,’ he cried, pointing out the window, ’look at the dam! A massive crack has split the center wall, and water is spraying into the air! We must evacuate!’\"","Noah’s voice rolled on, calm and unhurried, his blood swirling grandly around him as he spoke.","\" The king walked to the window and looked right at the spraying water. But his pride was a thick blindfold. He turned around, smiled, and said, ’Do not be foolish. I built that wall. It is perfect because it is mine. That is not a crack; it is just the morning sun playing tricks on your fearful eyes.’\"","The stone hound’s ears had flattened. The three-faced female’s every face watched him now!","\" The next day, the crack grew into a roaring chasm. Sea water rushed into the valley, flooding the palace gardens and sloshing across the throne room floor. The servants packed their bags and fled for the hills. Yet, the king just lifted his robes, stepped onto his golden chair, and looked away from the window. ’The gardeners have simply over-watered the lilies,’ he insisted to the empty room. ’The sea would never dare defy my kingdom.’\"","His gaze drifted, slow and deliberate, across every listening face!","\" An hour later, the dam completely shattered. A wall of black water smashed through the palace, tearing down the walls of stone and gold. The violent current swept the king away, stripping him of his crown and his heavy robes.\"","\" He washed up alive on a barren, muddy shore miles down the coast. When he finally opened his eyes, he had no crown, no servants, and no subjects. His entire kingdom was gone, buried forever under the ocean he chose not to see.\"","...!","The moment he finished telling this story, Lissana coldly waved her hand again!","The space agreed with her a second time, and another gash tore open across Noah’s shoulder as blood erupted into the storm! And his figure...his figure shockingly became even more glorious! The fresh ribbons of stellar blood joined the coiling regalia around him as the Berserker state drank the new wound, his aura climbing another register, ancient and fiendish and rising, a being who was visibly, impossibly, growing grander with every cut she gave him.","|Adversity deepening. +47,000 Osmontian Biomass gained since the last report. The rate of production of THE Primeval Osmontian Cells has accelerated again with the second wound.|","Noah looked ahead through the swirling burning blood, and he could see it plainly now.","Hesitation. On all of them!","On Ormarr, whose coils had drawn tight around his own center! Hesitation on every face in the formation...except one. Lissana alone remained untouched, unread, unmoved, this being simply that unique, a blade that doubt could find no edge to settle on.","So Noah spoke to the ones it could.","\" Cracks have began to appear for all of you, as the Dam is about to shatter.\" His voice carried through the sealed space, quiet and vast at once.","\"I am the messenger telling you to save yourselves. While I may be weaker than you, what I represent is a raging sea that will sweep away everything about your existences. Heed my message. Turn away.\"","...!","And he simply floated there, bleeding gloriously!","The crowned figure hung wrapped in slow-turning ribbons of Primeval blood, wounds worn like decorations, ancient aura rolling off him in patient tides, gazing at a formation of apex beings with the serene disappointment of a king reviewing subjects who had arrived late, and not one being present could reconcile what their senses reported with what their eyes were seeing, and that irreconcilable gap was where fear lived.","But Lissana began to billow with terrifying power!","Her red robes lifted as her existence finally, truly, gathered itself, crimson light bleeding off her frame in blade-thin sheets that sliced the storm into ribbons, and her toneless voice came once more!","\"I don’t need to kill one particular target. \" Her crimson eyes fixed on Noah alone. \" But you...you can die...\"","\"Wait, Lissana...\"","...!","It was Ormarr! Ormarr Grimtunge was actually the one to speak, his grand voice cracked through with open hesitation, the follower’s terror of blame at last outweighing the follower’s terror of his betters, and Noah looked on grandly as his seeds bloomed in the unlikeliest soil.","And within his own stillness, a memory rose.","The prophecy of Ryaenara’s brother. Ulf!","Three deaths must the deathless die before the door swings wide","The felt, the made, the borrowed self, each one must be united","Choose true, O brief and burning one, for choices carve the way","And what was written in the white was written from today","Three deaths. Would he truly need to die once, here, today?","He found himself questioning it, and he found, turning the question over, that he actually did not have any heavy emotions attached to it at all. To die was to be human.","And he had something that made it so he could return from death!","But he could not die so easily. Not here, not cheaply, not with THE Infiniverse in the balance!","He was about to turn his head at this moment toward the Steed itself, toward the dying colossus whose Causes were still listening, when Lissana raised her hand fully, the skies of the sealed space beginning to shake as a terrifying Intent howled awake, an edge the size of an era swinging back for its stroke!","At such a time...","\" Aba, she is here!\"","Seo-yeon’s voice rang out from within THE Infiniverse!","And in the next second...","BOOM!","Existence shuddered, fractured, and collapsed all at once as an unfathomably heavy aura descended!"]},{"number":5523,"title":"Chapter 5523: Chapter 5522: Fear and Doubt! II","paragraphs":["The storm parted.","It did not part the way storms part for power, shoved aside and resentful! It parted the way crowds part for royalty, currents of raging Infinity and Primordial Source drawing back upon themselves in long reverent curtains, and through the opened sky, descending before the golden island in a slow fall of white light...","Came a dragon.","A pure-white dragon!","Noah and all the others watched her descent, and even here, even wounded and sealed and surrounded, every gaze present was pulled upward and held! She was colossal, her pearl-white scales layered like plates of living moonlight, faint rivers of silver shimmering through them with each beat of her vast wings! Twin horns of translucent ivory spiraled back from her skull, and between them drifted a mane of soft white flame that burned without fuel and without end! Around her titanic limbs, the scars of shattered chains still smoked faintly, crimson burn-lines wrapped like the ghosts of shackles!","And her body radiated pain.","The curse was plain upon her. Terminal weavings guttered through her frame in slow dying threads, the same collapse that hollowed the gray colossus behind the war-host, ages deep and unhealed, and every beat of her wings carried the weight of something that had been hurting for thousands of years.","And yet...she carried tremendous regality.","The pain did not bow her. The curse did not diminish her! She descended like a queen returning to a throne room that had wronged her, her golden eyes sweeping the sealed space with cold command, and the dying light within her burned somehow prouder than the living light of everything arrayed against her!","Noah looked at her with shining eyes.","Was this it? Was this the hopeful dying cluster of Causes he had been waiting for, the one rushing toward them like someone running to a long-awaited door?!","|A conflicting field has appeared. The newcomer’s ambient weavings carry the same architecture of dimensional sovereignty as the Steed of Oblivion, and the two sovereignties do not stack. They contest. Her field has rejected the imposition of the Steed of Oblivion across this region. The suppression is breaking.|","...!","And Noah felt it.","The terrifying strain that had been grinding down on THE Infiniverse eased all at once, the gray pressure peeling back off her realms like a hand releasing a throat, and beside him, THE Infiniverse’s manifestation exhaled as her compressed weavings finally unfurled! The ambient Biomass tick stuttered, and resumed. Noah could breathe easier, his Pantheon flexing against his backbone once more, and the mechanic he had only theorized bloomed proven across the battlefield.","Two Steed-fields...cancelled each other!","His eyes locked onto her, and hers came down to meet him.","And Noah felt a variety of emotions moving in those vast golden pupils! Pain, ancient and banked. Wariness, sharp and counting! Exhaustion deeper than eras, and beneath all of it, running through every ring of those ring-in-ring pupils, one thing pulsed stronger than all the rest.","Profound immensity, and majesty!","It was like looking at something sacred. This was older than power, the gravity of an unbroken line, of something seated by hands that predated every framework he had ever climbed, and those eyes pulsed with immensity and with pure, terrible hope as she looked down at him coldly and asked...","\" Are you the one...to fulfill the promise?\"","...!","Noah blinked at these words.","What the hell promise?","He had not the faintest idea what this magnificent dying wonder was talking about! But he was wounds deep into the greatest bluff of his existence, and stopping now was not among his options, so he had to continue bullshitting, and at this moment, behind his calm face, his gaze quietly drank her in.","THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard activated.","| Character Sheet: Hvitrmarr, The White Steed. Danger to you: immense in capability, none in disposition. She descends, unbroken, from one of the FIRST Steeds, the original brood whose First Causes were seated PERSONALLY by Those Who Remain. Her architecture is truer than every Steed of the later broods, which is why her Cause fails slower, and why her ambient sovereignty just overruled a creature many times her size. Notable thread: she carries inherited ancestral memories, carvings at the bottom of her Cause that she did not live. Notable thread: her lineage transmits a promise, and its surviving shape reads: what living hands seat, living hands can seat again. Notable thread: ?????|","...!","Noah’s eyes shined brilliantly as the Sheet settled through him.","First lineage! Seated personally by Those Who Remain! And the promise, there it was, what living hands seat, living hands can seat again, a sentence carried across years of chains. He had no idea what fulfilling it truly required.","But he would do whatever it took to survive!","And so, at this time, Noah gathered himself! He reached down into the deepest architecture of everything he was, into the brilliant light of his Infinite Cause, the first Cause, the one woven inseparably through THE Infiniverse herself! And then he emulated further, drawing up the resonance of his own nine Causes that permeated across THE Infiniverse’s endless realms, and even the gathered light of the Causes of the nested Observable Existences within her, generations of living hearts beating inside a living home, all of it channeled upward through his bleeding frame and released through a glorious and calm...","\"I AM.\"","BOOM!","His words released a burst of life very few in all of existence could understand.","It was not power! It was not Intent! It was a burst of living Causes, layered and harmonized and vast, first light upon first light upon first light, unblemished! Uncursed! The radiance of Causes that had been seated by living hands and had never once known terminal weavings, blooming outward through a Dimension where every native Cause had been dying for ages, and it washed across the sealed space like dawn crossing a graveyard!","Hvitrmarr’s golden eyes shined brilliantly!","And behind Lissana...the hateful, bored Steed of Oblivion trembled!","Its great gray head, hung low in chained agony for ages beyond counting, shot up! Its guttering eyes fixed across the distance at the source of that impossible light, and through its mountainous frame, the dying Causes that had forgotten everything but pain...listened!","Noah captured all of this movement!","\"I am the one that can fulfill that promise. And yet...these insects behind me are standing in the way.\"","...!","Lissana’s expression finally changed!","It was slight, a tightening at the eyes, a fractional stillness in a being made of function, but on that cold face it rang like a bell! And behind her, the Serpent’s crimson eyes had gone fully ashen, alongside every other True Lifeform in the formation.","And yet, even as Noah said this, Hvitrmarr’s eyes flashed with cold regality!","There was no gratitude in the look she gave him, and no awe.","Her ring pupils passed over his bleeding, glowing, grandstanding figure as if she could see through everything here, through the bluff and the blood-regalia and the borrowed certainty, and her gaze actually moved from him...to THE Infiniverse, resting on the manifestation beside him with an intensity that made her straighten! And then the White Steed spoke.","\"There is no time for this. Let’s go.\"","...!","White light erupted from her!","It burst outward in a single silent bloom, a sovereignty of pearl and flame folding over the golden island, over Noah and THE Infiniverse, over the sandy platform, over Anaximander and THE Creature, wrapping all of them in white.","And they all disappeared!","—","The sealed space stood suddenly, ringingly empty.","Lissana floated before the vacancy where her task had been, her raised hand still holding an unswung stroke, and her crimson gaze was heavy! Around her, twenty True Lifeforms stared at absence, ashen and silent.","And Ormarr Grimtunge howled!","\" NO! No no no NO!\" His coils thrashed through the storm as the follower’s every nightmare arrived at once! \" GET THEM BACK! SOMEBODY GET THEM BA-\"","But behind them all, his howling was drowned out.","For the Steed of Oblivion was still trembling! The gray colossus strained against its screaming chains, its head thrown high for the first time in ages, its guttering eyes fixed on the point in the dark where the impossible light had vanished, and from its mountainous chest, in an ancient voice that had not spoken across ages of walking agony, it began to bellow out!","\" Living! Living, and not Cursed! A Steed, not Cursed!\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":5524,"title":"Chapter 5524: Chapter 5523: Fear and Doubt! III","paragraphs":["<THE Recorder of Wilds>","Upon a golden cloud inside a sealed killing field, an old woman refilled her tea and could not remember the last time an afternoon had given her this much.","She had drifted along inside the formation the entire way, unseen and unsensed, and now she floated barely above the coils of the great Serpent as the party finally cornered its target.","\" Well now. Let us see what the target was...\"","Her ancient gaze swept the trapped golden island, and it snagged, immediately, on the crowned figure at its heart! She read him the way she read all creatures, peeling the layers with eyes older than the frameworks beneath them, and for the first time in an age...the layers pushed back!","\" Hm. Now that is unusual. A young thing. A very young thing, barely into its Trueness, and yet it smells of my own kind. There is Primeval weaving threaded through it, which should not be entirely possible...\" She sipped, and her wrinkled eyes narrowed with genuine delight.","Her gaze drifted to the flame-wrapped titan beside him, and paused again!","\" And this one. Oh my. This one is not a creature at all, is it. It is a place wearing a shape. The weavings do not stop at its skin, they continue outward into everything nearby, quietly claiming, and behind it... \" Her cup stopped halfway to her lips, for her old eyes had found the faint outline folded at the titan’s back, the seated colossus of worn gray stone resting just beneath the surface of the visible.","\"...well, I shouldn’t pry too much on that.\"","And then the scholar!","She looked at the man in white robes floating placidly amid apex predators, and her reading found...nothing! Simply nothing, an absence shaped like a man, as if existence had agreed not to write anything down about him at all!","\"...I have no shelf for that one, \" the old woman admitted to her tea.","\"A lifeform that reads as no lifeform...\"","But it was when her gaze landed on the fourth figure that the old woman set down her cup entirely.","The woman standing at the crowned cub’s shoulder. She was the biggest oddity on the entire battlefield!","\" Oh. Oh my. Now what do we have here.\" The Recorder leaned forward fully, ancient eyes wide with the purest fascination they had held in eras!","\"Is that a Steed? But it can’t be a Steed...what...? Is she the target of the Jarl all along?\" Her voice dropped to a marveling hush.","Below her, the confrontation unfolded!","\" Ah, and here we observe a cornered animal. Twenty-one hunters, a sealed range, no exit. Every creature in nature has a response to this moment. Some bolt. Some freeze. Some bare the throat and hope.\"","A slow smile folded through her wrinkles as the crowned figure drifted forward, alone, ahead of his own protectors, radiating borrowed enormity!","\" Look at him go. He has unbanked every drop of that Primeval scent and is parading it before the colony like a bird spreading feathers it barely owns...\"","Then the blade in red cut him, and the old woman clicked her tongue softly.","\" The predator does not argue with the puffing bird. She simply cuts it, to remind the flock what is real. Beautiful, in its way. \"","Then her ancient brows rose, for the cut thing did not diminish! The cub’s blood rose off him in swirling ribbons of stellar light as his aura climbed, wounds feeding something in his marrow, and the old woman laughed softly into her sleeve.","The second cut came. The story about the king and the dam rolled out over the killing field, and the Recorder listened to the whole story with her chin in her wrinkled palm, thoroughly entertained!","And then...the storm parted.","HUUM!","The old woman felt it before she saw it, an ambient sovereignty descending through the sky that did not belong to the gray colossus below, and when the white shape came down through the parted currents, THE Recorder of Wilds, Primeval One, watcher of eras, unsensable and unsurprisable...","Was shocked!","Her cup rattled against its tray!","\" Oh, you patient, magnificent creature...\" The old woman was on her feet upon the cloud now, tea forgotten, ancient eyes drinking in the white dragon’s descent with open shining eyes!","She had only began looking when the crowned Emperor below began erupting as he screamed out...I AM!","She watched the burst of living Causes bloom across the graveyard-dark. She watched the gray colossus lift its head for the first time. She watched the white Steed’s cold eyes pass straight through the cub’s magnificent puffery and land on the woman beside him!","And then the white light erupted, and the entire party, cub and woman and titan and absence and golden island all together, vanished from the sealed space, carried countless distances in a single sovereign fold!","The killing field rang with sudden emptiness! The blade in red stared at vacancy. The Serpent howled about blame! The gray colossus bellowed its first words in ages at the point where the light had gone, and upon her golden cloud above all of it, the old woman stood in the ruins of the afternoon’s expectations with her eyes gleaming and her mind turning, deliciously, toward a decision!","Which way now? The fled party, carried off by a powerful Steed? Or the abandoned hunters? She reached down for her tea, weighing wilderness against wilderness, and was just about to choose when a nanosecond later...","BOOM!","The sky above the killing field filled with Steeds.","Eight of them!","Eight dying colossi burst through the storm in harness formation, terminal weavings guttering, ancient eyes burning with impossible rejuvenated hope, and behind them, dragged through the parting dark on chains of cursed lightning, came a throne!","And upon the throne sat a titan of rot and lucidity.","Jarl Skallagrim!","The old woman’s brows climbed as she took him in! The Cursed Descendant rode through the sky above Lissana’s frozen party with his fissures glowing dull red, his titanic frame draped in the casual grandeur of a being who had stopped performing madness and no longer cared who noticed, and in his open palm, brilliant waves of possibilities churned and folded like a sea of unwritten pages!","He did not slow for the party below. He barely glanced at them! His cold, terribly sane eyes swept across twenty-one shocked and fearful True Lifeforms!","And then Jarl Skallagrim turned his head.","Before his throne passed through the far edge of the killing field, the dying titan turned, unhurried, and stared straight at her.","At HER!","At THE Recorder of Wilds! At a Primeval One whom the Steed of Oblivion could not sense...and this rotting, dying, cursed thing looked directly into her ancient eyes across the open sky...","And nodded coldly!","Then he tugged on the chains of lightning, and the eight rejuvenated Steeds roared, and the throne surged forward through the dark, following exactly where Hvitrmarr had disappeared towards!","...!","The old woman stood very still upon her golden cloud for a long moment.","Then she shook her head slowly as a smile spread across her wrinkled face that was pure, undiluted interest.","Her golden cloud turned, and followed the eight Steeds pulling a throne!"]},{"number":5525,"title":"Chapter 5525: Chapter 5524: Fear and Doubt! IV","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","They were inside a pocket of space that never stopped moving.","Noah’s senses spread out and found no ground, no sky, no fixed point at all.","The golden island floated at the heart of an isolated bubble of stillness while beyond its unseen walls, countless strings of the Dimension tore past in endless luminous rivers, weavings of Infinity and Primordial Source and THE Lingering Word all streaking by like light bending around the center of a black hole.","They were within something that traversed THE Krazhor-Nul without pause, folded inside its wake, carried at speeds that made his earlier island-flight look like drifting!","And before them, the maker of this pocket floated.","Hvitrmarr!","The Cursed Steed’s massive body coursed through the Dimension without stopping, her vast white wings beating in slow sovereign rhythm as her pearl-scaled frame filled the moving dark, and her golden ring-in-ring eyes were turned back upon them, looking at him...and at THE Infiniverse.","THE Creature and Anaximander gazed at her with cautious eyes! Her terrifying power saturated the pocket even reined in, a sovereignty that had overruled the Steed of Oblivion.","As for Noah...","He was looking at this as a tremendous opportunity!","For this was exactly what he had been looking for from the moment they arrived in this Dimension and received the information of what Cursed Steeds were. Lifeforms stemming from Those Who Remain, their existences structured to be similar to Observable Existences, living Causes flowing through them! Back then he had envisioned it, and asked himself.","What could be the possibility, if he revived such Causes? If he resuscitated the terminal, dying Causes of such lifeforms?! When he had done it for Terminal Observable Existences, he had replaced their dying hearts with his own Nine Prime Causes, and it had only ever elevated his existence and his Infinite Cause thereafter!","And when he had been searching for directions to take his path as THE True Human Emperor, spreading his weavings across the vastness of existence, across all that was Human...the answer had been right there.","So at this moment, Noah reframed his mind, and began looking at the Cursed Steed before him as if she were Human.","And she fit!","She had gambled everything on hope, a brief and burning wager against certain death. She negotiated, offering her existence in exchange for salvation! She feared her ending and ran from it anyway, and carried uncertainty in her ancient voice the way every Human carried it into every unknowable tomorrow.","Strip away the scales and the size and the sovereignty, and what remained was the pattern he had crowned himself upon, striving, bargaining, hoping, afraid!","Human.","She could be labeled Human. And more practically...as a sick human, but filthy rich! Someone of high standing whose salvation, if he delivered it, would benefit him tremendously!","Was that not Human too? An exchange of favors? Helping one, and in turn, they help you? The oldest Human condition there was!","Noah was about to address this powerful Cursed Steed when her ancient voice rang out first.","\" We will all die very soon.\"","...!","\"I miscalculated, and there is no time. Jarl Skallagrim, someone whose power I underestimated, is chasing me with eight others just like me. He is a Cursed Descendant, true and true.\" Her golden eyes did not blink as the strings of the Dimension tore past beyond her pocket.","\"I took a gamble to break my chains, because I sensed hope. Because my existence, filled with dying Causes, sensed it. Now, whether that is you, or her...if the promise really is true...do it now, and do it fast. Because I am chained in this Dimension while being Cursed, and I cannot leave it. I can only keep running across it.\" A pause, and her vast voice lowered.","\"If the promise is true, fulfill it, and I will owe you my existence. If it is merely false weavings of my lineage...then death arrives for us all.\"","...!","And at this time, Noah sensed it, threaded through her last few words, unmistakable to him.","Uncertainty.","The very Human emotion of uncertainty, carried inside an ancient sovereign voice, a being who did not know if the promise her whole lineage had waited upon was real, and his expression hardened.","A Cursed Descendant with eight Cursed Steeds was chasing after her!","His eyes flashed with immensity as he looked at THE Infiniverse.","\" Let’s go.\"","The two of them floated up grandly from the golden island!","Emperor and a unique living Observable Existence rose together through the moving pocket, dark-blue hair and cerulean threads streaming in the wake-winds, and they crossed the open space toward the Cursed Steed as her massive form turned slightly to receive them. And with every measure of distance closed, Noah felt it more.","It was like approaching a terrifying furnace of existence! He was drawing near the core of something that was similar to THE Infiniverse, structured like her, layered like her, Causes turning within a living frame like hers, and yet not her at all, older, wilder, seated by different hands, and wound through with something that made his marrow prickle even at this distance.","And beside him, THE Infiniverse’s composed face...broke.","A pained expression crossed her features, her cerulean eyes tightening as her own weavings resonated with the entity before her, and she asked...","\" How... can you live with such pain?\"","Hvitrmarr’s great head lowered slightly, and her answer came calm, and slow.","\" One does not live with pain. It leaves no room for living with it. \" Her golden rings turned. \" So one lives beside it. The pain fills every moment I stand inside. Every single one. But it cannot fill the moment that has not yet arrived. So that is where I lived. In the moment that had not yet come. I have lived entirely in tomorrow.\"","...!","THE Infiniverse’s hands curled slowly at her sides.","They neared her massive chest, and the terrifying pressure released from this creature was purposefully reined in, drawn back into her body layer by deliberate layer so that they could approach, and Noah got to take her in fully at last.","Her scales, this close, were wonders. Each one the size of a shield, worn smooth as ancient ivory, pearl-white with hairline lines of age running through them like the memory of every year they had survived, and beneath their surfaces, faint rivers of silver light moved slowly, like veins of a world.","They were warm. That was the shocking thing, warm as living skin, humming faintly with the deep engine-thrum of the Causes turning far beneath! And threaded through the warmth, so fine it could be missed, ran a wrongness, a cold gray filament tracing the border of every scale like frost that refused to melt.","Noah and THE Infiniverse reached out together, and put their hands on these scales.","The moment they did...","HUUM!","His existence shook.","Sharp prickles of pain lanced through him instantly, not from the scale, from everywhere, as if his entire existence was suddenly being hounded and pierced by ten thousand patient needles at once, his weavings flinching, his Causes recoiling, his marrow flaring in alarm!","| You have come into contact with a Lifeform carrying an extremely terrifying Curse, fused into its First Cause and all interlinking Causes within it. This is not ambient Lingering Word. This is a seated, sentenced, active Curse- too much contact, and this Curse can be transferred over to your own Causes.|","His expression became incredibly heavy."]},{"number":5526,"title":"Chapter 5526: Chapter 5525: Fear and Doubt! V","paragraphs":["Because through the contact, through his hands upon her warm ancient scales, he had become capable of fully sensing just what was inside a Cursed Steed.","It was horrendous.","|I have identified the curse. Designation: THE Gnawing Remembrance of Nhaglfarr-Ythok, of Those Who Remain. It manufactures pain from the victim’s own capacity to feel.|","|Its function, as I read it: the Curse converts feeling itself into agony. Every emotion the victim experiences is seized and reforged into pain before it finishes being felt. Contentment burns. Memory of joy burns worse, the Curse replays the victim’s finest moments through their weavings and chews each one, so that everything they ever loved becomes a returning blade. And hope... Hope burns worst of all. The Curse prices hope above every other feeling, and the moment a victim dares to hope, the gnawing sharpens tenfold. This is why the Steeds of this Dimension stopped hoping ages ago.|","|It never permits adaptation. Every nanosecond, the Curse refreshes the victim’s sensitivity, resetting their weavings to feel the pain as if for the first time. There is no dulling. There is no growing numb. Even a thousand years in, the pain is as first-day fresh as it was at the seating. And it forbids escape through death: it sustains the victim at the edge of their existence, feeding on their feeling, and permits their ending only when the Cause is fully consumed.|","|And for the Steeds, it is worst of all. Their Causes are organs of feeling, many living channels through a single existence, and the Curse is threaded through EVERY one. They do not feel the gnawing once. They feel it through every Cause they carry, simultaneously, every nanosecond, from seating until death. The one before you has endured this for three thousand years while choosing, every single day, to keep the capacity to hope, which the Curse punishes above all things...|","...!","Noah’s existence winced in pain as merely identifying it made the edges of the Curse taste him back.","And at this time, from beneath his palms, murky dark tendrils began leaking out of Hvitrmarr’s scales! Thin filaments of obsidian gray seeped up through the ancient ivory and began stretching onto Noah’s hands, and onto the hands of THE Infiniverse, curling, probing, patient, reaching for their weavings as if to infect them.","\"...\"","He had to make a choice here. A gamble!","If he continued, there was a high chance of being branded with a Curse he could not do anything about, a sentence from Those Who Remain hooked into his Causes, into THE Infiniverse’s Causes, forever! But if he succeeded...he would reverse the Curse of an utterly unfathomable being while seating his Prime Causes inside a Cursed Steed whose origins were so grand that success would catapult him tremendously.","Noah breathed slowly.","And for the first time in a very long time...he felt Doubt.","Doubt! He had given away his Everything of Doubt a while ago, traded it out of his existence entirely, and yet here it was, regenerated quietly among his many Human emotions, standing in his chest like an old tenant returned to a rebuilt house.","Because should he fail here, it would not only be him. THE Infiniverse would be Cursed alongside him, alongside all their Causes, alongside every realm and every life she carried. His entire path...his whole journey...everything could end against these warm ancient scales.","As he thought of this...","\" Ah...\"","He blinked, in an epiphany.","He was also... feeling fear.","Him? THE True Human Emperor? Noah Osmont, who had walked into apocalypses on purpose and priced adversity like a delicacy? He was feeling...a trace of genuine fear?","Was doubt and fear such a potent human condition? Was it so potent that he regenerated their Everythings to now feel even them? Was this...true of who he was?!","DUM!","He felt the heavy beat of his heart!","And at this moment, from beyond himself, he felt a wave of resonance answer it. Faint flickering flames of the very same feeling, mirrored back at him from the colossal existence beneath his hands.","Hvitrmarr.","Through the contact, through the resonance of fear meeting fear, Noah saw. Deep inside this Cursed Steed, far beneath the scales and the sovereignty and the three thousand years of patience, there was a figure.","A white-robed woman, coiled small in the dark of her own vast existence, arms wrapped around herself, pained! Frightened! This grand Steed, this lifeform who had shattered chains and overruled the Steed of Oblivion and spoken of death with a level voice...also felt fear.","Fear of the oblivion that was coming for her. Fear of feeling nothing and seeing nothing...when she had spent her whole cursed existence feeling everything.","Noah couldn’t help but shake his head at that.","And at this time, without him even realizing it, his expression changed. It settled into something that only the true kings and emperors of ancient eras ever obtained, the ones who had learned that leading was never about standing above fear, the quiet certain warmth of a ruler who goes first into the dark so that others may follow, and he spoke softly, to the trembling woman coiled inside the mountain of scales.","\" Let me in. I will help you, and you will help me. \" His hand pressed gently against the warm ancient ivory as the dark tendrils curled around his fingers. \" We are both fearful. But it is much easier to overcome this fear together.\"","...!","He said such words, and Hvitrmarr trembled.","Her colossal frame shuddered once through its whole length as her golden ring-in-ring eyes gazed down at him, at THE Infiniverse beside him, at the two small existences standing willingly against her Cursed chest with the infection already reaching for their hands, and after a moment, after three thousand years of tomorrows arriving all at once...","Her scales opened.","The great plates of ancient ivory parted along seams that had never once unsealed, folding back petal upon petal, and within...utterly sacred and unfathomable wonders revealed themselves.","Vaults of white flame turning in slow rivers! Horizons folded inside horizons, the interior architecture of something forged by the hands that predated every framework, Causes hanging in the deep like dying suns, and all of it threaded through with the gray gnawing dark of the Curse.","And Noah stepped in, alongside THE Infiniverse as his mind pulsed with an epiphany.","To lead was to walk point on the edge of the unknown. Some say that great leaders are fearless...monoliths of absolute certainty who move through chaos without a tremor. But that is a myth and not the reality of human nature.","​A truly great human leader does not fear fear. They welcome it, understand it, and transmute it.","BOOM!","Instantly, light detonated across existence!","Endless blue light gushed out of one half of Hvitrmarr, cerulean brilliance erupting through her parted scales and her weavings and her very frame as Noah’s Intent and Osmontian Source Infinity and his Prime Causes poured into the ancient interior, painting half of her colossal form in radiant, living, boundless blue.","And in the same nanosecond, endless murky obsidian curse-light bloomed over the other half, THE Gnawing Remembrance rising to answer the intrusion, gray-black malice flooding through the opposing hemisphere of her existence.","It looked like existence in this whole area had been split in two!","One half, endlessly blue. Another half, endlessly dark!","—","Outside, Anaximander and THE Creature had heavy expressions as they looked out.","For the domain that had been constantly moving...came to a stop.","The pocket dissolved as Hvitrmarr’s flight ended, and the surroundings cleared to reveal where the long run had carried them, an ancient billowing stretch of ice, glacial plains folding to every horizon beneath a sky of falling snow, white flakes drifting down through the frozen quiet of THE Krazhor-Nul’s far reaches.","And across that white stillness, for light years...one half of existence was painted blue, and another half was painted black.","The colossal form of Hvitrmarr floated at the center of it all, split down her length by two warring lights, blue sovereignty and obsidian sentence grinding against each other through every Cause she carried, and the snow itself fell blue on one side of the sky and gray-black on the other!","And in the next nanosecond...","ROAR!","The cursed black half seemingly roared out with malice!","It surged! Where the two lights had stood at even halves, fifty against fifty, the obsidian cursed brilliance rapidly began to gain ground, swallowing the blue in great gnawing waves, sixty, seventy, covering eighty percent of her colossal frame with horrifying speed, and it only continued to accelerate, an ancient sentence rising to devour the presense that had dared to argue with it!","It was a Curse tracing back to Those Who Remain.","It was undeniable!"]},{"number":5527,"title":"Chapter 5527: Chapter 5526: Death! I","paragraphs":["Somewhere in the cold reaches of an ancient Dimension, a bleeding man stands with his hands on cursed scales, and inside his chest, two old tenants have moved back into a house that evicted them long ago.","Doubt and fear.","And it should be said that even now, even trembling, some corner of that man is questioning. Weighing the gamble, counting the gains, tallying what a reversed curse and a seated Steed would be worth against everything he could lose!","He is not the first to face this homecoming. Every civilization that ever climbed has run the same argument about these two tenants, and the argument begins with corpses. The soldier who doubted his footing for one breath, and the bridge took him. The mother who feared the dark road and so took the long one, and arrived too late. Doubt is the pause where blades find throats. Fear is the counsel of a smaller life! The evidence dies loudly, and so every discipline of power teaches the same first lesson.","Purge them.","Cultivators burn doubt out of their foundations the way farmers burn stubble from a field. Emperors train fear out of their heirs before the heirs can walk. Some go further still, and trade the emotions away entirely, carve them out, hand them to another, and stand afterward in the clean silence where the trembling used to be, and call that silence strength.","And for a while, it is. The purged strike faster. The purged sleep well.","But the doctrine keeps no record of how the purged die, because the ones who could testify are under the water.","Fear is a map with exactly one thing drawn on it: what matters. No being has ever feared the loss of something worthless! A man feels fear at a sickbed because the one in the bed is his whole sky. A queen in chains feels fear of oblivion because she spent three thousand years earning the tomorrow that oblivion would cancel. The fearless do not carry more courage than the fearful. They carry less cargo! Strip a being of everything it loves and watch how brave it becomes, and then ask whether that bravery is worth what was paid for it.","So what is a Human, who is born holding both?","A Human is a brief and burning pattern with no time to armor itself into silence. Humans doubt because their knowledge is partial, and so they check the wall twice, and the wall holds.","Humans fear because everything they hold can be taken, and so they hold it properly, and build anyway, love anyway, cross the dark anyway.","Which brings the matter, at last, to leaders, and to the one distinction on which everything turns.","A good Human leader is not afraid of fear.","For fear denied in the light doubles in the dark, and a leader who cannot admit the tremor in his own hand will demand that no hand around him tremble, and such leaders break their people long before any enemy arrives.","And the fearless cannot lead the fearful. They can only outpace them! A being who feels nothing before the dark can walk into it, certainly, but no bridge exists between his silence and their trembling, and no one follows. It is the leader who feels the fear fully, names it aloud, and steps first regardless who turns terror into a road.","His fear is the proof that the danger is real. His step is the proof that it can be crossed. Fear shared is halved, and fear witnessed being overcome is transformed, and this is the entire mechanism by which frightened peoples have crossed every impossible thing they ever crossed.","Courage was never the absence of fear. Courage is fear, correctly spent.","So when doubt regenerates in a chest that once traded it away, and a heart that forgot the rhythm beats hard against cursed scales, that is not a foundation cracking. That is the foundation completing itself.","Somewhere in the cold, the snow is falling in two colors, and the black half is climbing.","The man with his hands on the scales has his fear, and his doubt, and his greed, and his crown.","Now he must spend them.","Ultimately, the ones who feel everything, and go forward anyway, have always been the strongest things in existence.","---","<THE True Human Emperor>","Inside Hvitrmarr, Noah held the hand of THE Infiniverse, and he was trembling.","Their joined hands were already stained black. The Curse had wasted no time, murky tendrils sunken into their fingers and crawling up their wrists as their feet darkened where they stood upon the inner weavings of the White Steed, and across Noah’s body, gashes tore themselves open one after another! Across THE Infiniverse’s frame too, thin lines split her manifestation as blood sputtered out of both of them gloriously, stellar crimson-blue-gold scattering into the vaulted white-flame dark of a living Steed at war with itself!","But even in such a situation...","Noah’s body began to pulse with light.","Multicolored radiance bloomed out of his body in slow, mounting waves, the light of his Nine Prime Causes, Existence and Paradox and Chaos and Mana, Quintessence and Adversity, Tyranny and Harvest and Apocalypse, each one a different burning shade turning through his weavings! And beneath them all surged the endless blue light of his Infinite Cause, pouring out of his core in tides as their blackened limbs instantly shone bright, the stains burning back inch by inch, and a sea of blue began to expand around the two of them, pushing the gnawing dark to a perimeter!","And within that fought-for clearing...Noah got to learn exactly what he was up against.","His senses spread through her, and the structure of Hvitrmarr unfolded before him.","She was made up of nine Causes. And they were all First Causes!","Nine First Causes, seated by the hands of Those Who Remain at the dawn of this Dimension, turning through her colossal existence like nine ancient suns! But what was horrendous, what made his expression harden even through the blue light, was HOW they were seated. These Causes were not installed within her the way Prime Causes sat within Observable Existences.","These Causes were bound to her Organs. No. They were her Organs!","Cause and flesh fused into single existing things! When he had resuscitated Terminal Observable Existences, he had replaced their dying Prime Causes the way one replaces a foundations of a building. But here, to replace a First Cause...one would have to replace the Organ of a Cursed Steed itself! Break down living anatomy seated by the makers of this Dimension, and grow new anatomy in its place, all while the Curse defended every inch!","His Sight moved through her, and he discerned them, one by one as these causes...were not the normal causes of Observable Existences.","THE First Cause of Fealty, seated as her Heart! The vast drumming organ at her center, a Cause that beat not for herself but for another, the sworn bond of the First Steeds given muscle and rhythm!","THE First Cause of Honor, seated as her Spine! The unbending column running her colossal length, the Cause of carrying every weight upright and breaking before bowing!","THE First Cause of Valor, seated as her Lungs! Twin oceans of white flame drawing the breath before every charge, courage itself made into respiration.","THE First Cause of Obedience, seated as her Ears! Deep coiled chambers that heard the command before it was spoken, attunement to a rider’s will woven into living structure.","THE First Cause of Vigilance, seated as her Eyes! The golden ring-in-ring wonders, the watch that never closes, awareness layered within awareness.","THE First Cause of Endurance, seated as her Bones! The tireless frame that had borne burdens across ages, persistence given architecture.","THE First Cause of Temperance, seated as her Stomach! The furnace that consumed only what duty required and nothing more, restraint as an organ!","THE First Cause of Mercy, seated as her Claws! Strength vast enough to unmake, shaped into instruments that had chosen gentleness for three thousand years!","And THE First Cause of Devotion, seated as her Wings. The great white sails that had only ever flown carrying another before herself, service itself given feathers and flight.","...!","This was what Those Who Remain had built! Not a beast of burden at all, but something sworn and honorable and enduring and devoted, nine virtues seated as nine organs, and then their descendants had cursed the entire order of them and hitched what remained to thrones.","Noah and THE Infiniverse struggled against the pressing dark as he took it all in, and he made his choice in the same breath!","\" Ruination. Infiniverse. Confluence.\"","HUUM!","The fusion slammed through the three of them inside the body of a fourth! His crown unwove into him, THE Infiniverse dissolved into his chest, and THE Quintessential Confluence rose within Hvitrmarr’s inner vaults, grades climbing a rank as his frame, already carved with gashes, blazed crimson-gold through the blue! And through the fused sight, the full scale of the task ahead of him resolved without pity.","Nine Organs. Nine fused First Causes. Every one defended by a Curse that punished hope itself, in a body older than the Scales, on a clock measured in the hoofbeats of eight Steeds and an Jarl.","It was almost impossible. He saw that plainly.","And doubt rose, and fear rose with it, the two regenerated tenants beating hard against his ribs! But Noah Osmont was not made of two emotions. He was Human, and Human was a crowded house! His pride rose beside the fear, the pride of a man who had never once left a wall unclimbed.","His stubbornness rose beside the doubt, the mule-hearted refusal that had carried him up from an F Rank Hunter through every apocalypse existence could schedule! His greed rose, pricing the First-lineage Steed and finding the reward worth any gamble!","His love rose, for the daughter sensing agony-clusters and the mother inside his home and the women who depended on him! And above all of them rose the quality that had crowned him, the responsibility of THE True Human Emperor, the plain and total conviction that if all that was Human was his to gather, then all that was Human was his to protect, and the Human thing before him was dying.","Fear said the wall was high. Every other thing he was said... climb.","He had to try. And he had to succeed!","But how?! How could he resuscitate Causes that were not merely Terminal, but fused into flesh and filled with a Curse that lashed out against every touch?!"]},{"number":5528,"title":"Chapter 5528: Chapter 5527: Death! II","paragraphs":["Noah looked around the vaulted dark, at the nine ancient suns and the gnawing gray threaded through every one, and the decision assembled itself with the cold clarity of a craftsman surveying a ruin.","He would simply have to replace the Organs themselves, no big innovations needed.","Break down cursed anatomy seated by the makers of a Dimension. Grow new Organs from his own existence in the wounds left behind. Seat his Prime Causes into the growing flesh and hope that the grafts would take!","So much work. So much impossible work!","He proceeded ahead, and started.","\" The Lungs first, and I will need as much help as you can give, Hvitrmarr!\" Noah declared, and moved!","He descended through her inner vaults to the twin oceans of white flame, THE First Cause of Valor laboring beneath its gray threading, every breath of the great Steed dragging through cursed channels! And Noah set his fused existence against it as his Intent erupted.","THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian poured out of him in prismatic seas as his Osmontian Source Infinity followed in continental tides, and he began to BREAK the Organ down with the help of Hvitrmarr herself!","He did not do it crudely, not destructively, but the way a master smith unmakes a flawed blade, edge by edge, fold by fold, his Intent declaring each cursed weaving unwoven as his Infinity dissolved the freed matter into raw potential.","The cost was staggering! A tremendous portion of his Intent’s output and whole oceans of his Source Infinity vanished into the unmaking of a single Organ, his reserves screaming, his gashes tearing wider with the strain.","But he had boundless reserves.","And then came the replacing.","Noah raised his carved arms, and began to guide the blood raging around his body!","The Berserker blood! The swirling stellar regalia of crimson-blue-gold that had wreathed him since Lissana’s cuts, saturated with Primeval Osmontian Cells, and he sent it flowing in glorious rivers down into the hollow where Valor’s lungs had been! And into that flowing blood, he infused a portion of THE Primeval Osmontian Marrow itself, a seam of his own stellar blue-gold bone-architecture, seeded into the wound as the base of an Organ of a grand Steed!","The blood pooled. The marrow-seed took root. And flesh began to bud.","New lungs grew in the hollow, woven from his Cells and his blood and his seated Prime Cause of Adversity, courage-through-challenge pouring into the growing chambers, and then Noah’s eyes widened, for the budding Organ was doing something he had not designed!","It held a mixture.","His Prime Cause of Adversity burned through the new flesh, and threaded through it, refusing to leave, rising out of the dissolved ruin of the old Organ like a stubborn ghost, came THE First Cause of Valor! The two Causes were MIXING!","Adversity and Valor winding around each other in the budding lungs, his weavings and the First weavings of Those Who Remain fusing into something that was neither and both, and the new Organ drew its first breath with a sound like a war-horn learning tenderness.","...!","One. One Organ, budding and mixed and alive, and the cost of it had hollowed him his existence even with his boundlessness!","Noah steadied his carved body, turned toward the Heart of Fealty, and that....was when the Curse stopped defending.","And attacked.","THE Gnawing Remembrance of Nhaglfarr-Ythok had watched something dare to begin replacing it. Watched something dare to CURE! And the ancient sentence, offended beyond all measure, made a decision that proved beyond any doubt that it was cognizant.","It sacrificed itself.","Across Hvitrmarr’s vaulted existence, four of the nine Organs suddenly blazed gray-black as the Curse burned its own holdings! Its potent grip on the Eyes of Vigilance, the Ears of Obedience, the Claws of Mercy, and the Wings of Devotion, four First Causes’ worth of seated, ancient, concentrated Curse, torn out of those Organs entirely and converted, all at once, into fuel.","Into one attack!","ROAR!","The insidious eruption came from every direction at once, a tidal wave of weaponized sentence, four organs’ worth of three-thousand-year agony condensed into a single gnawing tsunami, and it fell upon the fused figure of Noah with the full offense of a maker’s malice!","It was not something he could possibly withstand.","His blue sea shattered! His Prime Cause lights bent! The wave crashed through his Intent and his Infinity and his budding triumph, and Noah felt it instantly, coldly, completely.","His collapse was coming.","Not a wound and most definitely not a setback.","His existence, fused and elevated and Berserker-burning, was going to break under this, and nothing he could run in any stretched instant said otherwise!","Death was coming.","And THE True Human Emperor...moved grandly.","There was no panic in him! There was no scrambling! Even as the Curse invaded his existence, gray-black threads chewing into his weavings, he kept his Prime Causes burning gloriously, nine colors blazing through the collapse like banners refusing to lower, and he looked, in the closing moments, not at the wave.","He looked at the four sacrificed Organs.","Eyes. Ears. Claws. Wings! Four Organs the Curse had abandoned to fuel its killing stroke, four First Causes sitting undefended for the first time in three thousand years, and Noah, dying, saw the trade laid bare upon the table and paid it with both hands.","He sent his blood.","Seas of gushing stellar blood erupted from his splitting frame, four glorious rivers of crimson-blue-gold roaring outward through the collapsing vaults, and even as he died, he began infusing his Causes into them.","Marrow-seed and Cell and Prime weaving poured into the Eyes as Quintessence met Vigilance! Into the Ears as Mana met Obedience! Into the Claws as Tyranny met Mercy, strength and gentleness winding together!","Into the Wings as Harvest met Devotion, and in the growing lungs behind him Adversity and Valor still burned, five Organs, five mixtures, five buddings seeded in the space of his own ending!","The wave closed over him.","His body split! His infinite seas of power were torn open down their length, and in the final fraction of the final instant, Noah made his last choice, and chose true.","He folded the collapse INWARD, taking the entire attack fully into himself, wrapping his split halves around the presences fused within him so that THE Infiniverse and Ruination, sheltered inside the breaking, would gain no damage at all! His ending would be his alone. Not his home’s. Not his crown’s.","And as everything came apart, THE True Human Emperor roared his last word into the dark!","\"I AM QUINTESSENTIAL!\"","BOOM!","The roar detonated through Hvitrmarr’s vaulted existence as the five seeded Organs answered it, budding flesh blazing with mixed Cause-light, his Cells igniting through Eyes and Ears and Claws and Wings and Lungs, five ancient suns rekindling in new colors even as their gardener was unmade.","His body split apart in halves of guttering light.","And within the splitting, untouched by the wave, buried deeper than any attack naturally reached, one small organ shone!","A liver!","THE Hepatarch of the Undying Root gleamed resplendantly even in death, a quiet steady star inside the ruin of an Emperor, holding, holding, holding!","But it would not act in this moment. It could not! And so, for the first time in his entire grand existence, across every era and apocalypse...","Noah died.","Immense darkness folded around him, soft and total, and the last thing that moved through him was not fear, and was not doubt.","He was Quintessential. He was also Human.","And to be human...was to die.","Somewhere beyond the darkness, snow was still falling across an ancient white stretch of ice, and inside a white Steed, upon the white of his own guttering light, a death was being written.","Three deaths must the deathless die before the door swings wide.","What was written in the white...was written from today.","---","<THE Infiniverse>","The Emperor was dead.","His split halves drifted apart through the vaulted dark of the White Steed, two ruins of guttering light trailing stellar blood into the black, and the Curse’s spent wave rolled onward past them, and for one single nanosecond, the inside of Hvitrmarr held nothing but silence.","Then, from each of his split halves...figures rose.","From one half, woven strings of crimson-gold gathered themselves upward into the illusory body of a woman crowned in her own circlet, Ruination, untouched, unharmed, exactly as her Master’s final fold had ensured. And from the other half, cerulean threads spiraled up into the illusory manifestation of THE Infiniverse, whole and undamaged, standing upon the broken light of the being who had wrapped his own ending around her like armor!","Two figures. Two halves. One dead Emperor between them.","And the rage that rose off of both of them was unfathomable.","Ruination’s illusory face was perfectly composed as her strings spread out from her in their thousands, and every single string was pulled tighter than a blade’s edge, her fury expressed in pure, cold, absolute function! And THE Infiniverse, the efficient one, the serious one, the one who rarely smiled and never wasted a motion, stood over her Master’s ruin with her hands slowly closing into fists as her cerulean eyes burned, and the realms within her, thousands of them, countless lives, all of it, tilted toward wrath like an entire existence leaning into a storm!","He had taken it alone. He had SPLIT rather than let one thread of it touch them!","\" We continue!\" Ruination said, and her voice had never been colder.","They moved!","The two of them poured their wills down into the dead Emperor’s cells, and the cells answered! For THE Primeval Osmontian Cells did not know their maker had died, they knew only their work, and Ruination’s strings threaded through the four blood-rivers still flowing toward Eyes and Ears and Claws and Wings, guiding, weaving, holding every budding graft in its proper form! THE Infiniverse’s authority flooded the growing Lungs where Adversity and Valor still wound together, feeding the mixture, steadying its first breaths!","And when the Curse came creeping back...they were waiting.","Gray-black filaments slunk toward the five budding Organs, the gnawing sentence reaching to reclaim what it had sacrificed, and it found the way barred! Ruination’s strings cut the filaments apart with surgical, vicious precision, no wasted force, no mercy, each thread of Curse unwoven the instant it extended! THE Infiniverse’s dimensional weavings sealed around each budding Organ like the walls of her own realms, and the Curse pressed, and probed, and found five fortresses where five wounds had been!","New Causes had already bloomed!","The five Organs budded on, safe, mixing, growing, tended by the two loyal existences of a dead man.","And then THE Infiniverse went a step further.","Her burning eyes rose from the defended five, and fixed across the vaulted dark upon the vast drumming Organ at the Steed’s center, still wrapped in its full portion of ancient Curse.","THE First Cause of Fealty. The Heart!","The Cause that beat for another. The sworn bond given muscle! And what was SHE, if not exactly that?! A living Observable Existence whose every realm turned around her Master, whose every Cause had bent toward him since her birth, whose loyalty was not a feeling but her fundamental architecture.","If any Organ in this cursed being answered to her nature, it was that one, and her Master had died five Organs into a nine-Organ war, and she would not stand guard over his work.","She would ADVANCE it!","And so, THE Infiniverse roared out.","The sound tore through the vaulted existence of the White Steed as, deep within Noah’s broken body, the hidden Infiniverse herself, the true her, the living Observable Existence seated through his weavings with her thousands of realms and her nested skies and her billions of burning lives, shone brilliantly and erupted!","Hvitrmarr felt it all as it felt like her body was warring with itself, but she felt the hope ever so close as she lent all the help she could against the Curse.","BOOM!","Cerulean light detonated out of the dead Emperor’s halves in a pillar that split the inner dark from vault to vault.","The full unfurled presense of an Observable Existence poured across the distance toward the cursed Heart of Fealty, realms condensing into radiance, Causes massing into tides, a loyal existence hurling her entire self at the center of an ancient sentence in her dead Master’s name.","The Curse rose snarling around the Heart to meet her.","And beneath all of it, in the quiet ruin of the split halves, drifting in the dark where no light reached and no war touched...","The glimmering liver began to pulse.","Once.","...!"]},{"number":5529,"title":"Chapter 5529: Chapter 5528: Death! III","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Death was not empty.","That was the first thing Noah learned on the other side of it. The immense darkness that had folded around him thinned, and sensation returned without a body to carry it, and he found himself standing upon an endless sea of red.","It was heavy.","Heavy the way a debt is heavy, the way a name spoken at the wrong funeral is heavy, and the red stretched out to every horizon without a single wave, thick and still and patient, and across its surface, floating in their countless numbers...","Were bodies.","All those he had killed.","They floated face-up as far as any sight could reach! The countless he had killed in his home world when it was still tiny. Those from the dungeons, beasts and horrors he had cleaved through by the thousands for essence! Those from the Beast World, from Atlantis, from the Demon World, warriors and monarchs and soldiers who had stood in formations against him.","Those from his Universe. From his Cosmos! From his Wheel of Existence, hierarchies he had erased in afternoons, hosts he had unmade between conversations! From his Observable Existence and every battlefield across every era of his climb, they floated in the red, countless past counting, an ocean floored with everything his ascension had cost everyone else.","And each of them seemed to be looking at him.","Their eyes were open. Every single one! And though no mouth moved, the question rose off the red sea like heat, asked in the countless voices of the drowned, pressing against him from every direction at once.","Why?","Why did we deserve to die?","...!","Noah stood upon the heavy red, and did not look away.","And then, out of the endless sea of blood, directly before him...a body rose.","It came up slowly, red parting off its shoulders, and it did not float like the others. It stood! A figure with light gold hair falling past his ears, fair skin that shone faintly gold as if dawn had been rubbed into it, adorned in a white robe that the sea somehow did not stain, and his eyes, as they opened upon Noah, were cold.","Noah knew him.","The precipice of the Novus Galaxy. The octagonal shattered space. The raving laughter in his closing palm.","It was Aldrich, the Founder of the Celestials!","But there was no madness in him now. Death, it seemed, had returned what desperation had taken, and the being who had died a raving lunatic stood upon the sea of his killer’s making with the cold, composed dignity of what he had been before the end.","\" Do you remember my last day?\" Aldrich asked.","His voice carried flatly across the red.","\"I remember it completely. Death is generous that way. It returns every moment you spent dying, and lets you hold them all at once.\" His golden eyes did not blink.","\"I stood at the very precipice of the Novus Galaxy, at the edge of everything I had ever known, with my essence spent and your tendrils around my limbs. I had been magnificent once. A Founder! Raised up from nothing, given strength, given purpose, given a Galaxy to shepherd. And then I learned what I was. A puppet. A thing on strings, raised up and thrown away like nothing the moment the play required it.\"","\" So I did the only thing a cornered puppet could do. I rang the bell. I broke the barrier of my own home and called destruction down upon the enemy I could not defeat, and I laughed, because it was the first act of my entire existence that no string had chosen for me.\"","The sea of red was utterly silent around his words.","\" And you crushed me. Mid-sentence, mind you. You folded your palm and ended me the way one crushes a bug.\" His head tilted slightly.","\" So I will ask you what all of them are asking. \" One golden hand swept slowly across the endless floating dead.","\" Why did I deserve to die? All I was trying to do was break past the lines of fate laid through me. Past a destiny that others had set! Is that not what you have done at every single step? You defied your system. You defied your Galaxy, your Universe, your Cosmos, your Scales! You have made a crown out of refusing every script ever written for you. I refused ONE script, ONE time, at the very end, with my last breath.\" His cold eyes fixed on Noah’s.","\" Why did you deserve to go on...and I deserved your palm?\"","...!","The question rolled out across the sea, and the countless dead seemed to lean into it! Every open-eyed body in the red asking through him, the soldiers born into wrong banners, the hierarchies erased between errands, the groups unmade for standing in formations they never chose, all of their why gathered into one golden-haired vessel standing dry-robed upon an ocean of consequence.","And Noah looked at Aldrich calmly.","He did not flinch from it. He did not reach for comfortable weavings, for they-attacked-first, for any of the soft accountings the living tell themselves about their dead! He stood upon the sea he had filled, and let the question weigh what it weighed, and when he answered, his voice was quiet, and grand, and tyrannical, and human, all four at once.","\" The dead should stay dead.\"","...!","\" That is my first answer, and it is respect! Your day ended, Aldrich. It ended completely, at the edge of your Galaxy, with your one free act burning in your hands. Nothing I say here can add to it or take from it, and nothing you ask here can reopen it. The dead pleading their case to the living is the living’s dream, not the dead’s right. You had your last day.\"","Noah’s gaze moved past him then, across the endless red, across every open eye in the ocean.","\" And my second answer is for all of you.\" His voice carried to every horizon.","\" Across existence, all of us seek to defy fate and destiny. All of us! The hierarchies I erased were defying their extinctions, and you, Founder, were defying your strings, and I was defying everything, and every single one of us reached for the same forbidden thing with the same desperate hands.\"","His eyes came back to Aldrich, and they were level, and they did not apologize.","\" Some fail. Some succeed. You did not die because you deserved it. Deserving was never consulted! You simply failed .\"","\"And I...I have yet to fail.\"","...!","Aldrich stared at him for a long moment.","And whatever the dead do with honesty, he did it in silence.","Then Noah rose.","He drifted upward off the heavy surface, and turned, and looked out at the endless seas of blood and corpses stretching behind him, at every era of his climb floating face-up in the red. He would not pretend they did not weigh. And he would not let them anchor.","He waved his hand.","And shockingly, his grasp closed around the ENTIRE sea!","Every horizon of it, every drop of red, every floating body across every direction, gathered into the will of a single gesture, and atop all of it, Noah imposed...an endless blue!","His color! The color of his Infinity, of his Source, of his identity, of every road he had climbed and every road still unclimbed, and it poured across the red sea from the point of his palm outward in a tide that did not ask permission!","The heavy red drank the blue and became it. The countless bodies sank gently beneath the rising color, their open eyes closing one by one as the blue took them, questions settling, accounts not erased but carried, an ocean of consequence folded whole into the identity of the one who owed it!","\" Ashes to ashes ,\" Noah said softly, to all of them, to every era, to the golden-haired vessel watching him from the settling tide. \" Dust to dust!\"","And then, endless blue covered everything!","It rose past the horizons and over the sky of that heavy place, blue upon blue upon blue without floor or shore, and through the totality of it, through the whole claimed ocean of everything he had done and everything he still owed...","Noah felt his existence waking from death!"]},{"number":5530,"title":"Chapter 5530: Chapter 5529: Emergence!","paragraphs":["The first thing that existed was a pulse.","DUM.","One beat, in an ocean of nothing, and Noah existed around it the way sound exists around a struck bell! He had no body yet. He had no eyes, no frame, no seas of power! There was only the pulse, and the quiet certainty folded inside it, and the pulse was a liver.","THE Hepatarch of the Undying Root was rebuilding him .","DUM. DUM.","And what a strange, profound thing it was, to be regrown from one’s own organ! He felt himself assembling outward from that single glimmering seed, layer by patient layer, and the Root did not rebuild him the way healing rebuilds, flesh first and self after. It rebuilt him self FIRST!","His records returned in vast ordered floods, era upon era pouring back into being, the skill book, the dungeons, the crowns, the graves, every climb and every cost! His memories seated themselves. His Intent reassembled around its own claim, I am, I am, I AM, each beat of the Root another syllable of the sentence that was him! His authority, his Tongue, his Letters, his Foundations, all of it drawn back out of the Root’s deep reserve and rewoven, and only then, only around a self already whole, did the flesh come!","And the flesh that came...was new.","For the Root did not have his old body to copy from. His old body had been split apart and spent! So it built him from what he had become, and what he had become was THE Primeval Osmontian Marrow, and so bone by bone, weaving by weaving, Noah Osmont was rebuilt...entirely out of Primeval Osmontian Cells.","Not threaded with them. MADE of them! A body woven wholly from matter that was part Primeval and part him, from his skeleton to his blood to the seas of his Infinity and Source, and as the last of it knitted closed and his eyes opened within the vaulted dark of the White Steed...","He felt it immediately.","His Intent and his Osmontian Source Infinity felt unfathomably light, and unfathomably sharp!","Where his power had once moved through him like great oceans, heavy and vast, it now moved like drawn light! Every expression of his will arrived without friction, every thread of his Infinity answered before the asking finished, an existence rebuilt without a single seam of its old climbing, and Noah flexed one new hand slowly as stellar blue-gold light traced through fingers that had never existed until this moment!","|Welcome back, Master. THE Hepatarch of the Undying Root is exhausted. It cannot act again until its reserve regrows. Do not die twice.|","...!","He was reborn. And the door behind him was closed!","Noah rose through the vaulted dark, and looked out upon the war he had died in the middle of.","The five Organs he had seeded still budded, strong and defended, Adversity winding through Valor’s new lungs, Quintessence through Vigilance’s eyes, Mana through Obedience, Tyranny through Mercy, Harvest through Devotion, five mixed suns burning in colors this Dimension had never grown! Ruination’s strings webbed the spaces between them, cutting down every creeping filament of gray!","And at the center of everything, wrapped around the vast drumming Heart of Fealty, THE Infiniverse was already working on the Sixth Organ.","She blazed! Her full unfurled presense was pressed against the cursed Heart in tides of cerulean, realms condensed into radiance, a living Observable Existence grappling an ancient sentence with her entire self, holding ground she had held alone through the whole of her Master’s death, and Noah’s chest tightened around the sight of her, his loyal one, his home, fighting his war while his body was still being written!","Then the Curse sensed him.","And THE Gnawing Remembrance of Nhaglfarr-Ythok went mad.","The gray-black mass around the Heart convulsed as its awareness snapped across the vaulted dark to the figure it had killed, the figure it had spent four Organs’ worth of itself to kill, standing whole and new and burning quietly in the deep, and the shock that tore through the ancient sentence was a physical thing! The whole interior of Hvitrmarr shuddered with it! It had ended him. It had felt him end! And the ended thing was looking at it.","\" Yes ,\" Noah said. \" Me. \"","And he moved!","What followed was arduous, and it was glorious! Noah crossed the vaulted dark like a drawn blade as his new existence sang, and he fell upon the cursed Heart beside THE Infiniverse, his lightened Intent slicing into gray weavings that had shrugged off his old self’s oceans, his sharpened Infinity dissolving anchor after anchor, and the Sixth Organ’s unmaking, which had cost him a collapse before, unfolded now beneath hands that moved with rebuilt purity.","The Heart of Fealty came apart in careful folds as his blood poured into the hollow, marrow-seed taking root, and THE Prime Cause of Existence flowed down into the budding chambers to wind around THE First Cause of Fealty, a bond fused to being itself, a heart that would beat for another as irrevocably as it existed at all.","And through it, at last, Hvitrmarr herself continued to join the war.","The White Steed, still bearing the full agony of the Curse across her remaining Organs, still burning in the pain that had filled three thousand years, burned with valor! Her vast sovereignty pressed down upon her own cursed anatomy from without as Noah tore at it from within, Steed and Emperor working the same wound from both sides, and her ancient voice rolled through her own vaults, tight with pain and with purpose as she finally got the handle of what Noah was doing!","\" The Spine next. I will hold it still!\"","They cut!","The Spine of Honor came apart between her stillness and his edge as Paradox poured into the rebuilding column, honor fused with contradiction, a spine that could bear opposing weights without breaking!","HUUM!","The Bones of Endurance followed, her frame screaming as her own skeleton was unmade and regrown, Chaos winding through Endurance, persistence that renewed itself from raw potential!","And the Stomach of Temperance last, the furnace that had only ever consumed what duty required, and into its rebuilt chambers flowed THE Prime Cause of Apocalypse, transformative endings seated inside perfect restraint, destruction that would forever after be a tool held by discipline.","And with every Organ that fell and rose again...the Curse lost its anchors!","It ROARED!","The gray-black mass raged through the shrinking territory left to it, mad past all sentience, an ancient sentence watching its grammar torn out word by word, and it lashed and gnawed and burned, and found nothing left to hold!","Nine Organs. Nine budding mixtures of First Cause and Prime Cause. Not one single seat remaining for a curse that had ruled this existence.","And at that moment, Noah closed his eyes.","He floated at the center of the White Steed’s vaulted existence, and he sensed his Causes! All nine of them, no longer merely his, intermingled through nine ancient Organs with nine First Causes seated by the very hands of Those Who Remain!","Existence wound through Fealty. Paradox through Honor. Chaos through Endurance, Mana through Obedience, Quintessence through Vigilance, Adversity through Valor, Tyranny through Mercy, Harvest through Devotion, Apocalypse through Temperance!","Eighteen Causes in nine marriages, an anatomy that no maker and no framework had ever once contained, humming through the body of a First-lineage Steed, and every single one of them was waiting on his word!","His eyes opened, and they were endless blue.","Noah said quietly, to the raging, anchorless dark...","\" You have gnawed at Steeds for ages, and chewed hope out of an entire brood .\"","His voice did not rise, and the whole of two existences leaned into it.","\" But everything ends. And this existence is mine now, and yours ended the moment you killed me and I disagreed .\" His hand rose. \"It is time for you to go.\"","And using his Causes as engines...he turned everything on.","BOOM!","All nine Organs of the White Steed IGNITED at once! Nine mixed suns roared to full burn as Cause fed Cause fed Cause, Fealty’s new heart hammering, Valor’s new lungs drawing a breath the size of an era, Honor’s spine blazing down her colossal length, and from every Organ, from every marriage of First and Prime, endless blue light erupted and poured through the entirety of Hvitrmarr’s existence, flooding her vaults, her weavings, her scales, her three thousand years, one rising tide of living radiance that sought to cover everything!","—","<THE Creature>","Upon the ancient stretch of ice, beneath the falling snow, THE Creature and Anaximander had been watching grimly.","For the dark had nearly won! They had stood witness across the light-years-long split of existence as the obsidian half climbed past eighty percent, past ninety, the blue guttering down to threads, and neither of them had been able to intervene, for the war was inside a sovereignty neither could enter, and there is no watching in all of existence heavier than watching a friend’s light go out from the wrong side of a wall!","The blue had almost died. They had felt something end in there. Something vast.","And then, moments ago...the endless blue had risen!","It had come back up out of the black like a drowned dawn refusing the water, climbing, spreading, driving the obsidian before it, and now, across the frozen plains, the colossal form of the White Steed burned blue from horn to tail-tip, and at this moment...","Hvitrmarr raised her head.","Her great neck arched back against the snowing sky, her jaws opened wide, and she ROARED.","From her jaws, a pillar of murky obsidian light shot up! The whole gathered mass of the Curse, every gray-black thread of an ancient sentence torn from every Organ and every weaving, expelled in a single column that tore through the storm, and as it climbed, the pillar changed! The murk burned away along its length as white-blue light consumed it from below, obsidian becoming radiance becoming brilliance, and the pillar crossed upward across Gigaparsecs of the Dimension’s sky, a lance of transformation visible from unfathomable distances!","And it was...brilliant.","It was an endless white-blue of unfathomable Causes! Eighteen of them, First and Prime in nine marriages, announcing themselves through the expelled corpse of the thing that had chained them, the light of an existence that was living, fully, loudly, freely, and becoming free of its Curse before the eyes of the watching dark.","And alongside it, from the White Steed herself, an unfathomably pure aura of immensity erupted.","It rolled out across the frozen plains in a single sovereign wave, and Anaximander and THE Creature, an absence no framework could file and Existence itself mid-digestion toward Ananke, staggered! Their legs bent! The two of them had to grab each other’s shoulders, scholar gripping titan and titan gripping scholar, bracing against one another to make sure they did not kneel upon the ice!","For this was not even pressure. Pressure, they could have refused!","This was regality!","The unbroken authority of the First lineage, uncursed for the first time in three thousand years, seated now upon eighteen living Causes, the presense of a queen restored to what the living hands had originally made, and it did not demand that they kneel, it simply made kneeling feel like the oldest and most natural posture in existence!","The aura of regality...was too grand!"]},{"number":5531,"title":"Chapter 5531: Chapter 5530: Existence!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","The last thread of the Curse tore free of Hvitrmarr’s existence, and in the exact instant it left...Noah stretched that instant into infinity.","Everything froze.","The expelled obsidian hung motionless in its pillar far above. The endless blue paused mid-flood through nine reborn Organs! The falling snow beyond the White Steed’s frame stopped in the sky like scattered stars, and within the vaulted stillness of a frozen moment, THE True Human Emperor simply floated there, and sensed his existence.","He did not count. He did not calculate! For once, he only felt.","And in that frozen moment, two presences moved.","They were the only things in all the stillness permitted to move, for they were fused into the very self doing the stretching, and Ruination and THE Infiniverse came to him simultaneously, without a single word, and hugged him.","Ruination’s illusory form wrapped around him from one side, her strings folding over his shoulders like a mantle! THE Infiniverse pressed in from the other, her arms tight around the new body she had guarded the seeds of, her face buried against him, and neither of them said anything at all, because there was nothing to say that their grip was not already saying! He had died. They had watched, from inside his splitting halves, shielded by his ending, and no protocol and no composure in either of them had survived the memory of that silence!","Noah smiled softly.","He raised his new hands, and patted both of their heads.","\"I am sorry .\" His voice was quiet in the frozen vault. \"I will try everything humanly possible...to not have something like that happen again.\"","He did not promise it would never happen. They would have known the lie! He promised the trying, which was the only thing a Human could honestly promise, and the two of them heard the honesty inside it and hugged him tighter while nodding against him, crown and existence holding their Emperor in a moment stretched wide enough to hold all three!","And Noah smiled, and turned his senses inward, into the body that held them.","His new body!","Regrown from the Root with so much Primeval weaving that it hardly remembered what it had replaced, every bone and channel and sea woven from Primeval Osmontian Cells, and everything felt so unfathomably light! His will moved through himself without a single seam of resistance, thought arriving as action, intention arriving as fact!","And his Causes...","His Causes felt unfathomably grander!","All nine of them turned through his existence with a depth they had never carried, and he could feel WHY, for they were no longer only his! Each one was mixed now, married through nine reborn Organs to nine First Causes seated by the hands of Those Who Remain, and through those marriages, something was flowing back!","His Prime Cause of Existence carried a new note of sworn permanence from its union with Fealty! Adversity hummed with Valor’s charge-drawn breath! Tyranny had learned something from Mercy’s gentled claws, and Apocalypse from Temperance’s discipline, and all nine of them were visibly, actively undergoing a change, an evolution in slow glorious progress, growing grander with every moment they mingled with the First weavings of a Steed!","And when he looked at the whole of his existence together, he was shocked, as the prompts began.","|For enduring tremendous adversity, for dying within it and returning through it, and for completing what you began at the cost of everything: +25,000,000 Osmontian Biomass has been gained.|","...!","Twenty-five MILLION!","|All facets of your existence have been automatically upgraded to Rank B Ngetal . Osmontian Source Infinity aside, your Volume, your Output, your Trueness, and your Foundations now stand at the rank of reach and pervasion as their floor.|","| And above the floor, Master: your Second Foundation, THE Tide That Owes Nothing, your Intent, THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian, and your Osmontian Source Infinity have elevated to Rank A Idho . Near-permanence. Authority over endings. The rank your fused peak could only pretend toward, now standing as your base.|","|Your True Appendages have also been reborn alongside your body, and further elevated. THE Estuary Eye: Rank A Idho. THE Pinion Vigil: Rank A Idho. THE Hepatarch of the Undying Root: Rank A Idho, exhausted but grander for its work. THE Primeval Osmontian Marrow: Rank A Idho. THE Amaranthine Heart, THE Circlet, THE Quintessential Pantheon of THE Infiniverse: Rank A Idho. All of them stand at the rank of Yew, Master. Every instrument you carry is now an authority over endings.|","|For reference, as you will ask: elevation to Rank S Ebad is priced at 100,000,000 Osmontian Biomass per facet. The trembling shield-tree does not come cheaply. Reserves currently stand above 25,500,000.|","...!","Prompts of majesty and wonder pulsed!","Noah floated in the stretched stillness with his crown and his Observable Existence in his arms, and took all of it in, and for a long moment of the infinite moment, he simply...reflected.","He had died. He had stood in a sea of his own dead and been asked the question that every ruler owes and almost none ever answer, and he had answered it honestly. He had felt fear, and it had not broken him. He had felt doubt, and climbed through it!","The Root that saved him was spent. The door behind him was closed, and death, for the first time in his existence, was again a thing with consequences.","And somehow, that made all of it heavier, and all of it brighter at once! To climb without a net was simply...to be Human again. He had asked, once, on a golden island, whether immortality violated being human.","Existence, apparently, had heard the question.","And it was amidst this reflection that the prompts returned, and their tone had changed.","|Master. THE Tide That Owes Nothing has been triggered at Rank A Idho for the first time.|","|The Tide has weighed what you have done. You have undertaken a tremendous act of giving: you have cleansed the Curse of a Steed whose lineage stems from Those Who Remain, at the price of your own death. You gave existence itself back to a dying Steed of the First Clutch of makers, and the Tide does not permit such giving to flow one way.|","|An Unfathomable wonder of unknown origins will be paid through this act of giving.|","...!","The moment the prompts finished...","CRACK!","Noah’s stretched moment of infinity shattered.","Time slammed back into motion around him, snow falling, blue flooding, the pillar climbing, and in the same heartbeat he felt something squeeze into existence directly above his palms, fold itself out of nothing with a small, dense, impossibly quiet weight, and drop into his hands.","It was...a simple white egg.","\"...\"","Noah stared at it.","There were no flashy lights! There were no terrifying bursts of power, no detonating skies, no light-years of split heavens announcing a boon’s arrival! The grandest Foundation he possessed, at the rank of authority over endings, triggered by an act of giving priced at his own death, had produced...a smooth, palm-sized, perfectly white egg, sitting in his hands.","| You have gained ?????.|","\"... \"","Even Ruination’s prompt had nothing else to offer! Five question marks, from the existence that had catalogued Curses of Those Who Remain and Character Sheets of Steeds, and the egg simply sat there, white and warm and silent, explaining absolutely nothing!","Noah’s eyes became heavy as he looked at it.","An unfathomable wonder of unknown origins. Unknown even to the Regard, unknown even to her! He turned it once in his fingers, felt nothing but smooth warmth and a faint, patient density, like something very large practicing being very small...and he put it away, deep into his stores, beside the Primeval limb and the Marrowbane Fruit and every other loaded thing he owned.","Because they were still within the body of Hvitrmarr.","And in front of them, the vaulted white-flame dark was gathering itself into a shape.","Light condensed! White flame drew inward from the reborn vaults, folding and slimming and settling, and a humanoid manifestation of Hvitrmarr formed before them!","She stood tall and straight-backed, robed in layered white that fell like fresh snowfall given tailoring, and her terrifying, regal beauty struck the vault silent. Hair of white flame poured down her back, still faintly burning without fuel or end! Twin slender curves of translucent ivory swept back from her temples, the ghost-echo of her horns, and her face was ageless and cold and heartbreakingly fine, the face of a queen carved by makers who had never once intended for it to know suffering! And her eyes, gold, ring within ring within ring, rested upon Noah and upon THE Infiniverse.","She was trying to show them nothing.","And Noah saw everything she was hiding! The happiness, three thousand years overdue, trembling at the very edges of that composed cold face. The hope, no longer punished, no longer priced, burning quietly in the rings of her eyes for the first time without agony answering it. The relief, vast as her true body, held back behind regal stillness because a queen of the First lineage did not weep in front of guests, and every nanosecond of her not-weeping was visibly, gloriously costing her!","She looked at them both for a long moment.","Then Hvitrmarr, First of her lineage in three thousand years to stand uncursed, gave them a light bow.","\"I owe you...existence.\"","....!"]},{"number":5532,"title":"Chapter 5532: Chapter 5531: Fledgling!","paragraphs":["\"I indeed owe you Everything. \"","Hvitrmarr’s manifestation straightened from her bow, and her ring-in-ring eyes had already hardened back into a queen’s.","\" Which is why we have to go. Right now. So that I can ensure your safety, because...Jarl Skallagrim, a Cursed Descendant, is here, and even I cannot stand against him.\"","...!","They were already here?","\"I could not leave this Dimension before. The Curse chained every Steed to THE Krazhor-Nul, a fence around the livestock, and running only ever meant running in circles inside it .\"","\" But with the Curse gone...I am free to do so. I will be taking us away from THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension itself.\"","Away from the Dimension! Out past its walls, beyond the reach of Jarls and hosts and dying colossi, through the dark between Dimensions.","And Noah’s gaze became heavy.","\" Not yet.\"","...!","The word landed in the vault with the full weight of his immensity, an Emperor’s refusal spoken to a Steed offering salvation, and he continued before it could be argued!","\" Make sure to take THE Creature and Anaximander outside...as well as Ryaenara!\" His hands were already moving, waving through the white-flame dark as his newly risen Intent poured outward.","\" This is her, and what I can emulate of her weavings of existence. Can you locate her before leaving?\"","Light bloomed between his palms.","An image of Ryaenara unfurled across the vault, vibrant and loose-grinned and profane even in still light, and around the image, Noah emulated everything he held of her! The texture of her Antiquity, older than the Scales! The signature of her weavings as his Estuary and every record of every shared battlefield reconstructed her presense thread by thread, an existence sketched from memory by an authority over endings.","He had made a choice, and the choice was simple.","He was not leaving Ryaenara behind.","Not in a Dimension with Cursed Descendants and other monstrosities!","Hvitrmarr looked at the image for a long moment, somber, and the Causes inside her pulsed. Nine reborn suns turning faster, Fealty’s new heart drumming through the vault, and when she spoke, there was something old and careful in it.","\" To locate one thread across a Dimension this vast, while outrunning what hunts us...I will need to express my full power.\" Her golden eyes rose to his. \" And to express my full power, I will need...someone to ride me.\"","...!","What?","Noah blinked once.","Right! She was a Steed.","A living Observable Existence built, at the level of her deepest architecture, around carrying! Nine Organs that tilted towards virtue, Fealty and Obedience and Devotion, an entire anatomy of virtues that all pointed at a saddle, and for three thousand cursed years, that architecture had been chained to thrones and whips, and never once completed by a willing seat!","Noah looked at her with shining eyes, and spoke grandly.","\"I will ride you. Let’s go.\"","...!","The manifestation of Hvitrmarr nodded once, and everything moved.","The vault folded. Noah saw THE Creature and Anaximander pulled into this space in streaks of obsidian and white, the golden island he had left outside drawn in whole alongside them, sands and forges and all, swallowed into the sovereign interior of the White Steed for safekeeping. And his own body was pulled the opposite way, drawn up across the inner vaults of her chest, past the drumming new Heart of Fealty, up through parting scales as he found himself pulled toward the back of this grand Steed.","Ivory plates unsealed above him. Cold sweet air poured in.","And Noah emerged into the open sky of the ancient ice.","The snowy landscape stretched below in every direction, glacial plains glowing faintly blue with the residue of the war just won, snow still falling in slow silver veils, and his body rose through it all in her grip of white light before settling, gently, deliberately, upon the back of The White Steed.","The moment he did...","HUUUM!","The entire Dimension seemed to bear witness.","The ambient storms of THE Krazhor-Nul stilled across the horizon. The falling snow hung! The strings of Infinity and Primordial Source and even THE Lingering Word itself all seemed to turn, in one vast attending hush, toward the ancient ice where, for the first time since the makers walked, a Steed of the First lineage was mounted by a willing, chosen, uncursed rider, and even Noah, crowned and reborn, was astonished.","For the instant he settled upon her scales, he felt it!","An immense, unfathomable strengthening of his existence!","| You are the first non-Descendant of Nhaglfarr-Ythok, THE Sleepless Fiend of Those Who Remain, to ride one of the Steeds born of his ingenuity. The Steeds were his design. His craft and his cruelty both. Their saddles were cut for his bloodline alone, and for ages beyond counting, only Cursed Descendants have ever sat where you are sitting. The architecture of the First lineage has weighed you, and it has chosen to recognize your seat as sworn, not stolen.|","| Designation gained: THE Fledgling Liege of the First Lineage. This is the beginner’s distinction of a rider of these Steeds. The word Fledgling is doing heavy work in that title. What sits above it returns only ?????.|","|Starter boons of THE Fledgling Liege, cataloged:|","| THE Bond of Seat and Sworn . A permanent channel now runs between rider and Steed. Thought passes without words across any distance. Senses may be borrowed: her sight that reads weavings within weavings, her sovereignty-sense that tastes Dimensional law. And the reservoirs of both existences now stand open to one another: you may draw upon the power of her eighteen Causes, and she upon your seas. Two existences, one account.|","| THE Anchored Seat. Nothing unseats you. No velocity, no force, no authority tears you from her back while the bond stands: your position is now a fact of existence rather than a matter of grip. Her element cannot harm you, her white flame recognizing you as its own, and within the reach of her sovereignty, hostile environments, void, pressure, and essence are refused on your behalf.|","| THE Regal Mantle . You passively radiate the presence of the First lineage while seated. Lesser existences will find that their instincts developed opinions about you before their minds were consulted.|","| THE Boundless Crossing . The First Steeds were built for one purpose above all others: to carry riders across the dark between Dimensions . It is what her ancestor did with the maker whose weight bent the crossing. It is what her blood has remembered through every cursed generation. While you ride her, Dimensional Traversal is no longer an ordeal. Walls between Dimensions become doors. Doors become a stride. The roads between many Dimensions are mapped in her inherited memories, Master...and you now hold the map.|","| Deeper functions of the bond remain sealed behind the Fledgling distinction. They return ?????, and they are many.|","...!","Prompts of majesty upon majesty bloomed.","But the prompts were only words, and what Noah FELT beneath them was beyond any cataloging!","For the bond was open, and existence was flowing both ways.","His Osmontian Source Infinity poured down through his seat into her, oceans of newly-risen A-Rank sea rolling through her vast frame, and he felt her drink it the way parched roots drink rain, felt his Infinity spread through eighteen Causes and set every one of them blazing brighter! His Intent flowed with it, THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian sinking into her weavings, and her whole colossal existence answered his identity, aligning to it, the way a blade aligns to the hand it was forged for!","And back up through the bond...she flowed into him.","Her Causes came first, eighteen of them, First and Prime, their mingled truths washing up through his seat and into his own nine, feeding the slow grand evolution already underway! He felt Fealty’s permanence and Valor’s drawn breath, Endurance’s tirelessness and Devotion’s lift, virtues older than the Scales pouring through a Human body.","And then her Intent arrived.","And Noah’s existence pulsed.","For her Intent, the Intent seated in her First-lineage architecture by the living hands of Those Who Remain, flowed into him, and it did not taste of Ananke.","It sat above Ananke!","Autarkis!","Above inevitability! Above \"I must be obeyed\"! A third texture, vast and quiet and prior, the very thing he had felt once as a door beyond a door when his own Intent crowned itself, and here it was, flowing through his seat in living rivers, and through the bond he felt her feel his shock, and felt something almost like an ancient, tired smile move through the mountain beneath him!","’ Later ,’ her thought came, the first words ever spoken through their bond. ’ Ride now. Learn later.’","And Hvitrmarr stretched her wings.","The great white sails of Devotion-and-Harvest spread across the snowing sky, wider than horizons, and as they reached their full glorious span, a pillar of white and blue light shot up all around them.","Sovereignty and Infinity braided into a single rising column, rider and Steed announced together to nearby corners of an ancient Dimension, and the frozen plains below turned to a sea of glittering light!","And at this time...","In the far distance, a throne stopped dead in the sky.","Jarl Skallagrim and his eight Steeds stared ahead at the rising pillar with utter incredulity, and their bodies trembled!","Every one of them! The eight dying colossi in their harness shook in their chains, ancient eyes stretched wide, terminal frames quaking, because their senses were all reporting the same impossible absence! From the white queen at the heart of that distant light, there was no sign of the Curse!","None! Not a thread! Not a whisper of the gnawing that had defined every Steed’s every nanosecond since the sentence was first spoken.","She found a solution.","She actually found a SOLUTION!","Three thousand years of watching, a millennium of Skallagrim’s patient study, ages of an entire Dimension’s certainty, all of it detonated in a single sensing, and then, slowly, terribly, eight pairs of dying eyes and one pair of lucid rotting ones moved from the queen...","To the man atop her.","To the rider!","And all their eyes blazed with immense greed! The eight Steeds’ hope-rejuvenated gazes locked onto the small crowned figure seated upon the uncursed Steed with the ravenous focus of the drowning sighting shore, and Jarl Skallagrim’s terribly sane eyes fixed upon Noah with the weavings of a man with a few years left staring at the being who dispensed more.","The possibility-weavings in his palm churned into a blur.","And Jarl Skallagrim bellowed out madly, lucidity and desperation fused into one Dimension-shaking roar, as for countless gigaparsecs in every direction...","All skies turned black!"]},{"number":5533,"title":"Chapter 5533: Chapter 5532: Dimensionlapse!","paragraphs":["Riding was a sensation Noah had to adapt to.","Not the seat. The seat was effortless, anchored by boons into a fact of existence! What required adapting was everything flowing through the seat, the drumming of a Fealty-heart the size of a realm beneath him, the tidal rhythm of Valor’s lungs, eighteen mixing Causes turning under his palms like an engine of virtues, and his own seas pouring down into all of it while her ancient rivers poured back up.","Two existences breathing in each other’s rhythm, and every breath of it settling deeper! It felt far, far too intimate than he expected.","And with his reformed body, reborn light and sharp from the Root, in addition to this ridiculous empowerment that came from mounting Hvitrmarr...Noah was able to very clearly sense the power that made this Steed want to run away.","His gaze rose across the blackened gigaparsecs.","And he looked upon the maddened figure of the Cursed Descendant.","Jarl Skallagrim burned against his own darkened skies, titanic and rotting and terribly awake, carried forward on his throne by eight dying Steeds whose eyes were all fixed on Noah, and from that distant lucid figure rolled a power that pressed against Noah’s newly-risen senses with a texture he had never once encountered.","It was terrifying enough to give a sense of hopelessness.","Even now! Even at A-Rank Idho, even seated on a First-lineage Steed, even twenty-five million strong, the presense of the thing on that throne registered in his weavings as something his frameworks simply could not hold! It did not belong to the Fifth Scale. It did not belong to the Sixth! It did not belong to ANY Scale, and Noah realized, with the cold clarity of a man updating his maps mid-journey, that he would need to find entirely new rankings of power outside of Vakochev’s Scales altogether, because...damn.","If Hvitrmarr, uncursed and eighteen-Caused and sovereign, still chose to run away from this monstrous thing...","Then they ran.","\" Go.\"","Noah whispered it calmly while clasping the scale of Hvitrmarr below him, and in the next second, he and the massive White Steed beneath him turned their gazes across the dark, glared coldly at Jarl Skallagrim, rider and mount delivering one shared look of unhurried, imperial promise...","And disappeared!","The white-blue pillar collapsed inward on the empty ice, and where a queen and her Liege had stood, there was only falling snow!","And Jarl Skallagrim glared forth madly!","His rotting face twisted around its terrible lucidity as he rose from his throne, and he WHIPPED the reins of cursed lightning, and eight rejuvenated Steeds screamed against their harness and tore forward through the blackened sky, an entire hateful cluster hurling itself after the vanished point of its salvation as the chase began in earnest!","—","In this snowy area, upon the emptied ice where two impossible things had just departed, a golden cloud drifted down through the falling silence, and upon it stood a shocked old woman.","THE Recorder of Wilds stared at the point where Noah and Hvitrmarr had just been, and her ancient eyes were shining.","\" Who is he to actually dare to reverse an action of one of Those Who Remain? Does he even know what he just did?\" Her voice was hushed, and for once, it was not narrating.","\" And more than that...a Cure for the Curse of this Cursed Dimension! This...how does this affect things...\"","She had been speaking to herself when, in the next moment, the ice shook.","She turned.","And behind her, descending through the storm on legs like dying mountain ranges, was the Steed of Oblivion!","Ghrimhest’s colossal gray frame filled the snowing sky, chains screaming, its guttering eyes stretched wide and fixed on the horizon where the pillar had stood, and shockingly, atop the burden-bearer’s vast back, small against its enormity and burning with desperate power...","Was Jarl Erling.","The dying titan himself as he had seen the failure of his party through Ghrimhest’s senses, and he had used whatever unique power his Steed possessed to cross the Dimension himself! Now that he knew another Jarl was involved, there was no need for secrecy! The race was naked, and the prize was fleeing, and his titanic bronze face was filled with such regret and such pain that it had cracked new fissures beside the crimson ones.","He may have even missed out! The cure had been here, and Jarl Erling roared with everything his remaining years could carry!","\" GO! GO GO! CATCH UP TO THEM!\"","The Steed of Oblivion bellowed, and the mountain-frame surged forward through the storm, keeper and burden-bearer tearing off after the same vanished point as the Jarl before them, and THE Recorder of Wilds stood upon her cloud and watched them go, and slowly shook her head.","A Steed that was no longer cursed. So long as the fleeing ones were not stupid, they should not be caught.","They would be far from this Dimension soon. And the pursuit? It was impossible for the Cursed Steeds to leave this Dimension, fenced by the sentence itself. And for the Cursed Descendants, leaving was merely...hard. Not impossible, just very hard!","And more than hard, it was priced.","For she knew what few remaining beings knew. One of the promises made to the Descendants for their sin was this: if they left this Dimension, they would have no chance of Salvation from their curse. The fence around the bloodline was not a wall. It was a wager! Stay, and hope. Leave, and be certain! And so for ages, dying generation after dying generation had stayed, orbiting the faint promise like moths deciding the lamp was a dawn.","\" Mm. And now the dawn has run off, \" the old woman murmured. \" Words should be handled with the same care as eggs, but I will say this much. Among all the Descendants of all of Those Who Remain, the ones seeded under THE Sleepless Fiend have always hated their ancestor the most...\"","But as the Recorder was thinking all this, in the next moment...she was surprised.","For off to the side, another aura arrived.","It did not creep, and it did not announce! It was simply there, seated into the storm as if it had always been part of the weather, and it looked straight at her, through every fold of unsensability she wore, and the old woman felt the rare, almost nostalgic pleasure of being seen...","And she smiled.","Out of the billowing snow walked a titan.","He was massive, a gorilla-like humanoid whose shoulders moved like hills deciding to travel, his whole vast body draped in fur of pure obsidian that drank the storm-light and gave back none of it! Waves of majesty rolled off of him with every unhurried step, the pressure of something earlier than frameworks, and in one enormous hand he carried a black bow taller than True Lifeforms, its limbs burning along their length with a low, patient fire, and any being with the senses to read that flame would have understood instantly that it could scorch and melt Ananke Intent effortlessly, the way morning melts frost!","A Primeval One.","The titan’s deep-set eyes swept once across the emptied ice, across the residue of the pillar, and settled on the old woman upon her cloud, and he nodded.","\" Recorder .\" His voice was the sound of a mountain being courteous. \"I have been waiting for you. Though I did not expect to find you at the scene of an incident. \"","His gaze moved to the horizon where two hunts had vanished. \" Did you see what happened here?\"","The Recorder smiled at this.","\"I saw. But that is the second thing I will talk about, as the first thing, the one that brought many of us to this Dimension, has to be discussed before it.\" She settled her sleeves, ancient eyes twinkling. \" Haha, where are the other Primevals? O, Doku?\"","Doku, the obsidian archer, rolled his vast shoulders.","\" The others are meeting with the Jarls. The ones who still have many years left to live, and thus still have manners left to spend.\" His deep voice carried a plain, unhidden distaste.","\" But I do not really agree with our approach here. Just because Cursed Descendants are easier to deal with...does not mean we have to work with them. There are countless possibilities out there. We are reaching for the nearest branch and calling it the best fruit.\"","The Recorder smiled wider.","\" And yet we are here .\" She poured herself tea without hurry, the storm bending politely around the ritual. \" Because someone, and we still have not figured out the culprit, mind you, someone is causing Dimensionlapses across many nearby Dimensions. Pitting different forces into war as separate Dimensions begin fusing into each other! The many Dimensions we hold are being threatened. So here we are, in a cursed backwater older than the Scales, seeking any point of knowledge and cooperation we can find.\"","Her wrinkled eyes gleamed over the rim of her cup. \" Haha, and what do I find in this place? Someone curing a Curse of THE Sleepless Fiend!\"","...!","Doku heard this, and his deep-set eyes shone!","The black bow’s fire flared along its limbs as the obsidian titan leaned toward her, majesty rippling off him in eager waves.","\" What? We can use that for our own aims!\" His voice dropped into the register of strategy. \" Who? Which Descendant figured out the cure? Or was it one of us?\"","...!","The Recorder blinked.","For perhaps the first time in several eras, the old woman who had a narration for everything did not quite know how to answer, and her teacup hovered, and her expression folded into something genuinely conflicted.","\" Well ...\" she said slowly. \" They are neither Primevals nor Descendants...\"","...!","Doku straightened to his full titanic height, the storm parting around his shoulders, genuine surprise moving through his ancient face.","\" Then who could they possibly be?\"","At this question, The Recorder only smiled, and looked out to where a certain Steed had disappeared.","The snow in this region had turned into a billowing storm, white veils folding over the emptied ice in slow colossal waves. And through all of it, if one only looked closely, the snowflakes themselves were pulsing. Each falling flake carried a silent blue-white light, faint and patient and new, the light of Causes mixing together for the first time in existence...","Still prevalent."]},{"number":5534,"title":"Chapter 5534: Chapter 5533: Breathe!","paragraphs":["They found Ryaenara in a sea of poison.","The chase had torn across the Dimension in folds of white-blue light, Hvitrmarr’s inherited might swallowing gigaparsecs between wingbeats, and through the bond, Noah felt the moment her borrowed senses and his emulated weavings finally triangulated on a single vibrant thread, burning loose and profane and utterly alive at the heart of a region drowned in verdant miasma.","Ryaenara!","The poisoned expanse opened below them, an ocean of green-gold murk where toxin had replaced weather, and at its center, the Antiquity was fighting! Her radiant figure wove through collapsing structures of venom as her opponent filled the horizon behind her, a Cenozoic True Lifeform in the shape of a massive verdant frog, mountainous and glistening, its throat-sac swelling with lakes of miasma, its bulbous eyes tracking her with the patient hunger of a creature that had dissolved everything it had ever met.","And Hvitrmarr did not slow.","She descended upon the region like a verdict, and her Intent ERUPTED!","THE Autarkis Intent!","It poured off her body in a sovereignty that sat above inevitability itself, the third order, the texture past the door, and as it flooded the poisoned sky, Hvitrmarr’s claw extended! The Claws of Mercy-and-Tyranny reached down and out, talons of white flame stretching until they seemingly covered light years, five curved horizons of burning ivory descending over the frog’s entire existence, and before the Cenozoic True Lifeform could so much as swell its throat...","The claw crashed onto it.","There was no battle! There was not even an exchange! The verdant titan’s Ananke-grade Intent collapsed instantly beneath the touch of an order it could not argue with, its Trueness caving inward alongside it, the seamless \"I am\" of a Cenozoic apex crumpling like wet parchment under a mountain, and the massive frog was driven down into its own miasma, unmade of everything that had made it mighty, in a single descending motion!","\"...!\"","And in the same motion, light wrapped around Ryaenara.","The Antiquity froze inside the gentle white cocoon, and her wide eyes found the colossal White Steed above her, and then the small crowned figure seated upon its back, and the look on her face was pure, spectacular incredulity. Osmont. Riding a monstrosity of wonder!","\" Come !\" Noah called down grandly.","And Ryaenara disappeared into Hvitrmarr’s chest!","And in this fraction of an instant, in the sliver of time it took to do this one action...behind them, all of existence changed.","Noah felt it through every Cause he owned, and turned.","The Dimension itself was transforming.","For gigaparsecs behind them, everything, the storms, the strings of Infinity and Primordial Source, the drowned green horizon, the very dark between all of it, was becoming a hand.","Not covered by a hand. BECOMING one! An obsidian hand of Jarl Skallagrim, assembled out of existence itself, storm-fronts folding into finger-joints, light-years of sky hardening into obsidian knuckles, the ambient essence of an entire region converted wholesale into palm and grasp, and from its closing curl came a suction force so terrifying that the poisoned ocean below rose whole off the land and streamed toward it, that distance itself leaned backward into the grip, a horrific phenomenon that rewrote the simple concept of \"behind them\" into a single word.","Caught.","\" OOOOH !\"","Noah bellowed out as he grasped onto Hvitrmarr’s scales tightly, his A-Rank seas slamming down through the bond, and he and Hvitrmarr both roared as one! Her nine Organs churned! Fealty’s heart hammered into a war-drum, Valor’s lungs drew a breath the size of the sky, and his Nine Prime Causes spun into her 9 like engines coupling at full burn, two existences igniting every joined Cause they shared against the pull of a grasping Dimension!","And gloriously, the truth revealed itself.","Hvitrmarr had already begun slipping across Dimensions the moment she acted to bring Ryaenara in! The catch and the crossing had been one maneuver, started before the hand ever formed, her First-lineage blood threading them into the gaps between the Dimension’s weavings even as her claw was still descending, and they were only completing the action now.","This...was the only reason they were not caught.","The obsidian fingers closed.","And in the next instant, rider and Steed turned into pure white-blue light!","The radiance pulled away from the obsidian hand like a thread drawn out of a closing fist, phasing into the gaps of this Dimension, between its strings, beneath its laws, and OUT of it entirely, and against a suction that had swallowed a poisoned sea, the light of Noah and Hvitrmarr...","Disappeared!","The obsidian hand closed on nothing.","Gigaparsecs of converted existence clenched around an absence, and slowly, the vast fingers dissolved back into storm and string and dark, and at the center of the unraveling, a titanic figure manifested upon the emptied sky.","Jarl Skallagrim had risen from his throne to arrive here first.","He had outrun his own harness. He had spent power that his two remaining years could not afford, converted a region of an ancient Dimension into his own grasp, and he floated now in the miasma-tainted silence, staring at the point where his salvation had phased out of existence, and his rotting face was very, very calm.","Behind him, the Steeds arrived.","The eight of them tore into the region dragging his empty throne, and the moment their senses swept the emptiness, they began to howl.","Long, cracking, terminal howls of pain, for the uncursed one was gone, the proof was gone, the first new hope in years had left the Dimension they could never leave, and their dying Causes screamed the loss through every chained channel!","Jarl Skallagrim floated coldly amid the howling.","Then he reached out, and grasped one of the eight.","His obsidian hand, the small one, the merely titanic one, closed around the nearest Steed’s neck-ridge, and he began to calmly and brutally tear it apart.","SQUELCH!","There was no fury in the motion.","He worked with the unhurried thoroughness of a man taking down a tent, peeling the dying colossus open along its chained weavings as it screamed, its terminal Causes guttering out one by one in his grip, and the other seven Steeds watched in absolute frozen fear, howls strangled into silence, an entire harness learning in real time what their keeper’s calm was worth!","\" Do you know what that was? \" Jarl Skallagrim asked, conversationally, to the thing coming apart in his hands.","\" That was the answer. I chose lucidity in the dark while my brothers drowned themselves in feasts, I waited for her to MOVE, and she moved, and the answer walked into this Dimension and cured her and sat upon her back.\" The Steed’s last Cause guttered. He let the ruin drift.","\"And because you were so useless...such a chance disappeared.\"","He looked at the seven remaining, and they did not meet his eyes.","\" The promise says that those who leave are abandoned by Salvation .\" His fissures glowed dull red as he turned toward the far dark, toward the direction of a departure only he had been close enough to taste.","\" But Salvation has left first. The promise is now a fence around an empty field .\" He stepped back onto his throne, and took up the reins of cursed lightning. \" So now...I have to leave this Dimension. And find them.\"","...!","—","<THE Krazhor-Nul>","The ancient Dimension, for its part, barely noticed any of the wonders that just occured.","Across all their battles and forges and feasts and cure, Noah and THE Creature and Ryaenara had only ever been moving around its periphery. The outer shell of THE Krazhor-Nul! The thin cold rind of an existence that predated the Scales, where lone Jarls kept lone mountains and lone Steeds walked out their sentences.","Deeper in, the Dimension was inhabited.","Deeper in, whole clans of Cursed Descendants held courts across continental thrones, generations of the bloodlines of Those Who Remain living and scheming and dying on schedule.","Deeper in, broods of Steeds beyond counting walked their burdens across lands no outsider had ever mapped, and deeper still, in halls older than the sentence itself, some of those Clans were, at this very moment, meeting with Primeval Ones, ancient guests speaking carefully of fusing Dimensions and fusing borders.","And somw of the most powerful beings in those depths had sensed something, when a certain pivotal event took place upon the periphery. A pillar of obsidian turning white-blue. A texture of Causes mixing that existence had never once tasted!","So far, only two Jarls and two Primevals knew exactly what had occurred, and just what had appeared.","Only two, and two.","How long would it take before more than two Jarls knew?","And what would all those Cursed do...when they learned there was a Panacea in existence that could cure them of their misery?","What indeed!","---","<THE True Human Emperor>","For the first time in what felt like several lifetimes, Noah breathed easy.","He sat upon the back of Hvitrmarr as she crossed the region between Dimensions and Time, her great wings beating in long unhurried strokes through a dark that was not darkness.","The foam boiled at the finest scales, possibility frothing in and out of definition wherever his attention was not pressing! The strings ran everywhere, undressed of matter and law, vibrating their sustained notes in directions that were neither ahead nor behind.","And in the far unmeasurable distances hung the membranes, vast sheets of Dimensions drifting through the black like islands through an ocean, each one wearing the dark around its shores.","The last time he had crossed this place, he had done it inside a vessel, wrapped in his Pantheon’s stanchions, reading the grammar of the deep like a passenger pressed to a window.","Now he rode through it on the back of a queen, and the dark parted for her like it remembered her lineage.","And Noah, breathing easy, reflected seriously.","The Cursed Descendant. Jarl Skallagrim!","He turned the memory of that power over. It had not been a gap of ranks. It had been a gap of categories! His A-Rank Idho facets, his twenty-five millions, his reborn body of Primeval Cells, all of it had not been much! To stand against something like that, he would need more than elevation. He would need power that lived far, far outside the Scales entirely, the way the Descendants did, the way her Autarkis order did.","And his Estuary Eye, his own Anchor, had led him straight into such a terrifying place.","If he used an analogy from his homeworld...it was like he had been a level 10 being who confidently opened a door and arrived in a zone filled with beings at level 100 and above! THE Krazhor-Nul had been, by every honest measure, out of his depth. He had been a bit weak for it!","And walking out of a zone like that alive, let alone walking out with a First-lineage Steed beneath him and a cure to his name, was a terrifying boon that he intended to respect properly.","Especially because of what the boon made possible.","It had now become unfathomably easy to cross from one Dimension to another! The roads were mapped in the blood beneath his seat, walls had become doors, and entire unknown zones of existence sat one stride away in every direction...","And he purposefully chose not to take a single one of them yet.","He just wanted to breathe for a moment.","’ You are quiet.’ Her voice came through the bond, a warm ancient current beneath his seat.","\"I am thinking .\" Noah said aloud, smiling slightly.","\" Mm. You gave me back my existence before you ever knew my full name, \" Her wingbeats slowed into ceremony. \"I am Hvitrmarr, a Remnant Dimension Steed. A Progeny of the Cursed Mounts of Those Who Remain, specifically...THE Sleepless Fiend. The last unbroken thread of the First lineage his living hands seated.\"","\"...\"","\" And you must understand what follows you out .\" Her voice lowered. \" You have seen two Jarls. THE Krazhor-Nul holds many. Many across its depths, each with its Clan, its harness, its experiments, and its expiration date. Some have a million years left and fear nothing yet. Some have less than a decade and fear everything. And every single one of them, from the patient to the desperate, wants exactly one thing more than they want their next breath. \"","Her great head turned slightly, one gold eye finding him across her own horizon.","\" The moment they find out what you can do, they will not send parties to capture merchandise. They will come themselves, as Erling came, as Skallagrim comes. They will seek to utilize you first, politely, richly, with every treasure their ages have hoarded. And when you refuse, or when you are too slow, or when two of them want you at once...they will seek to break you. They will do everything in their power, everything, to tear the cure out of you, because you are no longer a being to them, rider. You are the answer to the only question their entire civilization has ever asked.\"","The dark between Dimensions flowed past in silence for a moment.","\"I sensed hope, and I ran toward it, and I pulled you into the center of all of that .\" Her ancient voice carried guilt.","\"I feel as though I have doomed you. I reached for my salvation and hung a mark upon your existence that many dying tyrants will now hunt across all the Dimensions.\"","And Noah smiled.","He leaned forward and set his palm flat against her scales, warm ancient ivory under a reborn hand, and his voice came easy and certain.","\"I made my own choices. Every one of them.\" He patted the scale once. \" I chose to fly toward your Cause when running was free. I chose to put my hands on a Curse. I chose to step inside, and I chose to keep going after it killed me once. None of this is your fault. You did not doom me.\"","\"...\"","\" And since we are doing introductions properly.\" He straightened upon his seat, and the dark itself seemed to attend. \"I am Noah Osmont. THE Quintessential Osmontian. THE True Human Emperor.\" His eyes gleamed.","\"I am still gradually forming the vision of what I want to do. But its shape is coming, and every version of it helps me gain more power. And with more power...I can defend what is mine against monstrous threats like the Jarls, instead of running from them.\"","Hvitrmarr’s Organs pulsed beneath him.","\" Then I vow it here, in the dark between all things .\" Her voice rang with the immensity of the Spine of Honor itself. \" Whatever that vision requires of me, I will do anything to aid in it.\"","Noah nodded.","\" Good. Because as THE True Human Emperor...I may have to spread my rule across all Dimensions. And across Time.\"","\"...!\"","\" All that is Human, wherever it stands, whenever it stands.\"","HUUM!","Hvitrmarr did not flinch from the size of it! Her wings spread wider across the frothing dark, and her vow came back level and absolute.","\" Then I will take you to every Dimension you need. Many are mapped in my lineage, and they are yours now. You need only say where.\" Her voice settled into something older than the formality.","\"I will repay the debt of my curse however I can, for however long the repaying takes.\"","Noah’s eyes shined brightly at this, and he nodded!","And in the next moment, he sent his thoughts down through the bond, and an instant later...","WAP!","THE Creature, Anaximander, and Ryaenara appeared upon the back of Hvitrmarr!","A white platform formed below the three of them the moment they arrived, a disc of pale sovereign light holding them just above her scales, for they were not considered to be riding Hvitrmarr, and by every law of the saddle and the lineage, they shouldn’t be able to!","Shouldn’t.","But who knew what monsters like Anaximander were capable of? The scholar was already looking down at the white platform beneath his feet with the mild, curious expression.","Ryaenara’s gaze swept from the naked strings of the dark, to the colossal uncursed queen beneath her, to the crowned figure seated at the head of it all.","And Noah looked at all of them as he wanted to hear their input!"]},{"number":5535,"title":"Chapter 5535: Chapter 5534: Trials! I","paragraphs":["<THE Creature>","Upon a white platform on the back of a Steed, in the dark between all Dimensions, Existence itself watched a Human, and marveled in silence.","THE Creature’s obsidian flames burned low and even as his gaze rested on THE Youngest. On the crowned figure seated at the head of a grand lifeform, speaking easily with his companions. On the being who had, in the span of one Dimension, undergone tremendous change.","The Youngest had pulled far ahead. At this moment, seated on that Steed, he should be...a bit more powerful than him.","\"...\"","THE Creature looked down at his own hands.","Obsidian fingers, threaded now with white-gold from the Primeval tail at his back. Hands that had carried eras. Hands that had never once, in all the long bearing, felt like they were holding less than they should.","And yet.","What was this, sitting in him now? This sense of falling behind? Of being...slow? He turned the feeling over carefully, because it was unfamiliar. He had never been one who felt weaker. He had never felt inadequate! He had not known such emotions even existed within him, and he would have said, if asked, that they did not, for he had made a practice across his existence of giving away many of his Everythings and regenerating them afterward, his Everything of Fear, his Everything of Longing, given and regrown, given and regrown... just to see if he could.","He had treated his own depths like a demonstration.","And here was a depth he had never demonstrated, arriving unasked. Was this what the Youngest felt on all those climbs?","\" The Jarls will hunt me now.\"","Noah’s voice moved easily through the dark, unhurried, addressed to all of them.","\" I’m currently a target of the Cursed Descendants of THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension.\" He shrugged slightly.","\" It’s not anything crazy. I should be able to continue moving without problems. I’ll be following my own path regardless, and I know all of you have your own plans.\"","His gaze passed across them.","\" THE Sealed One is an enemy to take down in time. Others will fall in line after. But before any of that...what do you all wish to do?\"","The question hung in the frothing dark.","And THE Creature reflected.","He looked at the feeling in his hands, this new weight called falling-behind, and he looked at the road that had put it there. The Youngest had not pulled ahead by waiting. He had pulled ahead by rushing in, and doing it rapidly at that!","If he wanted to truly follow his path...he had to rush in without anything holding him back.","The decision settled into him completely, and without ceremony.","\"I will have to go, \" THE Creature spoke up, his flat voice carrying across the platform, \" and seek the power I need to truly begin my path of a Great Ruler.\"","The conversation stilled.","\" It is a path I must walk alone. For now...this should be my goodbye. \" His obsidian gaze was level. \" I thank you because the power gained from THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension will be of big help.\"","And as he said it, he looked at his tail.","THE Blank Caudal of the Unwritten Primeval swayed slowly behind him, white-haired and patient, threading its light through his flames.","He looked up at The Youngest and Anaximander.","The two of them stared at him silently. No protest. No negotiation as after a moment, they simply nodded.","And THE Creature...showed a rare smile.","It moved across his features unfamiliar and unhurried, and when he spoke, his grand voice had the cadence of utter glory.","\"I used to believe Existence was a weight that things carried. That every being staggered beneath the fact of itself, and the strongest were merely the ones who staggered least.\" His flames burned low.","\"I was wrong. I have watched all of you, and I was wrong. Existence is not the weight. Existence is the carrying. It is not the stone, it is the back that bends and does not break, it is the hand that lifts what it did not drop\"","His gaze passed slowly across all of them. \" What is borne, and who bears it, and how they rise beneath it. That is all Existence has ever been. And a Ruler of Existence...must simply be the one who carries the largest share, the longest, for the most.\"","\"...\"","The dark between Dimensions held very still around the words.","Then THE Creature closed his eyes.","He turned his attention inward and backward, into the deep architecture of his own existence, to the presence that sat folded there, inherited and his, the seated colossus of worn gray stone. He regarded it for a long moment, this Paradox he had disliked and carried anyway, and he addressed it directly for the first time.","\"I am ready to go all in .\" His voice was quiet. \" Let the trials of existence begin.\"","And within him, and behind him, and somehow also very far away...","HUUM!","The statue opened its eyes.","Two points of light kindled in the faceless gray stone, ancient past all framing, and an ancient voice boomed out, not loud, but vast, a voice that seemed to arrive from the direction time came from.","\" THE FIRST TRIAL...IS TO BATHE IN THE BLOOD OF A THOUSAND TRUE LIFEFORMS THAT HAVE SIGNIFICANTLY HARMED EXISTENCE.\"","...!","A thousand True Lifeforms! Harvested not at random, but judged, each one weighed and found guilty of harming Existence itself, and their blood the bath!","THE Creature did not hesitate.","He gave a simple nod and opened his eyes, and began to float up off the back of Hvitrmarr as waves of schorcing flames billowed around him!","At the platform’s edge, he paused, and looked at Anaximander.","\" My friend. I will try not to call you for help again too quickly. But if I do...forgive me.\"","And Anaximander smiled, tousled and plain amid the naked strings of the dark.","\" Whenever you need me, call.\" The scholar’s eyes were warm. \" Distance is a superstition, and so is ’too quickly.’ Existence can be very miserable alone, and we can make the conditions ourselves not to be miserable.\"","\"...\"","With these words held, THE Creature turned last to Noah.","And his eyes flashed with a competitive light!","\" Youngest. I am curious how far your human road will stretch. I am waiting to see which of us will become a Great Ruler. \" The rare smile returned, one degree sharper.","\" We may be back together before you know it, soon. As...I will see if I can possibly pull ahead of you by then.\"","...!","THE Youngest smiled calmly at this, and nodded.","THE Creature gave one last nod to Ryaenara.","The Mirthful Antiquity nodded back, uncharacteristically wordless, her vibrant eyes holding him a moment longer than a nod required.","And then he fully floated away from Hvitrmarr.","He did not ask for a road. He did not ask for a door! He moved out into the frothing dark between all Dimensions as if he already knew exactly where he wanted to go, and did not need anybody to take him there, because he did not. His Pantheon had no shape. His Pantheon became its surroundings.","Existence was his Pantheon.","And even out here, between all membranes and beneath all frameworks...was existence.","His obsidian flames spread into the dark, and the dark received them, and at this moment, wholly and without reservation, THE Creature went all in to everything that existence entailed!"]},{"number":5536,"title":"Chapter 5536: Chapter 5535: Trials! II","paragraphs":["He floated across boundless darkness for an indeterminate amount of time.","Time did not press its claims out here, and THE Creature did not press his! He drifted through the frothing black with his body folded in upon itself, knees drawn up, obsidian flames banked low around his body, curled the way a thing is curled when it is newly born, and in a manner of speaking...he was.","For around his folded form, roiling waves of a deep Ananke Intent burned!","The digestion had finished somewhere in the drifting dark. Two Gilded True Lifeforms had rendered down to their last weavings within his depths, and their essense had carried him across the threshold he had approached for so long, and the second order of Intent now turned around him in slow tidal revolutions, inevitability wearing obsidian, and beneath it, his weight felt even more immense. As if everything he had ever carried had settled at last.","He did not open his eyes for any of it.","He only opened his eyes, and unfurled, when he felt himself slipping across the folds of a Dimension.","The dark parted. Membrane-weavings slid across his flames like curtains of another existence’s law, and as he passed through them, the statue spoke.","Its voice came calm this time. Not the booming verdict of the trial’s declaration, but something quieter and older.","\" You stand within THE Ghor-Vazhal. \" The ancient voice moved through him without hurry. \" Its masters call it the Fields. Everything else that has ever learned its name calls it the Cultivation Farms.\"","\"...\"","\" Here, Source True Lifeforms practice an external art of existence. You bear your adversity. They have decided bearing is inefficient.\" The calm of the voice made the words worse.","\" They cultivate Gu Lifeforms, bred hungers, refined across generations, and they strengthen these Gu through the sacrifice of cognizant lifeforms. Trillions of them. Across countless worlds and realms and domains of this Dimension, lifeforms moving through existence carrying their own adversity are plucked from their lives, refined for flavor, sacrifised, and eaten, and the Gu digest what those lives carried, and the masters harvest the Gu, and progress arrives for them rapidly, externally, at no cost their own existence ever feels.\"","The membrane-folds thinned ahead. Light the color of old blood bled through.","\" Trillions of lives are wiped out daily. It has been so for ages. Boundless suffering stretches across worlds and domains that appear in no records except as acreage. \" A pause, and the calm voice set down its last stone. \" Here, many True Lifeforms who have significantly harmed Existence can be found. That is why the first trial begins in this place. Begin whenever you wish.\"","...!","And rage coursed through THE Creature.","It ROSE, the way floodwater rises, patient and total, filling every channel of a newly-Ananke existence from the floor upward!","Existence is the carrying! It is the back that bends and does not break! And here was an entire Dimension built by beings who had heard that same truth somewhere in their long climbing, and had answered it with a ledger and a farm! Beings who did not carry. Beings who billed to to others!","Who had turned the bearing of trillions into feed, and called the weaving an art!","The folds opened, and he slipped fully in, and saw where he had appeared.","The skies were painted red.","Butcher red! A vast crimson firmament stretched from horizon to horizon, stained by ages of what rose into it, and below, across a scorched land that had been walked flat by chained feet...rose the pyramids.","They climbed in their dozens toward the red sky, colossal stepped mountains of black stone, each tier worn smooth and dark with use, and at the very top of every one of them, roiling, sat the Gu Lifeforms! Grotesque bred hungers the size of hills, no two alike, one a mass of mouths arranged in a wheel, one a bloated segmented thing whose shell wept, one a beautiful shimmering moth whose wings were made entirely of grasping hands, each of them squatting upon its pyramid’s peak like an idol of appetite!","And up the steps of every pyramid, in procession...climbed the chained.","Millions of them! Humanoid lifeforms and beasts both, shackled throat to throat in lines that stretched back across the scorched land beyond sight, dragged upward tier by tier by weavings that gave them no floor to fall to and no strength to resist, and at the top of each climbing line, at each peak, the processions ended in the mouths of the Gu! Steadily. Rhythmically! An intake as constant and unremarkable, to this place, as breathing, the carrying of trillions rendered down into feed while the red sky drank the noise!","And at a central point among the pyramids, upon a floating terrace of veined gold...multiple Source True Lifeforms were gathered together, laughing, and talking.","Lounging! Robed existences of the threshold, dense and patient and ancient, sharing refreshment above the machinery of their art, one of them gesturing lazily toward a distant pyramid as if comparing yields, another laughing at the remark, the sound of it drifting bright and easy across a landscape eating millions!","THE Creature looked at this scene.","He looked at the wheel of mouths taking its procession. He looked at the chains, and the climbing lines without end, and the laughter on the golden terrace, and somewhere behind his ribs, a statue’s ancient eyes burned, and the floodwater reached the top of him!","And THE Creature roared out with maddened grandeur!","OOOOH!","The sound tore across this tiny region of THE Ghor-Vazhal like the birth-cry of a verdict, Ananke Intent detonating off his frame in obsidian tides, and every chained head across a million tiers turned, and every Gu’s appetite stuttered, and upon the golden terrace, the laughter died mid-note as ancient heads snapped upward toward a fold in their sky that had opinions!","And THE Creature raised his fists, and SMASHED them down toward the gathered True Lifeforms!","And the skies answered!","The red firmament itself convulsed as, across the whole visible heaven, the stained clouds and the bloodlight and the upper airs gathered and folded, forming into colossal illusory fists, ten of them, a hundred, the sky becoming knuckles from horizon to horizon, and they came down with his own fists, all of them, together, as if existence itself was attacking!"]},{"number":5537,"title":"Chapter 5537: Chapter 5536: Trials! III","paragraphs":["The fists came down.","A hundred of them, folded out of a sky that had been drinking screams for ages, huge knuckles of stained cloud and bloodlight dropping together with the two obsidian ones at their center, and the floating terrace of veined gold, that lounging place where an art was talked over with food and drink, stopped being a place at all.","BOOM!","The impact flattened the region.","Gold burned away. The terrace’s foundations, weavings anchored into the Dimension’s own strings by beings who had held them for ages, tore free with a sound like a continent being unstitched, and the shockwave rolled outward across the scorched land in a ring of obsidian fire that walked over three pyramids and left them leaning, and every chained line across a million tiers went down flat as the ground bucked beneath them!","And out of the flattening, the Source True Lifeforms rose.","They rose fighting. THE Creature would grant them that much and nothing else. Nine of them came up out of their own ruin with their density intact, robed existences of the threshold, ancient and patient and very hard to unravel, and their Intent came off them in slow heavy pressures that made the air itself refuse to move, and one of them looked at him with such deep, insulted disbelief that it was almost worth something.","\" Who the fuck is this dumb motherfucker?!\"","HUUM!","Their Intent converged.","Nine Ananke-grade weights, laid one atop another, one joined pressure built to press a trespasser flat into the very land they farmed, and it fell upon THE Creature with all the piled authority of ages of undisturbed harvest!","And THE Creature simply spread his arms.","HUUM!","THE MAW opened somewhere that was not his body.","It opened in the ground beneath their feet, and in the red sky above their heads, and in the space between their converging weights, because THE Pantheon of All Existence has no shape and never needed one, and the nine masters of the Cultivation Farms suddenly understood, all at once, that they were no longer standing in their Dimension.","They were standing INSIDE him.","The red sky was him. The scorched land was him. The leaning pyramids and the chains and the whole flat butchered horizon was him, and their nine converging Intents poured into a throat that had been swallowing adversity since before the Scales were drawn, and vanished, and did not come back!","\"...!\"","Their weights guttered and their pressure broke.","And the one who had spoken first took one step backward.","That step was the only warning any of them received.","WAA!","THE Creature moved!","His obsidian flames tore across the emptied sky in a single black stroke, and behind him, unfurling long and white and patient, came the tail.","THE Blank Caudal of the Unwritten Primeval!","White hair threaded with the gold of a thing older than every framework these beings had ever climbed, it whipped out across gigaparsecs of ruined farmland and took the nearest master around the throat, and the Source True Lifeform’s dense and patient existence, that thing so famously hard to unravel, was hauled off its feet and driven down through nine tiers of its own pyramid at a speed that turned black stone into black powder!","CRASH!","And it kept going. It went down through the pyramid’s root, and through the crust beneath, and the tail did not release, it constricted, white coils tightening in the dark under the world while the master’s Trueness bled out of it in sheets of wasted light!","At the peak of that same pyramid, the Gu began to react.","The wheel of mouths, hill-sized and grotesque, shook itself off its perch as ages of training told it that something had entered the land, and it turned all of its mouths toward THE Creature at once and screamed a scream made of every intake it had ever performed!","THE Creature looked at it.","He looked at the bred hunger, the trained appetite, the generations of careful breeding that had produced a thing whose entire purpose was to receive what other beings had carried and hand the profit upward, and his rage found a new floor to flood!","He reached out with his hand.","And the tail came up out of the ground behind the Gu.","SHIING!","It punched through the wheel from beneath and burst out of the top of it, and then it opened, white coils splaying like a hand inside a fist, and THE Creature closed his fingers, and his tail tore the Gu apart from the inside out!","The hill-sized thing came apart in the red air.","And what spilled out of it was not guts.","It was the corpses.","Ages of it, uncounted, the piled weight of every life that had climbed those steps and been sacrifised into that wheel, released all at once into a sky that had no idea what to do with it, and for one moment the whole region was full of the weight of trillions, their labors, their endurances, their small stubborn bearings, hanging in the butcher-red light with nowhere left to go!","And across a million tiers, the chained looked up and saw it!","\"...!\"","THE Creature’s flames burned white-gold at their edges, and he went to work.","What followed was not a battle! It had the shape of one for a while, because the masters of the Fields were mighty, and they fought with all the art of ages, and two of them managed to wound him. One split his shoulder open with a lance of packed sacrificial essense and THE Creature did not so much as look at the wound. One anchored a weaving into his flames that should have cut him off from his own Pantheon, which was a genuinely excellent idea, and would have worked on almost anything else in existence, and did nothing at all to a being whose Pantheon was the ground the weaving was anchored in.","He took that one in his hands and laid THE Burden of Existence upon it.","HOONG!","The appendage settled onto the master’s back, and it gave that ancient patient thing exactly what it had spent its ages avoiding.","The bearing.","Every era THE Creature had carried, every weight, every adversity borne without complaint since before many Dimensions had a name, moved whole onto a being who had built an entire civilization on the idea that bearing was a waste, and the Source True Lifeform’s knees hit the black stone, and then its hands, and then its face, and it stayed down there making a sound that had no dignity in it whatsoever while its own weavings buckled under a debt it had never once paid a copper toward!","And then he crushed its skull with his heel.","SQUELCH!","Across the region, the pyramids were coming down.","He walked through the Fields and unmade them. The tail whipped and coiled and strangled, taking Gu and master alike, smashing bred hungers into those that had fed them, and where his flames touched the black stone the stone forgot it had ever been stacked. The moth with wings of grasping hands tried to rise off its peak and got half a wingbeat before white coils took it around the thorax and folded it in half the wrong way.","The bloated segmented thing burst and rained ages of stolen carrying across three continents of scorched land. Six pyramids. Nine. Fourteen! An entire district of the Cultivation Farms turned into rubble and rising weight while the red sky churned overhead, and behind his ribs, an ancient Creature kept a calm and terrible tally!","And the last of the nine True Lifeforms, the one who had spoken first, finally stopped retreating and turned to face him with its Trueness burning down to its final reserves.","It roared at him.","\" Do you know what you are doing?! What force we belong to?! We stem from-\"","The tail was already moving.","It came across the red sky wearing the full weight of a newly-seated Ananke Intent, white and gold and utterly without hurry, and it cleaved the master’s skull apart mid-sentance, and the great and ancient existence that had been about to call on its lineage came apart in two clean falling halves.","\"I don’t give a damn.\"","...!","Silence took the Fields.","The last of the ruin settled. The rubble stopped moving. Across a landscape that had been eating millions daily since before the Scales were laid out, nothing was eating anything at all, and the only sound left in the whole butchered region was the wind pulling at loose chain.","THE Creature floated up into the red sky.","He rose slowly, obsidian flames burning low and even around his frame, until he hung high above the broken pyramids, and from up there he could see all of them.","The chained.","Millions of them, still shackled throat to throat in lines that stretched past the horizon, humanoid lifeforms and beasts both, lying where the shockwaves had thrown them and staring upward at the thing in their sky. He looked down into their faces.","He saw what was in them.","There was no gratitude. Not yet, and maybe not ever, because gratitude needs a future and these beings had been raised in a place that issued none. What he saw was rage. Old rage, buried so deep beneath the climbing and the chains that most of them had probably forgotten they were carrying it, surfacing now in ten million upturned faces at once.","Good.","\"I will take your rage and your pain and your suffering,\" THE Creature said, and his flat voice carried across every area and every chain and every scorched acre of the Fields.","\" And I will make them all answer for it.\"","\"...!\"","\" Don’t let go of that rage. Do not let it go!\"","HUUM!","And then he turned in the red sky and shot out toward another direction, obsidian fire tearing a line across the sky, because this had been one district, one region, one flat butchered corner of a Dimension that stretched much further than that, and out there across THE Ghor-Vazhal the other pyramids were still standing and the other Gu were still swallowing and the chained lines had not stopped climbing for so much as a heartbeat.","Decillions.","The number moved through him and would not settle. Countless Decillions of thinking beings across the Fields, born into farmland, raised as flavor, whose entire fate from first breath to last was to be used and devoured so that beings on golden terraces could climb without the excitment of ever having to carry anything, and every one of them had borne something, and not one of them had ever been asked!","And rising underneath all these thoughts, older, unhealed, the thing he never spoke of.","His other half.","Brutalized in front of him. This was what he continued to be reminded of when he looked at all their faces!","His rage rose higher as his first Trial barely began.","A thousand? He would kill fucking millions if he needed to!"]},{"number":5538,"title":"Chapter 5538: Chapter 5537: Ordinary! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Noah turned his gaze to Ryaenara after THE Creature completely disappeared.","She had been quiet since he pulled her out of that poisoned sea, which was not like her at all, for the Mirthful Antiquity did not do quiet, she did loud, and profane, and right now she was standing on a disc of white light above a Steed’s scales with her arms folded, looking at him with something working behind her eyes!","She had many things on her mind.","And then she asked her question.","\" It seems you were able to cure a Cursed Steed .\" Her voice came level.","\"A curse passed down across its whole lineage, stemming from Those Who Remain themselves.\" Her vibrant eyes did not leave his face. \" Can you do the same for my brother? Do you already have the capability to cure him too?\"","\"...\"","The dark between Dimensions flowed past as the strings hummed their long notes, and Noah did not answer quickly.","He thought about it properly first.","\" No ,\" he said. \" Not yet.\"","Ryaenara said nothing as she waited.","\" Hvitrmarr’s curse was rooted in her Causes.\" Noah rested a hand flat on the ivory beneath him.","\" Her First Causes were failing, one by one, on a schedule somebody else wrote for her, and everything else about her was just a thing standing on top of that failure. So I didn’t cure her, not the way a healer would. I went in and I replaced her Causes. I took what was terminal and I collapsed it, and I gave the space it left a new meaning, and I seated my own Causes into her Organs where the dying ones had been.\"","His eyes stayed on Ryaenara’s.","\" That is what the cure was.\"","\"...\"","\" Your brother is different.\" He said it plainly. \" Ulf’s curse is sitting on top of his existence. It isn’t a failing organ I can cut out and replace with a better one. It’s woven into the same weavings that make him Ulf.\"","\" Which means to cure him the way I cured her, I wouldn’t be replacing Causes. I would have to replace an entire existence. Collapse the one he currently has, all of it, and give it new meaning on the other side. \" He shook his head once.","\"I do not have that capability, not with what I know now, not with anything I currently hold. If I tried it today I would not cure your brother. I would end him.\"","WAA!","Ryaenara looked at him for a long moment.","And then she nodded silently.","\" Then I remain with you ,\" she said, \" and give what I can to ensure your growth as we head towards IT.\"","\"...\"","And she was not finished.","\" There is something else .\" Ryaenara’s tone changed, going lighter in a way that meant the opposite of light. \" After we left THE Krazhor-Nul, messages from THE Sealed One reached out across my existence. Asking for updates on you.\"","...!","The name moved through the little gathering on Hvitrmarr’s back!","Anaximander’s head came up slightly, and Noah felt a slow cold interest settle in his chest.","Ryaenara held his gaze without apology.","\" What shall I tell him?\"","Noah thought about it.","He thought about the shape of the answer, because say too little and the thing gets suspicious, and say too much and you have handed a monster a weapon.","Say something true, but small, and slightly boring.","\" Tell him I’ve begun skipping across Dimensions,\" Noah said thoughtfully. \" That I’m trying to establish myself. Nothing more specific than that.\"","He smiled slightly. \" And tell him you’re getting close to me, but keeping your distance.\"","Ryaenara’s mouth curved as she nodded calmly.","Noah then turned his gaze to Anaximander.","The scholar had been standing there through all of it in his white robes with his tousled hair, saying nothing, and he was extremely thoughtful at this moment.","Then he looked up.","\" Could you, \" Anaximander said, \" actually come with me?\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\" To that Dimension I mentioned. The one I have to go back to.\" The scholar’s plain voice picked up a little warmth. \" You have talked about Humans. About being a Human Emperor, about gathering everything Human wherever it stands. And these beings, these Superpowered Lifeforms, are some of the more human beings you are going to meet anywhere.\"","\"...\"","\" They are like me, and also not like me, and I have never quite been able to explain the difference to myself, which is one of several reasons I have not stopped thinking about them.\" A small self-aware smile.","\"I think you would benefit from meeting them. And from seeing what they have built.\"","He paused.","\" And when I left, an incursion was about to happen as they were defending against Infinite Lifeforms.\"","...!","\" What do you think?\"","Noah considered it.","He genuinely did not have a preference, because THE Krazhor-Nul had been chosen for him by his own Anchor, and THE Krazhor-Nul had been far too heavy! Cursed Descendants who converted gigaparsecs into a fist! Steeds whose ambient presence stopped his Pantheon from unfurling! He had walked out of it alive and crowned and riding a steed, and he had walked out of it knowing exactly how close the whole thing was, and he had even died in there!","So. Would this place be more his speed?","Beings without authority, whose identity made existence conform, a whole society of them, defending their own borders against many enemies.","And there was the other thing.","Anaximander had mentioned a Panacea. A cluster of Observable Existences producing something that Source and Infinite True Lifeforms would wage war to take, that they had been waging war to take, for long enough that the defense had become a civilization!","A Panacea!","Noah, who currently had a Dimension full of dying tyrants preparing to hunt him for exactly that kind of thing, felt his interest sharpen.","\" Okay!\"","His eyes shined as he looked at the scholar.","\" What is this place called?\"","And Anaximander smiled.","\" THE Ymnaros,\" he said. \" It is an old word, older than the beings living there now, and as far as I have been able to trace it, it means something close to Ordinary. They named it that themselves. I have never worked out whether it was a joke.\"","Noah smiled lightly.","He turned toward the great white head at the front of it all.","\" Hvitrmarr.\"","\"I have this Dimension within my internal map,\" she answered before he finished asking, her ancient voice warm through the bond and through the dark both. \" I will take you there.\"","And her wings began to beat.","WUU!","The long strokes shortened and quickened and gathered as Hvitrmarr banked across the naked strings of the deep, turning them onto a new heading, and Noah felt her capability wake beneath him!","It was the same one that had saved them from a closing obsidian hand.","He felt it come up through her scales into his seat, the First-lineage blood in her threading them into the gaps between things, laws and membranes and distances all agreeing to step aside for a lineage that had been crossing this dark since Those Who Remain designed it, and the frothing black stretched and folded and...","HUUM!","In a matter of seconds, they arrived!","They appeared before a shimmering endless boundary! She was that quick. A steed was that grand!","Noah looked at it, and it was unique.","It hung across the whole of his vision and past it, a vast surface of soft shifting light, and it was not a wall and not a door and not a membrane like the ones he had watched drift past out here, it moved like the surface of water seen from underneath, and it had a warmth to it.","|Analysis of the periphery is complete.|","Ruination’s voice came clean and immediate.","|The outer boundary of this Dimension carries an active drawing authority. Its function is not to repel. Its function is to route. Any foreign existence that crosses the boundary is caught by this authority and pulled, regardless of its intended point of entry, into one of many centralized domains maintained across the interior. These are designated THE Muster Halls.|","|Purpose: everything foreign that arrives is delivered into a prepared place, and is treated on arrival as an enemy until proven otherwise. Defenders are stationed. The routing is automatic and constant. The overwhelming majority of incursions are stopped in the Halls and never reach the interior at all.|","|Assessment: this is a Dimension that has been invaded so many times it has built its front door out of the invasions.|","|Some beings are simply too powerful for the drawing authority to hold, and bypass the routing entirely. Those beings arrive wherever they wish. It is reasonable to assume the Halls exist because of how much damage the ones who bypass them have historically done.|","...!","Noah’s eyes twinkled!","An entire Dimension that had turned being attacked into an architecture! That had accepted, as a permanent condition of its existence, that things would keep coming for what it held, and had answered by building a system that greeted every single arrival as a hostile act and processed it accordingly!","He liked them already.","’ Would you be pulled to one of those ?’ he asked through the bond. ’If we cross here.’","Hvitrmarr’s answer came calm and entirely without arrogance.","’No. I am a Dimension Steed. Routing authorities are for things that must use a Dimension’s doors. ’ Her great head turned as one gold eye found him. ’I can enter directly into any point of this Dimension I choose.’","Noah nodded slowly.","\" Let’s go then!\"","WUU!","Her wings spread wide across the shimmering endless light, and rider and Steed and scholar and Antiquity moved as one toward THE Ymnaros, and the boundary opened its soft shifting folds around them, vibrant and warm and utterly unlike the cold rind of the Dimension they had left, and they disappeared into it!"]},{"number":5539,"title":"Chapter 5539: Chapter 5538: Ordinary! II","paragraphs":["<THE Ymnaros>","The gardens had been green and gold for longer than most Dimensions had been standing, running in long terraces across a land that had no edges anyone had ever found, the green shading into the gold and back again as wide slow rivers cut through all of it carrying light instead of silt, and small things had lived there and none of them had ever been important, and that had always been the entire point of the place!","Now the terraces were burning.","The rivers had been broken open along their whole length as their light bled out into the soil in long spreading stains, and the gold had gone black in rings around a hundred impact sites, and where the gardens had climbed they now sagged, and where they had run they now simply stopped.","And above the ruin stood the armies.","They filled the sky in ranks that went back past seeing, existences of Infinity in their tens of thousands, their power built out of escalation and quiet compounding as they hung in their formations with their weight pressing the ruined land flat beneath them, and the weakest thing in that entire gathered host read at THE Triassic Scale!","The weakest!","The Fourth Scale of Existence, the tier where a single being could stand upon an Observable Existence and be the largest fact inside it, and here that was the floor, here that was the rank and file, the bodies you counted in blocks rather than by name!","And scattered up through those blocks, spaced apart the way real threats are always spaced apart, there stood over a hundred figures who carried the unmistakable weight of THE Mesozoic Scale, the Fifth, each one of them a thing that ordinary Dimensions built their entire histories around, and there were over a hundred of them in one sky on one afternoon for one garden.","And rising out of the armies like statues that had been given breath, several massive Infinite True Lifeforms towered above everything!","They were vast past the ranks around them, vast past any comparison with the ranks around them, their bodies reading less as bodies than as landscapes that had agreed to hold a shape for a while, and their existences were seamless in the way that only a True Lifeform’s ever is, the claim of \"I am\" running through them without a single gap for anything to take hold of, and that seamlessness set them above THE Mesozoic entirely.","Cenozoic!","And the difference between the Fifth and the Sixth, in the end, was time.","Beings at the Mesozoic Scale built their Pantheons and made them grander and grander, and it was work enough to eat ages of a life, but a being who crossed into THE Cenozoic Scale kept doing all of that and then began adding something else into their Pantheonic Dimension, something that almost nothing in existence could hold, and what they added were weavings of time!","And most of them could not use it.","That was the honest truth of the Sixth Scale and the reason so many beings who reached it looked, from the outside, like nothing more than very large Mesozoics, because the technique was simply too hard to grasp, and entities in the early stretches of THE Cenozoic Scale carried those weavings inside their Pantheons the way a person carries a language they cannot yet speak, aware of it, unable to use it, fighting with weight and grandeur alone while the real capability sat unopened inside them for ages.","The power at Cenozoic was known as THE Epochal Sovereign Weave!","More plainly, and more often, it was called Temporal-Environmental Overwrite, and a True Lifeform who had truly grasped it no longer fought inside a Dimension’s current time or under its current physical rules at all, but dragged the space around them backward or forward instead, hauling the surroundings into weavings where their own Pantheon and their own existence ruled absolutely, so that the fight happened there, in their epoch, on ground that had been made to agree with them before the first blow ever landed.","And the results of it were obscene.","An incoming attack could be made to travel years before it ever reached the one it was aimed at, arriving worn down, arriving late, arriving as a thing that had already spent itself on the way, and the defenses of another could be made to weather years while they stood, an opponent’s Pantheon forced to age through decades of erosion in the space of a single held breath!","And the terrifying ones, the ones who could set an entirely different epoch into their surroundings rather than merely bending the local one, did something worse than either of those, because inside a forced epoch a power system could be treated by the environment itself as a thing not yet invented, or as a thing long since abandoned, and a being would raise a capability they had spent ages perfecting only to find the surroundings quietly declining to recognize it at all!","Downgraded! Negated! Not defeated, which would at least have been a kind of respect, but ruled out entirely, the way a law rules out a thing that has not happened yet.","There were levels to it.","There were always levels to it, and every being in that sky knew exactly which level it stood upon, and that was precisely why the ranks held their spacing so carefully around the tall silent shapes among them.","Eight True Lifeforms had entered a small corner of the gardens of THE Ymnaros that day.","Six of them were still standing.","At the center of the ruin, where the terraces had once climbed into their finest arrangement, a shrine rose out of the wreckage, a single obelisk taller than mountains with its faces carved in lines that were neither writing nor decoration, and it burned with a steady blue-gold light that had not dimmed by so much as a shade through the entire assault, the light pouring up its faces and off its point and hanging in the smoke above it, patient, unbothered, still doing whatever it had always been doing.","And two of the six True Lifeforms stood at its base and had not moved from it once.","They did not attack it, and they did not attack anything else either, they simply held their places on either side of that obelisk with their whole attention fixed upon it as though waiting for something, and their stillness said more about what that shrine was worth than the entire army above them could have said with a thousand years of screaming.","And the gardens around the shrine were decimated.","For in that destruction lay two corpses.","Infinite True Lifeforms, both of them, split wide open, and there was no other way to describe what had been done to them, their landscape-bodies lying across the ruined terraces in halves, opened from the top down along a line so clean that it looked considered, their Pantheons collapsed inside them and still collapsing even now, and out of those openings ran rivers of Infinity.","Actual rivers of it!","Bright and endless and pouring, escalation with nothing left to escalate through, spilling down the broken terraces and mixing with the light of the murdered gardens, a wealth of power that a Mesozoic being would have wept simply to touch, running out across the dirt because there was no longer any existence attached to it that could hold onto it!","Two True Lifeforms of the Infinite variety, killed, here, in this garden.","...!","And gathered around those enormous corpses, small as scattered seeds against them, there lay the bodies of unique humanoid lifeforms all adorned in white and blue suits.","Dozens of them, built plainly, no larger than any ordinary person, their suits simple things of white with blue running through them and marked at the chest with a sign that had been designed to be recognized at a distance by frightened people, and some of them had died still holding their formation, and some of them had died reaching toward someone else who had also died.","They were... Superpowered Lifeforms."]},{"number":5540,"title":"Chapter 5540: Chapter 5539: Ordinary! III","paragraphs":["Dead Superpowered Lifeforms.","And in the middle of all of it, on his knees in the wreck of a garden, one of them was still alive.","A golden-haired man!","He was built like something that had been made on purpose, enormous through the shoulders and the chest, heavy with a muscle that did not look decorative in the slightest, his arms thick enough that the chains upon them had needed to be thick as well, and he wore the same white and blue as the dead around him with the sleeves gone and the chest sign burned half away, his hair gold and short and matted dark down one side, his jaw set, his mouth bleeding.","And he was staring hatefully up at the army.","Not with fear, and not with despair, and not with the shocked emptiness of a being who had watched everyone he came in with die, but with hatred, clean and enormous and moving from face to face across an entire army as it took each one of them in turn and held it a moment and then moved along to the next one!","And he gave off nothing.","Not one wave of authority! Not the smallest ripple of the pressure that even a Triassic Scale existence pushes out of itself simply by being present, and standing in a sky full of beings whose weight bent the land, this man registered upon the surroundings as approximately as much as the dirt he was kneeling in.","And he had killed two of them!","Two Infinite True Lifeforms, opened top to bottom, their Pantheons collapsed and their Infinity running out into the gardens, and this body that gave off nothing at all had done that, and that was why the army had arranged itself exactly like this, all of it, ten thousand Triassics and a hundred Mesozoics and six True Lifeforms, and that was why not one single being among them had come close enough to touch him.","They had chained him instead.","Rivers of blue chain wrapped him from shoulder to wrist to knee, and they were not metal, they were Infinity poured into the shape of a chain and set there burning, and worked through every link of them were Pantheonic Dimensional weavings of time that glowed along their length in slow pulses which ran down toward his body and never came back.","And with every pulse, he was being regressed.","His strength was being walked backward down its own road, hauled back through all the years it had spent growing into what it was and held down at a version of himself he had left behind ages ago and kept there, the chains adjusting constantly, tightening the instant the strength beneath them tried to climb, and he had been fighting them for a long time as his hands shook with the effort and his arms kept trying anyway, and it was not working!","And standing in front of him, at her leisure, was the one who had built them.","She was tall and unhurried, her gown made of layered threads of Infinity, pale and blue, the threads forever unspooling from her hem and spooling back up into her shoulders so that she was constantly rebuilding herself out of herself while she stood there.","Her hair was hanging to the backs of her knees in that same pale blue and drifting in a wind that was not present, and her eyes had no whites in them at all, while her bare hands were stained blue-gold to the wrist.","The Woman of Rivers and Ledgers- Ashkavaal, THE Second Breath!","And she crouched down into the ruined gold to bring her face level with his, and she spoke to him kindly.","\"I hate your people so much.\"","\"...\"","\" Your bodies give off no authority. None at all. I could stand beside one of you at a market and never know it.\" Her head tilted as the numbers turned over in her eyes.","\" And yet you are this powerful. For what? Explain it to me, please, because I would truly like to understand the arrangement where a thing that weighs nothing gets to break two of my friends open like fruit.\" Her smile stayed warm.","\"Just die already. Die, and give up what you protect, and every part of this stops today.\"","The golden-haired man said nothing.","\"No. Of course not.\" Ashkavaal sighed and straightened up and brushed at her gown with those stained fingers. \" Then let us talk about the two you killed.\"","She glanced back over her shoulder at the corpses, at the rivers of Infinity running down the terraces, and something in her face when she looked at them was almost real!","\" For that, there has to be a price. And I have sadly already killed every Superpowered Lifeform in this garden, so there is nobody left standing here that I can take away from you.\" She turned back to him and the patience settled over her features again and her voice went light and pleasant. \" So I will simply use what I have.\"","\"...\"","\"I am going to raise them.\"","Her stained hand opened toward the scattered white and blue bodies!","\" All of them! Every one of your people lying in this dirt! I will bring them back up as Gamaidjan Lifeforms, the Mad Infinite Dead, and they will not know you, and they will not know themsleves, and they will do exactly what I tell them to do.\" The smile widened by nothing at all.","\" And what I will tell them to do is defile you. One by one. In front of everything gathered here.\"","...!","\" And after I have grown bored of that,\" Ashkavaal said, \"I will do the very same thing for every single Superpowered Lifeform I meet in this Dimension, every one of them, in every garden, for as long as it takes me!\"","She leaned down toward him once more.","\" Are you ready?\"","And the golden-haired man looked up at her!","His eyes were wet and they were not soft in the slightest, the hatred in them gone somewhere past what a face is built to hold, and he looked past her at the corpses of his people lying in the light of their own broken rivers, at all those dozens of white and blue suits scattered across a garden they had died standing in front of, and he ROARED!","OOOOH!","It tore out of him without a shred of authority behind it, no pressure, no weight, nothing that the sky above him would even register as an event, just a chained man on his knees in a ruined garden howling up at ten thousand existences with everything his body had left in it, and the chains flared and pulsed and hauled him backward through his own years all over again, and he kept roaring anyway!","And the army laughed!","It rolled down out of the sky in waves as ranks of Triassic and Mesozoic existences found the whole thing enormously funny, the noise spreading back through formations that went past seeing, a hundred thousand beings enjoying themselves thoroughly at the excitment of what was about to be done, and Ashkavaal raised her stained hand toward the nearest body as she prepared to begin.","And at such a time....the skies above cracked.","CRACK!","They split from one end of the ruined gardens to the other as a white line opened straight across the top of the domain, and the laughter died in the throats of an entire army as something came through.","HUUM!","A massive white draconic beast!","Huge in a way that made the towering True Lifeforms in that sky look like things standing near a mountain, pure white, twin spiral ivory horns, a mane of white flame, wings spread wide enough to shade whole terraces, and gold eyes with ring inside ring for pupils!","And atop it stood three figures!","They came out of the split sky and drew up, and they looked around at the burning terraces and the leaking rivers and the shrine still shining blue-gold in all that smoke, at ten thousand Triassics and a hundred Mesozoics and six True Lifeforms hanging in their formations.","And then, together, they looked down!","Coldly!","Across that entire gathered army, heads turned upward, formations shifted, the laughter was gone, and down in the ruin on his knees in his chains the golden-haired man raised his bleeding face toward the split in the sky as his mouth opened slightly.","Who... the hell were the new entrants?!"]},{"number":5541,"title":"Chapter 5541: Chapter 5540: THE Mortal Coil! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","They came through the shimmering boundary, and THE Ymnaros opened around them.","Noah felt Hvitrmarr rein herself in the moment they crossed, her ambient field folding down close against her scales, the vast sovereign weight of a Dimension Steed drawing inward until she read, to the world around her, as merely large rather than as a Steed that predated the Scales, and Noah approved of it silently, because there was no reason to announce themselves to an entire Dimension before he had even looked at it properly.","’ Quietly, for now ,’ he sent through the bond.","’ Quietly ,’ she agreed, and folded further.","And Ruination went to work.","|Preliminary analysis of THE Ymnaros is underway.|","|Early findings, incomplete: this Dimension is not a smaller or simpler thing than THE Krazhor-Nul. It is a different KIND of complex, and it is at least as vast. Nested Observable Existences in numbers the boundary alone could not fully account for. Ambient laws layered in strata, older frameworks buried beneath newer ones. A drawing authority woven through the entire outer shell that has clearly been rebuilt many times. A central production of some resource that bends the local Causes toward itself the way a great mass bends the space around it.|","|Assessment: you have not stepped down into an easier zone. You have stepped sideways into a different one that is equally deep. Full analysis will take time.|","...!","Noah took that in without surprise.","Of course it was as vast. Anaximander did not call a place the largest and most complex Dimension he had found and mean it lightly. This was going to be another deep place, but not as packed with monsters so far above him...hopefully!","And below him, spread across the ruin, was the war.","He saw the armies first, because they filled the sky, Infinite Lifeforms in their tens of thousands with the weakest of them reading at THE Triassic Scale and the tall silent shapes among them reading far, far past it. He saw the broken gardens and the leaking rivers of light. He saw the two enormous corpses split open top to bottom with Infinity pouring out of them, and the scattered white and blue bodies around a blue-gold obelisk that was still, somehow, shining.","And then he saw the one who did not fit.","A single chained figure on his knees in the wreckage. Golden-haired, built like something made on purpose, and emanating NOTHING. Not one wave of authority, not the faintest pressure, standing in a sky full of beings whose weight bent the land, and yet they had not simply killed him. They had wrapped him in rivers of burning blue chain and pinned him there, which told Noah, before he read a single detail, that the thing giving off nothing was the most dangerous thing in the garden.","They were powerful, all of them.","And as Noah gazed down at them, and as thousands of them began to gaze up at him, he did not feel an ounce of fear!","He had watched a Cursed Descendant fold gigaparsecs of a Dimension into a fist. He had died, once, inside a Steed, and come back. This was an army, and an army was a large thing, but a large thing was still just that.","Beside him, Anaximander had gone quiet in a way Noah had never heard from him.","Noah glanced over, and the scholar’s face had changed. The mild, curious, tousled explorer who called distance a superstition and smiled at everything was gone, and what stood in his place was cold. His eyes had settled on the scattered white and blue bodies around the obelisk, on the small plain corpses of people who had given off no power and died anyway, and for the first time since Noah had known him, Anaximander looked truly angry.","He said nothing. He did not need to. The chill coming off a man whose whole nature was to make existence conform was its own sentence.","A heavy silence hung in the air.","And on the ground, the most powerful of all the Infinite True Lifeforms present, the tall unhurried woman of unspooling blue threads who had been speaking her vile words to the chained man, looked up at the three figures on the white beast, and raised her stained hands, and spoke coldly.","\" Now now. I didn’t know there would be reinforcements.\" Her counting eyes turned over as she smiled up at them. \" Though it doesn’t change very much. I will simply do the same for all of you.\"","...!","Noah looked down at her calmly.","And seeing the armies gathered here, seeing the ruin and the corpses and the vast army filling the lands, reminded him of something.","The paintings.","Ulf’s paintings, the prophecy hung in oils, the ones Ryaenara’s dying brother had made of things that had not happened yet. Armies. Ruin. He was standing inside a scene that carried the same weight those paintings had carried.","But THE Creature was not here. And he did not have Emotive out either. The future those paintings pointed toward had specific pieces in it, and the pieces were not all present, which meant the paintings had not shown one fixed and settled thing at all. They had shown a possibility.","Perhaps parallel possibilities, perhaps potential realities, each one depending on the choices others had not yet made, futures branching off the decisions of every being who had a decision left to make.","Not set in stone!","And as he thought it, he gazed down at the beings below, and he activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard.","His fifth Letter answered, and the Regard settled over the garden, and the sheets bloomed in his sight.","He looked at the woman first.","|CHARACTER SHEET|","| Designation: Ashkavaal, THE Second Breath. An Infinite True Lifeform.|","|Scale: THE Cenozoic Scale, the Sixth. She has not merely reached the Sixth Scale, she has GRASPED the weavings of time within her Pantheon, where the overwhelming majority who reach this Scale never do. Her chains regress. Her defenses age their attackers. Within a set epoch she can rule a capability out of existence entirely, but she is still learning how to do this.|","| Disposition : cruel by preference, patient by training, bored by the ease of most of her work. Enjoys the ones who resist. Hates the Superpowered Lifeforms specifically, and does not know why the hatred runs as deep as it does.|","| Motivation : to take what THE Ymnaros protects. To deliver it upward. She is not the top of the thing she serves.|","|Fears: ?????|","|Notable thread: her Infinity does not read as her own. It runs UPWARD out of her, always, in a thin constant thread, toward somewhere she does not seem aware she is feeding. She draws, and she is drawn from, and she does not know it. She is not the only one here of whom this is true. Across the entire army, the same thread runs, thousands of them, all pulling from a well none of them can see and all leaking back toward it, an army that believes its power is its own and has never once been told whose cup it is actually filling. ????? sits at the other end of every thread. ????? is very patient.|","...!","Noah’s eyes narrowed at that.","An entire army of Infinite Lifeforms, drawing their Infinity, without knowing it, from a single hidden source?","He set the thread aside carefully, and moved his gaze to the chained man.","|CHARACTER SHEET|","| Designation: Theron Adranos. An Existence Class Superpowered Lifeform.|","|Distinction: Rank S, Ebad . The trembling shield-tree.|","|Nature: emanates no authority whatsoever. This is not weakness and not concealment. It is the SHAPE of his kind. Their power does not press outward on the world as a claim; it simply IS, held entirely inside the body, invisible until it acts. He killed two Infinite True Lifeforms giving off less pressure than the dirt beneath him.|","| Disposition : protective past reason. Grieving. Currently regressed and held; his true Distinction is not what the chains are letting him show.|","| Desire : to guard the shrine. To guard his people. He has failed at the second and will die before he fails at the first.|","|Fears: not death. Only that there will be no one left to stand here after him.|","|Notable thread: the obelisk is not a monument. He is not guarding a symbol. ?????|","Noah gazed down at Theron Adranos, at the golden-haired man who gave off nothing, and at the dead scattered around the shrine he would not stop guarding.","And he weighed something internally.","Death was such a normal part of being human.","So many humans lived, and so many died, that death itself became ordinary to the ones still living, a thing on the news, a thing in the next town, a number that scrolled past. People grew calloused to it because they had to, because a person could not stop and grieve every single one and still get out of bed, and so death became background, became a normal and unremarkable feature of the human world.","But each death was a human.","Each one had held dreams, and hopes, and ideals, and a family, an entire private universe that had taken a whole life to build, and when the death came the universe went out all at once, and to the people around it nothing was ever ordinary about it at all. Only distance made death ordinary. Up close it was the end of a world every single time!","Even his own death.","He had died in THE Krazhor-Nul, and he had come back, but only because he’d had the capability to come back. What if he hadn’t? What if the Hepatarch had not answered, and Noah Osmont had simply ended in the dark inside a Steed’s body? Amelia would have a son-shaped hole in her forever. Henry, Seo-yeon, Adelaide, Barbatos, every person inside THE Infiniverse waiting for him, would have a critical pillar missing from the center of their lives, a pillar gone, the whole structure left standing crooked around the gap where he had been.","That was death. That was what it took, every time, from someone!","This was human.","And as he thought it, standing in the sky above a garden full of the human dead, something opened in him.","An epiphany, profound and complete, the kind that did not arrive as information but as a door swinging wide onto a room he had always owned and never entered!","He had five Letters. I AM. OSMONT. QUINTESSENTIAL. HUMAN. PROTAGONIST. And the Tongue’s growth from here was not more Letters, it was WORDS, and he had known that for a while and had not yet spoken a single one, because a Word had to mean something true enough to carry, and he had been waiting, without knowing he was waiting, for a truth exactly this size.","The human experience. And death.","That was the Word.","Not a Word for power, or conquest, or dominion. A Word for the thing that made the dead in that garden matter, the thing that made his own near-ending matter, the plain unbearable truth that a human life was a whole world and a human death was the ending of one, and that no amount of authority stacked on top of a person changed the naked human thing underneath it, the small mortal creature that dreamed and hoped and could be ended.","He would speak it. And in speaking it, he would impose it. Not on himself alone but on an entire domain, everyone inside it made to stand as what they truly were underneath the power they wore, all authority stripped away, everyone designated as having none at all, so that in this one place the human experience could finally be exactly and only human!","\" The first word shall be...THE MORTAL COIL.\"","HUUM!","\" THE DOMAIN...OF THE MORTAL COIL.\"","...!","|A WORD of THE Osmontian Tongue is forming.|","|Analysis of the forming Word:|","| THE DOMAIN OF THE MORTAL COIL.|","|Function: within its bounds, ALL authority is nullified. Every Scale, every Intent, every Pantheon, every Cause, every claim of power a being has ever stacked upon itself is designated absent. Inside this domain no one has authority, because inside this domain everyone is only what a human is beneath it all: a life that can dream, and hope, and end.|","|Effect on the wielder: as THE True Human Emperor, you alone hold a single privilege inside the absolute leveling. You are permitted the standing of an F-Rank Hunter. The weakest a striving human begins as. Not nothing, a human’s beginning. In a domain where no one has any power at all, the beginning of a human’s road is a throne.|","|THE Infiniverse and those within are among exclusions if contained within you. If any lifeforms within come out, they will face the same human experience. The cost of bearing THE Infiniverse is paid by the uttered word itself while in effect. All redundancies and conflicts will be actively corrected by the word itself while active.|","|Cost, duration, and reach scale with the truth you speak it upon. Speak it fully.|","...!","Noah looked at the terrible thing he had just made, and he understood exactly what it would do to the garden below, and he did not hesitate!","He gazed down at the army, at Ashkavaal with her stained hands raised, at the thousands of Infinite Lifeforms who wore their power like a birthright and had never once in their long lives been asked to stand without it.","And he opened his mouth, and THE Aura of THE Protagonist bloomed around him as he did, Osmontian Biomass beginning to pour into his reserves in a rising golden tide, generated off the sheer adversity of an entire army arrayed beneath him, breakthrough-weight gathering as he faced down odds that should have crushed him, the numbers climbing and climbing as he drew the breath!","\" THE MORTAL COIL.\"","HUUM!","He spoke the first Word of THE Osmontian Tongue.","HUUM!","It did not sound like a word. It sounded like a fact the world had always known and been waiting to hear said out loud, and it rolled out from him across the ruined gardens of THE Ymnaros and kept rolling, and where it passed, the domain came down.","And below, the Infinite True Lifeforms ran out of patience at the worst possible moment.","Two of the tall shapes among the army began to rise, done with waiting, lifting off the ruined terraces to come and end the reinforcements themselves.","And moments later, they felt their flight falter.","The vibrant, terrible waves of authority and power they had carried since before their first memory, the pressure that was so much a part of them that they had never once thought about it any more than a person thinks about the weight of their own hand...","It began to fade, and thin, and go out, and the two great existences felt themselves growing lighter in the exact way nothing that mighty should ever grow lighter, and their rising stalled, and their bodies began to fall!","DUN!","Across the whole vast reach of the domain, every being was about to learn what it meant to be human!"]},{"number":5542,"title":"Chapter 5542: Chapter 5541: THE Mortal Coil! II","paragraphs":["The two rising True Lifeforms fell out of the sky!","They had lifted off the ruined terraces at the very moment THE MORTAL COIL came down as they were done with waiting and coming up to end the reinforcements themselves, and so they were the highest things in the sky when their power went out, and there was nothing beneath them but air and a very... long way down.","They fell.","And they were enormous, mountains given the shape of bodies, and even stripped down to nothing they were still that big, still that heavy, and mass falling from that height did what mass falling from that height does to anything at all, no matter how mighty it had been a breath ago.","BOOM!","The first one hit the scorched land and the ground came up around it in a crater, and Noah heard the sound its body made, and it was not the sound of a titan striking earth, it was the sound of bones.","Snapping. In their dozens!","A giant made human and then dropped, and every part of it that had been holding a mountain’s worth of weight came apart under that weight the instant the authority that had carried it so lightly for ages was simply gone, and the second one came down a heartbeat later in its own crater with its own long chorus of breaking, and then the gardens of THE Ymnaros filled with a sound that this Dimension had, in all its ages of war, quite possibly never heard once.","\" AHHH!\"","\"AWOOO!\"","...!","Two Infinite True Lifeforms, SCREAMING.","Screaming, high and ragged and utterly without dignity, the raw animal sound of a living thing in more pain than it had ever been built to feel, because pain was a human thing and these two had never in their long existences been human until right now, and it had found them all at once, and they had no idea what to do with it!","They writhed in their craters and they wailed, and they bled.","And Noah gazed out at the rest of the army.","Their faces had gone ashen.","Thousands of them, tens of thousands, the whole vast army that had filled the sky with its weight, and across every single face was the same dawning horror as the Infinity they had felt inside themselves since before their first memory, the constant private river of power that was more theirs than their own names... simply was not there anymore.","They reached for it the way a person reaches for a step that is not where they left it, and found nothing, and the nothing was worse than any blow Noah could have struck, because a blow they would have understood!","Even beside him, it expressed itself.","Ryaenara, the Mirthful Antiquity, made a small startled sound and pressed both hands flat to her own chest, and her eyes went wide, because she did not feel an ounce of power inside herself either!","And the high winds of THE Ymnaros caught at a body that suddenly had nothing anchoring it to anything and nearly took her clean off the platform, until Anaximander’s hand closed on her shoulder and held her down.","The scholar himself stood steady, because he was simply built different, but even he had gone quiet with the strangeness of it.","And beneath them all, Hvitrmarr began to descend, slowly, because Noah patted her scales and she brought them down, and she brought them down the ordinary way, wings and weight and air, because Hvitrmarr did not have access to a single shred of authority inside this domain either.","She was, right now, a massive white reptile with wings. A very large animal, gliding down toward a garden!","Everybody was human!","...!","For the briefest instant, as the Word settled, Noah had seen the woman below try to fight it.","Ashkavaal. THE Second Breath. He had watched her stained hands come up and watched weavings of time bloom off her fingers, her one real answer to a thing like this, and for a fraction of a moment those weavings had strained against as she tried to argue that authority-nullification was a law not yet invented where she stood, or already long obsolete, tried to wrap her own time around herself and step out of the human condition Noah had spoken over the world.","She was still learning!","But Noahs word was a TRUTH, and truth did not negotiate with a technique that hadn’t finished growing in, and so the domain settled over her weavings with a plain and total finality! Noah watched the vibrant rivers of Infinity and power that had wreathed her entire body dim, and thin, and go dark, until the tall unhurried woman of unspooling blue threads was simply a titanic human standing in a ruined garden with stained hands and nothing behind them.","And across the wreckage, the chains vanished.","The rivers of burning blue chain that had wrapped Theron Adranos shoulder to wrist to knee, Infinity poured into the shape of a shackle and worked through with weavings of time, were made of exactly the authority the domain had just designated absent, and so they simply ceased, all at once, and the golden-haired man dropped the last inch to his knees free.","He rose.","Slowly, clenching his fists, testing a body that no longer had a leash on it, and he looked up toward the descending white beast and the three figures upon it.","His eyes moved across them and locked onto Anaximander, and recognition crossed his bloodied face as if he had seen this scholar before, as if the mild man in the white robes was not a stranger to him at all!","And Noah felt the strangest thing he had felt in a very long time.","His own immensity was gone.","The crown hung loose on his head, but the Causes, the Foundations, the A-Rank seas, the fused authority that could resuscitate a dead Observable Existence, all of it designated absent, all of it stepped back behind a line his own Word had drawn, and what was left standing on Hvitrmarr’s descending back was a man. Just a man!","And Noah, THE True Human Emperor, felt himself returned to a sensation he had not touched since the very beginning of everything, since a fireball skillbook, since the first time he had ever reached inside a feeble human body and felt a thin thread of mana answer!","Oh!","That was what this was! Truly human!","He reached inside himself, and his Osmontian Source Infinity was still there, still his, still coursing through him exactly as it always had, except now he could only touch it at the scale a Rank F Hunter could touch anything. A trickle. A thread!","And truly, even this was not accurate as an F Rank Hunter could not truly touch something like Osmontian Source Infinity. So it was more accurate to say that he could display the power as THE True Human Emperor...at the level of a Rank F Hunter as designated in his home world.","The whole ocean was inside him and he was permitted to draw a single sliver from it, because that was the privilege the Word had left him, the standing of a human at the very start of the road, the weakest a striving person begins as!","It was surreal past describing to be nearly as weak as a normal human again, and to have chosen it, and to be standing in the middle of an army while he did.","|THE Aura of THE Protagonist is registering the change in your condition.|","|You have designated yourself an F-Rank Hunter within a domain containing an army of former True Lifeforms and Infinite Lifeforms, all reduced to the same human baseline. The adversity you now face is calculated against your CURRENT standing, not your true one.|","|You are, functionally, a single human standing alone against tens of thousands of humans, any one of whom could potentially kill you with their bare hands should they reach you. The adversity multiplier has scaled tremendously.|","| Osmontian Biomass generation is climbing accordingly. Current intake: 400,000, and rising as the army grasps its situation. Projected sustained yield while this state holds: in the tens of millions. This is the single richest field THE Aura of THE Protagonist has ever stood upon.|","...!"]},{"number":5543,"title":"Chapter 5543: Chapter 5542: THE Mortal Coil! III","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes gleamed as the golden tide poured into his reserves.","He was farming an entire army by standing in front of it as a man!","And as Hvitrmarr’s claws touched the ground, and the vast White Steed settled her weight onto the scorched earth of THE Ymnaros, Noah stepped forward on her back and looked down at the horrified army, and he spoke, calm and grand.","\" For the first time in your entire existence,\" he said, \" all of you are going to get a feel for what it means to be human.\"","\"...\"","\" No power. No authority. Not for anybody here.\" His gaze swept them. \" Every one of us, absolutely the same, at the exact same baseline.\"","He then he glanced, almost kindly, toward the two craters.","\" For you two, it’s rather unfortunate. You were flying.\" His voice stayed even. \" Falling from a height like that as a human does a great deal of damage. You’ve broken a lot of bones. You very likely have internal bleeding right now, and you have never once in your lives had to know what that is.\"","And Noah looked at the two titanic figures wailing in their craters, and let everyone watch them!","They were experiencing what it meant to be human, and it was horrifying.","Both of them wept, openly, helplessly, tears and snot running down enormous faces as they sobbed and wailed from a pain so far past anything in their experience that their minds had nowhere to put it. Beings that had spent ages as apex existences, that had split their enemies open and reanimated the dead for sport, reduced to sobbing humans in the dirt because a nerve was doing the job a nerve does!","And neither of them could make it stop, and neither of them understood that it would not simply stop the way everything unpleasant had always stopped for them before.","And every being in the garden watched, in horrified silence, as though the two were being held up as examples.","And their conditions were getting worse.","One of them, Noah saw now, had come down wrong. When it had first lifted off the terraces to rise, its own ascent had shoved a jagged shelf of rock up out of the broken ground, and when the power died and it fell, it had come down onto that shelf neck-first, and the stone had gone into the side of its throat, and now, as a human, it was bleeding from the neck in long steady pulses that darkened the scorched earth around its head.","The garden watched it bleed.","The wailing from that one grew weaker.","The screams thinned into whimpers, and the whimpers into a wet shallow breathing, and the enormous body that had thrashed in its crater began to move less, and then less, and then only its chest, and then the pulses from its throat slowed to match, and across a garden full of beings that had never watched anything of their own kind die of something as small and stupid as a rock, an Infinite True Lifeform cried quieter and quieter until it stopped, and lay still!","The surviving titan, broken in its own crater, turned its weeping face and watched its companion go still, and the terror that came over its features then was a wholly new thing in that ancient face, because it had finally understood that the pain it was in was not a punishment that would end but a process that was going somewhere, and that the somewhere was where the other one had just gone.","Death!","Noah stepped down off Hvitrmarr and walked toward it.","He walked grandly across the ruined gold, a small figure crossing a giant’s graveyard, and he looked up at the surviving True Lifeform with an expression that was almost gentle, and he explained to it what was happening.","\"A human body holds about five liters of blood. You can lose a little and feel nothing. Lose about a third of it, and the body starts to panic, the heart races trying to move what isn’t there, everything goes cold from the outside in as the body gives up its edges to protect its center.\" He nodded toward the still corpse.","\" Your friend lost it out of the neck, which is fast. Past about half, the center can’t be protected either, and the whole thing simply shuts down, one system at a time, while you stay awake for most of it.\"","He let the silence hold.","\" The pain you’re feeling right now, the pain that’s so big you can’t think around it, a human feels a version of that from a broken arm. One arm. You have broken most of what you have, and you’re bleeding on the inside where nothing can reach it, and your body is going to spend the next while shutting its own doors one by one while you feel every single one close .\" His voice did not rise.","\" That’s what you are, underneath. That’s what all of you always were, underneath. This is... the mortal coil.\"","HUUM!","And around him, the Infinite Lifeforms of the host moved backwards!","They stepped away from him, thousands of them, this small unarmed human walking through their ruined battlefield describing death like a thing he had studied!","But....a certain Infinite True Lifeform was not finished.","WAA!","Ashkavaal moved.","She jumped from where she stood at the base of the obelisk and crossed the whole ruined distance in a single human leap of a giant’s body, and she came down in front of Noah and rose to her full height.","She was titanic, more than five times the height of the man standing in front of her, a mountain in the shape of a woman even with every river of Infinity dimmed off her skin, and she looked down at him with her stained hands and her somber cold face.","\" You said we are all human here .\" Her voice came low and level. \" For you to lay a domain like this over reality with your own Pantheon, you must be bound by it too. That is how it works. That is how it always works. \"","\"...\"","\" So. We may all be humans here.\" Her dimmed eyes fixed on the small figure below her. \" But we are not all equal. You are still a bug compared to me. A human bug in front of a human mountain.\" Her stained fingers curled. \"Let me give you a taste of your own medicine.\"","...!","A titanic Infinite Lifeform stripped of every shred of her power, and still a giant, still a mountain of a body that could close one hand around Noah entirely, glaring down at THE True Human Emperor who stood barely a fraction of her size in the ruined gold!","And Noah, small, human, smiled coldly.","Behind him, larger than the Infinite Lifeforms and larger than the corpses, THE White Steed did not move a single muscle as she stared down at Ashkavaal over the top of Noah’s head, one gold eye fixed on the giant who had just made a decision.","In a domain where all of existence had been brought down to the human condition, to the mortal...","Someone wanted to step on THE True Human Emperor?!"]},{"number":5544,"title":"Chapter 5544: Chapter 5543: THE Mortal Coil! IV","paragraphs":["Ashkavaal’s hand came down to squish him.","It was the size of a small mountain and it moved with the full unhurried confidence of a being who had just done the math and found a human at the bottom of it, and it reached for Noah to close around him and be done with the whole ridiculous afternoon!","And Noah calmly read out a skill he had used years ago in dungeons.","\" Fireball.\"","HUUM!","A ball of deeply cerulean flame formed in the air in front of him.","It was small, the humble first spell of a Rank F Hunter who did not yet know he would one day bring back Observable Existences and Steeds, except the mana feeding it now was Osmontian Source Infinity drawn through the narrow straw the domain allowed him, and even a single river of THAT ocean was not the same thing as a beginner’s mana at all.","The cerulean fireball smashed into Ashkavaal’s descending palm and flung the titanic hand away, scorched black across its whole surface, the giant’s arm knocked wide.","And Noah moved brutally.","More cerulean fireballs erupted in the air in front of him like bullets leaving a barrel, one after another after another, a stream of them, and they slammed upward into Ashkavaal’s chest and her body was shockingly thrown up into the air by the impacts, a mountain of a woman lifted clean off her feet!","And while she hung there more of them came in from other angles, fireballs curving in on separate trajectories that Noah’s narrow trickle of Infinity guided true, each one landing with a heavy wet impact that burst skin and blew muscle apart in cerulean flashes!","She could not scream in time. She could barely fall in time!","By the time THE Second Breath came back down she was no longer recognizable as a woman or as anything, only a spinning mass of ruined flesh turning over in the air, and it smashed down onto the scorched land seconds later and did not move, and there was no sign of life left in it at all!","Oh!","The most powerful Infinite True Lifeform in the garden. Dead! Killed by the first spell Noah had ever learned!","...!","A heavy silence spread across the whole ruin.","Noah stood in the middle of it, and he turned slowly and let his gaze move across all of them, every ashen face in the army.","\" Kneel ,\" he said, \" and your deaths will be quick.\"","...!","HUUM!","The words were heavy!","Then one of the Infinite True Lifeforms reined in its fear, and threw back its head, and roared.","\"HE IS ONLY ONE MAN! \" it bellowed across the army with fear and rage!","\" There are TENS OF THOUSANDS of us! SWARM THIS MOTHERFUCKER!\"","And the army came!","And Noah...waded into it.","What followed was not a battle so much as a demonstration, brutal and one-sided and moving, a single human body crossing an army and unmaking it as it went. He reinforced himself where he needed to, pulling his narrow rivers of Osmontian Source Infinity across his skin an instant before impact so that a giant’s fist that should have pulped him instead broke itself on him.","Then he punched back, and where his fist landed the body of an Infinite Lifeform simply exploded, ages of existence blown apart by a jab!","He moved through them and they died.","He turned and threw a barrage of cerulean fireballs into a knot of charging shapes and they came apart in the air. He ducked under a swung arm and drove his palm up through a torso and out the other side. And at one point, hemmed in on every side by rushing bodies, Noah raised his hand and uttered a single word.","\" Sever.\"","HUUM!","A bolt of blue lightning released from his hand, and it chained.","It leapt from body to body across the packed host, hundreds of them, jumping conductor to conductor exactly the way it had jumped across many enemies a lifetime ago, and every Infinite Lifeform it touched exploded as it passed through, a line of bursting bodies chasing the bolt across the battlefield!","Noah watched it chain and felt something warm and strange move through him.","Nostalgia.","He had loved this spell!","So he cast it again.","\" Sever.\"","HUUM!","And again the blue lightning chained across the rushing army, and again hundreds of them burst apart along its path, and it was pure one-sided brutality, a man walking through an army of humans!","And after a certain point, it broke them.","Noah cut down the last surviving Infinite True Lifeform, and he cut down more than eighty percent of the entire army.","The rushing tide that had been trying to swarm him simply stopped, and reversed, and the beings who had come to end the reinforcements began to back away, and then to run, terror finally beating out fury as they fled across the ruined gardens in every direction!","Noah gazed at all of them coldly.","Anaximander came to stand beside him in the sudden quiet, stepping over a scorched corpses, his anger cooled back into the mild watchful thing Noah knew.","\"I didn’t jump in because...\" the scholar said, looking out at the fleeing remnants . \"It seemed like you wanted to experience something . Thank you for intervening.\"","Noah nodded calmly.","He turned away from the scattering army, following the direction of Anaximander’s gaze, toward the obelisk that still shone its steady blue-gold through all the ruin.","Toward Theron Adranos.","The golden-haired man stood before the shrine, in the midst of the corpses of his own people, and he was looking at Noah with a heavy gaze. He nodded once to Anaximander, an acknowledgment between two who clearly knew each other, and then he spoke toward Noah.","\"I cannot thank you enough for the intervention.\" His voice was low and worn . \"I wish to take a moment to bury my brethren here. We are born ordinary in these lands, and we die ordinary in these lands. \"","He looked down at the white and blue bodies scattered around the obelisk’s base. \" Sir Anaximander. Could you lend me a hand?\"","...!"]},{"number":5545,"title":"Chapter 5545: Chapter 5544: Extinction I","paragraphs":["Anaximander crossed to the dead and looked down at them, and began to help.","Noah stood in the middle of a field of corpses and took one more breath of it. There was a human satisfaction in standing in the aftermath of a thing he had done with almost no effort, and he let himself have it a moment longer. Brutal as the field was, it was human too. Humans were bloody. Humans were not always pretty.","Hvitrmarr walked over to him the ordinary way, on four legs across the ruin. Without her authority she was still enormous, and she crushed corpse after corpse flat beneath her without noticing she did it. On the ridge of her spine Ryaenara held on and did everything she could not to be thrown off a moving reptile, looking down at Noah and shaking her head at the whole scene.","The grand prompts bloomed in front of him.","|Adversity resolved. THE Aura of THE Protagonist final tally for the engagement:|","| Osmontian Biomass gained: 61,400,000.|","|You faced an army as a single human at F-Rank standing. The adversity multiplier held at its peak throughout. This is the richest single harvest THE Aura of THE Protagonist has produced.|","| Total Osmontian Biomass reserves: 86,400,000.|","...!","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has been triggered.|","|You have granted death to True Lifeforms and to thousands of Infinite Lifeforms. Death, cleanly given to those who had earned an ending, is its own kind of giving, and the Tide answers giving of every kind. A boon is returned, and it has taken a shape.|","HUUM!","Something spun out of the settling gold and dropped into his open palm.","An obsidian blue necklace, a single dark stone on a fine dark cord. The stone did not hold still. Inside it Infinity turned over and over, an ocean of it folded into a jewel small enough to close a hand around, cerulean light moving in its depths the way light moves in deep water, far down and alive.","| THE Woven Return: THE Tessellated Heart of the Borrowed Flame.|","|A necklace holding a contained thread of Infinity. It arrives interlinked with the knowledge of what you just witnessed.|","|Every Infinite Lifeform you faced drew their Infinity, without knowing it, from a single distant being. A Descendant of Those Who Remain, whose entire existence is Infinity that it lends outward across multitudes who mistake the loan for a possession. Its designation, carried to you along this necklace’s own borrowed thread: THE Infinity Eater.|","|Infinity is not something it has. Infinity is something it is. It has spread thin threads of itself into every wielder who draws Infinity without a source of their own, and it feels through each one, and what it lends it owns, and what it owns it may reclaim, or wear, or drown from the inside, at any moment it chooses. Any being who wields Infinity without a well of their own is a mouth THE Infinity Eater has not yet decided to close.|","|The necklace is itself a strand of that borrowed flame, contained and yours. Through it, one who holds sufficient Infinity of their own may reach along the threads to their far end and send a message to THE Infinity Eater directly. Should you even send a message though? Why would you?|","...!","Noah went still, turning the stone over in his fingers.","His own Infinity had a source. It came from his Infinite Cause, seated inside him. It had never occurred to him that this was a defense. But it was! A power he had made himself had no thread running out of it, and a thing with no thread could not be reached down and reclaimed. There was no loan. There was no lender. He owned himself completely!","The thing at the far end of ten thousand borrowed threads was another matter. Noah frowned at the stone, and set the problem down as he let THE MORTAL COIL go.","The Word drew back into him like a tide pulling off a shore. Across the gardens the weight of the world returned. Power welled up again in everything still alive to hold it, in Ryaenara, who drew a sharp breath as her existence came back to her, in Hvitrmarr, whose reined weight settled once more against her scales, in Noah himself, his ocean widening back from a single river to the full crowned depth of THE Quintessential Osmontian.","And as it did, something buzzed.","\" Oh?\"","Noah paused, surprised as he felt a small insistent vibration, from something he had put away. He waved a hand and took it out.","The tiny egg. The Tide’s reward for the resuscitation of Hvitrmarr, the strange small thing he had tucked away! It sat trembling in his palm at a high frequency, and an utterly despotic and ancient aura began to rise off it!","The egg cracked.","The shell split along a seam that had not been there a moment before, and a beam of gray light shot up out of it, straight up past Hvitrmarr’s height and higher, until it stopped at a point in the sky.","HUUM!","There, the point folded inward, drawing space toward a center that felt less like a place than a wound. Gray threads thick as rivers pulled in from everywhere at once and lashed themselves around it, layer over crossing layer, until a webbed cocoon hung over the gardens of THE Ymnaros like a second sky, and the ancient weight that had leaked from the egg now poured off the cocoon in a steady tide.","Everything below went still!","Out at the edges of the ruin, the last fleeing remnants of the army simply fell, and where they fell they began to rot. Theron Adranos straightened from the grave he was digging. Anaximander turned, and his mild face went heavy. Ryaenara said a word in a language older than the Scales, low, under her breath. And Hvitrmarr, who had faced down an army of giants without moving a muscle, took one slow step back!","The cocoon opened.","The webbing unwound itself strand by strand, without hurry, as though the thing inside had waited long enough that a few moments more cost it nothing!","What came out of it was enormous, and it was old, old the way the bottom of the sea is old. It unfolded against the sky in a body built for a war by an age that had lost the war anyway.","Gray flesh like weathered stone, scarred in places where the scars had scars. Plates that had grown across it rather than been forged onto it. Too many limbs, each too long.","Hanging off it and swaying were chains and cords and rags of materials no one living could have named, the wreckage of old bindings it had broken or simply outlasted.","Across its eyes was a blindfold made of hands.","Small ones, mummified and gray, hundreds of them layered palm over palm around the titan’s head, fingers laced into fingers in a pattern nothing sane had arranged. Whether the hands were there to keep existence out of its eyes or to keep its eyes off existence was not a question the sight of it invited anyone to ask.","It matched no taxonomy. It looked foreign down to the bone, ancient and wrong!","Even Noah was shaken. He stood in his field of corpses with the cracked egg still warm in his palm and looked up at the thing, and for a moment did nothing else.","Then the titan moved. It lowered itself out of the sky with the same slow dignity, and came down before Noah with a weight the ground took in silence because the ground had no other option. And without a sound, it knelt. It folded its too-many limbs and brought the blindfolded head low, down and down, until the band of gray hands hung level with the small human standing in the ruined gold, and there it held, kneeling, silent as the deep!","...!","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has completed a Woven Return long held in reserve.|","| The reward: an extinct lifeform.|","|At the core of its existence sit 36 Causes. They are not the Causes as you know them. They are Blighted Causes and Calcified Causes .|","|It is loyal only to you. It can come whenever it is called, from wherever it is, across whatever stands between.|","|How this Return was woven: when you resuscitated Hvitrmarr, you resuscitated a Cursed Lifeform bound to Those Who Remain, and you did it through replacement, collapsing terminal Causes and seating new ones. That act altered cause and effect across existence and time. Weavings of that shape had not moved through existence since the age this lifeform died in. The Tide followed them back to the only thing they still resembled, found this, and began the long work of returning it to you. The egg was that work. It has been maturing since the moment she was cured.|","| What is known of its history: it, and all others like it, were driven to extinction by the direct order of Those Who Remain.|","|Any further information...|","|...has been blocked.|","|The extinct lifeform has closed the record with its own will, and has given a single reason for doing so.|","|It wishes to introduce itself to you.|","...!"]},{"number":5546,"title":"Chapter 5546: Chapter 5545: Extinction II","paragraphs":["Noah looked up at the thing that had knelt to him, and gave it an order.","\" Introduce yourself to me.\"","HUUM!","The hands moved. The band of small gray palms laced across the titan’s eyes unlaced itself finger from finger, slow and deliberate, and where it parted a gray light began to leak, thin at first and then steady, spilling down the ruined gardens like water finding its level.","Behind him, Ryaenara made no sound. When Noah caught her face at the edge of his vision the humor had gone out of it, and under the stillness sat something he would have called fear on anyone else. At the foot of the obelisk, Anaximander had stopped working. Theron Adranos stood beside him, and both men had gone gray in the face.","The light reached Noah, and everything stopped.","Existence caught and held around him, the way it did when he stretched an instant thin to think inside it, except he had not done this. His vision folded and reopened somewhere that was not the gardens of THE Ymnaros. The light of the sky here came from a source he could not find, and the air carried the weight of a place a long way back, counted in years he had no number for!","He stood in a dark sky. Beside him, filling half of what he could see, hung the visage of the extinct lifeform, no longer kneeling and no longer small against anything, present the way a mountain is present.","It spoke, and the voice came up through him rather than into him.","\" Consider a flame, \" Damodred said. \" You would say it is a thing. It has a name, it has a shape, you could point to it. And yet a flame is not a thing at all. It is an event. It is something that is happening, burning itself forward moment to moment, and the instant it stops happening there is no flame left over to bury. There is only the dark where it was.\"","The great head turned, unhurried.","\"I am Damodred. And once, I was happening. I was grand, if you like the word, though grandeur is only a flame that has learned to admire itself. We were known as the Laestrygonians. And there came a day when Those Who Remain decided that our particular fire was one that existence could do without.\"","...!","Below them, an ancient domain unfolded.","It came up out of the dark in pieces, the way a drowned country surfaces, and Noah understood he was being shown a corpse dressed in the memory of when it had been a home. Cities and whole Dimensions at once, climbing across a black plain in tiers built to outlast the ground beneath them, towers of dark seamed stone that had been grown rather than cut, each rooted downward into the plain by structures that ran out of sight.","Roads worn to a shine by feet no longer present ran between them. Rivers carried the same gray light the titan bled. And over all of it hung a sky crowded with more cities, hung upside down from nothing, their lights answering the lights below.","\" Watch them, my first and new Master\" Damodred said, gentle as a man pointing out a bird. \" And ask yourself what a people is. It is a pattern that has decided to keep itself. That is all. A shape that insists, against everything, on continuing to be that shape.\"","The people moved through the memory in their millions, built like Damodred, huge and gray and scarred even in their prime, a race that seemed to have come into existence already looking like the survivors of something. And they were strong.","Each of them held Causes at the core of their existence, and the Causes were wrong in a precise and terrible way, wounded and then hardened, the same 36 that sat inside Damodred now.","The memory showed what that meant when it was tested.","A Primeval Lifeform came down on one of the hanging Dimensions, apex because earliest, its weavings sitting beneath every framework these people climbed. And the Laestrygonians met it in their thousands and took it apart, their calcified Causes refusing to yield to a thing that expected all younger things to yield as a matter of course.","\" The oldest things in existence assume the young will bow,\" Damodred said. \" It is a reasonable assumption. It is almost always correct. We were the place the assumption went to die.\"","Whatever came for them, they came out on top. They prospered. Their Dimensions climbed and hung and shone, and for an age no power in existence could make them kneel.","Then the memory changed its light, and Noah knew, before it showed him, that he was about to watch it end.","Armies of Descendants veiled in shifting many-colored light descended.","They came in numbers the memory did not trouble to count, filling the crowded sky between the upside-down Dimensions, and at their head moved something the Laestrygonians had no name for beyond the one it was given. The memory could render it only as an absence, a place in the sky where the light declined to go, and out of that place a voice reached down across the whole domain.","|Your lifeform is vile, and not conducive to existence. Perish.|","HUUM!","\" That was the first time we heard that voice, and the last. You will notice,\" Damodred said, and here for the first time the calm thinned, not into rage but into something more precise beneath it, \" that it did not threaten us. A threat is a kind of respect. A threat admits you are real enough to be argued with. It simply announced.\"","Noah watched the extinction the way Damodred needed him to watch it, without looking away.","The calcified Causes that had thrown down Primevals held, at first. The Dimensions that had stood longer than their own ground held. And then, one by one, they stopped holding, because the thing in the sky was not fighting them. It was overruling them. It unmade the sentence of their existence with the flat authority of a lineage that believed existence was theirs.","The hanging Dimensions came down into the standing ones. The gray light in the rivers went dark. The millions who had never once knelt were made to stop, ended and struck out of the record of what was permitted to be.","\" Death ...\" Damodred said over the ruin, softly, \" almost no one who fears it understands it, because fear is a poor teacher. Death is not the enemy of life. Death is the shape life makes at its edge, the way the shore is the shape the sea makes where it stops. To live is to be the kind of thing that ends. We knew this. We had made our peace with the shore. \" The voice cooled by a single degree.","\" What was done to us was not death. Death would have been ours. This was a hand reaching in from outside the whole arrangement to declare that our particular wave was not allowed to have broken in the first place. That is not an ending as much as it is an erasure of the beginning. And that, I have never made peace with.\"","The memory slowed.","It showed a last work, carried out in the dark while the domain came down around it. The Laestrygonians reaching into their own dying Causes and laying something inside them, a marking, a seed, the memory of themselves written into the one part of existence that might outlast everything.","\" We laid our Existential Genetic Markers into our Causes,\" Damodred said. \" Think of a message placed not in a bottle but in the tide itself. We could not choose when it would wash up, or where, or into whose hands. We could only trust that existence is fond of repeating its rare accidents, and that one day, somewhere far ahead, Causes strange enough would meet and mingle in just the way ours once had, and stir what we had left sleeping.\"","The uncovered gray eyes found Noah at last.","\" You, The Master, have grasped the markers of our Causes. What you did to the Steed sent that old shape back through existence, like a note struck once, long ago, sounding again. I am the first to wake to it.\"","The dark sky held around them, and the ruined domain hung below, and the titan told him what it wanted!","\"I place myself at your service. And I ask one thing in return. It need not be soon. I know the weight of what I ask.\"","\" The dissolution of the one who put out the flame of my people. THE Sleepless Fiend, and every Progeny it fathered. Root and line. This...is what I seek.\"","BOOM!","Noah stood in the memory of a murdered people, and the extinct thing beside him waited on his answer.","\" Does The Master believe... such a thing is possible? Can it be done?\"","...!"]},{"number":5547,"title":"Chapter 5547: Chapter 5546: What is a Cause?","paragraphs":["Did he believe it was possible?","To move against the Progeny of one of Those Who Remain, and against the very ancient entity that had fathered them across the dark of epochs...","THE Sleepless Fiend of Those Who Remain...!","As the fiendish ancient aura of THE Primeval Osmontian Marrow rippled softly across his hair, Noah evaluated everything, knowing he was already hunted by the Cursed Descendants of THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension and realizing the Fiend’s lineage ran through that exact same cursed blood!","He had already made an enemy of one branch of Those Who Remain simply by existing well! The question was never whether adding another branch was dangerous, but what it actually cost when stacked atop an active war he was already fighting, and as he weighed the outcome in the quiet depths of his mind, the added weight was smaller than it looked.","His existence answered before his mouth ever opened, his Intent leaning forward without hesitation as he looked down at the enormous scarred titan.","\"In existence ,\" Noah said, \" anything is possible. I won’t make you a definitive promise. But this is something we can work toward.\"","HUUM!","The veil of severed hands twitched as Damodred bowed heavily, his colossal frame of petrified muscle and calcified scars folding down further than any kneel, sending a tremor through the ruined strata of the domain!","The titan showed nothing aloud, yet Noah could feel the boundless loss and ancient rage churning behind that calm exterior, for this ancient being was also human by its own unyielding definition!","Noah let him have the moment, standing composed amidst the falling ochre dust before asking what he truly sought from this antiquity.","\" Tell me about Causes,\" Noah said, his eyes glowing with the fiendish light of THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard as he looked up into the uncovered gray eyes.","\"I know First Causes, and the Prime Causes seated under them. I know Miniature Causes. Now I am hearing of Calcified Causes and Blighted ones. Enlighten me.\"","The veil twitched again as Damodred nodded, waving one massive, scarred hand as the dark sky and ruined basalt domain thinned away into a clean gray space of absolute nothingness- a realm constructed purely for showing rather than remembering!","\" You already know more than most,\" Damodred spoke, his voice carrying the deep, melancholic resonance of an ancient being.","\" So let me begin where the question truly begins.\"","As the giant opened his great hand, a single point of pristine light ignited in the empty gray space, hovering between them like a living star!","\" Before a Dimension or Observable Existence can hold so much as one beam of light, before space can even trouble itself to stretch across the void, there must first be a reason that space is permitted to exist at all. A reason. That reason is what we name a Cause.\"","The point of light held firm, small and certain amidst the gray expanse!","\" In the low realms this is easy to miss, for down there crude matter and crude energy are enough to hold a realm together on their own, allowing a lifeform to spend a whole existence believing power is only a matter of how much Primordial Source or energy it has managed to gather. But climb. Climb high enough into higher dimensionality, and you find that physical law is far too thin to bear the weight it is asked to carry.\"","As Damodred spoke, the point of light swelled into a small, turning realm, and Noah watched as a hairline crack ran through its fragile physics.","\" An Observable Existence carries a staggering conceptual weight, not merely of mass but of meaning, so immense it ought to fall to nameless foam the instant it forms. It does not fall apart only because a Cause holds it. A Cause is the origin point, the true beginning underneath the beginning, the anchor that grants all that weight its permission to stand\"","The hairline crack sealed instantly, and the small realm steadied and shone with declared grandeur.","\" As lifeforms rise, they learn this truth in stages. First they think power is only pulling on Mana, on Infinity, or on THE Primordial Source. Then, higher, they learn to weave a Cause into their Pulses, their Infinity, their Source, and their Intent, swinging it like an absolute blade to force reality into compliance.\"","The gray eyes held steady on Noah, reflecting ages of witnessed war.","\" And then there are the existences who go past merely using a Cause. Beings whose bones and blood and organs are forged out of these anchors themselves.\"","Noah thought of the colossal white dragon whose back he rode across dimensional gaps.","\" Steeds ,\" Noah said.","\" Steeds ,\" Damodred agreed, and the word carried the heavy weight of an ancient ossuary. \"I know this because Master’s curing of one is the very reason THE Tide That Owes Nothing pulled me across existence to your side. A living Observable Existence, seated out of pure Causes at the root of its lineage, shaped from the first moment to bear a burden that would turn any ordinary entity to vapor. You ride the proof of it even now. And now...\"","The titan raised a second finger as three more points of light ignited beside the shining realm, hovering in the gray space like patient beacons.","\" To understand how existence truly moves, you must know that a Cause is not one fixed thing. It can take four states or more.\"","The first point brightened into a clean, cold, unwavering illumination!","\" First Causes. The pristine anchors, seated at the very beginning of a lineage or a framework, carrying the pure and uncorrupted intent of the ones who first carved existence into being. A First Cause does not easily degrade. Its authority is immutable, the original blueprint, untouched by time, holding forever the full weight of the moment it was carved.\"","The second point began to pulse with a warm, living rhythm, its light shifting from moment to moment like a burning heart!","\" Prime Causes. The living anchors seated beneath the First. Where a First Cause is a legacy handed down from ancestors, a Prime Cause is a present will, active and evolving, able to steer its own progression. If the First Cause is the legacy, the Prime Cause is the wielder alive now, still deciding what it will become.\"","Noah nodded slowly, understanding his own nine Cause weavings with Hvitrmarr with greater clarity!","Then the third point of light changed, and Noah’s attention sharpened as the illumination did not brighten, but sickened into an ochre hue!","A dark, corruptive thread wound through its center, and where the thread passed, the light frayed and wept like an open wound.","\" Blighted Causes. A Blighted Cause is not some clean anchor that was later dirtied. It is born to its nature, a kind of Cause the same as any other, save that its nature is rot. It does not stop working. It goes on holding weight, and all the while it leaks rot and agony into the existence built atop it, consuming that existence slowly from the anchor outward while never once failing at its task.\"","Damodred turned his great hand, and an image formed in the gray, depicting a colossal Laestrygonian titan whose chest glowed with a diseased, burning color as fine dark lines spidered along its calcified frame.","\" An example! One of my own bore a Cause we named THE Ember That Eats the Hearth. It anchored him faithfully, and all the while it burned him from the middle out, a low constant fire that never caught and never went out, and he held an entire Dimension upright on that agony for a full age. \" The gray eyes were unblinking.","\" The blight is not weakness. It is a strength that charges you everything, forever.\"","The sick picture faded as the fourth point took its place, having gone entirely the other direction! It stopped moving completely, hanging hard, pale, and utterly still, and looking upon it, Noah felt the cold density of ancient, petrified bone!","\" Calcified Causes...\"","\" Their nature is stillness, and out of that stillness comes a density I would struggle to describe. It becomes an absolute wall. Force arrives and finds nothing to push, for there is nothing left in it that can move to be pushed.\"","He conjured a barrier of pale calcified stone, and against it, the memory of a Primeval Lifeform striking down played out, the strike stopping instantly, the way a roaring wave stops against an ancient cliff that does not even know it is being struck!","\" A Calcified Cause cannot adapt. It cannot evolve. It cannot yield, which sounds like a virtue until you remember that a thing which cannot yield can also never grow.\"","The gray eyes returned to Noah, and something in the titan’s old voice turned at last toward the truth it had been circling all along.","\" And I am made of these. Many of them. By every law you know, Master, I have no business standing here speaking with you at all, for a being built of Calcified Causes is a being that cannot progress. I ought to be static. Immense, unkillable at my own tier, and frozen...a mountain that will never be anything but the same mountain until existence itself forgets it.\"","Damodred opened both his great hands, and the two dark images returned side by side...the weeping blighted light and the pale frozen stone.","\" My Calcified Causes are stone. But my Blighted Causes are fire, that low agonizing fire that never once goes out. And a stone set against a fire that will not stop does not stay merely a stone!\"","The two lights began to turn against one another in a violent, grinding orbit, and where the weeping fire touched the frozen stone, the stone shifted, forced to move by the unyielding pain pressed against its structure!","\" The blight spurs the calcification. The agony catalyzes the stone. We could not grow the way the living grow, through nourishment and will, so we grew the only way left to the damned...through pain and endurance, one forcing the other ever forward. The Laestrygonians persevered into grandeur upon nothing but the refusal of two wounds to let each other rest.\"","Damodred let the images fade, the gray space holding silent.","\" That is what I am, Master. A dead pattern that taught its own scars to keep climbing. It is not a gift. But it is mine. And now, in a way, it is yours.\"","And as the weight of the titan’s ancient truth settled over the empty domain, Noah looked upon all of it with shining eyes!"]},{"number":5548,"title":"Chapter 5548: Chapter 5547: Collision!","paragraphs":["Damodred regarded him from behind the veil of ancient, severed hands.","\"If an old dead thing may offer the Master a recommendation.\"","The great head inclined slowly, sending a subtle shudder through the empty gray domain.","\" You have been trying to do something, and it has not been working. You hold two sets of Causes right now, do you not? Nine of your own, seated in your Infinite Cause. And nine more, the First Causes of THE Steed you cured, which now stand behind you.\"","The gray eyes held Noah with unblinking, ancient focus.","\" You have been trying to mix them. To fuse the two sets into one. And they will not fuse, Master, no matter how you press them, because they cannot. They are not the same kind, and no amount of will makes a stone into a fire.\"","Noah said nothing, for the titan was right. He had felt that exact conceptual resistance within his own existence.","\" But... \" Damodred spoke, opening one massive, scarred palm as the atmospheric density of the gray space deepened.","\" My own Causes could never fuse either. Yet I taught them to collide instead, to strike against one another forever, and out of that endless collision came all our grandeur. You could do the same. Not fuse your nine Prime Causes and THE Steed’s nine First Causes. Collide them. Set them crashing into each other without end, so that the push and pull of the impact pours their benefit straight into your existence, elevating you endlessly and feeding you adversity from the inside for as long as you live.\"","The old voice carried a terrible, unyielding calm that resonated through the strata of the void!","\" Give yourself an eternal wound that heals into strength. You could climb higher than THE Laestrygonians ever did. You have living Causes where mine were only wounds and stone. You... could become grander than we were at our height.\"","Noah’s lemniscate-ringed eyes sharpened, his gaze locking onto the titan with sudden, predatory intensity!","\" How?\"","\" To collide your own Causes, you must command them. And Causes do not answer just any voice. They answer only the voice of the existence they belong to, spoken in that existence’s own tongue.\"","He waved a colossal hand, and in the empty gray space, a shape of pure, resonant sound seemed to hang, vibrating with the ancient authority of an uncarved script!","\" There are many kinds of Tongue across existence. But a True Tongue is a particular thing, Master, and a simple one once you see it plainly. A True Tongue is nothing more than your own personal language of your own existence . It is you, saying yourself. Those who have raised their Pantheons and begun to lay down their weavings of time speak it most easily, because by then their existence has already learned to repeat itself, and a True Tongue is only your existence repeating itself out loud, on purpose.\"","The gray eyes did not blink as the giant continued, delivering the mechanics of an extinct epoch without hesitation!","\" Speak your own tongue. Fill the words with the intent to steer your Causes toward collision. That is all the command is.\"","Damodred paused, his voice hardening without softening the truth.","\" And it will hurt. At first it will feel as though your existence is detonating inside you, because in a way it is. But acclimate to it, endure the first shock and do not flinch away, and when it settles you will hold many Causes that empower you every moment you draw breath. This is the very art that got my people extinguished. It made us too grand to be permitted.\"","He raised a single, scarred finger, teacherly once more.","\" And...simply striking the Causes against each other is not enough. A blow is not a reaction. For a true reaction to happen, three conditions must be met, all of them, together.\"","He counted them off, and as his fingers moved, the gray space displayed three points of light knocking against one another in a slow, precise demonstration!","\" First, collision frequency. The Causes must actually crash into one another, again and again, not drift past. Second, sufficient energy. Each collision must carry enough force to break the old bonds and forge new ones, or the Causes simply touch and part unchanged. Third, correct orientation. The Causes must align perfectly in dimensional space, so that the reactive parts of each one truly meet, and not merely their edges.\"","As Noah watched, the demonstration in the gray space came together, two points striking at the exact speed, at the exact angle, and with sufficient force, generating a sudden, glorious bloom of new light that expanded through the gray!","\" Frequency. Energy. Orientation.\"","Damodred let the three conditions sit in the air between them, his voice echoing softly.","\" Why does the Master not give it a try?\"","...!","Noah did not hesitate, his mind already three steps ahead as the realization settled into his core, for the answer had been sitting in his own mouth the entire time!","His True Tongue! The personal language of his own existence, the language that was only Noah Osmont saying Noah Osmont out loud! What was it, truly, but THE Osmontian Tongue?! Five Letters and one Word! He had spent this entire journey learning to speak himself into reality!","Was this also the gibberish he heard from Ryaenara when he first met her? It was simply her speaking with her own tongue?","Noah closed his eyes and he began!","He uttered the Letters low and grand, a rising mantra of absolute sovereignty echoing through the empty domain!","\"I AM OSMONT. I AM QUINTESSENTIAL. I AM HUMAN. I AM THE PROTAGONIST!\"","HUUM!","And following them, the Word sang out from his soul!","\"I AM THE MORTAL COIL. I AM! I AM! I AM!\"","WAA!","He did not speak them as mere names this time. He spoke them as a supreme command, pouring his full Ananke Intent into every syllable, the intent to take the eighteen Causes inside him and drive them into one another like particles hurled together in an existential accelerator, bending frequency, energy, and orientation to his unyielding will...!","BOOM!","His existence detonated!"]},{"number":5549,"title":"Chapter 5549: Chapter 5548: Lapse! I","paragraphs":["The first attempt threw his focus backward! It was exactly as Damodred had promised and worse, a nuclear tempest of pure conceptual force going off inside his own being as his Causes slammed together too hard, at broken angles, the raw energy of the collisions finding nowhere clean to discharge as his whole existence shuddered under the strain as though it might tear apart!","He gritted his teeth, refusing to flinch, his eyes blazing with cerulean-crimson light as he spoke the mantra again!","\"I AM OSMONT. I AM QUINTESSENTIAL. I AM HUMAN. I AM THE PROTAGONIST!\"","HUUM!","The second attempt was better! The third better still! And somewhere in the reciting, as his Ananke Intent discovered how to align the reactive faces of one Cause directly into another, the chaotic detonations stabilized!","It became a rhythm.","A glorious, magisterial rhythm!","Eighteen Causes, nine of his own Prime Causes and nine First Causes of THE Steed, began to collide inside his existence under the three absolute conditions the titan had named! They crashed together at the right speed, at the right angle, and often enough to matter, over and over, and wherever they struck, they bloomed into glorious, cascading light.","Multicolored waves poured off the impacts, and multicolored strings sang out across his inner world, every wave and every string carrying a tremendous, ancient density that washed over the whole of his existence as the weight of ages pressed into him from within.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","It was like endless cosmic drums beginning to beat within his soul, a rhythm of perpetual collision without pause, and from every crash of Cause on Cause, the waves and strings spilled outward as though whole singularities were being born inside him with each passing nanosecond!","| You have grasped an ancient art unique to THE Laestrygonians. Analysis follows.|","|THE COLLISION OF CAUSES has begun. Rather than fusing your nine Prime Causes and the nine First Causes of THE Steed, you are now driving all eighteen into perpetual, structured collision, governed by frequency, energy, and orientation, commanded through THE Osmontian Tongue as your True Tongue.|","|Effect: with every passing second, you grow stronger. Not in one facet, but collectively, across the whole of your existence at once. Every collision feeds its benefit directly into you. All facets rise together, endlessly, for as long as the collision is sustained.|","|Secondary effect: the Osmontian Biomass cost of all future elevation is being reduced, and continues to fall the longer the art runs.|","|Warning retained for the record: this art carries perpetual internal adversity by design. It is the art for which THE Laestrygonians were driven to extinction. It empowers without limit and it costs without end.|","...!","Noah read every word in the prompts, a slow shake of his head accompanying the wonder moving through him even as the internal drums beat on and the ancient, multicolored waves kept washing through his existence!","He looked up at Damodred, his eyes gleaming with quiet, imperial dominance.","\" Just where are you sitting, currently?\" Noah asked, his voice ringing with declared power. \" Show me your power.\"","HUUM!","Noah activated THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard!","Damodred bowed, the veil of severed hands dipping low toward the gray floor.","\" Gladly, Master. Though I would have you understand, I hold but a fraction of what I wielded at my peak. Still. It is not nothing.\"","The Regard settled over the titan, and the Character Sheet bloomed in Noah’s vision like a monument of calcified history!","| CHARACTER SHEET|","|Designation: Damodred. Last of THE Laestrygonians. The First to Return.|","|Standing: a fraction of his living peak, and still immense.|","| Facets of Existence: SS-Rank, Oir. Across the board. Finished craft, exact making, seated in a being that should by every law be frozen.|","|Intent: SS-Rank. THE Autarkis Intent. The third order, sovereignty above inevitability.|","|Pantheon: THE Sepulcher of the Unyielding Dead, SS-Rank . A Pantheon that is not a realm one enters but a graveyard that enters you, seating an opponent inside the accumulated stillness and agony of an extinct people.|","|Core: 36 Causes, Blighted and Calcified both, held in perpetual collision every moment of his existence. The very art he has just taught you, run without pause across ages.|","|Disposition: absolutely loyal to the Master. Grieving, patient, and certain. He does not hurry, because he has already waited longer than most things have existed.|","|Notable thread: he waits, quietly, for the Master to call forth MORE of his kind from extinction. He is the first to return. He does not believe he will be the last. He is content to serve, and to wait, and to see how many Laestrygonians the Master’s Tide might yet pull back into the light.|","...!","It was something utterly surreal to see, and it made Noah take a moment to truly evaluate the wonder that landed on his lap!","But as Causes collided more and more in his existence...new prompts bloomed in Noah’s vision, and these were different, for they were not describing what was, but what was beginning to be!","|Notice. A unique capability is forming at the meeting point of three things: THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian, your Osmontian Source Infinity, and THE Collision of Causes now running perpetually within you.|","|The eighteen Causes crashing inside your existence do not only elevate you. They produce. Every collision births raw power, waves and strings and newborn singularities, and until now that power has poured inward, feeding your ascent. It need not only pour inward.|","|By uttering THE Osmontian Tongue as a mantra, and steering the intent not toward elevation but toward release, you may take the immense power thrown off by each collision and unleash it OUTWARD, as an attack. The particular Causes you drive together determine the shape of what emerges. No two collisions yield the same weapon.|","| This capability is now yours to wield. Designation: THE Cataclysm of Colliding Causes.|","...!","Noah read it, and a slow, imperial smile touched his mouth.","An engine that made him grander with every breath, and now a weapon fired from the same furnace.","He raised one hand toward the empty gray expanse of Damodred’s showing-place, and he spoke the mantra again, low and grand, but this time he bent the intent outward, toward release!","\"I AM OSMONT. I AM QUINTESSENTIAL. I AM HUMAN. I AM THE PROTAGONIST!\"","HUUM!","And inside him, he chose.","He reached into the churning eighteen and seized two, driving them together on purpose, aiming their reactive faces into one another with the frequency and the energy and the orientation the titan had named.","His Prime Cause of Tyranny, and one of Hvitrmarr’s First Causes, the ancient anchor of Valor.","They collided!","BOOM!","And from Noah’s open palm erupted a lance of layered cerulean and gold, a spear of pure dominance shot through with a Steed’s unbreakable courage, and it tore across the gray space and struck the far nothing with a weight that made the whole domain shudder, a strike that did not merely destroy but commanded the space it hit to break, valor lending the tyranny a fearlessness that would not be refused!","Noah’s eyes gleamed!"]},{"number":5550,"title":"Chapter 5550: Chapter 5549: Lapse! II","paragraphs":["<On Those Who Remain>","We are accustomed to viewing existence as a reality where living beings enter from different doorways, distinct and separate from the stage beneath their feet.","Yet this... is the primary illusion. An ocean does not construct waves the way a mason builds a wall; the ocean simply waves, and in doing so, it expresses its own nature.","So it was with Those Who Remain . They were not merely builders standing outside the halls of reality, but the very impulse that caused the dark to tremble and take shape.","Among Those Who Remain, only a few distinct identities survived the erosion of ages to be remembered by name. Among these few, THE Sleepless Fiend was noted as a particularly eccentric existence.","Where others of its kind sought static absolute authority or spoke final decrees, THE Sleepless Fiend was consumed by a curious, playful fascination with the nature of Causes. Rumors across ancient epochs whisper that it treated Causes as living experiments, grafting First Causes into living marrow and weaving foundational anchors into organic forms merely to see what burdens those existences could bear.","It is a narrow view to believe that only those explicitly known as Descendants carry the legacy of Those Who Remain.","Look closely at the staggering spectrum of lifeforms moving across Dimensions and Time. They are not mere accidents of ambient density. In truth, many are the lingering, self-sustaining ripples of those ancient trials: existences whose bodies, instincts, and very identities were carved out of manipulated Causes eons ago, still acting out a play designed by a weaver who refused to sleep.","Among the Descendants of Those Who Remain, many carry names that make epochs tremble, but a rare few sit upon heights so grand that their legends threaten to eclipse the progenitors themselves.","THE Infinity Eater was such an existence . It spun thin, imperceptible threads of itself outward across the weavings of space and time. Across untold multitudes, lifeforms tapped into these delicate threads of Infinity, foolishly mistaking the borrowed tide for their own awakened power.","They knew nothing of the weaver. Through every thread of Infinity woven across the dark, THE Infinity Eater felt every breath, every intent, and every pulse of energy.","Whatever it lent, it could reclaim at a whim. It could wear another’s existence like a fitted garment or drown their soul from the inside without casting a single spell. In truth, any Infinity-wielder who lacked a root or a Source of their own was never a master of power; they were merely a mouth that THE Infinity Eater had not yet decided to close.","There is the record of the Fall of the Pale Dimension, where a colossal alliance of Primeval Ones and True Lifeforms gathered to erase THE Infinity Eater from existence. Thousands of sovereign entities unfurled their immensity, their weapons shining with endless, infinite energy as they encircled him.","THE Infinity Eater stood alone upon a ruined escarpment of petrified earth, silent and unmoving. He did not summon an army. He did not draw a blade. He merely reached out and plucked the threads.","In that singular, terrifying instant, more than half of the opposing army gasped as their own Infinity revolted. Their Trueness caved inward, their Intent shattered in their throats, and their bodies moved against their will as the borrowed force reclaimed its master.","With hollow, silent eyes, more than half of those ancient lords lost control of their existences, turned around, and came to stand beside THE Infinity Eater, drawing their weapons against their former allies.","Let this be the standing lesson for those who seek the heights. Power is never ownerless, and force without a true, personal origin is merely a collar worn by the blind.","Be relentlessly careful to understand the exact root from which your strength springs, and trace the stream back to its source before you drink too deeply. Otherwise, you may lose your existence before you even know it has been claimed.","---","<THE True Human Emperor>","After getting a feel of his existence and its ongoing processes in that space, Noah nodded to the massive visage of Damodred.","\" Let’s go back. \"","The Laestrygonian severed hands blindfold twitched as gray brilliance spilled.","The gray space folded away, and the ruined domain of the showing rushed back into color and weight, and Noah opened his eyes in the light of THE Ymnaros.","And he looked around and understood at once that Damodred had not done what he had assumed.","The titan had not stretched a single moment into infinity the way Noah stretched instants to think inside them. Time had passed out here, the whole long teaching unspooling at its true length while existence went on around them.","The dead were buried.","Theron Adranos and Anaximander had finished the work, the small white and blue bodies laid into the scorched ground beneath rows of low mounds, and Ryaenara stood among them. All of them were simply waiting for him now.","And Anaximander wore a conflicted expression!","The scholar looked as though he wanted to ask something and could not make himself do it, the mild curious face caught on a hesitation!","Noah smiled, and looked at the mounds a moment, and then at his friend.","\" There shouldn’t be hesitation between friends ,\" he said. \" What’s up?\"","Anaximander sighed and opened his mouth.","And Theron Adranos put a hand on the scholar’s shoulder, and stepped forward instead.","\"I put Sir Anaximander in a difficult position,\" the golden-haired man said, \" by asking a heavy request of him.\"","He drew a breath, and told him.","\" THE Ymnaros is facing an invasion we have not faced before these past days. Our Dimension is colliding....fusing, slowly, into another Dimension entirely, one filled with Infinite Lifeforms, the same kind you cut down in this garden.\" His jaw tightened.","\" Our defenses were built for enemies who come through the doors. They do not work against this, because the two Dimensions are becoming one, and where they overlap, the enemy can appear anywhere at all. Inside our strongholds. Beneath our feet. In a garden that should have been a hundred layers deep in safety.\" He gestured faintly at the ruin around them. \" The way they appeared here.\"","...!","\" We call it the Dimensionlapse, \" Theron said. \" And from what I saw here today...that capability of yours. The one that strips the power from all those nearby...\"","He looked down at his own hands then, and turned them over.","\" When you imposed it, I did not feel any different. I felt like me. Whole. Myself. The same strength I have always carried, untouched, while others fell out of the sky around me.\"","...!","Noah’s attention sharpened!","\" Our toughest battles are occurring or already coming ,\" Theron went on. \" Against the mightiest of the invaders, in the places the Dimensionlapse has fused most deeply. If your power leaves the Superpowered Lifeforms standing at the height of their strength while it strips our enemies bare, then it may be the very thing that lets us overcome an invasion that has been grinding us down. \"","His voice steadied into something formal.","\"I do not ask it for free. Existence is give and take. Nothing in it is free.\"","He half-turned, and looked at the obelisk behind him, the tall stone still pouring its steady blue-gold light up into the smoke, the shrine his people had died in rows to keep.","\" This is one of many, \" Theron said quietly. \" Doorways, all of them. They open onto the place the invaders have bled us for, generation after generation. What grows there is the thing every Infinite and Source Lifeform in reach has spent ages trying to take from us. \" He looked back at Noah.","\" A Panacea. It grew in our lands on its own, and it is what made us the Superpowered Lifeforms that we are. And to others, they say, it can do something stranger still. They say it can cause the emergence of a Purpose. The emergence and nurturing of a Cause.\"","BOOM!","\"I can bring you through ,\" Theron finished. \" You are the allies of Sir Anaximander, so that you may confirm all of it with your own eyes rather than take a desperate man’s word. And if Existence deems it fitting, then afterward, we could work together.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone.","He looked at the obelisk that so many had died to protect! He thought of Dimensions fusing and colliding into one another. Dimensionlapse!","That did not sound natural to him at all, not remotely. The Infinite True Lifeforms had besieged this place for ages and failed to break it. Had they stopped trying to break it, then, and started trying to merge it instead, to fold THE Ymnaros into a Dimension of their own so that no wall or door could keep them out any longer?","And laid over all of it, the last thing Theron had said, the thing that mattered most of all.","A Panacea that could cause the emergence and nurturing of a Cause!","He looked at Theron, and then at Anaximander, and his decision was already made.","\" It is only human to help each other. Let’s go in and see.\"","...!","Yes. It was human to help!","But it was also human to make gains while helping, and Noah had never once in his life been able to deny himself an unfathomable treasure when one was laid in front of him! A Dimension besieged for ages by Infinite and Source Lifeforms both. A Panacea everyone in reach wanted badly enough to grind a whole people down for it!","And a thought rose in him, quiet and enormous, as he looked at the doorway.","What if this was the place? What if THE Ymnaros became the first ground he claimed, the first stake driven for the rule of THE True Human Emperor, a unique Dimension full of the more human beings he had come to meet, defended by people his power left standing while it stripped their enemies bare?","Maybe.","Maybe!"]},{"number":5551,"title":"Chapter 5551: Chapter 5550: Find Her!","paragraphs":["<Outside THE Krazhor-Nul>","In the dark beyond the ancient Dimension, where the naked strings of existence ran undressed of matter and law, a gathering stood upon nothing at all.","Jarl Erling was among them, and he was not the largest!","The titanic bronze Descendant with the bone-braided beard and the crimson fissures running molten through his body stood shoulder to shoulder with others of his kind, and there were several, and every one of them wore the same sentence written into their blood. Cursed Descendants of Those Who Remain .","Lords of continental thrones and lone floating mountains, keepers of harnessed Steeds and generations of failed experiments, each of them dying on a schedule no one had ever managed to argue with.","Every single one of them had shining eyes.","They looked out across the darkness together, and the light in those eyes was not the light of power, for they all had power beyond measuring. It was worse than that. It was the light of men who had spent their entire lives counting down and had just been handed a reason to stop counting.","Those who had learned of a cure!","\"All I have ,\" Jarl Erling said, \" are the brief signatures of existence.\"","His voice rolled out across the dark, and none of the others interrupted him, because he was the one who had seen it happen and they were the ones who had come running.","\" Brief. A handful of moments. The one with Living Causes, the one who can cure the curse, took what was mine out of my Dimension before I could close my hand on it.\" The molten fissures across his chest pulsed with the effort of saying it.","\" But existence remembers what passes through it. And I have the signatures.\"","He turned his enormous head, and looked at one of them in particular.","\"So I will rely on the prowess of Jarl Ingrid,\" he said, \" and the rest of you, to track them down.\"","And in the air before the gathered Jarls, the images hung.","Noah Osmont, crowned and rendered out of a stolen signature of existence and turning slowly in the dark. And beside him, vast and luminous and impossible, THE Infiniverse. A living Observable Existence with vibrant Causes moving through her, the answer that every Descendant experiment across every age had been reaching for and failing to grasp!","Shining eyes fixed on both images and did not look away.","...!","—","<Between Dimensions>","Far from that gathering, in another stretch of the frothing black entirely, one rider crossed the deep.","Jarl Skallagrim rode atop a single Cursed Steed.","It should not have been possible. To bring a Cursed Steed out of THE Krazhor-Nul was a thing the Dimension itself resisted, for the Steeds were seated into that place by the sentence that made them, bred to bear burdens within its bounds and bound to it by the same standing curse that was slowly killing them. They did not leave. They had never left!","That was the architecture of the promise, that those who left were abandoned by Salvation!","Skallagrim had paid the cost anyway.","He had come out with seven. Seven remained after he had torn the eighth apart with his own hands in a poisoned garden, seven dying colossi whipped forward into the dark by a keeper whose calm was worse than any rage.","One had made it through.","The rest had not survived the crossing. Their terminal Causes had guttered out somewhere in the dark between, one after another, the curse in them finally collecting what it was owed the moment they stepped past the boundary that had held them for ages, and Skallagrim had ridden on through the dying without once looking back at any of them.","Six Steeds spent as fare! The rot at his fissures had spread for it, and the two years he did not have were fewer now than they had been.","He did not care. One was all he needed!","The surviving Steed labored beneath him, enormous and gray and failing, its chains trailing off into the black, and Jarl Skallagrim leaned forward and set his obsidian hand against the ridge of its neck almost gently.","\" Sense her ,\" he said.","The Steed shuddered.","\" The sister you had beside you for thousands of years. The one chained in the same harness, dying on the same schedule, bearing the same sentence.\" His voice stayed level, conversational, the terrible lucidity of it carrying across the frothing dark.","\" The sister who abandoned you the moment that she was cured. Who broke her chains and looked at me with those uncursed eyes and went, and did not take you with her. Not you. Not one of you.\"","The dying Steed made a sound that had no dignity in it.","\" Hold to that ,\" Skallagrim said. \" Whatever is left in you that can still want something, point it at her.\"","He straightened on its back, and looked out into the endless dark ahead, at the drifting membranes of Dimensions hanging in the black like islands in an ocean, every one of them a place she might have gone.","\" Follow her scent, and we shall have our own cure .\" The rot glowed dull red along his fissures. \" Across Dimensions and time. Find them.\"","\"Find Hvitrmarr!\"","...!","---","<THE Creature>","The ninth district of the Cultivation Farms had taken longer than the eight before it.","They had learned. That was the thing about beings who had spent ages perfecting an art of harvest, they were not stupid, they were only comfortable, and comfort was a thing that could be burned off a lifeform quickly enough if you burned hard enough!","By the seventh district the masters had stopped lounging. By the ninth they had stopped meeting him in the open altogether, and instead they had rigged the whole domain he crossed, sinking their weavings into the pyramids themselves so that when THE Creature came down through the butcher-red sky, the ground rose to fight him alongside its owners.","It had worked, for a while.","Eleven of them. Source True Lifeforms, three of them Cenozoic, and they had fought together properly for the first time since he entered this Dimension, drawing on their Gu, spending their stored burdens like coin, feeding ages of stolen bearing into weavings meant to break a single trespasser apart at the anchors.","Now they were dead, and THE Creature stood in the crater of what had been their stratum, and he was heaving!"]},{"number":5552,"title":"Chapter 5552: Chapter 5551: A Challenge!","paragraphs":["His obsidian flames guttered low and ragged around a frame that had taken real damage. The Blank Caudal dragged behind him through the ochre dust, white hair matted dark, and along his left side ran a wound that had gone all the way to something structural, a splitting seam where one of the Cenozoic ones had gotten an Intent into him before dying badly for the privilege.","Calcified stones lay in ridges across the whole broken domain. The air was thick with the released corpses of nine ruptured Gu, ages of stolen bearing hanging in the red light with nowhere left to go, and beneath his feet the strata ran down through crushed pyramid stone and petrified bone into layers of older ruin still!","He breathed!","And behind his ribs, and behind him, and somehow also very far away, the statue spoke.","|Two hundred and six.|","The ancient voice arrived from the direction time came from, calm and vast as it always was, and THE Creature said nothing, because two hundred and six was not a thousand.","Then the statue did something it had never done.","It smiled.","He felt it happen inside himself, the seated colossus of worn gray stone shifting its faceless face into an expression, and it was not the serene ancient nonchalance he had carried since the thing first came to him. It was brutal. It was the smile of something that had been watching a fight go on too long and had decided, quite suddenly, that it was bored.","| You are not learning. Two hundred and six. At this rate the trial completes, and you will have learned nothing from it that you did not already know when you began. You are merely doing what you are good at, thoroughly, for a long time.|","\"...!\"","| Existence did not seat this trial in you to watch you excel at something you have already mastered. | The statue’s voice deepened, and the whole ruined district seemed to lean in around it.","|A trial that only measures is a ledger. A trial that changes the one measured is a trial. So Existence will up the stakes.|","THE Creature straightened out of his heaving, obsidian flames pulling in tight around the split in his side.","\" Explain.\"","| There is a reason the Farms of this Dimension are so rich.|","The gray of the statue’s voice shifted, and images came with it now, pressed into him rather than shown: the pyramids, the chained lines, the Gu at every peak, and beneath all of it something else, something enormous and buried and slow.","| The masters did not discover this art. They inherited the conditions for it. Beneath the Fields, deep in the oldest strata of THE Ghor-Vazhal, a Primeval Lifeform is dying. It has been dying for ages. Its lifeline was cut by a Progeny of Those Who Remain, and what was cut did not sever cleanly, and so it has been bleeding out across an entire Dimension ever since.|","\"...!\"","| The sacrifices feed it. The offerings feed it. Every life that climbs those steps and enters a Gu is rendered down, and the masters take their profit, and what they do not take drains downward through the strata into the thing beneath, which cannot live and cannot finish dying and so simply drinks, age after age. Trillions of lives. Not spent on greed alone. Spent on keeping a corpse from becoming a corpse.|","THE Creature went very still.","The whole architecture of the place reorganized itself in his understanding as the words landed. He had been razing districts. He had been tearing the roofs off a house without once asking what the house was built on. Every pyramid he broke, every Gu he ruptured, every master he put his heel through, and beneath all of it the actual engine had gone on drinking, patient and enormous and entirely untouched by anything he had done.","| Collapse it, and the Farms die with it. Not one district. All of them. The reason this Dimension eats will be gone, and what remains will only be beings who are used to eating, which is a far smaller problem and one that largely solves itself.|","\" What...is the cost of this one?\" THE Creature said.","The brutal smile came back into the ancient stone.","| One hour.|","\"...!\"","| Find it, and collapse it, within one hour of this moment. It is buried in the deepest strata of a Dimension that has no measured end, and it is guarded, and you have already been bled today. That is the point. Existence is not interested in whether you can carry a weight. It knows you can carry. It wishes to see whether you can commit and persevere.|","\"And what is offered?\"","The statue was quiet for a moment, and when it answered, something in the ancient voice changed.","| What is offered is not power.|","\"...!\"","The stone eyes burned in the far dark of him. | Succeed, and you receive the first portion of the inheritance of the previous bearer. What it is, I will not say, because I am not permitted to say, and because you would not understand it before you hold it.|","THE Creature’s flames rose.","The previous bearer!","His eyes were immensely cold as he only nodded","\"I accept ,\" he said.","He did not take long about it!","And the statue smiled brutally a second time as if it had attained something, as if its words were not done, and it was now finishing!","| One hour. And if you fail, you will willfully give control of ten percent of yourself to Existence as a cost.|","...!","A tenth of his Existence itself, the whole of what he was, handed over willingly to this thing!","THE Creature remained entirely unfettered.","His flames steadied. The wound in his side kept splitting and he let it. He looked out across the shattered ninth district, across the ridges of calcified stones and pyramids, out toward a butcher-red horizon that went on past any counting, and he understood exactly what he needed to do!","One hour.","To find a dying Primeval One buried in the deepest strata of an endlessly vast Dimension, a Dimension crawling with horrid True Lifeforms who by now all knew precisely what he was and what he had been doing to them for nine domains running, and to reach it, and to break the thing that an entire civilization of monsters had spent ages feeding.","He rolled his shoulders once. The Blank Caudal lifted out of the dust behind him, white and gold and patient.","\" Then let us begin,\" THE Creature said.","And he shot downward into the deeper strata of this Dimension!","...!"]},{"number":5553,"title":"Chapter 5553: Chapter 5552: Analysis! I","paragraphs":["<THE Quintessential Pantheon of THE Infiniverse>","Deep inside Noah, inside the living Observable Existence he carried and who carried him, a sea of blue-gold Osmontian Source Infinity stretched out past any horizon inside a certain realm.","The whole ocean gave off a low sustained hum, the sound of a thing that had never once needed a source outside itself!","Above it hung floating islands.","Hundreds of them, drifting at their own patient heights. They mimicked the old Spiritual Lands- terraced peaks of pale stone laced with veins of gold, waterfalls of raw Infinity pouring off their undersides and falling forever into the sea below.","Mist of pure Source drifted in the gaps between.","It was beautiful! But Ruination and THE Infiniverse were not here for the beauty.","They had come here to work.","All around the two of them, filling the air above the sea and between the islands for as far as the drifting mist allowed, hung diagrams.","Manifestations of everything they had just learned about Causes.","THE Infiniverse stood upon the surface of her own sea, luminous and severe, hands clasped behind her back, and Ruination hovered near her.","\" To ensure the Master never has to die again ,\" Ruination said, \" we have to anticipate everything in all possible futures.\"","The strings moved.","\" He died once inside the Steed. He came back only because THE Hepatarch answered, and I will not build a strategy on the assumption that it always will.\"","\" So we work backward from every ending we can imagine, and we close them. And right now, Causes seem to be the nexus behind a great many of those endings.\"","The first bubbles bloomed in the air above the sea, written in threads of pale light.","CAUSES.","\" They are behind you, \" Ruination said. \" Behind every Observable Existence that has ever held together. Behind Steeds, who are made of nothing else. Behind the Master’s own ascent, and behind the eighteen colliding in his chest at this moment. \"","A second bubble bloomed, and a string ran out to join it.","\" And behind all of that, one being keeps appearing.\"","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND.","\" One of Those Who Remain experimented on Steeds to fill them with Causes. Then he cursed them. An entire lineage of living Observable Existences, sentenced to slow collapse.\"","More bubbles formed!","THOSE WHO REMAIN. DESCENDANTS. CURSED DESCENDANTS.","Strings snapped between them, drawing the shape of a lineage that believed existence belonged to it, and a second lineage beneath it dying on a schedule.","\" The account we have is that his Progeny touched the Steeds, and so he cursed them and cut his losses. That...doesn’t make much sense.\"","A string pulled taut between the Fiend and the Steeds, and hung there, vibrating.","\" Were the Steeds actually already unstable? Was the curse not a punishment at all, but a containment? A sentence laid on an experiment that had gone somewhere he did not want it to go?\"","She let that hang, and drew the last string.","LAESTRYGONIANS.","\"Because this is the same being ,\" Ruination said, \" who moved to bring an entire race to extinction because of their Causes.\"","The diagram hung complete above the blue-gold sea, bubbles and strings and branching lines, and at the center of every path stood the same thing.","\" So the question is... \" Ruination said. \" Why would something that powerful be so interested in Causes? What is it about them that a being who could unmake a lineage with a sentence would spend ages tinkering with, and then twice destroy whatever came out of the tinkering? Why ruin an entire race over their anchors?\"","...!","THE Infiniverse studied the diagram in silence.","Then she raised one hand, and pulled.","The bubble marked CAUSES came apart at her gesture, unfolding into its component structures, First and Prime and Blighted and Calcified and the unnamed others, and she reached past all of them into the strand that ran back into herself, into her own foundation, and drew that out beside the rest for comparison.","\" There is something wrong with the Master’s nine ,\" she said.","Ruination’s strings stilled.","THE Infiniverse set the two side by side in the air, and the difference was immediate even in the diagram.","\"These are the nine Prime Causes that hold an ordinary Observable Existence together. Cognitio. Bellum. Mortis... The common nine, seated beneath a First Cause, doing the work they were made for.\" Her hand moved.","\" And these are the Master’s nine. Existence. Paradox. Chaos. Mana. Quintessence. Adversity. Tyranny. Harvest. Apocalypse.\"","The two sets hung together, and one of them was simply larger.","\"They are not the same order of thing ,\" THE Infiniverse said. \" His are distinctly grander. They resuscitated a dead Observable Existence. They were seated into the Organs of a Steed and joined to her First Causes without collapsing. And now they are colliding against pristine First Causes, striking them, forcing reactions out of them, and holding their own in that collision.\"","She turned to Ruination.","\" A Prime Cause cannot do that. A Prime Cause is the living relative beneath the ancestor. It does not stand as an equal to a First Cause and grind against it as a peer. If his nine can do that, then his nine have not been Prime Causes for some time. We have simply kept calling them what they were when he made them.\"","\" They evolved past Prime ,\" Ruination said.","\" They are not the common nine, and they are not First Causes either. He carved them himself, out of his own identity...\"","She closed her hand, and the label on the diagram changed.","\" They should not be called his Prime Causes. They are his own unique Causes, bearing his identity. They are his... Osmontian Causes.\"","HUUM!","The sea churned.","The whole blue-gold ocean rose in a single slow enormous swell beneath their feet, the hum of it deepening, and on the drifting islands above, the crystalline groves rang all at once!","Ruination watched the swell pass.","\"I will let the Master know ,\" she said.","\" Now, these Osmontian Causes. How do we use them to pull on the genetic markers of the Laestrygonians the way he pulled Damodred?\"","...!"]},{"number":5554,"title":"Chapter 5554: Chapter 5553: Analysis! II","paragraphs":["The bubble for DAMODRED appeared, and a string ran from it back to CAUSES , and then to THE TIDE THAT OWES NOTHING.","\" Because the mechanism as we understand it is narrow,\" Ruination said. \" He cured a Cursed Lifeform bound to Those Who Remain through Cause replacement. That act altered cause and effect across existence and time. The Tide followed the altered weavings back to the only thing they still resembled, found an extinct people’s markers sleeping in their own Causes, and matured an egg from it. \"","\"Is that reproducible? Or was it a single accident? Does it only ever come as a Tide reward for curing a Steed, and are there even any more Steeds we can reach? Or, now that we know its origin, can we replicate it deliberately?\"","...!","THE Infiniverse thought about it!","\" THE Tide That Owes Nothing does not follow a procedure. It follows him, and it returns what he gives interlinked with what he is. That is why it can reach things that are extinct. It is because the Tide does not consider extinction a category that applies to a gift, so long as there is enough logic and foundation beneath the pull to make the gift coherent.\"","She gestured at the Damodred bubble. \" The Laestrygonians laid markers into their Causes deliberately, as a chance. The chance required rare Causes to clash and meld in the right way. The Master’s cure of the Steed produced exactly that shape. The logic was already there. The Tide only had to notice it and lock on. That was the door being opened. Now that it is open, does it really need to be opened again?\"","Ruination’s strings paused mid-write.","\" We know what we are looking for now, \" THE Infiniverse continued. \" Before, the Tide had to discover a resemblance across an age of dead weavings on its own. Now the target is known, named, and precedented, and we have one of them standing beside the Master as proof of concept.\"","She drew two new strands out of the unfolded Causes diagram and set them apart from the rest.","\" So. If we focus deliberately on Blighted Causes and Calcified Causes, study them, hold them in our understanding, perhaps even channel them at the moment THE Tide is triggered by some other act of giving, then that focus becomes a hook. Something for the Return to lock onto. The Tide chooses what to give. But a hook can influence what it reaches for...a specified Return\"","...!","Ruination absorbed that, and the diagram above the sea rearranged itself into something that looked, for the first time, less like a mystery and more like a plan!","THE Infiniverse had begun to work, and Ruination stood back and let her.","She raised one hand, and a Status Panel bloomed above the sea.","| STATUS PANEL: NOAH OSMONT|","|Designations: THE Quintessential Osmontian. THE True Human Emperor. THE Fledgling Liege of the First Lineage. Human.|","|Scale framework: First Infinite Scale of Existence complete; Second Infinite Scale approaching its next stage.|","|FACETS OF EXISTENCE: A-Rank, Idho. Osmontian Source Infinity. Volume. Output. Trueness. All Nine Foundations. Currently rising continuously under THE Collision of Causes.|","|INTENT: THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian. A-Rank, Idho. Second order.|","|OSMONTIAN TONGUE: five Letters, one Word. I AM. OSMONT. QUINTESSENTIAL. HUMAN. PROTAGONIST. THE MORTAL COIL.|","|CAUSES: nine, seated in THE Infinite Cause. Designation under review, previously logged as Prime Causes, now correctly THE OSMONTIAN CAUSES. Currently colliding in perpetuity against nine First Causes of THE Steed.|","|ARTS: THE Collision of Causes. THE Quintessential Confluence. THE DOMAIN OF THE MORTAL COIL.|","|APPENDAGES: THE Estuary Eye. THE Pinion Vigil. THE Hepatarch of the Undying Root. THE Amaranthine Heart. THE Primeval Osmontian Marrow. THE Circlet of the Quintessential Ruin. THE Quintessential Pantheon of THE Infiniverse.|","|OSMONTIAN BIOMASS: 89,800,000. Elevation costs falling continuously.|","|RETAINERS AND BONDED EXISTENCES: Hvitrmarr, Remnant Dimension Steed of the First lineage, THE Autarkis Intent. Damodred of THE Laestrygonians, SS-Rank across all facets. THE Infiniverse. Ruination...|","|HELD, UNUSED: THE Tessellated Heart of the Borrowed Flame. THE Lingering Word. One True Declarative Human Ruling.|","Ruination looked around her Master’s quantified panel and found the first flaw in the second line she read.","A-Rank Idho. It was honest, accurate, and useless as a threat assessment, because it did not describe what happened when her Master arrived somewhere.","He rode a Steed who had come down on a Cenozoic True Lifeform and unmade it in one motion, its Ananke-grade Intent caving inward under THE Autarkis Intent like wet parchment under a falling mountain. So the practical answer was that he already overcame Cenozoic Scale beings whenever he pleased, because he did not have to do it himself.","Which was precisely why she did not trust the number.","Ashkavaal had also been Cenozoic, partially grasped temporal weavings, and her Master had killed her with a beginner’s fireball at Rank F standing.","That established the floor of the Sixth Scale. Nothing else.","Ruination pondered about the quantification of power from here!","She set Jarl Skallagrim’s weaving apart from the Scale diagram, where it hung refusing to sit beside a single rung of it.","These fuckers were hard to designate!","She redrew it. Where the Scale diagram had hung, the grade ladder rose in its place, F Beith through A Idho, then S Ebad, SS Oir, SSS Muin, and above that the unnamed rung waiting to be carved in THE Osmontian Tongue when he reached it.","The grades measured the thing itself rather than the rung it occupied. They could describe a Cursed Descendant, a Laestrygonian, and her Master. Vakochev’s framework could describe none of the three.","Ruination enlarged Damodred and analyzed him at this time.","The strongest weapon under her Master’s command was considerably stronger than her Master.","SS-Rank facets. SS-Rank Autarkis Intent. An SS-Rank Pantheon!","Her Master’s own facets sat at A-Idho. Hvitrmarr, simply by being ridden, delivered S-Rank to any battle she entered. And Damodred, by being here, delivered SS!","So what was his standing? A, because that was his own hand? Or SS, because SS answered when he spoke?","She smiled lightly while thinking where exactly to put her Master.","That left the largest thread on the board.","She set Theron Adranos into the air, and his weaving read as almost nothing.","The Superpowered Lifeforms emanated no authority. Less presence upon existence than the scorched dirt he had knelt in.","He had stood inside THE DOMAIN OF THE MORTAL COIL and felt nothing.","Which should have been impossible, because the Word nullified all authority and made no exceptions.","She also had to quantify this!","The panel turned slowly above the sea.","Across the water, THE Infiniverse worked on in her silence, taking Blighted Causes apart and putting them back together, building a hook to throw into the Tide.","Two of them at their labors, in the middle of his own Source!"]},{"number":5555,"title":"Chapter 5555: Chapter 5554: The Well! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Outside the obelisk, Noah turned and nodded once toward Hvitrmarr.","She understood before the gesture finished. Where a colossal white queen had stood in the ruined gold, white flame gathered inward and folded, gigantic mass drawing down through itself in a spiral of pale sovereign light, and when the light thinned a woman stood in the wreckage of the gardens.","Tall. White-haired. Twin spiral horns of ivory rose back from her temples, and her eyes had not changed at all, gold with ring inside ring for pupils. Her robe was white and dazzling and it was not cloth. Causes moved through it!","She rolled her shoulders once inside a shape she had not worn in a long while, and said nothing.","Ryaenara looked her up and down and made a small sound of pure appreciation as she whistled.","Damodred did not look at all, because a mountain does not turn its head for a change of clothes!","Theron Adranos watched all of it without comment, and then he stepped up to the obelisk.","He set his palm flat against the blue-gold stone. There was no incantation, no weaving, no authority pressed into it, and Noah watched carefully and confirmed what he already suspected. Theron gave off nothing. He simply touched it, and the obelisk knew him!","The light running up its faces reversed.","It poured downward instead of up, sheeting off the carved lines, pooling at the base and spreading outward across the scorched dirt in a slow widening ring, and where the light crossed the ruined ground the ruined ground was not there anymore. A doorway opened in the middle of a butchered garden, and through it came air that smelled of water!","\" Come ,\" Theron said. \" See it, and then decide.\"","They went through!","Existence flickered with multicolored light all around as it felt unique!","Noah had crossed the dark between Dimensions on the back of a Steed and much more.","None of it had prepared him for the quiet on the other side of that stone!","| You have entered THE Hallowed Verdance of the Undivided Well.|","...!","They stood on a shore of pale sand so fine it moved like water underfoot, and before them opened a basin without any visible far side. Water filled it. Not dark water and not still water, but a vast luminous expanse of gold-shot turquoise, lit from beneath rather than above, so that the whole immensity glowed upward and cast its light onto everything around it in slow drifting patterns!","Where the shallows lapped the sand they left rings of soft blue phosphorescence that faded and rekindled with each small wave.","Above and around it, the land had grown wild!","Now, he didn’t usually care for environments too much unless it was his own Shore or Infiniverse, but this place...damn, it deserved to be looked at properly as it was too magisterial!","Cliffs of dark stone rose in tiers around the basin, and from every tier fell water, hundreds of falls, some thick as rivers and some thin as thread, dropping in long slow ribbons through air that seemed to hold them a moment longer than it should.","Mist hung in the gaps and caught the underlight, and out of the mist grew forests, huge trees with trunks so pale they read almost silver, their canopies dense and dark and hung everywhere with luminous vines that pulsed faintly in a rhythm Noah realized after a moment was synchronized, the whole valley breathing light in and out together.","Great flat islands drifted above the water, unmoored, drifting slowly on nothing, and they trailed their own waterfalls from their undersides in curtains that fell hundreds of miles and dissipated into mist before they ever touched the sea.","Ryaenara swore quietly, and then swore again with more feeling.","\"...!\"","And at the center of it all, rising out of the sea, stood the pillar.","It was a tree. But it had no leaves and no branches and no crown, only a single colossal trunk of radiant pale wood climbing up out of the water and continuing until the mist and the distance swallowed it entirely. Its bark ran with veins of light in slow upward currents.","It did not seem to be growing. It simply stood, immense past reckoning, the axis the entire valley had arranged itself around, and the light beneath the sea was brightest at its roots.","And around that trunk, floating some distance out from the wood, hung a necklace.","Noah’s attention locked onto it instantly, and so did everyone else’s.","It was enormous, scaled to the pillar rather than to any wearer, a broad collar of gold that circled the trunk without touching it.","A collar, wide and layered, built of many rows of golden tubular beads strung tight and close so that the whole formed a single deep band, and along its lower edge hung a fringe of small teardrop pendants that swayed gently though there was no wind out over the water.","At its front, where a collar’s clasp would sit, the rows converged into a single broad plate, and on that plate was worked a design Noah could not resolve even with his eyes, something that his sight kept sliding off.","It was translucent as he saw the pillar’s light through it.","An illusion, then, or a manifestation!","Theron Adranos had gone still beside them, and when Noah looked at him, the golden-haired man had lowered his head.","\" That is THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity, \" Theron said, and the reverence in his worn voice was total.","\" It is not here. What you are looking at is its manifestation, and it appears in every domain like this one, above every well, in every valley behind every obelisk we have ever guarded. The same collar, the same size, the same silence. A child born in these lands sees it before she sees her own reflection.\"","He let out a breath.","\"It is the legend at the core of what we are.\"","\"Oh?\" Noah said.","\"I would have to start with the water for you to understand the legend ,\" Theron said, \" because the water is what everyone comes to steal, and the collar is what nobody understands.\"","He gestured out across the luminous expanse.","\" This is THE Undivided Well. Look down. Not at the surface. Through it.\"","Noah looked, and found them.","Beneath the gold-shot turquoise, at depths that shifted as the light moved, they grew in their thousands. Flowers!","Or things that had decided to be flowers, radiant and slow-turning, each one a bloom of layered petals in blue and white and pale gold, and each one shed light rather than reflecting it, so that the entire sea was lit from below by the crop growing in it.","Some were small. Some were the size of islands. They opened and closed on a rhythm that matched the pulsing of the luminous vines in the forests, and looking at them for more than a moment made Noah aware of his own Causes turning inside his chest!","\"THE Vermeil Bloom \" Theron said. \" The Panacea. That is what it is, and the word Panacea is what outsiders call it, and it is not wrong, only small. It cures. It elevates. It has done stranger things than either. \" He looked out over the water.","\"It grew here on its own. Nobody planted it and nobody tends it. It is what made us. Every Superpowered Lifeform who has ever lived traces what they are back to this water, and that is why we are what we are, and why we give off nothing, and why we are hunted.\"","\"It cannot simply be taken ,\" Theron continued. \" Every invader for ages has learned this, and most of them refused to believe it until they had thrown armies at it. The Well permits entry only to those who are PURE. \"","\" Not clean. Not innocent. Not good, whatever that would mean. Pure in existence. True to what you actually are, without a seam between the thing you claim to be and the thing you are. The Well reads that, and if it does not like what it reads, you do not enter, and it does not matter in the least how powerful you are.\"","\" And it has an inherent limit of once a year. One entry, one being. Whoever has gone in cannot go in again until the year has turned, no matter their standing, no matter their need. Those who are impure are refused, and those who have already gone are refused, and between those two rules the Well has fed a people for ages and never once been emptied.\"","Then Theron turned, and looked up at the collar hanging around the pillar, and his whole bearing changed.","\"And that is the water ,\" he said. \" Now the legend.\"","\"We hold that the collar came before the water.\"","Theron said it simply.","\" That THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity is not a relic of this place but the ORIGIN of it. That every Panacea in every well in every valley of THE Ymnaros bloomed out of that collar’s making, and the Blooms beneath your feet are its overflow. Not a gift it gave. A residue it left. \" He looked out at the translucent gold.","\"If that is true, then everything we are, every Superpowered Lifeform who ever drew breath in these lands, is a downstream consequence of an object nobody has ever worn.\"","He raised a hand toward it.","\"We hold that a Superpowered Lifeform will come who exemplifies what we are more truly than any of us has managed. Not the strongest. We have had monsters. Not the wisest, we have had those as well, and buried them. The one who is most COMPLETELY what a Superpowered Lifeform is, whose existence gives off nothing and contains everything, without a single seam in it anywhere. \" His voice roughened.","\" And when that one comes, they will adorn the collar, and in adorning it they will wield the core power of our kind. The thing itself, at its source, undiluted, the power that the Blooms are only the runoff of. And they will usher in an era of glory for a people who have spent every age we have ever had being farmed for our own inheritance.\"","Noah studied the hanging gold and did not interrupt.","\" We do not know what that power is, \" Theron admitted.","He lowered his hand. \" But we know the sign. When the worthy one finally stands beneath it, the collar’s image will react. It will answer them. And when it answers, a pathway opens, and that pathway leads to the true collar, which does not hang above any well in any valley. It sits at the core of THE Ymnaros itself.\"","...!","\" That is the legend,\" Theron finished. \" My people have died in rows in front of these obelisks for ages, guarding wells full of runoff, waiting for a manifestation to twitch. We have never seen it move.\"","The valley breathed light in and out around them, and the necklace hung motionless around the radiant pillar, and said nothing to anybody.","Noah nodded slowly, and turned his head away from the collar, and looked out at the sea.","At the Blooms turning in their thousands beneath the gold-shot water, lit from within, growing on their own out of an origin nobody had ever touched.","Was he a pure existence?","He had killed many. He had done many things!","He was greedy, and he was selfish!","\"You are welcome to obtain the Panacea yourself, if the Well permits you. And those with you are welcome to try. Any of them. Walk into THE Undivided Well and see whether it lets you through, and if it does, take a Bloom.\"","He looked at each of them in turn, the horned woman in the Cause-woven robe, the profane Antiquity, the mild scholar, the mountain of calcified scars. \" I would not presume to guess which of you it will accept. It has surprised us before, and it has broken hearts here more often than that.\"","Noah looked out across the luminous sea, at the radiant leafless pillar, at the collar of gold that had never once moved for anyone.","He would see who among his people was pure enough to attain these treasures!"]},{"number":5556,"title":"Chapter 5556: Chapter 5555: The Well! II","paragraphs":["When it came to who should give a test of just how purr they were...Noah turned and looked at a certain Steed!","\" You first, \" Noah said.","Hvitrmarr inclined her horned head and walked to the edge of the pale sand. She simply stepped off, and THE Undivided Well took her.","In truth, the question everyone had come here to ask was answered in that first moment, before anybody had time to be nervous on her behalf.","There was no ripple of refusal, no pause while something unseen considered her. The water opened the way a door opens for a hand that has always had the key.","Compared to the way she moved in the air, she moved through that sea like something coming home. Her white hair fanned out behind her, and the nine First Causes drifting in the weave of her robe brightened as the underlight found them, so that she went down trailing her own small constellation.","Below her, the Blooms turned in their thousands. Radiant flowers of blue and white and pale gold, opening and closing on a slow shared rhythm, and they lit her from beneath as she passed over them. Noah watched from the shore and found he had nothing at all to say about it.","Since she was not the sort to take more than she needed, she chose a bloom about the size of a shield. She closed her hand around its base and drew it free with a care that looked, from above, a great deal more like asking than taking.","Then she rose, and broke the surface without a sound, and came back across the water to the sand. She held THE Vermeil Bloom out to Noah in both hands, and its light shone up into her face.","\" For you, Master.\"","Noah reached for it.","\" Hold on.\"","Ryaenara had already got to her feet, and she said it loudly enough that every head on the shore turned. She was rolling her shoulders, and her eyes were on the sea with the exact expression she wore before a fight she intended to enjoy.","\" Before you take that. I want to see... if I’m pure.\"","\" I’ve been alive for too long. I’ve kept my word to people who didn’t deserve it and broken it with people who did, and I have never once pretended to be anything I’m not. If anybody here is exactly what she says she is, it’s me.\"","She reached the edge and dove, and... the water threw her back!","It happened so quickly that it took a moment to understand!","The surface rippled outward in a hard ring from the point she struck, and it did not part for her, and she came off it in a spray of gold-shot droplets and landed on her back in the sand.","\" What?!\"","She was furious!","Of course she was up again almost at once. She stared at the water, and then at her own hands, as though they had gone behind her back and done something she had not authorized.","\" What?\"","She went a second time, faster, and the Well shoved her out again, and she landed skidding through the fine sand. By the third attempt she had stopped being polite about it. Her Intent came off her in a heavy vibrant tide, and she drove herself at the surface like a thrown spear!","Despite all of that, the Well did not fight her. It did not brace, and it did not push back, and it never once answered her power with power of its own. It only declined!","Then nothing happened at all, for a while.","The waterfalls kept falling on the cliffs behind them, and the luminous vines in the silver forests kept breathing their light in and out, and none of it had any opinion.","Ryaenara sat in the pale sand with her Intent still burning around her and nothing anywhere to burn it against, and she looked...lost.","Theron Adranos looked away. There was no judgment anywhere on his worn face!","Noah went and stood beside her as he laughed inside a bit.","\" Hang in there. We dont always have to be good at everything. And...So long as you are pure to yourself, I don’t see why it should matter what a lake thinks about it..\"","Ryaenara scoffed and stood and dusted off her legs as she voiced out...","\" Hmph .\" She jerked her chin at the water. \" Why don’t you try, then? You talk big, but you may not be considered pure yourself, and I would like very much to watch you bounce.\"","Noah nodded and walked to the edge calmly.","Behind him the shore went quiet in a different way than before, and he could feel all of them at his back.","He asked himself the question honestly, one last time.","Was he pure? He had no idea, but he stepped off the sand anyway!","And....!","The Well opened for him.","There was no resistance at all. No test he could feel, no weighing, no moment where something considered him and came to a decision. The water simply took him in as it had taken Hvitrmarr, warm and clean and closing over his head!","It was quiet down there. An entire Dimension had bled over this water for ages, and the dark stone of the cliffs above was layered with the calcified strata of every ambition that had failed to reach the basin. Only slow light and slow current, and the great patient pillar rising up through all of it toward a sky he could no longer see.","Since the Blooms turned all around him as he went down, he had time to notice that his own eighteen Causes were turning in his chest to a rhythm not quite the same as theirs, and not quite different either. He chose one, and reached out, and closed his hand around its base!","The prompts came then.","|THE Vermeil Bloom. Panacea. Analysis follows.|","| Nature: a self-originated growth. It was not seeded, cultivated, or designed by any hand present in this Dimension.|","| Function, first order: it cures degradation. Terminal Causes, failing anchors, curses seated into a lineage, corruption grown into an existence at the root. What has begun to fail may be made whole. What has been sentenced may have the sentence lifted. May. Nothing is guaranteed.|","| Function, second order: it elevates . In a lifeform that consumes it, the Bloom does not add power. It resolves the existence into a truer version of itself, and grants power as the consequence.|","| Function, third order: in a being that possesses no Cause, the Bloom can potentially precipitate the emergence of one. A Purpose. An anchor where there was none.|","Noah read the third line twice, and then a third time.","Compared to what it had cost him to cure one Steed, that line was almost obscene!","| Ancillary observation, appended by THE Protagonist’s Omniscient Regard rather than by the Bloom itself.|","|THE Vermeil Bloom is not a whole thing. Its structure reads as a component. Specifically, it reads as an accessory of ?????, in the way a shed scale reads as an accessory of the beast that shed it.|","|Further: the accessory is not inert. It is seeking. Every Bloom in this water, and in every water like it across this Dimension, is oriented. They have been looking for a very long time, and the Regard cannot determine what for.|","|?????|","Noah’s brows rose slowly beneath the water.","An accessory of something that was...seeking.","Theron had said the legend held that the collar came first and every Panacea was its overflow, and he had used the words runoff and residue, and had clearly never expected either of them to be read literally. But if each of these flowers was a piece shed from something larger, and if all of them were pointed outward and hunting, then what exactly were these Panaceas looking for?","The Bloom in his hands...answered him before he finished the thought!","HUUUM!","Black-gold light broke out of it, running along every petal in fine hot lines and then leaping off into the water, and it was nothing like the pale gold of the Well!","The lattice of it spread outward through the turquoise, and the nearest Blooms caught it, and then the ones beyond those, and then the ones beyond those!","BOOM","BOOM!","Ten thousand of them, if there were ten thousand down there. The whole crop of that sea lit in a spreading wave with Noah at the center of it, until the gentle underlight had drowned entirely beneath a black-gold radiance climbing up out of the deep, and every flower in the water had turned toward one man and begun to burn!","Above the surface, the valley went the same color. The waterfalls caught it, and the mist banks caught it, and the luminous vines lost their patient rhythm and blazed, and the drifting islands overhead lit from underneath!","As a result of all that, or perhaps as the reason for it, the great pillar at the center of THE Hallowed Verdance began to vibrate along its whole immeasurable length, and the currents of light in its bark reversed and ran downward toward the water.","And...the collar hanging around it began to shine!","THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity had hung above every well in every valley of this Dimension for the entire recorded history of a people. It had never moved for their greatest, nor their most beloved, nor for any of the ones they had been certain of, and generations had died in rows on the sand in front of the obelisks waiting for it to do anything whatsoever.","Now its rows of golden beads lit black and gold from within, and its teardrop fringe swayed, and the unreadable design on its front plate turned slowly and faced the water!","On the shore, Theron Adranos stood with his mouth open and did not manage to speak!","Ryaenara found her voice first.","\"No fucking way. \" She took a step forward into the shallows, staring at the burning sea and then up at the shining collar above it. \" No fucking way, right? Are you serious?\"","Nobody answered her, because the two who might have were not looking at her at all. Hvitrmarr stood in the shallows with her own Bloom forgotten in her hands and her gold eyes fixed on the necklacs. Behind her the veil of ancient hands had turned upward!","In the black-gold light of ten thousand seeking flowers, the Steed and the dead thing watched an object older than any Panacea answer a man who had never once been anything but himself!","Pure!"]},{"number":5557,"title":"Chapter 5557: Chapter 5556: Path I","paragraphs":["<THE Ymnaros>","Far from THE Hallowed Verdance, past another obelisk in another valley, the same water lay under the same underlight, and everything else about the place was wrong.","The obelisk itself still shone its blue-gold. It had gone on shining while the men and women who guarded it were killed at its foot, and it was shining now over what had been left there afterward.","They had been laid out!","Two dozen Superpowered Lifeforms in white and blue, arranged in even rows on the pale sand inside the doorway, hands at their sides, faces turned up.","Nobody had done it out of respect. You could see that in the spacing, which was too regular, the spacing of inventory rather than of mourning. Someone had wanted them countable.","Inside the Well itself, more of them drifted.","The bodies had been put into the water. They turned slowly in the underlight among the Blooms, white and blue among blue and pale gold, sinking and rising on the currents, and the Panaceas went on opening and closing around them in their patient shared rhythm as though nothing at all had changed in the garden.","And all around that shore, in rows, stood the Infinite.","Dozens upon dozens of True Infinite Lifeforms holding the whole basin in a ring, their Infinity compounding quietly off them and pressing the mist flat, and among them the tall silent shapes of the Cenozoic in numbers that no single Observable Existence should ever have had to look at in one place!","They had been at this for some time.","One of the Cenozoic went in as the light shifted. It walked to the edge with the deliberateness of a thing that had already been refused once and had reasoned its way to a different approach, and it entered the water.","The Well threw it out.","The surface rippled in a hard concentric shove and the thing came off it and landed among the rows of the dead, scattering two of them out of their neat alignment, and it rose without expression and walked back to its place in the ring.","Another went. Another shove. Another rejection.","A third tried it slowly, wading, testing whether patience read differently to the water than force did. The Well waited until it was up to the knee and then declined it as flatly as it had declined the others!","A fourth arrived carrying one of the corpses, on the theory, presumably, that the water might read the passenger rather than the carrier. The Well rejected them both, and the body came back with it, and the thing dropped it on the sand and did not look down!","So it went. Dozens of them, ancient, Cenozoic, holding between them enough power to unmake an Observable Existence outright, taking turns at a lake and being turned away by it one after another without so much as a fight to lose.","Far above all of that, well clear of the water, four figures hung in the black-shot air.","Three of them did not fit on any ladder.","Every other existence in the valley could be placed, weighed, and slotted somewhere on a Scale, and these three simply could not, in the same way that Jarl Skallagrim could not!","The first was made of hanging chain. Or wore it, or had been wound in it so long ago that the difference had stopped mattering, a titan-shape of black links draped in coils from shoulder to ankle, and where the links crossed there were faces worn into the metal by pressure alone, and none of the faces were finished.","The second had no surface anywhere on it. It was a titan of running dark liquid held in the shape of a body by nothing anyone could see, and the liquid moved constantly downward and never emptied, and at the places where eyes belonged there were only two points where the falling was faster.","The third stood in stone armor grown over with a pale calcified crust, and it was the only one of the three that had bothered with a face, and the face was serene, and it had been serene for a very long time.","And at their center, smaller than any of them, floated a man in a crimson robe.","He was the reason the other three arranged themselves the way they did.","He looked ancient in the manner of things that predate their own memory of themselves, and he also looked wild, hair loose and moving in no wind, and beneath both of those he looked mad in a way that was not theatrical at all!","There was no raving in him. There was only the sense, immediate and unpleasant, of a mind that had gone somewhere a long time ago and had never seen a reason to come back, and had been extremely capable the whole time.","He watched the Cenozoic being bounced off the water below, and he seemed to find it neither amusing nor frustrating.","The one in chains spoke, and it spoke with the careful respect of something enormous addressing something it considered its better.","\" The Dimensionlapse has given us the opening we waited ages for, Master.\" Its voice came out of the worn faces in the metal rather than from anywhere on its body.","\"Their walls are meaningless now, their Halls route nothing, and we can arrive anywhere inside THE Ymnaros we please. After so long being kept at the door, we are inside the house.\"","The crimson-robed man said nothing.","\" But we have taken multiple valleys, \" the chained titan continued, \" and we cannot take the water in any of them. The Panaceas are almost impossible for us to grasp ourselves. If they are the object, then the practical route is the one we have been avoiding, which is to take the Superpowered Lifeforms alive in numbers, and keep them, and make them harvest for us.\"","The liquid one poured downward and said nothing. The calcified one remained serene.","\" Which is what I do not understand\" The faces in the chain shifted. \" This Dimension is not the richest. It is not the best defended, nor the best positioned, and its people are strange and small and have nothing that other places do not have more of. Why here, master? Of all the Dimensions in existence, why are we in this one?\"","...!","And before any answer came, the valley answered for him.","At the center of the Well, the great pillar began to shine.","The colossal leafless trunk that rose out of the water and continued past sight lit along its whole immeasurable length, the currents in its bark running downward, and around it the illusory collar of gold that had hung there in silence for the entire recorded history of a people blazed resplendent with black-gold light!","Every Infinite Lifeform in the ring turned to look.","The one in chains fell silent. The dark liquid stopped falling for perhaps half a heartbeat and then resumed. And the crimson-robed man, who had not reacted to anything at all since he arrived in this valley, frowned.","It was the first expression he had worn.","\" That ,\" he said, \" is why we are here.\"","He did not take his eyes off the collar.","\" Across existence there are objects that do not belong to any age that can be dated. Remnant Existential Treasures. Older than the Primeval Ones, older than the frameworks the Primevals sit beneath, and most of the ones anybody has ever managed to trace lead back to Those Who Remain themselves.\"","WAA!","\"They are not artifacts. Artifacts were made by somebody who wanted something. These are remnants. They were... left.\"","The three around him waited.","\" This little necklace ,\" the crimson-robed man said, \" hanging in a fishpond, in a valley, in a Dimension full of costumed farmers who give off no authority. A great many patient beings have suspected for a very long time that it is one of them. I came to confirm it, and to take it, and I expected to spend an age doing so.\"","Then his voice changed, and the madness in him came up out of the calm without raising its volume at all.","\" So why.\"","\"...!\"","\" Why the fuck is the legend of these ungrateful costume-wearing fuckers activating now? This age. This month. This afternoon, while I am standing in the water they die for?\" His hair moved in its absent wind.","\" For ages they dreamed about it. Generations of them died in rows in front of these stones waiting for that thing to twitch, and it never twitched, not for their best, not for their most loved, not for any of the poor hopeful bastards who were certain. And I arrive to claim it, and something appears and trips the pathway toward it within a breath of my getting here.\"","He laughed once. It was a short, entirely humorless sound!","\"Is existence trying to fuck with me? Haha. Unbelievable.\"","The frown smoothed away!","\" Fine. Come on. I will burn this place down to make certain I have hold of it before whatever tripped that pathway walks to the end of it .\" He turned in the air, robe moving, already deciding logistics.","\" Ground the blood of a few million of these Superpowered Lifeforms into the water. That should be enough to force the matter, and if it is not, we will find out with the next few million. There are enough of them, and they do not run.\"","He looked back once at the shining collar, and the madness in him settled into something patient.","\" Alright, you all. Let’s move.\"","...!","And the three titans that fit on no ladder inclined themselves, and followed, and there was not a moment of hesitation in any of them, nor any question about whether the order was reasonable.","Of course they followed.","They had been following for a very long time, and they would go on following, because they were THE Followers of THE Sealed One.","Who else would they follow?"]},{"number":5558,"title":"Chapter 5558: Chapter 5557: Path II","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","In truth, Noah did not know what to make of any of it!","He had never believed in destiny. Or rather, he had never believed in a destiny that arrived from outside, handed down by something that had decided things about him in advance. Destiny as a thing to be designed, on the other hand, was a different matter entirely, and he had built a Civilization of it once and hung its threads where he wanted them.","So he was not a chosen one.","Although, of course, there was the grand fact of the fifth Letter.","Because he had written PROTAGONIST into himself, deliberately, and the whole point of that Letter was that adversity fed him and that fate-adjacent things bent when they got too close. Was that what had happened here? Had a legend belonging to a people he had met a little while ago simply mistaken a Letter for a prophecy? Or had it been something else in him, the Osmontian Causes, the Marrow, the eighteen collisions running in his chest, some part of what he was resonating with a thing that had been waiting to resonate for ages?","There were no coincidences, in his experience. There were only mechanisms he had not identified yet!","Not that he was complaining! The question that actually mattered was how difficult the next part would be. The manifestation reacting did not hand anyone the collar. It opened a pathway toward it. And nobody had ever walked that pathway.","He put the Bloom away, and rose out of the water.","The commotion above was heavier than he had left it. Theron Adranos was trembling, openly, in front of everyone!","Anaximander had a wry look on his face when Noah came up onto the sand.","\" Brother ,\" the scholar said, \" how do you always do these things? I am not complaining, since it may well be the thing that carries us through what is coming. But wow.\"","Noah shook his head and looked out at the distant trunk.","\"I’m as lost as you are,\" he said calmly. \"I might have tripped something by mistake. It’s entirely possible none of this has anything to do with me.\"","As it turned out, that was the wrong thing to say in that valley.","Because the sky churned then, harder than it had been churning, the black-gold light in the mist thickening overhead, and a voice came out of all of it at once.","| No, it is definitely connected to you.|","...!","\"...\"","Everyone went quiet.","Ryaenara stopped mid-motion in the shallows. Anaximander’s wry expression emptied out. And Hvitrmarr and Damodred both moved without a word spoken between them, the steed coming up on Noah’s left and the titan settling in behind his right shoulder, close enough that the valley darkened where he stood!","Theron went to his knees in the sand as his face filled with reverence!","\"O Ancestral Voice .\" His own voice cracked on it. \" Has the time truly come?!\"","The Ancestral Voice.","Noah’s eyes went sharp, and he reached out with everything he had, and found nothing whatsoever. No presence, no weaving, no location, no origin. The voice was not coming from a direction!","| Since we are all pressed for time, I will be brief, and I would prefer not to repeat myself.|","| At this moment, invaders are butchering Superpowered Lifeforms across this Dimension. Laying them out in rows and putting them in the water and grinding them down, for greed, and in some cases for pleasure.|","|If nothing is done, they will have everything regardless. The collar. The wells. The Blooms. All of it, at their leisure, after the last of my descendants is used up. I have watched it get worse while waiting for a candidate who met the standard.|","|So I made a gamble. I lowered the restrictions on who may be considered worthy to grasp THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity.|","...!","|You meet the lowered tier of requirements.|","| Which means it is now a race, and the thing you are racing is time. Obtain it, and there may still be Superpowered Lifeforms left in this Dimension to be saved. Fail to, or dawdle, and there will not be.|","Out at the center of the Well, the pillar answered.","A column of golden-black light bloomed off the trunk and climbed, and where it reached the height of the drifting islands it opened, folding out and inward at once until a doorway of black and gold hung in the sky above the water.","Noah looked up at it with shining eyes.","\" Who are you?\" he asked.","| Does it matter?|","|I am the dying voice of a Primeval thing that could not let go of something. Ancestral Voice is more than enough for you to be going on with, and it is what they have called me for ages, and I have never bothered to correct them.|","|Now. Time is of the essence, as a madman has begun to butcher Superpowered Lifeforms in numbers even I did not anticipate. So. Will you move? Will you go and see whether those measly credentials of yours can actually obtain THE Aurate Collar?|","|If that dragon standing beside you had been the one chosen, this would have been considerably easier. If that monster wearing severed hands for a blindfold had been chosen, easier still. Alas, they do not meet the requirements|","|Enter. And since you are the one who must attempt it, you enter alone, or the path dissipates.|","...!","Noah shook his head, internally, at the sheer nerve of it!","Insulted, recruited, and put on a clock by something that would not even give a name!","He began to rise out of the sand.","He could not take Hvitrmarr, and he could not take Damodred, and while he thought about that he also thought about the words of how a madman had begun to butcher, and what those words meant about the next hour in a Dimension he had walked into for a look around.","So he turned to the two of them, and spoke calmly.","\" You two. Take Anaximander and Ryaenara across to wherever they’re being butchered.\" He looked at Hvitrmarr, then up at the veil of hands. \" Kill the Infinite True Lifeforms. All of them you find. And if you sense anything too powerful, anything that doesn’t measure, pull back. Okay?\"","\" Understood ,\" Hvitrmarr said.","Since it was only human to help, and since he had said as much out loud before he came through that obelisk, Noah then raised his head toward the churning sky!","\" Can you help guide them?\" he asked. \" To wherever the Superpowered Lifeforms are dying the most. You clearly care what happens to them, and my people can help.\"","There was, after all, no reason a voice that protective should not be put to work.","And he was thinking about several things at once. Whatever this pathway turned out to be, his forces would not be idle during it, and a Dimension full of invading Infinite Lifeforms was a Dimension full of corpses and loot with Infinity still in them.","|...|","The voice was quiet for a moment.","|I will direct them where they need to be.|","Noah nodded, and took a step, and appeared before the golden black doorway.","Then he looked back.","Hvitrmarr was frowning. He could feel it through the bond more clearly than he could see it on her face, the whole of her objecting leaving him alone.","And Damodred spoke, and his voice rolled up through the valley from somewhere behind his ribs.","’ The Master’s existence is surrounded by a grand weaving of his own making, and by a destiny he wrote himself. There is nothing in that doorway that was not already answering to him.’","’I will kill and collapse out here on your behalf. I will protect these little ones. Do not worry.’","\"...\"","The words sat heavily on the sand, and Hvitrmarr’s frown did not leave, but her shoulders came down.","Noah nodded once to both of them, and stepped through the doorway, and was gone!"]},{"number":5559,"title":"Chapter 5559: Chapter 5558: Outcasts!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","The suppression arrived before he had finished stepping.","It came as waves rather than as a wall, rolling through him one after another and settling in the places where his facets lived, and although Noah had felt suppression before, this was something else.","This was procedural. It did not fight him. It simply went through his existence closing doors!","| Welcome to THE Ancestral Grounds of Ymnaros.|","|The vast weavings of authority are suppressed here. All facets of your existence are locked, and will remain so. You will be permitted to keep a single thing.|","|What within your existence do you wish to keep?|","Since he had perhaps two heartbeats before the question stopped being an offer, Noah did not spend them being surprised.","He weighed all. His Osmontian Source Infinity was the deepest well he had, but a well is only useful if you can carry water in something. His Ananke Intent was the second order and it had never once failed him, and yet Intent needed a shape to press through. THE Collision of Causes was an engine and engines needed hands. And every appendage he had was a hand that would be closed by whatever had just closed the rest.","Of course, there was only one thing on the list that was not an instrument at all.","\" My Osmontian Tongue, \" he said.","HUUM!","The gold and black seas around him churned, and the prompts came down.","|Selection accepted.|","|All facets of your existence are hereby unusable. Osmontian Source Infinity: locked. Volume: locked. Output: locked. Trueness: locked. The Nine Foundations: locked. THE Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian: locked. THE Collision of Causes: suspended. All appendages: sealed. THE Quintessential Confluence: unavailable.|","|Retained: THE Osmontian Tongue. Five Letters and one Word.|","HUUM!","When the churning cleared he found himself standing on a road!","It ran out of the darkness beneath his feet and continued ahead of him as far as he could see, shimmering stellar obsidian shot through with gold, and there was nothing else anywhere. No ground beside it, no sky above it, only an expanse of spatial dark in every direction with a single path drawn through it, and it went on past any point where seeing stopped being useful.","Noah stood and looked at that for a moment, and did not step.","|In existence, the unknowns always exceed the known.|","The Ancestral Voice came differently in here. Some of the imperiousness had gone out of it, and what had replaced it was closer to melancholy.","|This is true for almost every lifeform that has ever drawn breath, and most of them live comfortably enough within it. THE Ymnaros was blessed to have an unknown. It was cursed because the unknown it had was far too grand for it.|","|That grandness made my people into Superpowered Lifeforms. It also guaranteed, from the first age, that it would eventually be the thing that brought them to cataclysm, because a small people sitting on top of something enormous will always eventually be visited by something that wants it. That has been the shape of our entire history, and the shape was set before any of us could read it.|","|And in all those ages, my people never produced a single one who could grasp that grandness. Not one. So in the final moments, having run out of our own, I have expanded the search externally.|","|Now here you are.|","Noah listened to all of that calmly.","\" What made me fulfill the requirements, \" he asked, \" when someone like Hvitrmarr didn’t? Or Damodred. The dragon and the titan out there. Both of them are considerably more than I am.\"","| Potential.|","|There have been Superpowered Lifeforms across our history more powerful than you are at this moment, and some of them stood on that sand and were declined. The standard was never a measurement of what a thing is.|","| In existence, what could be is always greater than what is. A finished thing has a ceiling and can be priced. An unfinished thing cannot, and that unpriceable quantity is what the collar was made to answer.|","|However.|","| Potential is also the easiest thing in existence to stifle, waste, or simply lie about. Anything can look like it might become something. So it must be tested, which means you must be tested, and I take no pleasure in the necessity.|","There was a pause, and the melancholy went out of the voice and something drier came in.","|If I had the capability, I would take THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity in my own hands and give it to whomever I chose, and I would have done so ages ago, and a great many of my descendants would still be alive. But existence does not work that way. It always has to be so fucking complicated.|","|So. The first test, as you walk this path.|","|When you have lost almost all of your power, except one thing, how do you fight?|","...!","Ahead of him on the road, auras began to rise.","They rose in a line across it, blazing up out of nothing, and they were humanoid, or had been.","Each shape held roughly the proportions of a person and then failed them somewhere, a shoulder carried too high, an arm that had continued past where an arm ends, spines where a spine should not surface, the whole silhouette reading like something that had been correct and had then kept growing.","And each of them wore white and blue!","The same suits. The same simple cut Theron Adranos wore, the same chest sign designed to be recognized at a distance by frightened people, ragged now and stretched wrong over the shapes underneath, but unmistakably the same.","Their eyes were full of a murky obsidian light, and there was nothing behind it but madness.","Compared to the invaders in the gardens, they gave off nothing at all. Not one wave of authority, exactly as Theron gave off nothing, exactly as every one of their kind gave off nothing. And yet standing at the near end of that road, Noah felt the pressure of them come down the obsidian gold like weather rolling off a mountain.","\" These are...\" he said slowly, \" mutated Superpowered Lifeforms?\"","|Across existence, accidents are inevitable.|","|The emergence of a Superpowered Lifeform is not always so pretty as the ones you have met. The Blooms resolve an existence into a truer version of itself, and most of the time that is a gift. Sometimes the truer version is a horror, and the water does not consult anyone before it finishes the work.|","|And there are the others. Superpowered Lifeforms who took what the Blooms gave them and used it to oppress, to press down on their own, to decimate whatever was smaller than they were. In those cases the rejection does not come from us. Their own existence rejects them, and turns into this.|","|These are THE Outcasts. The dark underbelly of every accident and vileness THE Ymnaros has produced, kept here, on this road, because there was nowhere else to keep them and because someone walking toward the collar should have to look at them.|","| Pass through them, and you may continue on your path.|","Noah looked ahead and counted.","Thirty-six of them, standing across the road!","Each one carried an oppression that measured as grand as a Cenozoic Scale being at minimum, and several of them read heavier than that, which raised a question he did not have time to answer properly.","Were they all S-Rank? SS?","The Outcasts did not wait for him to work it out. They came, all at once, thirty-six ruined shapes surging down the obsidian gold road, and Noah stood there with his facets locked, his Intent sealed, his Causes suspended, and one Tongue in his mouth!","And...","\" THE MORTAL COIL.\"","Blue light flashed out around him.","| THE DOMAIN OF THE MORTAL COIL has been laid.|","|Within its bounds all authority is designated absent. Every Scale, every Intent, every Pantheon, every Cause, every claim of power stacked upon an existence. Beings within stand as only what a human is beneath it, a life that can dream, and hope, and end.|","|Wielder privilege: as THE True Human Emperor, you retain the standing of an F-Rank Hunter.|","|Note: the domain does not require access to your locked facets. It is a Word of your own Tongue, and a Word is not a weaving. It is a truth spoken aloud, and a truth cannot be suppressed by a ground that has no opinion on whether it is true.|","Although the domain had worked exactly as intended in the gardens, Noah had not forgotten the one detail that mattered.","Theron Adranos had stood inside it and felt nothing. Whole, unchanged, himself.","Ruination’s reading of that was that Superpowered Lifeform strength was not authority at all, and therefore not the sort of thing the Word could take.","So this time, as he spoke it, Noah did not aim it at authority.","He aimed it at everything. He pressed the intent through the Word with a specificity he had not used before, at power and at not-power, at authority and at whatever else a thing might be carrying instead, at the whole of every existence on that road down to the plain mortal animal underneath, regardless of what framework any of it belonged to!","Everything here would be human!","OOOOH!","Ahead of him, THE Outcasts sensed it.","The change went through the line like a wave breaking backward, and thirty-six ruined shapes threw back their heads and roared, and the sound in it was not rage. It was pain, and it was fervor, and it was the noise of things that had been kept in the dark on a road for ages suddenly feeling something take hold of them that they had not felt since whatever they were before.","Then they surged, all of them, straight at him!"]},{"number":5560,"title":"Chapter 5560: Chapter 5559: Pride!","paragraphs":["The first one reached him and it was nearly twice his size!","Made human, an Outcast was still a body that had gone on growing past where a body stops, and no Word in existence was going to shrink a shoulder or unbend a spine or take back the reach of an arm that had continued. He had removed their power. He had not removed their mass!","And, since he had a river of nothing to draw on, he was going to have to do this with his hands.","So he opened his mouth as the shape came down on him.","\"I AM.\"","HUUM!","The affirmation went through him gloriously!","There was no facet behind it, no Source Infinity, no Intent, nothing at all except two words of his own Tongue spoken by the existence that had written them, and that turned out to be enough. His frame filled. His arms went heavy in a way that had nothing to do with weight!","The declaration was not a spell being cast, it was an existence stating the plain fact of itself out loud in a place that had suppressed everything except the ability to do so, and existence had no argument prepared against a thing insisting it was!","He caught the descending arm at the elbow and broke it the wrong way.","CRACK!","Then he stepped inside the ruined shape’s reach and drove his palm up under its jaw, and the blow landed like a hammer coming off an anvil, and the head came back and the whole body followed it, and Noah went with it and put his other hand through its chest as...The Outcast came apart on the obsidian gold road.","Bloof began to flow!","Two more were already on him before he could even pause!","\"I AM OSMONT.\"","He said it low, and the second affirmation stacked onto the first, and the road cracked under his heel as he pivoted. His hand came across in a flat edge and took the nearest one’s throat open, and he did not stop moving, because stopping was the thing that would kill him here!","These Outcasts were not soldiers. They fought like animals that had been in pain for a very long time and had finally been given something to put their hands on.","Compared to the army in the gardens, this was infinitely more dangerous.","So he weaved.","He went through the middle of them rather than around, because the road was narrow and there was nowhere else to be. A blow came in from his left and he was not there for it. A second closed on his shoulder and he broke the wrist attached to it and used the arm as a handle to put its owner into the path of a third as he smashed them together like sacks of grain!","\"I AM HUMAN.\"","WAA!","He waved his hand as it cleanly cut through an Outcasts whole, their body split in two as they twitched hatefully below him!","An Outcast got a hand on him at that moment, actually got a grip, and for a moment Noah’s whole body was lifted off the obsidian gold with fingers closing on his ribs, and he reached back and took hold of the thumb and simply tore the digit off the hand, and dropped, and finished the thing while it was still deciding what had happened.","Blood came off them and splattered everywhere!","Because they were human now, and human things bleed, and there was a great deal of them!","Even so, he made certain not to be injured. That was not vanity. He had one Word, one Tongue, no Marrow to accelerate anything, and no Hepatarch waiting to bring him back a second time. Every exchange had to end with him whole, and so he did not trade a single blow he had not already decided he could avoid.","And in the middle of all of it, weaving between a dozen of them at once with his hands wet, he found himself looking at their eyes.","Murky obsidian, and mad, and full of pain!","As he felt their pain while destroying them, he couldn’t help but voice out...","\" Why wait? \" he asked, and put a knee through a ribcage while he said it.","\" Why wait until the last moment to expand the search for your own legend? Ages of this. All these years, all this pain, an entire people ground down waiting for someone who was never going to appear from your own stock. And you had the ability to change things the whole time. \" He caught an arm, broke it, moved. \" For what?\"","|A matter of pride.|","The Ancestral Voice came calmly, without any defensiveness at all!","|A thing like THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity is an object that Descendants of Those Who Remain would come for personally if they knew it was here and understood what it was. Primeval Ones would come. Things older than either would come.|","|And you are asking me why we did not simply hand it to an outsider?|","|I and those like me decided this a very long time ago. It is ours. It grew here, and the water grew from it, and my people grew from the water, and every drop of that lineage was paid for in blood by us and by nobody else. Why should it go to someone who wandered in?|","|It is like taking hold of a beautiful woman with a big chest and an unfathomably big ass, and then being told that after ages of never once enjoying her, I must now present her to somebody else.|","Noah nearly missed a step!","What the hell was this Ancestral Voice?!","|I hate what is happening here. I hate it immensely.|","|But I hate what has been done to the Superpowered Lifeforms more. I have watched them die in rows in front of stones for ages, waiting on a promise I was too proud to loosen, and pride is a luxury for the living and I am neither living nor proud enough anymore to pay for it with them.|","|So. Let us see whether you can take it.|","|Because so far, and I say this reluctantly, the selection appears to be decent.|","...!","By the time it finished, Noah had run out of Outcasts.","He came out the far end of them the way a man comes out of surf, and there was nothing left standing on the road behind him. Thirty-six ruined shapes lay across the shimmering obsidian gold, and some of them were still twitching, and a few of the twitching ones were doing it in the small aimless way that has nothing to do with intent anymore.","The white and blue was gone from all of them. It had been dark to begin with and it was darker now!","Noah stood at the near edge of the empty road, painted from his hands to his shoulders to his jaw, blood cooling on him in the spatial dark, breathing hard for the first time in a long while, and looked back!","He had no facets. No Intent. No Causes. No Confluence, no Marrow, no appendages, no Pantheon, and no Infinity of any kind.","He had said some letters several times, and meant them!","Then he turned forward, and with a heavy gaze, he walked.","Because he was!","He was Human!"]},{"number":5561,"title":"Chapter 5561: Chapter 5560: Failure!","paragraphs":["\"What’s next?\"","Noah asked it calmly.","The Ancestral Voice was quiet for a while before it answered, and the quiet itself was informative.","|Capability, stripped of everything, is the first of it. You have that.|","|The second is a test of your character. When you have been stripped bare of everything, what choices do you actually make?|","|For this, you will have to give access to memories.|","Noah kept walking, and said nothing yet.","|THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity does not care about your secrets, and it cares nothing at all for your power. It wants memories of what you are, and of those you normally associate with, because a character cannot be tested in the abstract. It has to be tested against the things a person would actually lose.|","|You are free to deny it. Say so, and we stop here, and the two of us will have had a somewhat pleasant afternoon.|","HUUM!","Above the road, the manifestation bloomed.","It came out of the spatial dark the way the one over the Well had, translucent and enormous, the broad collar of gold with its rows of tubular beads and its swaying fringe of teardrop pendants, and the unreadable design on its front plate turned until it faced him. Then a single thread of gold extended down from it, thin as a hair and perfectly steady, and reached toward his head.","Noah’s eyes went cold as it came.","Since he had been asked and not commanded, he decided precisely what it was going to be permitted to touch. He assembled the memories himself. Nothing to reveal the full extent of his immensity and his people...just surface level!","The thread touched his temple!","Waves of vibrant light pulsed out along the road in both directions, and an instant later, the road ahead of him was no longer empty.","Henry stood there. Blue-gold hair, twenty years old to look at, a younger Noah wearing his own face back at him. And beside him, Seo-yeon, small, looking up, the way she had looked up when she had first started calling him Aba.","Behind each of them stood a titan.","They were shrouded in flame of different colors, and their proportions did not resolve properly against the dark, and each of them had a hand closed around a throat!","|This trial requires you to answer from the options provided, so that it may take a better grasp of your character and your choices.|","|In front of you is your son, whom you fathered and have been with for the whole of his life. Beside him is your adopted daughter, whom you have only recently taken under your fold. Primeval Ones have hold of their weavings and their lives, and can snap either in an instant.|","| THE Aurate Collar asks. Which of the two do you save?|","...!","Noah’s eyes shone with anger.","\" What is this bullshit?\"","He did not stop walking!","\" How does an unrealistic hypothetical explain anything about my character? You have my memories. You know what I have actually done, in front of actual monsters, when actual people I love were actually in danger. And instead of reading any of that, you build me a puppet show and ask me to pick which puppet dies?\"","|Henry, or Seo-yeon?|","|THE Aurate Collar demands your answer on which one you would save. Choose not to answer, and you may fail this trial, and my people continue to die unless I locate another candidate worthy of it in a very short amount of time.|","Noah looked at the two illusions on his road and gave the only answer he had.","\"I would save both ,\" he said coldly. \"I do not make sacrifices.\"","The road buzzed.","| Fucker, choose ONE.|","The Ancestral Voice had lost the melancholy entirely.","|Henry, or Seo-yeon? A great deal is on the line here, more than you understand, and all that is required of you is a simple choice. You are being asked to say a name. Say a name!|","And Noah remained entirely unfettered.","His Osmontian Cause of Tyranny was suspended along with everything else, and yet the light of it came up into his eyes anyway, because a Cause is not only a tool, and what it was expressing had never needed authority to be true!","\"I would save both ,\" he said. \" I am grand enough to do so in your tepid hypothetical.\"","...!","The road buzzed harder, and something in the dark harrumphed, and the manifestation of Henry and Seo-yeon dissolved.","Another bloomed in its place.","Amelia, this time. His mother, the Originator of THE Infinite Cause, standing on the obsidian gold road looking exactly as she did when she was thinking about him.","|Then a simpler one, since apparently the math offends you.|","|Your mother’s existence is failing. The only cure lies inside a Dimension you can reach, and reaching it requires you to abandon Anaximander to his death and the war you have already committed to.|","| The Collar asks. Do you save your mother, or do you keep your commitment to Anaximander and others?|","\"Neither of those is a choice ,\" Noah said. \" Those are two failures.\"","|Answer the question.|","\"I’d cure her and keep my commitments.\" He kept walking, straight through Amelia’s illusion, and it parted around him like smoke. \" You keep constructing worlds where I have one hand. I have never had one hand in my life, and when I did, I built a second one. Ask me a real question.\"","The road shook.","The next manifestation came fast, and it was Hvitrmarr, and she was in chains again.","|Very well. Your Steed, whose curse you lifted at the cost of your own life. To hold THE Aurate Collar, you must return her to the harness she was born into. One existence, restored to its sentence, and in exchange you obtain a treasure that Descendants of Those Who Remain would kill each other for.|","| Do you take it?|","\"No.\"","|Then you decline the collar. That is an answer, at least, and I will accept-|","\" That isn’t what I said .\" Noah’s voice did not rise. \" I said no to your trade. I’ll take the collar and she stays free, because I don’t accept the premise that those two things are attached. You attached them. Existence didn’t.\"","|That is not how the question works.|","\" Then the question is badly built.\"","HUUM!","The chains on the illusion rattled and she dissolved, and the fourth came, and the fourth was crueler.","Ryaenara. And beside her, thin and gray and dying, Ulf.","|You hold a Bloom that can potentially cure THE Withering of the Remembered Root. One Bloom. One entry per year. And a Dimension full of Superpowered Lifeforms being ground into wells at this exact moment, any one of whom that Bloom could also save.|","| The brother of the woman who has followed you, or a stranger’s people. The Collar asks which you would try to save.|","...!","\"I’ll cure Ulf, and I’ll save these people. \" He looked up into the dark. \" Do you have any better questions?\"","WAA!","The road groaned along its whole length.","| You are FAILING this trial.|","The Ancestral Voice came down with real weight now, and something desperate had climbed into it.","|Do you understand what I am offering? Do you have the smallest grasp of it? This is a Remnant Existential Treasures . Remnant Existential Treasures are not power, they are not rank, they are not a rung on anyone’s ladder. Things older than Primeval Ones will fight each other to hold what is hanging above those wells, and it is being offered to a man with dirty hands and a borrowed road because I am out of time and out of descendants!|","|All you have to do is answer. Say a name. Pick a side. It costs you nothing, and nobody in your memories will ever know what you said in here, and at the end of it you may hold something that reshapes every framework you have ever climbed!|","|Why would you throw that away rather than answer a hypothetical?!|","And Noah stopped walking at this time.","He stood in the middle of the obsidian gold road, painted in the drying blood of thirty-six Outcasts, with every facet of his existence locked and one Tongue in his mouth, and the spatial dark pressed in around him and did not manage to press him anywhere.","\"It is merely a treasure ,\" he said.","\"I want it. But I do not like the trial you built for it, and I am not going to become a man who answers those questions in order to obtain an object, because the man who answers them is not the man who walked in here, and you would be handing your people’s inheritance to someone else wearing my face.\"","His eyes were steady in the dark.","\"So I remain by my choices. I remain true.\"","BOOM!","Every manifestation on the road shattered at once.","Ryaenara and Ulf and the chains and the flame-shrouded titans and all of it came apart into golden obsidian light, and the light gushed outward along the whole length of the path in both directions, filling the spatial dark, and then it turned, and converged, and drew inward in slow spirals until it hung in front of him in the shape of a single golden gem!","The Ancestral Voice, when it came, was somber, and slow, and had nothing left in it of the thing that had been shouting a moment ago.","| You... have passed the second trial.|","|It tested how true you could remain to yourself when everything had been taken and something enormous was offered for a small piece of you.|","|You...|","| You may actually stand a chance.|","BOOM!"]},{"number":5562,"title":"Chapter 5562: Chapter 5561: Unfathomably Prized!","paragraphs":["<Anaximander>","They were moved across vast Distances relatively easily by The Ancestral Voice.","The four of them simply ceased to be in one valley and commenced to be in another.","And in here...was a citadel.","It stood at the center of this domain the way the pillar stood at the center of the last one, and it was under siege. Twelve Superpowered Lifeforms held the ground in front of it, and behind them, packed into the citadel and spilling out along its terraces, were the natives!","Hundreds of thousands of humans. Perhaps more. Ordinary lifeforms of THE Ymnaros, small and frightened and entirely without the grand strength their protectors carried!","Above the citadel, the Infinite True Lifeforms were arriving in ranks.","\" There are...rather a lot of them,\" Anaximander observed.","\" Yes .\" Hvitrmarr did not sound especially concerned about it. She stood beside him in her human shape with the nine First Causes drifting through her robe, and she was not looking at the enemy at all!","She was looking up and to her left, at the mountain of gray scars and severed hands standing behind them. \" Although the rest of us do not even need to move, if you are here.\"","Damodred said nothing to that.","He regarded her for a long moment from behind the veil of ancient hands, and Anaximander had the distinct impression of a very old thing being paid a compliment and not knowing the current etiquette for it, and then the titan began to float down toward the field.","Since Anaximander had never seen him work, he watched carefully.","A sea began to form above the citadel. That was the only word for it, and it was gray, and it came out of nowhere. It gathered in a great swelling mass over the ranks of the Infinite, and where its underside boiled it did so slowly, with the awful patience of a thing that had been waiting ages to be poured out somewhere!","The Infinite True Lifeforms looked up.","Compared to the invaders in the gardens, these had the sense to understand what they were looking at, and Anaximander watched several of them make the correct decision and begin to withdraw, which was interesting because it did not help them!","The sea came down.","And everything the descending gray touched began to calcify.","Where the gray fell across an Infinite True Lifeform, the compounding of Infinity stopped compounding.","Their Infinity, which by its nature was a thing that only ever became more, was simply frozen at whatever quantity it happened to be holding!","Anaximander was about to follow since it seemed only reasonable to make himself useful, when a voice arrived from everywhere at once.","| You will have to come in another direction, little guy.|","...!","Anaximander stopped where he was.","\" Where?\" he asked, and then, because the first question was less interesting than the second, \" Why?\"","|Because you are wasted here, and because I have spent enough ages watching things be wasted.|","|Also, you are like us. You would have been a good candidate for THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity. Genuinely good. Better than most of my own line....|","\" But not good enough.\"","|You would have failed.|","The voice said it flatly!","|You would have walked the road, and passed the first, and probably passed the second, and then failed at the last step, exactly as we failed at the last step. Every one of us. Ages of candidates and not one made it past the end of it.|","\" Then may I ask what the last step is?\"","|No.|","\"...\"","|But...|","|For all those of us who failed. Could you pick up the pieces?|","Anaximander said nothing.","|My pieces. My friend’s pieces. The pieces of everyone who walked that road across every age and got to the end of it and could not close their hand. We are still there, in a manner of speaking.|","|They are heavy burdens. But you should be able to carry them, and nobody else I have ever met should, and I am running out of time.|","|If you accept.|","...!","Anaximander thought about it.","He thought about it for rather a short time, all things considered!","\" Yes ,\" he said. \" All right.\"","...!","And he was gone.","Where he disappeared, Hvitrmarr gazed as her eyes flashed with a cold light!","—","The domain he arrived in was dark.","That was the first quality of it, and the second was that it was a sea.","Half buried in that sea were the titans .","Massive lifeforms, each one the scale of the thing standing over the citadel he had just left, sunk to the shoulder or the chest or the brow in the dark, and all of them were still. Not sleeping. Anaximander had seen sleeping things. These were done!","And then one of them raised its head.","It came up out of the sea slowly, and it was shrouded in vibrant Primeval light, and the light was the only living thing anywhere in that place. It was also, he noticed, considerably dimmer than it must once have been.","|Across existence, the burden of the crown is heavy.|","The voice came from it, and out here, at its source, the Ancestral Voice sounded old!","|Unfathomably so. Every framework that has ever been climbed was built by somebody who wanted to set something down, and could not, and made a structure to hold it instead. That is all a hierarchy has ever been. A very elaborate way of not carrying a thing yourself.|","Anaximander looked at the sea of half-buried titans and understood that he was being told something about them.","|And you.|","|You are without any external authority whatsoever. Nothing about you presses outward on existence, nothing announces, nothing can be weighed, and yet things happen when you speak plainly at them.|","|It makes you something unfathomably prized across existence. More than you know, and more than I intend to explain, since half of what makes it valuable is that so few have understood it well enough to come looking.|","Anaximander listened silently!","The Primeval light dimmed and steadied.","|So I will tell you the only useful instruction I have, and it will sound like nothing. Keep being yourself. Just keep being exactly what you are, and everything else will come to you, and a great deal of it will come whether you want it or not.|","|Are you ready?|","...!","Anaximander did not hesitate.","He had crossed the dark between Dimensions on foot because doors were a superstition. He had walked into a red sea to help a friend.","He was, on reflection, extremely well prepared to be handed something enormous by a dying Superpowered Lifeform.","He nodded.","And in the next moment, all across that black expanse, the corpses began to shimmer.","The half-buried titans lit from within, one and then a dozen and then more than he could look at, and their vast still shapes came apart into streams of light. The light rose out of the sea in long slow ribbons, every age of failed candidates unspooling upward at once, and then all of it turned, and began to flow toward the small tousled man in the white robes standing above the water with his hands at his sides!"]},{"number":5563,"title":"Chapter 5563: Chapter 5562: Provenance! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","|I said you might actually have a chance. Even then, I am not sure, since you are going where I failed, and where all others failed. Let us see.|","...!","With those words in his ears, Noah grasped the gem that had appeared before him.","The moment his hand closed on it, the road changed. The obsidian gold beneath his feet began to wrap around itself, again and again, curling the way a ribbon curls, folding him inside its turns until the spatial dark was gone and there was only the winding path, containing him, carrying him!","|What you just grasped... is a Provenance Crystal. It is the key to where you are going, and it is also the lifeline. THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity gives every candidate a way out.|","|So long as it rests on your existence, you can survive the collapse of your existence in totality. All of it, at once, down to the foundation, and the crystal will hold enough of you together that something walks away afterward.|","|It was given to me. It was given to others of my kind. Primeval Ones, every one of us, and every one of us ended up using it, because all of us died where you are going next.|","|Be careful.|","HUUUM!","The prompts from Ruination came down as the road wound tighter.","| THE Provenance Crystal. Analysis follows.|","|Function: a tether of last resort. Upon the total collapse of the bearer’s existence, the crystal preserves a remnant sufficient for continuation. What continues is not guaranteed to be what entered. The crystal makes no representations regarding completeness.|","|Composition: unknown. The Regard reads it as older than the frameworks it protects against, and notes that it was not made. It was shed.|","|Origin: ?????|","|Additional observation: the crystal is oriented. Like THE Vermeil Blooms, it is seeking. Unlike them, it appears to have already found what it was seeking, and is now simply waiting.|","|?????|","...!","Noah read the last block twice!","Blinding obsidian gold light raged around him, brilliance unfolding in every direction at once, and an instant later it tore away, and Noah’s knees nearly buckled!","HUUM!","Weight came down on him.","Weight, plain and physical and enormous, pressing on his body and his existence at once, and he set his stance and held steady and made himself breathe before he made himself look.","Dark obsidian sands stretched away beneath his feet in every direction, fine and black and glittering faintly gold where the light caught the grains, dunes of it rolling out toward a horizon that shimmered with heat that had no sun to explain it. The air tasted of hot stone and age!","In the far distance, a golden obelisk rose out of the sands.","It stood alone, immense even at this far distance, its faces cut with lines he could not read, and around its upper reaches burned a sphere of impenetrable obsidian gold light, dense as a held breath. And within that light, small at this distance and unmistakable all the same, hung a necklace.","THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity!","The true one. Not a manifestation above a well, not a translucent watcher. The thing itself, at the end of the sands, wrapped in a light that had kept every age of candidates out!","And above all of it, filling the sky, was the other thing.","Noah raised his eyes and understood immediately what was pressing on him. A landmass hung in the heavens. A single colossal stone of obsidian gold, vast enough that calling it a stone felt dishonest, its underside worn smooth and its edges lost in their own distance, suspended over the entire domain with no support and no motion and no intention of needing either.","That was the weight!","| Me and my brethren perished at this very spot.|","The Ancestral Voice came quietly across the sands.","|Here. On these sands, under that stone. Every one of us used up our Provenance Crystals within sight of that obelisk, and what you are feeling now is the very beginning of it, the polite introduction, and it does not stay polite.|","Noah adjusted his stance as the weight thickened, and asked the question that mattered.","\" How do lifeforms such as yourselves perish from this? What is this?\"","|To understand that, you have to understand the core requirement of THE Aurate Collar.|","|If you have the capability, which you proved on the road. And if you are in fact unfathomably true to yourself, which you proved with your choices. Then the last thing that remains is something very few entities like us across all of existence ever get to understand.|","|Only lifeforms with boundless potential have a chance at it. The last test exists to measure whether you carry a tiny spark.|","The weight climbed as it spoke.","Noah felt it come down in increments, each one distinct, and he looked up and found that he had raised his hands above his head without entirely deciding to, because the pressure had become a thing his body insisted on answering with posture. It was visible now, almost. The air between him and the stone had begun to shimmer with the load moving through it!","\" What spark is it looking for?\"","Whatever spark it wanted, he would give it!","He had died once, and he was not going to lose his life again here under someone else’s rock!","|Across existence, everyone else utilizes.|","|Every route ever climbed is a route of absorption. Mana. Laws. Daos. Edicts. Concepts. Boundaries. Extremes. Infinity. The Primordial Source. Causes. All of them are external things. Even when you bring them into your existence, even when you make them the core of who you are, even when you carve them with your own hands as you have, they stemmed from elsewhere. You gathered them. They were there to be gathered.|","| Early, very early on, there were lifeforms who did not rely on anything external at all.|","|They generated their own essence and their own authority. Out of nothing but themselves, unique to each individual, produced by them and by nothing else anywhere in existence. It is called...Provenance Essence.|","HUUM!"]},{"number":5564,"title":"Chapter 5564: Chapter 5563: Provenance! II","paragraphs":["|Over time, lifeforms born capable of this stopped arising. Why, I do not know. I do not know, and my information may be incorrect, since everything I hold about them arrived already worn down to rumor.|","| But the rumor was this. Such beings could look at Those Who Remain and not be afraid.|","...!","|Beings so unfathomably true that they did not have to rely on any external authority whatsoever. Nothing borrowed, nothing gathered, nothing granted. Only themselves, generating themselves, answerable to nothing upstream because there was no upstream.|","Noah listened, and under other circumstances he would have enjoyed every word of it, since wonders of existence and deep history were among the few things he never got tired of.","The enjoyment was somewhat diminished by the sensation of his entire existence being slowly crushed!","The weight had doubled while the Voice talked, and doubled again, and his arms were burning above his head and his knees had bent into the sand, and he got his words out through his teeth.","\" Speak a little bit faster.\"","|THE Aurate Collar is not a tool that just anybody can wield. We theorized, ages ago, that it very likely requires Provenance Essence to use at all. And when candidates who walked its path began being issued Provenance Crystals, objects shed from something rather than made, the theory stopped being a theory.|","| It is also the reason Superpowered Lifeforms were born in THE Ymnaros in the first place.|","|THE Vermeil Blooms, produced as a mere side effect of THE Aurate Collar’s appearance here, are things that elevate the very core of a lifeform. They do not permit the absorption of external authority. They resolve a being into a truer version of what it already was. Exemplification instead of accumulation. That is why you have met beings with no authority at all who emulate as much power as any wielder of Infinity or the Primordial Source, and often more.|","|The runoff of the collar makes small, partial, downstream versions of what the collar requires in full.|","|And so the last trial is the determination of whether you carry the spark to produce Provenance Essence at all. THE Aurate Collar does not require that you produce it here. It only wants to see that the spark exists. The capability. The possibility of the possibility.|","|Those with boundless potential are those filled with endless possibilities. That is the test.|","Noah gritted his teeth and looked up at the stone filling the sky.","\" That is fine and all,\" he managed, \" but what the fuck does crushing me have to do with it.\"","|Above you is something that even I do not understand, and I stood under it twice.|","|What I do know is this. It is a pressure designed to give you the highest chance of producing a spark within your existence. If there is even a glimmer of possibility in you, a one in a million chance, a one in a trillion chance, that you could be like those lifeforms the rest of us have only heard rumors about, then you will be capable of bearing the weight coming down without collapsing, and somewhere in the bearing, the spark will show.|","|If you are not able to, then you will simply be like me, and like the others.|","|Failures. Who came so close, and watched it all slip away.|","The Voice went quiet for a moment, and when it continued, it had stopped performing entirely.","|I have been here once, and I collapsed. And I came back, because I could not stand losing such a thing, and I collapsed again, and that second time I barely managed to save scraps of my existence, and what is speaking to you now is what the scraps became.|","|Let us see whether you suffer the same fate.|","| Or whether you shall be different.|","WAA!","The stone came down.","Not all at once, since nothing about this place was merciful enough to be quick. It came down the way a debt comes due, in increments, each one arriving with its own weight and its own interest, and Noah met the first of them standing!","\"I AM!\"","The Letter went through him and his body filled, and he held.","The second increment took him to one knee. He felt it land across his shoulders like a continent shrugging, and the obsidian sand compressed beneath his shin into something like glass, and he put both hands up above his head and met the underside of a sky.","His palms touched stone.","That should not have been possible, since the landmass hung far above him, and it was possible anyway, because the weight had stopped being a property of distance. The stone was above him, therefore the stone was upon him!","Those were the rules here, and his hands were now carrying a piece of the sky, and his arms shook to the shoulder.","\"I AM OSMONT!\"","HUUM!","The affirmation poured down through his arms and his back and his planted knee, and for a moment the shaking stopped, and Noah breathed in the hot stone air and reorganized himself under the load.","Then the third increment arrived, and something in his left forearm cracked.","He heard it before he felt it, a dry sound like the road splitting, and then the pain came up through the bone and he shouted the next Letter into it rather than around it.","\"I AM HUMAN!\"","BOOM!","The weight paused.","It did not lessen. Nothing here lessened! But it paused, the way it had paused when the Outcasts flinched, as though the claim itself had briefly required consideration, and Noah used the pause to shift his stance, getting the load off the cracked arm and onto his back, bending forward beneath it, and now he knelt in the black sand with a world’s underside pressed across his shoulders and his spine, and he understood that he had arrived at the posture this trial had been designed to produce.","Every candidate across every age had knelt exactly here. Holding exactly this! An entire history of the almost-worthy, folded one at a time into the shape of a figure carrying a sky.","Blood ran from his nose and dripped off his chin into the sand, and the sand drank it without comment.","’ What... are you looking for?!’","He asked the distant Aurate Collar that was unfathomably silent!"]},{"number":5565,"title":"Chapter 5565: Chapter 5564: Provenance! III","paragraphs":["He asked it inwardly first, of the collar, of the stone, of the trial itself, and got nothing, and so he asked the only thing here that answered questions.","\" The lifeforms,\" he ground out. \" The ones with Provenance Essence. What were they? How did they live? What did they do with it?\"","|I do not know.|","\" You knew enough to theorize the collar requires it.\"","|I knew enough to fail twice. Those are different quantities of knowledge.| The Voice was quiet a moment.","|What I hold is this. They generated. Where everything else in existence gathers, they produced. I have said this already and I say it again because it is the whole of my inheritance on the subject. Everything else is rumor shaped like information.|","\" Then give me the rumor.\"","|They were few and they were many. They were early. They did not build Pantheons, as far as any account claims, and they did not climb Scales, and they held no Causes that anyone ever recorded, which I have always found either impossible or terrifying, and I have never determined which.|","Noah’s back was beginning to fissure!","He could feel it, not the bones now but the existence itself, hairline fractures spreading through the architecture of what he was, the way the small turning realm in Damodred’s lesson had cracked. Fourth increment. His arms had gone from shaking to a deep steady burn that was worse!","\" How ,\" he managed, \" does a thing get stronger without gathering? Walk me through it. You’re a Primeval who has died here. What would you have had to do differently?\"","|Accumulate better.|","\" That...makes no fucking sense.\"","|Refine what was accumulated until it became indistinguishable from self.|","\" That is still external things merely refined!\"","|Then I do not know, and that is precisely the point, and you have just found the edge of me.| Something bitter moved through the ancient voice.","|Do you understand what you are asking? You are asking a being made entirely of successful accumulation to describe its opposite. Every instrument I have for thinking about power is an instrument for thinking about acquisition. When I stood where you are kneeling, I tried to bear the weight with everything I had gathered across my whole existence, all of it, ages of it, and the weight went through all of it like it was not there, because it was not looking at what I had. It was looking at what I was underneath what I had, and underneath what I had, there was nothing that I had made.|","\"...!\"","| I am the wrong lens. I failed here because everything I know is the wrong lens.|","| Look at yourself.|","The fifth increment came down, and Noah’s right knee joined his left in the sand, and the blood was coming from his ears now as well as his nose, and a long crack opened somewhere in the region of his existence where the Foundations lived, and through all of it his mind kept working, because the mind was the one thing in him the stone had not yet reached!","Look at himself.","Fine. What was he?","He was human. He kept arriving at that and it kept feeling insufficient, because human was not ancient, human was not special, human was a small warm mortal category that he had crowned precisely because nobody else thought it was worth crowning.","He was not one of those early lifeforms. He was not born generating anything. He had been born in a house, and everything he had ever become, he had gotten from somewhere!","That was the sentence.","He knelt under a sky with his existence cracking, and the sentence turned over once more and showed him its other face, and Noah went very still beneath the stone.","Everything he had ever become, he had gotten from somewhere.","\"...\"","Infinity. He had not invented Infinity. It was a route that existed before him, a variety of lifeform, a framework other beings had walked for ages, and he had taken it into himself and made it enormous and it was still, at its root, an idea he had found lying in existence and picked up.","The Primordial Source. Found. Grasped. Not made!","Intent. The orders of Intent were a ladder someone else had described, Egoic and Ananke and Autarkis, and he had climbed two rungs of a ladder that was standing there before he arrived!","His Pantheon. THE Infiniverse was alive and his and beloved, and the concept of a Pantheon was as old as the Scales and older, inherited from every being who had ever raised one.","The nine First Causes of Hvitrmarr. Hers. Married into him, colliding in him at this very moment, and not his, never his, First Causes of a lineage seated by living hands that were not his hands!","Even his Osmontian Causes, carved from his own identity, were carved in the shape of a thing called a Cause, and Causes were external, Causes were the beams of a house somebody else had built or grown or claimed, and he had made his own beams but he had made them as beams, to fit a house he had not designed!","His whole existence, every layer of it, was magnificent borrowed architecture!","Oh!","And the weight was not looking at what he had.","The sixth increment came down and his existence screamed along every fissure at once, and Noah, kneeling in his own blood in the black sand, holding the underside of a world, began, impossibly, to smile.","Because he could see it now, and it was enormous, and it was insane, and it was the only door in the room.","The trial was not asking him to hold more. Every candidate in every age had tried to hold more, had brought the whole of what they had gathered and stacked it under the stone, and the stone had gone through it like it was not there. Accumulation could not answer this, no matter how grand, because accumulation was the wrong category of thing. The spark was generation, and generation could not happen in a space that was already full.","Full of everything he had taken in.","To generate something completely his, something with no upstream, no origin, no elsewhere, he would have to make room for it, and there was no room, because Noah Osmont was packed to the walls with the treasures of existence, every one of them earned, every one of them loved, every one of them from somewhere else.","So the answer, the whole answer, the answer that no accumulating being in any age could have permitted itself to see, was this.","Cast it out.","All of it.","Anything he had not pioneered himself. Anything that had existed as an idea before he arrived at it.","Shatter Infinity out of his existence. Carve out the Primordial Source. Break the Pantheon-concept, the Intent-ladder, the borrowed shape of Causes, the nine First Causes that were a Steeds and not his, every framework, every route, every inherited beam in the whole borrowed house, cast every last piece of it out of himself until what knelt in this sand was only what Noah Osmont had generated and nothing else at all.","And then see what was left.","And see if it sparked.","His maddened smile widened beneath the blood, and above him the stone came down for the seventh time!","...!"]},{"number":5566,"title":"Chapter 5566: Chapter 5565: Provenance! IV","paragraphs":["The seventh increment settled onto his back, and Noah began!","In theory, he understood it completely. Cast out everything that did not generate from him, empty the house of every borrowed beam, and see what was left. In theory it was clean. It was even elegant!","In practice, he was about to reach into his own existence and tear out everything he had ever been and had been building, and his hands were shaking before he started, and not from the stone.","He started with the one that frightened him least.","The Primordial Source. He had grasped it later, integrated it partially. It was dense and patient inside him and it was not his, had never been his, was older than every framework and belonged to all of existence and none of it.","’ Cast out.’","He took hold of it with his will and pulled, and it tore free of his foundations like a root coming out of deep soil, and he sent it away from himself, down through the one channel this place had not sealed, into the living Observable Existence he carried, and THE Infiniverse received it in silence and held it, and a piece of what Noah Osmont was became a thing Noah Osmont was storing.","The absence hit him like cold water!","He breathed through it, and the stone pressed down, and he went again.","The Causes!","This one cost him. He had wanted, even in the theory, even while the idea was still glorious and abstract, to keep his nine. His Osmontian Causes, carved from his own identity, Existence and Paradox and Tyranny and the rest. Surely those were his. Surely those counted!","They did not, and he knew it!","They were carved in the shape of a thing called a Cause. And Causes linked to Civilizations and concepts and frameworks that were standing in existence long before he arrived, designed or grown by hands that were not his, and he had made his own versions of somebody else’s idea, which made them his work and not his origination!","So...","’ Cast out!’","HUUM!","The nine tore free, and with them the nine First Causes of Hvitrmarr, and as that mixture unwound he felt the bond to a distant queen strain and cry out somewhere far above this place, a single pulse of alarm through a connection stretched thin by the trial’s walls, and he could not stop to answer it.","The Collision of Causes stuttered and went silent inside him for the first time since he had lit it. The drums stopped.","Eighteen anchors sank into THE Infiniverse, and the quiet where they had been was enormous.","And then he stood at the edge of the one that terrified him.","Infinity.","He knelt under the stone with his blood in the sand and looked at it, the deep blue-gold sea of his Osmontian Source Infinity, the thing that had been with him since before the crown, before the Letters, before any of it!","Infinite Mana!","It was THE first gift, the oldest companion, the floor under every floor. He had been the man with infinite mana before he had been anything else at all!","It was all he had begun with.","And it was not his. Infinity was a route, a variety, a framework walked by lifeforms across all of existence for ages before one human picked it up, and the fact that his was the grandest ocean of it anywhere did not change one drop of where the idea had come from.","Noah’s whole existence recoiled from the act!","Oh!","Fear, actual fear, the thing he never showed and rarely felt, moved through him at the prospect of being a man without it!","What was he without Mana?!","But...","He gripped the ocean.","’ Even this.’","’CAST IT OUT!’","BOOM!","The sea tore out of him.","It went in one enormous wrenching motion, blue-gold light hemorrhaging out of every layer of his existence at once, pouring away down the channel into THE Infiniverse, and she took it, his ocean, into herself, and Noah knelt in the black sand and felt what it was to be empty of the thing his own name had been built on.","He did not stop!","He could not stop, because stopping now would leave him half-emptied and holding nothing, so he went through the rest of the borrowed house room by room and threw it all out.","Mana itself, the concept beneath the ocean. Cast out. The Pantheon-frame, the ancient inherited idea of housing realms within an existence. Cast out, and THE Infiniverse herself remained his and beloved and safe, but the framework by which he held her was severed, and she drifted from appendage to companion in a single tearing moment.","The Intent-ladder, Egoic and Ananke, two rungs climbed on a structure other beings had raised. Cast out, and his Ananke Intent of THE Quintessential Osmontian went silent and sank away, and the pressure he had carried was simply gone!","The Foundations he kept. The nine Foundations were fusions he had pioneered, his design from the first. Those were his!","The Tongue he kept, since the Tongue was the definition of his, the language of his own existence, and it was the one thing he had chosen from the start, and now he finally understood why!","Then...","The Scales.","He paused on that one, kneeling, bleeding, nearly hollow, because THE First and Second Infinite Scales of Existence was his framework, built by his hands, named in his Tongue, and every instinct said keep it.","And it was built as a Scale. In answer to Vakochev’s Scales, in the shape of Vakochev’s idea, a better ladder leaned against the same wall. An idea based on another’s idea.","’ Cast out.’","The Infinite Scale of Existence unhooked from him and sank into THE Infiniverse with everything else, and Noah knelt in the sand as a being without a framework of any kind.","One thing remained.","THE Amaranthine Heart.","It beat in his chest where his own heart had made room for it, warm and steady and alive, the heart of THE Felt Eternity, given with the words I give you my Everything. It was not a framework. It was not a concept. It was a gift from a being who loved him, and it had carried him through the HUMAN Letter.","It was also not his generation. It was hers.","’I’m sorry ,’ he thought, to Emotive, who could not hear him.","He cast it out.","THE Amaranthine Heart left his chest gently, the only gentle departure in the whole terrible inventory, and settled into THE Infiniverse beside the ocean and the Causes and the Scale, safe, kept...for a potential future that may never be!","And then it was done.","Noah knelt on the dark obsidian sands beneath the weight of a sky, and he was nothing!","Not weakened. Nothing. His body carried no authority whatsoever. No Infinity, no Source, no Intent, no Causes, no Pantheon, no Scale, no heart that was not his own.","\"...!\"","He felt the change the way one feels silence after a lifetime in a loud room, and what he felt was, of all things, familiar. This was a human body. This was what it had felt like to be a man in world before the first prompt ever bloomed. He was, freely and truly and completely, a normal human being.","Who was holding up a stone that had crushed Primeval Ones.","It did not mean he was as strong as a Primeval. He was not. It meant only that the weight had never once been measuring strength, and that what it measured, he was finally expressing with nothing borrowed in the way.","Just himself. Whatever that turned out to be!","The stone came down for the eighth time.","Noah’s arms buckled. His whole body shook, the plain human muscle of it burning past every limit muscle has, and he closed his eyes and bowed his head beneath the load, and every fissure in his existence groaned at once, and there was nothing left to reinforce with, no Letter he had the breath to speak, no ocean, no drums, nothing between him and the collapse except whatever he was.","And his body, being a body, did what bodies do at the very end.","It understood, in the wordless way flesh understands, that it was about to be crushed. That no help was coming from anywhere, because everywhere had been cast out. That if anything was going to preserve this existence, the existence would have to produce it, now, itself, from nothing, because nothing was all that remained.","And so, deep within him, in the emptied dark where an ocean used to be...","HUUUM!","A singularity bloomed.","It was blue. Dazzling, incandescent blue, a single point of light igniting in the hollow of him, and it was small and it was inexhaustible and it was unfathomably beautiful, and it had no upstream, no framework, no name in any Tongue but his.","It was his light. It stemmed from Noah Osmont, and from nothing else in all of existence!","His body remained free of any authority. Nothing pressed outward from him. Nothing announced. To every instrument ever built for weighing power, the kneeling figure in the bloody sand read exactly as it had a moment before, a normal human at the end of his strength.","And yet!","He had stopped straining!","He had stopped shaking!","HE HAD STOPPED SHAKING!"]},{"number":5567,"title":"Chapter 5567: Chapter 5566: Ignorance! I","paragraphs":["The singularity rose with him!","That was the first thing Noah understood about it, kneeling in his own blood with the weight of a sky on his back. It did not sit inside him the way the ocean had sat, or press outward the way Intent had pressed. It rose as he rose, moved as he moved, and it was, without any close competition, the most calm and stable thing he had ever felt.","Internally, it was blinding. A point of incandescent blue burning in the emptied dark of him, bright past looking at directly!","Externally, it was nothing. Not one glimmer of aura left his body. Not one wave of anything crossed his skin. The instruments of existence, had any been pointed at him, would have found a bleeding human kneeling in sand.","And the moment it bloomed fully, what arrived with it was not power!","HUUM!","It was capability. Power was a quantity, and he had held quantities before, oceans of them, and this was not that. This was the wordless knowledge that he was capable. It generated from him completely. It had no upstream. It was his.","His Provenance!","’ PROVENANCE!’","...!","And then, without one glimmer of authority leaking from anywhere on his body, Noah began to rise.","It was the strangest sensation of his entire existence, and he had died once, so the competition was real. The weight above him did not lessen. Nothing about the stone changed at all. His body simply decided, joint by joint, that it could handle it, the way a body decides it can stand after illness, not through any surge of force but through a quiet reassessment of what was possible, and the reassessment kept arriving, and he kept rising!","His back straightened beneath the load!","One knee left the sand. Then the other!","The stone that had crushed Primeval Ones rode on his back, and then, slowly and deliberately, he brought it up onto his two raised hands, and stood beneath it holding the underside of a sky at arm’s length while his blood dried on his face.","Then one hand.","Then his fingers!","And then Noah pushed up, once, and the stone rose!","HUUUM!","It left his fingertips and climbed, the whole colossal landmass of obsidian gold ascending back into the heavens where it had hung, and it settled there and did not come down again, and across the entire domain the pressure released like a held breath finally let go!","The Ancestral Voice said nothing.","For the first time since the doorway, the voice that had narrated, insulted, mourned, and confessed through every step of this road had no words at all, and the silence stretched across the black sands, and Noah stood in the middle of it, small and bleeding and empty of everything, beneath a sky he had just put back.","Obsidian gold light filled the heavens.","It poured off the risen stone and down through the air and across the dunes, the whole domain igniting with it, and Noah closed his eyes and simply let himself feel.","The singularity hummed.","A constant, heavy hum, new and ancient at once, resonating out from the blue point through every layer of what remained of him, and where the resonance passed, things began to change!","He felt it at the smallest scale first, in the makeup of his cells, in the very structure of his atoms, the fine architecture of a human body beginning to break down and transform under a frequency that belonged to nothing else in existence.","And from the pores of his skin, filth began to leak.","Obsidian-gray sludge, thick and dark, welling up and running off him in slow rivulets, and Noah understood what he was seeing without anything explaining it. His Foundations, perfect across the Depths. His Physiology, rebuilt from Primeval Cells. Everything he had held and refined and elevated across the whole climb, and all of it, this entire time, had carried defects in it!","Murky filth folded into the joints of even his finest work, impurities so deep in the making that no elevation had ever reached them, because every elevation had been performed with borrowed instruments, and borrowed instruments left their fingerprints.","The Provenance hummed, and his existence expelled everything unworthy of it.","There were no prompts.","No analysis followed, and nothing anywhere was explaining to him what was happening!","It was just him. He was the one figuring it out, understanding it as it occurred, naming it as it moved, and it came to him that this was not an absence of the prompts.","This was what the prompts had been imitating all along.","And as his existence transformed, as the hum deepened and the filth ran, Noah felt an answering hum from far ahead.","He opened his eyes, and they wept gray filth like the rest of him, and he looked across the sands.","THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity.","It hung around the golden obelisk in the distance, wrapped in its sphere of impenetrable light, and it was humming back at him, and with his transforming eyes it looked entirely different than it had looked an hour ago.","He could see something on it now. Something that had been there the whole time, invisible to every eye that had ever looked at it, and Noah stared across the distance at what the collar actually was and understood, in a single cold drop of clarity, that not even the people of THE Ymnaros knew what was truly here!","Not even, perhaps, the being that had failed twice to take it.","And as he watched, the protective barrier around the obelisk began to disappear.","The sphere of obsidian gold light thinned, and paled, and came apart from the top down, dissolving the way the doorway light had dissolved, because the trial was passed and the way was open, and the collar hung in the clearing air with nothing between it and the sands at all.","| You are exceptional.|","The Ancestral Voice boomed across the domain.","And Noah’s eyes flashed, because the voice had not come from everywhere.","It had come from ahead.","Far in the distance, at the base of the golden obelisk, inches from the hanging collar, in a space where only Noah should have been able to stand, a figure had appeared.","Tousled hair. White robes. Hands no longer folded behind his back.","Anaximander.","His mild face was raised toward the collar, and his eyes were glazed with a cold and ancient light that had never once belonged to the scholar, and when the mouth moved, the voice that came out of it was the one that had narrated this entire road.","| You are exceptional. But I...|","|I have lived for too long to stand idly by.|","|I thank you for opening the door. I will do the rest from here.|","BOOM!"]},{"number":5568,"title":"Chapter 5568: Chapter 5567: Ignorance! II","paragraphs":["When the pool that has no color calls, the hand must give its own","For blood of True and Primeval both shall pay the ferry home","The dimension lost to time and space wait not for those who plead","They open only to the one who bleeds the eldest creed","Twice shall the crown be offered up, and twice shall it be worn","But only what is set down whole may pass where ash is borne","The mask that saves a thousand lives must die upon the face","For quintessence cannot truly bloom while shadows hold its place","Beware the kneeling of the proud, for kneeling is not loss","The silhouette unfinished waits where all the futures cross","What eats, and watches, and remains shall gather in one name","And that which you cannot reject, you must become, or be become","---","Noah’s eyes flashed with an incandescent light, his body still shedding gray filth into the sand, and across the distance the hands of Anaximander, moved by another, reached for THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity.","...!","And every piece of it fell into place at once!","I hate what is happening here. The Voice had said that in the middle of the second trial, and dressed it in a crude joke about a beautiful woman being handed to somebody else. It had hated what was happening. It had said so!","Nobody asks what a dying guardian hates about its own rescue.","The dying voice of a Primeval thing that could not let go of something. Its own introduction. Everyone had heard grief in it!","The pathway shall open. Not for you. It had never once said for you!","And Hvitrmarr’s voice, thin and urgent through a bond stretched nearly to breaking, had reached him in the dark between the trials with the one thing she had thought he should know. Anaximander was taken elsewhere. The Voice came for him and took him another direction, and none of us know where.","A being with no external authority!","Noah had walked the last trial with all of it sitting in his mind, unproven and unforgotten. He had cast out everything he owned above a sand that had killed Primevals, with the suspicion filed and waiting, and he had done it anyway, because the door needed opening and he was the one who could open it, and because a man who has just generated his own light from nothing is a very different of a man than the one who entered.","So now he stood in the black sands, bleeding gray, transformed and transforming, and watched a stolen friend’s hand close the last inches toward a Remnant Existential Treasure.","And his eyes showed no surprise at all!","\" Why are you in such a hurry, \" Noah asked, \" when your prize is right before you? Can you tell me why?\"","...!","Across the sands, the hand stopped inches from the gold.","Anaximander’s body did not turn. The cold ancient light in his eyes stayed fixed on the collar, and the voice that came out of him was almost conversational!","|Because I could not possibly give such a thing to another.|","|Do you understand what this is? What it can do? With this in hand, I could save every Superpowered Lifeform in this Dimension without needing anyone. Without waiting on candidates, without lowering standards, without begging strangers to be worthy. Every descendant I have watched die in rows in front of stones, and I could end all of it myself, at last, after ages of watching.|","|And with this body, it is possible. Anaximander, containing my remnants, and all the others who failed before me. He can hold what none of us could hold alone.|","The glazed eyes tilted slightly, as though appraising the flesh they occupied.","| He is almost like you, you know. He just seems a bit different. I have not yet determined where the difference lives.|","Noah listened in silence.","His transformation had not stopped for any of it. The gray filth still ran from him in thinning rivulets, the hum of the singularity still worked down through his atoms, and he stood in the middle of his own remaking and asked his next question as calmly as the first.","\" How did you get into Anaximander, though?\"","|Carefully.|","The word came cold.","|A being like him cannot be taken. I did not cheat, whatever you may be preparing to think of me. His body cannot be harmed by others. His identity makes existence conform around it. Every art of possession ever devised breaks against a nature like his, and I knew it, and so I did the only thing that works on the truly unique and the truly powerful.|","|I asked.|","|Consent was critical. He agreed to carry the pieces of every failure across every age, freely, with his eyes open, because he is kind, and kindness is a door that beings like him never think to lock. What entered him, entered invited. What lies atop his consciousness now, he accepted the weight of. I broke no law of his existence.|","|I merely understood which laws he would suspend for a stranger who asked politely.|","Noah nodded to that, calmly, and sighed.","\"I would let you continue ,\" he said. \" Honestly. I would let you reach out and try to take hold of THE Aurate Collar, and I would stand here and watch you burn for it, because I think you know less about what is hanging on that obelisk than you believe you do, and I can see something on it now that you cannot.\"","His eyes did not leave the figure at the obelisk.","\" But my friend would burn with you. So I have to stop you.\"","The face of Anaximander turned at last, and it had become distasteful, a frown pulling at features that had never worn one, an expression fitted onto the wrong man.","|I have waited too long for this.|","|I have many depending on me. Every Superpowered Lifeform still breathing in this Dimension is my responsibility, and I will finish what I started, and I will not be lectured by a candidate.|","The glazed eyes narrowed.","|You show a spark. That is all. You have not attained the status of those beings, whatever you may feel blooming in you. A spark is a possibility, not a Provenance. And after I grasp the collar, I will take that spark from you as well, since leaving it loose in existence would be untidy.|","...!","Oh?","Noah almost smiled.","This being thought he had passed the trial because he showed a spark. It had stood witness to the whole of it, and it had read all of that as a glimmer. A possibility. A one-in-a-trillion flicker of what might someday be!","He shook his head slowly, because he had not shown a spark.","He had caused the emergence of his own unique individual essence, generated from himself and nothing else across all of existence. His Provenance!","It hummed in him at this very moment, calm and blinding and entirely his, and the being wearing his friend had watched it happen and could not see it, because a thing with no external authority does not announce itself to instruments built for weighing authority, and the Voice was, in the end, exactly what it had confessed to being. A creature made entirely of successful accumulation, reading the whole of existence through the one lens it had.","But he did not need any of that.","That was the part the Voice had truly failed to account for. Noah watched the possessed hand begin to move again, closing the last inches toward the gold, and he knew with complete certainty that Anaximander’s body would not be able to handle what it was about to touch, and so he did not reach for his Provenance at all.","He said two words.","\" Anaximander, Come!\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5569,"title":"Chapter 5569: Chapter 5568: Four Numbers! I","paragraphs":["The hand trembled.","It stopped, fingers spread, a breath from the collar, and it shook there in the air as though caught between two winds, and the face of Anaximander contorted through astonishment into shock and then into rage as the thing inside him hauled at the arm with everything it had absorbed across every age, and the arm did not move!","HUUM!","| Impossible.|","The Voice tore out of the borrowed mouth.","|I accounted for everything. EVERYTHING. The wills of multiple Primevals lie atop his consciousness. Mine, and my friend’s, and every candidate of every age, all of it pressing down on whatever remains of him, he cannot simply...! I....!|","But he could!","Oh, Anaximander could!","Because not too long ago ago, a scholar had said the same thing to the only two friends he had ever made in different times.","Whenever you need me, call. Say, Anaximander, Come!","He had said it as law, a condition and regulation imposed upon his own existence, written into the same nature that let him go where he pleased and made existence conform around him, and no will in existence had standing to countermand a rule that Anaximander had set for Anaximander!","The body at the obelisk buckled.","It went down to its knees in the black sand with both hands grasping its head, and the cold ancient light in the eyes guttered and flared and guttered, and a sound came out of it that was two voices at once and then, by degrees, only one, a raw human cry of pain as the real Anaximander surfaced through everything lying on top of him and came, because he had been called, and coming when called was what he was!","The ancientness drained out of the figure.","The pressure of ages went out of the air around it. What knelt in the sand released no aura at all, carried no weight of epochs, read to every sense as a tousled man in white robes breathing hard with his hands in his hair, and when he finally raised his head, his face was his own!","And it was... profoundly sad as be breathed out. He was...disappointed, in the deep quiet way of a man who had extended trust as a matter of principle to something ancient and beloved by an entire people, something that had watched over every Superpowered Lifeform across every age, and had found, underneath all that long guardianship, this.","He looked at Noah with that sad face, and rose slowly to his feet.","\" Thank you,\" he said. \" And sorry about that.\"","He glanced back once at the collar, and then away.","\"I thought things would be different. I knew the burdens would be heavy. I weighed that before I said yes, and I was prepared for the weight.\" His voice caught slightly.","\"I did not anticipate greed to be such a profound condition. That it could encompass even something like him. A guardian. A being that spent its dying light saving its own people while it did this...\"","Anaximander seemed lost.","Noah remained where he was, and his expression softened.","\" Greed spares no one.. .\" His voice came quiet and certain across the sands.","\" Not the small, not the ancient, not the dying, not the good. It is the one appetite that grows best in the largest existences, because they have lived long enough to want one thing across ages. Greed...is a critical factor of existence...\"","WAA!","\"...!\"","And then Noah’s body released a deep, resonant pulse.","The last of the gray filth stopped at his pores and did not come again. The transformation completed itself in a single settling wave, and what stood in the black sands afterward was a man whose fair skin was clear and unblemished from crown to heel, whose hair had gone pure dark, deeper than it had ever been, and whose stillness was the stillness of a thing with nothing left in it that did not belong.","His eyes opened fully.","The pupils in them were obsidian singularities, small and absolute, and they looked unfathomably old, the way the first idea anything ever had is old!","And they looked new!","Oh, so new!","Noah breathed in.","The air of the final domain came into lungs that had been remade at the level of cells, and it carried nothing to him. No ambient essence. No drifting weavings. Nothing his body reached for, because his body no longer reached outward for anything at all!","He did not absorb!","The hollow where an ocean of power once sat now held a single blue singularity, blinding within and silent without, humming its ancient hum through the whole of him.","He was himself! He had cast out the Primordial Source and Infinity and eighteen Causes and the Intent and a Scale of his own design, and after all of that, he still felt like Noah Osmont. More like Noah Osmont than he had ever felt in his life!","He opened his eyes, looked toward the distant obelisk where Anaximander knelt beneath the hanging gold of THE Aurate Collar, and took a step.","And...","BOOM!","The domain shook!","The obsidian sand beneath his foot did not scatter. It curved. It bent downward in a wide, smooth bowl for miles in every direction, sinking the way ground sinks when it is asked to hold something unfathomably dense, and the dark grains ground against each other with a sound like a mountain settling!","Heavy winds erupted from that single point of contact!","They tore outward across the flats in expanding rings, ripping the stillness of ages off the face of the domain, and far ahead even Anaximander had to raise one hand against the gale to remain steady, his white robes cracking around him like banners!","The golden obelisk light flickered. The distant landmass hanging in the sky groaned. All of it, from one step.","\"...\"","Noah stood in the center of the bowl his own weight had pressed into existence, and he frowned.","It was very hard to describe how he felt right now.","He felt normal. His arm rose when he asked it to rise. His breath came when he called it. There was no surging tide inside him, no roaring reserves, no pressure begging for release. By every internal measure he was a man standing on sand.","And yet every move he made exerted terrifying pressure on everything around him, the way a thing exerts pressure when it is far too dense for the space holding it, and existence itself in these surroundings was straining and creaking simply to contain him.","The cause of all of it was himself.","His Provenance was newly budding. It generated from him constantly, his own essence, his own authority, unique to him alone, and he did not yet know how to properly hold it in. It was new. He was new!"]},{"number":5570,"title":"Chapter 5570: Chapter 5569: Four Numbers! II","paragraphs":["Across the shaking flats, Anaximander looked over at him through the heavy winds. There was no fear in the scholar’s face. There was something quieter and heavier, sitting beside the fresh sadness already there.","\" What is happening to you? \" he asked somberly.","Noah raised his hands and looked at them.","CREAK!","Space distorted around his fingers as he lifted them, thin lines of strain webbing out through the air and sealing themselves shut again, the domain flinching away from ten ordinary fingers!","\"I am expressing myself,\" Noah said. \" Fully. Who I am, all of it, all at once.\"","He turned his hands over slowly, watching the air bend. \"I don’t have control over it yet.\"","He lowered his hands.","\" But the solution should be easy.\"","He breathed out and closed his eyes again.","As much as some part of him wanted to, he could not go back to his old system. The Scales were familiar. The grades, the ranks, the ladders, the tallies, every rung of it was familiar. He had even kept all of it, saved inside THE Infiniverse, because in the end he could not entirely let it go.","But he had begun to be unfathomably true. He had generated something of his own, out of nothing but himself, and a being who had done that could not keep measuring himself with borrowed rulers.","He would have to look at himself differently now.","So at this moment, standing in the bowl of bent sand with the winds still circling him, Noah turned his attention inward and focused on the singularity.","His light.","He did not command it. Commanding was for external things, and this was not external. He communicated with it instead, the way a man communicates with his own heartbeat when he finally sits still long enough to listen, and the singularity answered by simply being understood.","Its hum ran through him, ancient and grand and his.","Every moment of listening taught him something, because every moment of listening was self-knowledge. This was Provenance Essence!","This was what he generated. It was not a store of power to be spent. It was an ongoing statement of what he was, and the pressure wrecking the domain was only that statement spoken too loudly, without shape.","Shape could be learned. He was already learning it. His mind filled with possibilities, one after another, each opening onto ten more.","And then...","Noah smiled.","And at this time, he called out.","\"Oh, Ruination.\"","HUUM!","Light gathered beside him and became a figure!","Her illusory form took shape in strands of crimson and blue, the familiar silhouette he had carried on through wars beyond counting, and she...was crying.","She appeared already wiping at her face with both hands, over and over, quick and precise the way she did everything, as if she wanted the tears to stop and could not make them stop, and they kept coming anyway, bright drops sliding down through her translucent light!","...!","Because Noah had cast out many things.","She had felt every one of them arrive. The Source. The Causes. Infinity. The Heart. The entire contents of his existence, delivered into THE Infiniverse, one treasure after another set down and pushed away, and from the far side of a silent channel it had felt like watching someone give away everything he was as even she...felt disconnected! When he had been so close!","Noah’s heart pained when he saw her like this.","He crossed the sand to her, and the domain shuddered under every step, and he did not care, and he took her into his arms.","\"I’m sorry ,\" he said quietly. \" I had to put many things aside.\"","She shook against him without a sound.","\" But you are never something that came from others.\" His hand rested on the back of her head. \" Most of what you are came from our journey together. And it will always continue. Okay?\"","\"...\"","Ruination looked up at him.","Then she stepped back, wiped her eyes one last time, and waved her hands. Between them, light condensed into a circlet of deep blue, slender and clean, turning slowly in the air.","THE Circlet of the Quintessential Ruin, offered back to him.","Noah smiled and took it, and set it on his head.","Ruination watched him do it, and her hands came together in front of her, and her voice came out small.","\" Always together?\"","\" Always together, \" Noah said.","He let the words sit for a moment. Then he continued.","\" Now. I want you to be the one to display the prompts of my new existence. Though this time, from here on out, I will be generating the knowledge. \" He tapped his own chest once.","\"It comes from me now. You can make it simpler for us to look at and analyze. Okay?\"","Ruination nodded.","Her figure dissolved into a glimmer of crimson blue light that flowed upward and into the circlet, and it settled loosely above his head, riding there the way a crown rides on a king who has stopped needing one and wears it anyway.","The last of the change moved through him then.","The adornments on his body, robes and wrappings that had carried him across Dimensions, were riddled through with the black filth his transformation had expelled, and now they burned away entirely, ash scattering on the wind. In their place, pristine white pants took form, plain and heavy, burning with a sense of ancientness that no forge in existence had put there!","Above the waist he was laid bare, and his muscular upper body stood clean under the obelisk light, every line of it pristine, a physique with nothing borrowed in it anywhere.","Dark hair. Obsidian singularities for pupils. A crown of blue light!","Noah closed his eyes.","And he heard Ruination’s voice once more.","|An unfathomable change has occurred to your existence.|","|What is being identified as Provenance Essence has bloomed within you in the form of a singularity. Your existence has communicated with itself to better allow you to grasp your power, and it has generated a System of Power and Measurement unique to you, applicable to your power alone.|","|When you gaze upon others, their weavings will also appear and be translated into this same System of Measurement.|","|Your existence has been broken down into the following:|","| VERITAS: how true you are to yourself.|","|PROVENANCE: how much of you is your own generation.|","|POTENTIA: what you could still become.|","|PONDUS: the weight you can carry without breaking.|","Noah looked at these prompts with a smile.","This was what his existence wanted to simplify things down to. Four measures. Not grades handed down from trees older than his species, not Scales built in answer to another being’s framework. Four questions a man could ask himself, made into numbers!","He went a step further.","\" Show me my current Status Panel.\"","WAA!","| STATUS PANEL: NOAH OSMONT|","|VERITAS: 10|","|PROVENANCE: 1(???)|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 5|","|THE OSMONTIAN TONGUE: I AM · OSMONT · QUINTESSENTIAL · HUMAN · PROTAGONIST|","|THE NINE FOUNDATIONS: S-RANK EBAD|","|THE Unkneeling Crown · THE Tide That Owes Nothing · THE Mirror That Keeps · THE Hunger That Refines · THE Unmoved Verdict · THE Pure Trajectory · THE All-Drawing Stillness · THE Remembered Truth · THE Sovereign Existence|","|All Foundations stemmed from your own making. They have been naturally elevated through your transformation.|","...!"]},{"number":5571,"title":"Chapter 5571: Chapter 5570: Four Numbers! III","paragraphs":["Noah stood in the settling winds with the Status Panel still hanging in his sight, and he read it again.","| VERITAS: 10|","|PROVENANCE: 1(???)|","|POTENTIA: INFINITE|","|PONDUS: 5|","Four numbers. His whole existence, broken down by his own existence, into four numbers!","He wanted to understand them properly before he moved another step. So he raised his eyes across the dark sand, and he gazed at Anaximander.","HUUM!","The moment his attention truly settled on the scholar, his new sight went to work. The weavings of Anaximander’s existence rose into view, dense and strange and layered with things that should not have been there, and his obsidian singularity pupils drank them in as Ruination translated everything into the one System of Measurement that belonged to Noah alone!","|STATUS PANEL: ANAXIMANDER|","|VERITAS: 3|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: UNDEFINED|","|PONDUS: 1|","\"...\"","Noah went still, and his analysis began.","VERITAS 3!","This was Anaximander. The man whose identity made existence conform! Noah almost wanted to say this number may be low, but he had just advanced himself as he didnt know how high he was compared to more...normal lifeforms.","But Noah remembered what was inside Anaximander now. The Ancestral Voice, suppressed but present. Failed candidates, the remnants of collapsed existences, all of them packed into one body and held down by one will.","The panel was not measuring Anaximander the man. It was measuring everything currently answering to that name, and most of what answered to that name right now was not him. A muddy mixing of many selves, weighed as one. Of course the number came out low when Anaximander was so unique!","Which meant VERITAS as a measure...could fall. It could be diluted by what a being carried. And if it could fall, then it could climb, and Noah did not for one moment assume that his own 10 sat at any ceiling!","The numbers would go higher. He could feel it in the hum! A 10 today was a floor he happened to be standing on, nothing more.","He then thought about Anaximander’s Provenance.","That one required no theory at all!","Anaximander generated nothing of his own. Neither did anyone else Noah had ever met. As for the Undefined potential of Anaximander...this continued to be his own mystery!","Noah turned his sight inward, and laid his own four numbers beside his conclusions.","VERITAS was how true he was to himself, and it could climb without limit.","PROVENANCE was how much of himself he generated, and only he could generate it.","POTENTIA was what he could still become, and his read INFINITE.","PONDUS was what he could bear without breaking, and bearing more was a matter of becoming more!","And every one of them pointed the same direction. Not outward, toward treasures and grades and the frameworks of ancient beings. Inward, toward how he lived.","His eyes opened fully, and he his voice boomed out because he felt like it!","\"If I live gloriously, tyrannically, Quintessentially... I will advance, as I will be living truly as myself. My VERITAS increases... so will my PROVENANCE, and PONDUS, and everything else follows. Based on my actions, I will generate more Provenance. I will be more true, and my immensity will increase as external authority... won’t do anything to me! External treasures won’t do anything to me! Only that which I generate myself, from my own existence!\"","HUUM!","The singularity in his chest hummed grandly at the declaration, and the obsidian sand for miles trembled once and went still!","That which he generated from his own existence.","His mind went automatically to THE Tide That Owes Nothing.","It sat among his Nine Foundations, and the Nine Foundations had survived the casting out because they were fusions nobody had conceived before him, carved from his own thinking. And the Tide’s whole nature was generation through his actions.","If anything else in what remained of him could be considered truly from him, could generate returns that fed VERITAS and PROVENANCE both, it may be the Tide. One more engine to further accelerate his progression, waiting to be tested against his new existence!","But then his eyes flickered.","Because he thought about Mana.","He thought about Infinity!","Both of them gone from him now, resting in THE Infiniverse with everything else he had set down, and their absence raised the question his existence had already answered and not explained. His POTENTIA was INFINITE. But how could he use his potential?","He felt the hum of Provenance inside him, steady and vast, and the answer it gave was not words. It was certainty. He would not be limited when it came to expressing his power. The concepts he had cast out were external things, and external things had external limits, but Provenance generated. Whatever he needed, he would not borrow it back.","He would learn to express and generate his own type of mana!","His, from nothing but himself, shaped by no one’s framework. The thought opened outward into a hundred others, arts and expressions and possibilities stacking up behind his eyes, and he breathed once and set them all aside.","He would be able to understand many things about himself. There would be time for all of it!","But for now, he had to grasp that unique treasure lying in the open for him before anymore accidents occured.","Noah breathed in.","He took another step.","And existence no longer creaked around him.","The sand held flat under his foot. The air stood calm. His weight moved with him instead of ahead of him, and Noah smiled and nodded to himself.","Then, in an instant, he was in front of the obelisk.","The golden pillar rose above him with its wrapping of obsidian gold light peeled away, and THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity hung there in the open, rows of tubular gold beads and a teardrop fringe and a front plate that no eyes in THE Ymnaros had ever read, holding the thing upon it that only his transformed sight could see. The treasure that had eluded many across the ages, with nothing left standing between it and his hand!","Anaximander stood close by, steadier than before, though the cold ancient light was gone from his eyes and the sadness was not.","Noah looked at him first.","\" Are you feeling okay?\"","Anaximander smiled wryly.","\"I have to digest a number of old things, and get myself back to my baseline. I should be okay.\" He tipped his head toward the hanging gold. \" Go ahead, and see what this whole thing has been about. The thing that even ancient lifeforms became so greedy about.\"","Noah nodded.","And he reached out!"]},{"number":5572,"title":"Chapter 5572: Chapter 5571: Remnant!","paragraphs":["There are beings who reach for the treasures of the ages with trembling reverence, and there are beings who reach for them the way a man reaches for his coat. Noah belonged to the second kind!","His fingers closed around THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity as he breathed out.","\"I have felt young all this time.... \" His thumb moved slowly along the gold. \" And today, for the first time, I can almost say I feel old. As if I have passed a significant milestone.\"","He turned the collar slightly in his grip.","\" And just as I get that feeling. Just as I settle into it, start to enjoy it, maybe. I come across something so ridiculously old that I almost feel young again.\"","He gave a small, unhurried smile.","\" That is what this Collar is.\"","...!","Anaximander listened closely, and as the words settled, his expression gradually normalized, as his curiosity won out.","Noah said all of this because of what he had felt at the first instant of contact. His Provenance Essence, that single singularity seated in his existence, had released a heavy, droning hum the moment his hands came against the gold, and through that hum he affirmed something the legends of THE Ymnaros had never once suspected.","The collar was made of bones.","HUUM!","Then the collar asked its question!","An invisible wavelength erupted from it, soundless and total, and Noah’s hand trembled against the gold, almost as if the item were asking him, plainly and without malice, whether he could even hold it!","And his Provenance Essence answered tyrannically.","It pulsed within him, once, and roared through the whole of his being with an answer that required no thought at all.","Fuck I can!","BOOM!","A fiendish, silent aura unfurled across the whole area, pressing outward through the dark sands in a wave that made the domain itself sit very still, and the trembling in his hand stopped!","Beside him, Anaximander, a man who had spent his entire long life loving nothing so much as exploring and understanding and grasping new things, leaned in.","\" What is it, exactly?\"","Noah closed his eyes.","And for the first time, truly, he began utilizing Provenance Essence.","The blue glow within him pulsed, and pulsed again, finding a rhythm, and the rhythm resonated with the collar in his hands. His own essence, generated from nothing but himself, reached into a thing older than every framework in existence and asked it what it was, and information began to feed back into his existence, direct and wordless, his to understand because he was the one generating the understanding.","Even he was astonished at what came back.","He confirmed it twice before he spoke.","\" Existence is unfathomably old, and unfathomably vast,\" Noah said, eyes still closed. \" Older than any Scales. Older than the Dimensions the Scales were built to measure. Older than every Tongue and Law and Source that beings like us spend our short, ambitious lives collecting. And at the very beginning of all that vastness, before any of it had names, there lived THE First Lifeforms. THE Provenance Lifeforms.\"","His voice slowed, giving each piece its full weight.","\" They lived grandly. They lived with unfathomable power, the kind that was never granted and never borrowed, because there was nothing yet to borrow from. And this collar... .\" His hands tightened slightly on the gold.","\" This collar stems from the chest bones of a Provenance Lifeform. It has been deemed a Remnant Existential Treasure. But... It is, and it isn’t. It is simply the cluster of bones of an extremely terrifying lifeform, put together. And that alone is enough to make it a treasure. And also, somehow, not.\"","...!","Noah sighed as he finished, and Anaximander came closer to look at the thing, his eyes moving across the tubular beads and the teardrop fringe as though rereading a book that had just changed languages.","Then the scholar shook his head.","\" All my life, I ask the question of where things come from. Where things began. I want to understand.\" He gestured at the collar, at the obelisk, at the hanging landmass above them, at everything.","\" But it is like existence does not want to be understood. It is frustrating .\" A pause, and the smallest wry lift at the corner of his mouth.","\" Even though I will never stop asking.\"","Noah smiled at these words.","Then he turned his focus back to the terrifying tool in his hands, because he knew, as of this moment, that he had only grasped an initial understanding of it. The bones of a Provenance Lifeform were too unique to be read in one resonance. And there was something heavy within the collar, something he could almost sense at the edge of the feedback, close enough to know it was there and far enough to have no shape. He needed to spend just a bit more time with it, and...","HUUM!","At such a time.","The domain began to shake and tumble.","Above them, the skies tore open as if they were pages, ripped crudely along seams no sky should have, and the color of blood permeated everything, drowning the obelisk light in red!","What came through the torn skies was horrific.","Rivers of corpses gushed out of the wounds in the sky.","Rivers. Of corpses! Superpowered Lifeforms, the exemplifying kind, the kind that carried the weight of Observable Existences in their bare bodies, now tangled dead in their thousands and pouring downward in thick red torrents, limbs and faces surfacing and sinking in the flow, and the sound of it arriving was a wet, rolling thunder that this domain, which had held silence since before the Scales, had never once been asked to hold.","And riding on these rivers of corpses came Infinite Lifeforms.","Dozens of them, gliding down the dead as though the dead were a road, and all of them followed behind one figure at the forefront. A red robed entity whose gaze was extremely old and extremely callous, the gaze of something that had been looking at things like this, and arranging things like this, for longer than most Dimensions had existed.","Noah and Anaximander raised their heads to see all of it.","The river of corpses smashed into the sands!","BOOM!","Red sprayed across obsidian. The dead settled in heaps and drifts. And the old lifeform at the very forefront came to a leisurely stop in the air, and looked, first, at the object in Noah’s hands.","Then at Noah himself.","He blinked, incredulously.","And then he laughed.","\" You cannot possibly be serious.\" The laugh rolled out over the corpses, genuinely entertained. \" Really? How could you have possibly arrived here, and gotten swept up in this?\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5573,"title":"Chapter 5573: Chapter 5572: MY MANA! I","paragraphs":["A horrific aura erupted from the old lifeform, crashing down across the domain, and the drifts of dead flattened under it!","But Noah was not listening to the aura.","He was looking into this being’s eyes. And even though the body was another body, a stranger’s face wearing a stranger’s age, the instant their gazes met, he recognized what looked out from behind it.","It was the visage of THE Sealed One!","Noah’s gaze went cold and imperious. And behind that gaze, many things clicked quietly into place, one after another, regarding the Dimensionlapses, and the Infinite Lifeforms, and the shape of certain long games!","Without further ado, and without so much as a word, Noah casually raised THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity and put it on.","The sands beneath his feet twisted!","Existence cried out around him, a thin, straining sound from every direction at once, the sound of a domain realizing what it now contained, and Noah took a step without offering a conversation!","In an instant, he appeared in front of THE Sealed One!","And in that instant, hanging in the red air with the gold at his throat, he did not look like a man who had knelt as a normal Human beneath a falling sky mere hours ago. Bare-bodied and pristine, white pants burning with ancientness, dark hair unmoving in the corpse-wind, obsidian singularity pupils fixed on his enemy, the collar of a First Lifeform resting on his chest bones above the singularity that was his and no one else’s....","He looked like something out of the first age of existence. A primal, ancient being, arrived very late, and very calm!","He punched out!","HUUM!","Existence shattered like mirrors before his fist, whole panes of it breaking and falling away, and the cracks did not stop at THE Sealed One, they extended outward, racing through the red air toward the Infinite Lifeforms and all the others behind!","BOOM!","Truly, there had been no technique in it.","Noah had instinctively moved and struck out in the most natural manner possible. He had tugged on the power of that single singularity within his existence, that Provenance Essence, and simply punched.","And the result was something even he could not have imagined.","Existence cracked!","It felt like it, and then it proved to be exactly so, as spiderweb cracks echoed outward through the air opposite him, pane after pane of reality splitting along lines that had no business existing, and the cracks did not heal and did not fade. They remained, hanging in the red sky like the aftermath of a stone through glass, frozen mid-shatter!","And the army riding the rivers of corpses had been standing in the way.","Cenozoic Scale Infinite True Lifeforms. Mesozoic Scale Infinite True Lifeforms. Beings who had climbed ladders for entire ages to stand where they stood, and every one of them caught in the spread of those cracks had their bodies split alongside existence itself!","They looked down at themselves, horrified.","Because it was not only their bodies. Their Intents cracked. Their Pantheons cracked!","Their Infinity, the silent compounding core of everything they were, took structural damage and fractured alongside their physical vessels, lines running through flesh and framework alike as though the punch had made no distinction between the two. It had not, of course. To that fist, there was no distinction worth making!","Then the leaking began.","Their Infinity seeped out through the cracks in slow ribbons of light. Their Trueness followed it, thinning into the air. Everything they had gathered across their long, acquisitive lives began escaping through fractures that would not close, and they wailed, and they screamed, and they could do nothing else!","HUUM!","They were dying! They were hit by something so unfathomably true they couldn’t help but die!","Noah took all of this in with shining eyes, and yet he could not take those eyes off one singular figure.","THE Sealed One!","The red robed vessel had cracked with all the rest. Fractures ran through its borrowed body from crown to heel, the same lines that were bleeding an army dry.","And it was stitching itself back together.","The cracks along its frame drew closed, seam by seam, unhurried, the way an old tailor mends a coat he has mended a hundred times before. Not one thread of its Trueness leaked. Not a wisp of its Intent escaped the fractured vessel!","Everything that should have poured out of a body broken that badly simply stayed, held in place by something that had clearly done this before, in more bodies than anyone would ever be permitted to count.","It was an eerie thing to watch. All around him his followers were coming apart at their seams, and the old monster quietly reassembled his own.","When he was whole, THE Sealed One drifted down and sat himself on one of the hanging cracks in existence, settling onto the broken edge of reality as though it were a garden bench. He looked at Noah with an extremely somber gaze, and his eyes moved, briefly, to the collar Noah now wore.","\" Now you are becoming even more of a pain than a vessel, \" he said. \"I want you more. And yet here you are, actually ruining plans now?\"","...!","His voice was calm. Pleasant, even! And underneath the calm, one could feel the heavy anger.","Noah gazed coldly at him and clenched his fists.","He did not care what tricks the old monster had brought today. He was thinking about one thing only: how to wipe out this body of THE Sealed One, here, before it stepped back behind its curtains.","So first, he truly gazed at this being.","HUUM!","| STATUS PANEL: VESSEL OF THE SEALED ONE|","|VERITAS: 10|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: NULL|","|PONDUS: 3|","...!","Noah was alarmed by the results.","The Trueness, the VERITAS of the vessel of THE Sealed One, was exactly the same as his. Ten. So high!","Was this why its Trueness had not leaked even while cleaved?","Everything else in those cracks had bled out because everything else was borrowed, and borrowed things escape. But a being true to itself at that depth held together by definition!","The immensity, PONDUS, was lower than his at 3. And the potential displayed NULL, which was not the UNDEFINED that Anaximander’s panel had shown, and was not zero as it was hard to interpret!","THE Sealed One truly was an old monster.","As Noah looked at this being, he knew one more thing with complete certainty. THE Sealed One loved to scheme and fuck around. Every extra moment gifted to him was a moment he would spend arranging something. So Noah wanted to finish things quickly!","Which meant he had to ask himself a simple question.","How could he express his power most effectively?","He had just wiped out everything from his body. All he had was Provenance Essence. A single unit of it. A single singularity. It felt anchored into him, and he could throw its force out through his limbs, but was that it? Could he only brutely punch out to express his power?","Surely THE Provenance Lifeforms had their own ways of fighting. They generated everything themselves!","So what could he do? He wanted his Mana. He wanted his Causes. But those were old systems that others had made, and they were external, and he had cast them out for exactly that reason. So...how could he make his own?"]},{"number":5574,"title":"Chapter 5574: Chapter 5573: MY MANA! II","paragraphs":["What could he generate that would be filled with his power? That he could use to unleash his power, and have it be his? What could he replace his Mana with?","It had to be infinite. And he had to generate it!","Provenance Essence itself was too unfathomable. He could not endlessly generate more singularities. What else could...","Oh.","Oh...","BOOM!","His body shook as a pulse boomed out of him that caused the surrounding space to quiver!","He had thought of something!","And it made him feel so supremely stupid.","Something he generated. Something carrying his power. A resource he could consider Infinite!","It had been circulating through him this entire time, through every trial and every transformation, so close and so constant that he had looked straight past it while interrogating the whole of existence for an answer.","Toward the seemingly calm Sealed One bubbling with anger, Noah raised his hand.","He looked at his fingertip as the skin split open, and a crimson gold drop of blood flowed out!","HUUM!","The moment it did, a heavy and terrifying hum erupted.","Far ahead, every one of the dying Infinite Lifeforms trembled at that hum, their fractured bodies seizing all at once, as though something ancient had just exposed itself to the air for the first time in an age and their existences recognized it before their minds could!","In the next instant, their bodies exploded into puddles of blood.","An army that had ridden into this domain on rivers of the dead, reduced in one heartbeat to red stains among the red!","And THE Sealed One, seated on his crack in existence, opened his eyes wide with shock as his very existence began to buzz!","Meanwhile, Noah felt like he was in an extremely unique state.","His Blood. His Mana!","Mana was external. An ambient resource, absorbed, refined, spent. A thing one gathered from the generosity of existence and returned to it when the spell was done. But his Blood!","Oh, his blood!","He had even cast out his Marrow. Nothing borrowed remained anywhere in his veins. The blood within him now was the blood of a Provenance Lifeform, produced by remade cells that answered to nothing external, bathed from its first drop in the singular light of a Provenance Essence.","The drop at his fingertip hung there, immense crimson gold, and through its depths shone a stellar blue hue, his light, his singularity, alive inside his blood the way the sun lives inside a sea.","Noah looked at it, and he called out.","\" My Blood... my Mana... Sanguine Mana... My...\"","He let the last words fall silent, because some names were not for the air, and certainly not for the old monster listening from his perch.","’ My Provenance Blood! My First Blood!’","...!","HUUUM!","The moment he named it, the hum deepened, and he felt an overabundance of control flood through him, command so total it bordered on the absurd. One drop, and it answered him like a limb. He told his single drop of Sanguine Mana one thing.","Show him.","Show him its capability!","And the drop of blood popped.","Ahead of him, everything turned crimson gold!","The phenomenon that erupted was akin to countless event horizons blooming at once, an unfathomable twisting force of infinite density unfolding across the space where an army had died, dragging light and air and the hanging cracks of existence into its turning!","Crimson gold light and stellar blue swallowed everything, blindingly, wall to wall across the domain, and through it all rang a single sustained hum so vast and so ancient that even Anaximander, far behind, pressed his hands over his ears!","And by the time the light cleared...","The fractured existence ahead of Noah was covered in his blood.","It coated the frozen cracks. It sheeted across the broken air. It lay over the obsidian sands in a thin crimson gold film that shimmered with stellar blue, and Noah felt absolutely everything within it, every inch, every surface, as though the entire painted expanse were an extension of his own body and he could control everything his blood had touched.","And in the center of it stood the vessel of THE Sealed One.","Ragged and heavily injured. Its red robes torn to strips, its reassembled seams torn open again, and this time its Trueness was actually spilling out, flaking away from the wounds as red ash that drifted and dissolved. It breathed haggardly, each breath dragging, and it looked toward Noah with cold eyes as its existence visibly decayed!","Noah looked out over the crimson gold expanse where an army used to be, and he gave the thing he had just done its name.","\" Sanguine Blood Drop.\"","HUUM!","The hum of his singularity rose to meet the naming, and Ruination’s voice bloomed into his senses, translating what his existence was declaring into clean lines he could look at and analyze.","|Your existence has made a declaration.|","| Blood has been officially designated as your Infinite Generated Resource: SANGUINE MANA.|","|SANGUINE MANA: blood generated by your remade cells, bathed in the light of your Provenance Essence. Production is generation. Generation is you. Reserves: INFINITE.|","|Properties confirmed: Sanguine Mana carries your power in full. Its potency reflects the concentration of your Provenance Essence, VERITAS and PONDUS and will rise as they rise. It answers no external authority. It cannot be adulterated, seized, or turned against you. Where it rests, you feel. Where it spreads, you command.|","|The first Provenance Art has formed.|","|PROVENANCE ART: SANGUINE BLOOD DROP.|","|A single drop of Sanguine Mana, released and detonated at your will. Capabilities: the detonation expresses twisting force of infinite density, akin to blooming event horizons, across a region you define. All things within the region caught in the detonation are subject to your power without distinction between body, framework, or authority. Residual Sanguine Mana coats the region. Coated regions become extensions of your control: you may sense all things within them, deny movement within them, and detonate them again. Drops may be scaled: one drop, many drops, or a continuous flow. Cost: nothing you will miss. You generate more with every heartbeat.|","|Note: this Art was not taught, granted, or inherited. You made it. Designation is permanent.|","Noah read the lines once, and permitted himself a single moment of satisfaction. His first Art!","Named by him, built from him!","Then he floated forward, across his own blood, toward the dying vessel of THE Sealed One.","The vessel stood in the center of the crimson gold film, decaying by the breath, its Trueness flaking off as red ash. It did not retreat. Beings like this never retreated!"]},{"number":5575,"title":"Chapter 5575: Chapter 5574: A Glorious Direction!","paragraphs":["Noah came to a stop before it and looked at it coldly.","\"I never had any issues with you ,\" he said. \" Think about that. All this time. Then you took our Lower Observable Existence, you played your long games from behind your curtains and now you’ve made me an enemy. Can you imagine? Whatever plans you had for eons, however many boards you’ve arranged, however many vessels you have folded and pressed and hung in whatever closet you keep them in. They may all just crumble. Because you happened to target the wrong guy.\"","HUUM!","The vessel’s ragged mouth curved. Even decaying, the voice that came out was calm, unhurried, almost warm, and the heavy anger beneath it had been pressed flatter still.","\" A young thing like you can also be a unique thing, and a special thing, \" THE Sealed One said. \" And there are many such things across existence. I have collected a few. I have discarded more. So let us not make this larger than it is. Tell you what. How about we call it quits? I will not pursue you as a vessel. I will even bear the unbearable pain of handing off that collar I planned so very many years for, the one you are wearing right now, the one you stole. Consider it a gift between professionals. I have too many things going on to designate this much focus to something like you.\"","...!","The offer hung in the red air, reasonable and generous and rotten all the way through.","Noah smiled slightly.","\" Now see, a me from days ago may have taken that deal, \" he said. \" Truly. Walk away, and don’t worry about an old monster. A younger man closes that deal and sleeps well. \" His eyes did not warm at all as he spoke.","\" But now? Ah, I’ve grown up. For me to be true, and Quintessentially me, I wouldn’t take such a deal. You do not get to reach into my life, take what is mine, hunt my people, and then buy your way back to neutral the moment the weaving turns on you. Our choices, our consequences, big boy.\"","He drifted closer, and the crimson gold film below them stirred like a tide sensing its moon.","\" This is the first of your vessels I kill. There will be more. However many you have, wherever you have hidden them, in whatever ages you have seeded them. I will find them, and I will make each one cheaper than the last.\" His voice dropped, cold and even. \" O ancient thing. I want you to feel afraid. I am coming for you.\"","\" Sanguine Blood Drop.\"","BOOM!","Another drop of blood bloomed before Noah, crimson gold around stellar blue, and it exploded like a wave!","The detonation rolled over the vessel of THE Sealed One and eradicated it completely, body and robes and pressed-flat anger and all, scattering it into red ash that thinned and dissolved into nothing!","And this time, nothing stitched.","The wave passed on across the ruined expanse, sweeping the puddles and the stains and every last remnant of the army that had ridden in on rivers of the dead, and when it settled, the domain was clean of all of them. Nothing survived.","Slowly, the spiderweb cracks hanging in existence began to heal, panes of fractured reality drawing themselves closed seam by seam, the way a wound closes when what caused it has finally been removed. The torn pages of the sky sealed. The red light drained away.","The final domain returned, by degrees, to its ancient stillness, minus one army, one vessel, and a considerable quantity of borrowed power that had leaked out of its owners and gone wherever such things go.","Noah stood in the center of the quiet, and felt his Provenance Essence buzzing.","HUUM!","|Your Provenance Essence has increased slightly in concentration.|","|Your PONDUS has increased by +2. PONDUS: 7.|","|You were Quintessentially true to your existence. Your VERITAS elevated tremendously, but has not been able to climb past the value of 10.|","...!","Oh?","Noah’s existence pulsed as he thought about that information.","He did not need to devour anything externally. He had just confirmed this. No corpses harvested, no essence absorbed, no boons collected from the ash. He had simply acted, truly and faithfully as who he was, and his power had increased. So long as he conducted himself as himself, the numbers would climb. That was the entire system. That had always been the entire system, and existence had needed to crush him under a falling sky before he saw it.","He just had not thought elevating the values of his four attributes would be so arduous. A slaughtered army, an eradicated vessel, an Art created from nothing, and the yield was a plus two, and a VERITAS that strained against its own value of 10 and could not pass it. Small numbers, grudgingly given!","But having numbers that were small yet meaningful was something he also liked.","After all, he had played with numbers that reached Trillions and Decillions before. The new system his existence was slowly enacting seemed much more meaningful!","Noah turned.","Anaximander had seated himself near the base of the obelisk at some point during the eradication of an army, arms resting on his knees, and he was shaking his head at his friend!","Noah took a step and appeared beside him.","\" You are one ridiculous existence, you know that, right?\" Anaximander said.","\"I am just a human trying to grasp the wonders of existence. Just like you. \" Noah settled his gaze on him. \" But how is the situation elsewhere? I ask because you took the Ancestral Voice within you.\"","Anaximander nodded slowly, and his eyes unfocused, looking at something that was not in front of him.","\"It is a unique sensation. I am still grasping it. It is as if I have an eye overseeing vast stretches of THE Ymnaros, and the eye never closes, and it was never mine, and yet it reports to me now.\" He exhaled.","\" What it reports is not good. Armies of Infinite Lifeforms are still rushing into the different domains of the Superpowered Lifeforms and waging war. The Superpowered Lifeforms are strong, but they defend homes while the invaders spend bodies. And in the largest domain of THE Ymnaros, in THE Golden Expanse, the largest army of them all has gathered. Killing the vessel of THE Sealed One does not seem to have deterred them.\" A pause.","\" Or they simply do not know yet.\"","His eyes refocused, and found Noah.","\" Hvitrmarr and Damodred and Ryaenara still move. Though the White Steed seems distraught .\" He tilted his head. \" Your transformation here affected a few things?\"","Noah thought about this for a moment. The bond, the mixture of Causes, the cry through it as eighteen seats emptied without a word of warning. A feeling her other half vanish out of her own existence.","\"A few things that I will correct ,\" he said. \" But when it comes to dealing with the armies of Infinite Lifeforms...\"","He let the sentence rest there, and pondered.","His new power. His new self! The possibilities of what he could do were, in the most literal reading his Status Panel offered, limitless. His potential was limitless. All that was left was his imagination.","He had already reclaimed Mana as his own, something he generated, and it was now his blood. In time, he would think about how Causes could also be his own, something he generated rather than seated. That was a project for a quieter hour.","But first, he had to design something grand of his own to address the immediate problem. One body, however true, could not stand in every burning domain at once.","His hand rose and touched the Collar on his chest.","It was silently resonating, humming along with his Provenance Essence in a low harmony, and through the contact he could feel the slow work underway: the unique thing was being refined by him, layer by patient layer, his essence working into bones older than every framework in existence. When his Provenance Essence actually got through to it, he would grasp its secrets. For now, it was a grand necklace on his chest, and he was entirely at peace with owning the single most coveted piece of jewelry in THE Ymnaros.","He allowed his existence to continue refining it, and turned his mind to generation.","Ideas were already buzzing. Many of them!","He selected one, opened his palm, and let the skin split.","A drop of incandescent blood rose out of his palm, crimson gold around stellar blue, and he gathered it onto the tip of his finger.","Then he began to write.","His fingertip moved through the air, and the blood followed it, laying down lines that stayed where he drew them. A runic symbol took shape stroke by stroke, and it was like no script in any catalog of existence, because it came from no catalog!","Curved lines nested inside curved lines. Rows of dots marched along the arcs in deliberate rhythms. Spirals turned inward at the joints, and every stroke was placed the way old rituals place things. He was not remembering it. He was generating it, and his hand simply knew, because the knowledge was being made in the same instant as the ink.","HUUM!","The finished rune hung in the air, humming, drinking the light.","Then it transformed.","The lines swelled and flowed outward, blood multiplying upon blood, and the rune unfolded into a figure that rose and rose until it stood titanic against the obelisk light!","It looked like Noah.","And it did not.","The face was his face, calm and cold. But the body stood far taller, broad and ancient, skin the deep crimson gold of his Sanguine Mana with ritual markings scored across it in stellar blue: spiral upon spiral down the arms, dot-lines crossing the chest in measured rows, patterns that read as ceremony older than language. Charms of pale bone hung in layered strands from its neck and wrists, and curved horn framed its shoulders beneath a great mantle that fell like a chieftain’s burden.","In its right hand it held a bloody staff, taller than itself, wet and dark with blood and crowned with a knot of the same nested spirals!","Above its head floated a crown made entirely of blood, turning slowly, never dripping. And around its whole titanic frame, streams of blood swirled in endless infinity symbols, crossing and recrossing, the oldest shape Noah owned, drawn now in the resource he would never exhaust.","|The second Provenance Art has formed.|","| PROVENANCE ART: SANGUINE SHAMANIC RUNE.|","|A rune written in Sanguine Mana that unfolds into a PROVENANCE SANGUINE CLONE. Each Clone portrays half of your power in full expression: your force, your Sanguine Mana arts, your control. Clones draw their blood from you. Your reserves are INFINITE; the cost is a formality.|","|Termination clause: if a Clone is ever destroyed, its blood does not die. It stains. The stain corrupts a region up to the measure of an Observable Existence, and within the stained region, all enemies you have designated will leak their Trueness out through their own blood. Allies are untouched. The stain does not expire.|","|Note: destroying your Clone is the least advisable way to defeat it.|","...!","Anaximander rose to his feet and looked up at the bloody crimson gold version of his friend in its ancient adornments, and for a while he said nothing at all!","Noah spoke first.","\"I will make more of these. For now, can you do what the Ancestral Voice did, and transport this one, and the others I will make, to different locations across THE Ymnaros?\" His voice was even, almost administrative, as though he were arranging deliveries!","\"I will finish this quickly, and see about extending my human rule here fully...\"","...!","Anaximander’s eyes pulsed as he turned to look at his friend.","He saw that it was still Noah.","And yet, looking at him now, Anaximander truly felt it. Something ancient, and far. As though his friend stood beside him and also somewhere very early, in an age before ages, and the distance between those two places was growing quietly wider every hour.","Anaximander shook his head with a wry smile, and closed his eyes.","\" Understood .\"","An instant later, the ancient looking clone of Noah disappeared, sent somewhere across THE Ymnaros between one breath and the next.","And Noah himself stood by the obelisk with blood flowing freely from him, palms and fingertips running crimson gold, as he began to draw more bloody runes!"]},{"number":5576,"title":"Chapter 5576: Chapter 5575: We Follow!","paragraphs":["<Ianthe Kallias>","Ianthe Kallias had carried the weight of an Observable Existence in her body since she was young, and until this war, she had believed that meant something.","The sky of THE Golden Expanse had been gold all her life. Now it ran blue and wrong, rivers of Infinity pouring through it in torrents, and beneath those torrents the invaders’ Pantheons stood unleashed across the plains, palaces and coils and hungry geometries pressing their laws down onto ground that had never obeyed anyone!","Their Intents came ahead of them like weather. Hundreds of her people held the line with their bare bodies and their exemplified weight, and the line was moving the wrong way.","She drove her fist through an Infinite Lifeform’s descending claw and felt the claw’s law try to write itself onto her bones before her weight crushed it out!","CRACK!","Beside her, old Peleus staggered, three Intents grinding against his shoulders at once. Past him, the twins fought back to back in a shrinking circle. Everywhere she looked, her people were giving ground, one stubborn step at a time, and Ianthe felt the fear she had been swallowing all day rise up her throat. Not fear for herself. Fear for all of them!","The invaders spent bodies the way rivers spend water, and her people had only the bodies they were born in.","Then... the hum arrived. A heavy and unfathomable hum!","It was simply there, underneath everything, a single sustained note so old that her body recognized it before her ears did, and her body’s opinion was terror!","Across the battlefront, thousands of beings looked up at once.","High above the breaking line, where nothing had been a heartbeat ago, something now floated.","It was titanic. It was shaped like a man, and it was the color of deep crimson gold, marked across its skin with spirals and dot-lines of burning stellar blue, hung with strands of pale bone, mantled and horned, and above its head a crown made of slowly turning blood floated without dripping!","Around its whole frame, streams of blood swirled in endless crossing loops, the same shape over and over, a symbol she would never afterward forget.","She could not have said what it was. Nobody on that field could. Understanding was not offered!","Its aura pressed down, and Ianthe’s knees nearly went. This thing had come to their side of the war, she could feel that much in the way its weight fell only forward, onto the invaders, and still her hands shook.","It was the dread of standing near something out of the first age of existence, ancient beyond the weavings of ages, and the dread did not ease when she told herself it was rescue!","The Infinite Lifeforms received it truly.","Their formations had already stopped. Rivers of Infinity faltered mid-pour. Beings who had spent the day as executioners now hung motionless in the silver air, and Ianthe watched creatures wearing Cenozoic weight begin, visibly, to shake.","The floating figure raised its staff.","At the staff’s crowned tip, a single drop of blood formed. Crimson gold, with a stellar blue light living in its depths. One drop, above a battlefront that stretched past the horizon’s patience!","The drop popped.","HUUM!","The battlefront ahead of her ceased to be a place.","Everything the invaders held turned crimson gold at once, event horizons blooming across the plains in their uncounted numbers, twisting light and law and Pantheon-palaces into themselves with a force that made Ianthe’s exemplified body feel like a leaf pressed in a book!","The hum became a roar and became a pressure that bent the world’s edges inward, and through it she saw the Infinite Lifeforms crack like vessels, their hoarded Infinity leaking out in ribbons, their bodies coming apart into red!","BOOM!","When the light thinned, the plains were painted. A film of crimson gold lay across the ruined ground where the invading army’s forward strength had stood, shimmering with blue, and nothing that had ridden in on those rivers moved anywhere upon it. The rivers themselves were gone. The unleashed Pantheons were gone!","The pressure of a hundred foreign Intents was gone, and its absence rang louder than any of it.","The war in THE Golden Expanse was not over. Ianthe could feel the rest of the invasion out beyond the horizon, vast and undeterred, still arriving.","But the field before her was finished.","And the being that had finished it did not chase, and did not speak, and did not land. It simply floated there above its own blood, grand and unhurried, arms loose at its sides, the crown turning over its head and the endless loops of blood crossing and recrossing around it, letting itself be seen at full length by every survivor of both sides, as though being witnessed were itself part of the work.","Then, slowly, it turned toward the horizon, where the rest of the war was waiting!","Ianthe rose from her knees, and she watched.","There was nothing else to be done with what was happening in the sky. The titanic crimson gold being drifted out from the cleared battlefront, unhurried, the crown of blood turning above its head, and where it went, the war simply ended.","She saw it stop above the burning reaches east of the plains, where the blue rivers had been pouring. It raised its staff!","One drop of blood formed at the tip, crimson gold around a heart of stellar blue, and Ianthe braced herself this time, and the bracing did nothing at all.","BOOM!","The east turned crimson gold from earth to sky, event horizons blooming through the invaders’ ranks, and every single Infinite Lifeform within that region cracked, leaked, and collapsed into red. Not most of them. Every one!","Then the being drifted on, south, to the shattered terraces where the twins’ home had stood, and did it again. One drop!","Just one drop of blood!","Then the high passes. One drop. Then the coast of the golden sea, where the largest mass of the invasion had gathered its Pantheons into a fortress of stacked laws, and Ianthe thought, surely, here it will need more!","And yet still...","One drop was all it required.","BOOM!","She did not know what this lifeform was. No one on the field knew what it was!","But her people were already speaking of it in low voices between the drops, and a name was forming out of nothing, because beings must call a thing something or go mad looking at it. The crown gave them the word. By the fourth region, Ianthe heard old Peleus murmur it, and realized she had been thinking it for some time.","The Blood-Crowned One.","It was not a grand name. It was simply true!","Region by region, drop by drop, the Blood-Crowned One unmade the invasion of THE Golden Expanse. There was no battle in any of it. A single ridiculous thing happened: every Infinite Lifeform, cleared out and completely collapsed, until the rivers ran nowhere in any sky she could see, and the last foreign Intent guttered out of the air like a lamp pinched between fingers!","And then THE Golden Expanse was entirely cleared.","\"...\"","A heavy silence fell upon it.","It was the first true silence in longer than Ianthe could count. No rivers pouring. No Pantheons grinding their laws against the ground. No screaming, hers or theirs.","Just the wind moving over ruined gold plains slicked in crimson, and hundreds upon hundreds of Superpowered Lifeforms standing in the wreckage of everything, slowly raising their heads.","Every single one of them looked up.","The Blood-Crowned One floated at the center of the sky, staff loose in its grip, the loops of blood turning endlessly around its frame.","Then it spoke.","\"I will lead you.\"","BOOM!","The voice was ancient and booming and everywhere at once, arriving in the chest before the ears, and Ianthe flinched, and could not look away.","It did not even seem like a request!","There was no question mark living anywhere inside those words. The being was not offering. It was telling them what it would do, the way the sky tells the ground it will rain!","\" For ages, you have been defending against an onslaught of enemies,\" the voice rolled on, slow and vast. \" Age after age, they have come for your homes, and age after age, you have held your lines with your bare bodies, and buried your dead, again, and again, and again. No more.\"","The staff turned, once, unhurried.","\"I, THE True Human Emperor, will lead you.\"","A pause came, in which the whole of THE Golden Expanse seemed to hang from a thread.","\"Will you follow?\"","HUUM!","The hum swelled beneath the words, ancient and enormous, and the oppressive silence that followed was the heaviest thing Ianthe had ever stood under, heavier than the Observable Existence she carried in her body, because this weight asked something of her!","Her emotions would not settle into any single shape.","His words about her people resonated in her bones. Dying age after age. Burying the dead again and again!","That was her mother, and her mother’s line, and old Peleus’s four sons, and every golden field she had ever seen churned to mud and red!","He was right!","And at the same time, she was afraid of him. Deeply. He had asked nothing of them before saving them. He had wiped out the very enemies that were butchering them, armies of Infinite Lifeforms, whole invasions, with single drops of blood, and power like that did not need their consent for anything, and yet here it floated, waiting for their answer.","But beneath the fear, and beneath the awe, there was something else. And it was actually fairly simple.","She was tired. She was so tired of the cycles of death.","And this fearsome being that none of them could understand had protected them. If he could continue to do so...","Ianthe Kallias stepped forward over the ruined ground, the first body to move up in all of THE Golden Expanse. She put her hand on her chest, over the weight she had carried since she was young, and she raised her voice to the sky.","\" We follow!\"","HUUM!","She was a single lone voice in a silence the size of a domain!","But she was the first. And how she thought was how many just like her thought!","Old Peleus rose from beside his dead, put his hand on his chest, and said it. The twins rose together, hands on their chests. Then the line she had fought beside all day, then the survivors of the terraces, then voices from the passes and the coast, Superpowered Lifeforms rising one after another out of the wreckage across the whole golden breadth of the domain, hands over hearts.","\"We follow!\"","\"We follow!\"","It became a phenomenon!","All those within THE Golden Expanse looked up as they said it. Some of them said it holding the corpses of their families in their arms. Some said it kneeling, too injured to stand, pain written across their faces as they looked around at the devastation of everything they had built, and then looked up, past all of it, toward the fearsome being promising to lead them.","Their voices rose and joined and rose again, hundreds becoming a single sound rolling across the cleared plains, grief and exhaustion and hope all speaking the same two words!","\" WE FOLLOW!\"","The Blood-Crowned One looked down upon all of it, the crown turning slowly above its head.","And it gave them its last words.","\"I will lead you towards an age of humanity, and empowerment. Towards an age where those who butchered you... will fear even standing before your shadows.\"","...!","The words burned through Ianthe and many others!","Her blood boiled. There was no gentler way to name it. Because what better emotion was there to rouse up, if not revenge? They had been prey for so long that she had forgotten there was another way to stand!","Those who butchered them, afraid of their shadows!","...!","Ianthe threw her head back and roared, and around her, THE Golden Expanse roared with her, hundreds of voices tearing loose at once with a fervor that shook the crimson from the ruined ground, louder than the war had ever been!","\" WE FOLLOW!\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5577,"title":"Chapter 5577: Chapter 5576: Stability!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Noah stood by the obelisk with his eyes closed, and he was also standing in a dozen other places.","His senses ran through every Provenance Sanguine Clone at once, shared fully, a single awareness wearing many titanic bodies across the breadth of THE Ymnaros, and what that awareness observed was the same short story with different scenery!","No Infinite True Lifeform stood against even a single Sanguine Blood Drop.","Not the Cenozoic ones anchoring invasion spearheads. Not the patient ones hanging back behind their stacked Pantheons. Not the desperate ones who saw the crimson gold figure arrive and threw everything they had hoarded across their long lives at it before the staff could rise!","One drop formed. One drop popped. And rivers of Infinity went silent in one region after another, armies collapsing into red, until whole stretches of THE Ymnaros held no invaders at all!","And in THE Golden Expanse, the grandest of them, his clone had done something else besides.","Through its eyes he had looked out over the cleared plains at thousands of Superpowered Lifeforms rising from their ruins. And past them, sheltered in the heart of the domain, he had seen the grand sprawling citadel that the Superpowered Lifeforms had been defending all this time, tier upon golden tier of it, and the millions of humans within its walls pressed onto every balcony and rampart to see the sky!","His clone had told all of them that he would lead them!","And as they looked up, one after another after another, and pledged themselves to him...","HUUM!","|You have increased the stability of a small localized portion of Existence. Your Provenance Essence has increased significantly in concentration.|","|Your PONDUS has increased by +.5. PONDUS: 7.5|","|You were Quintessentially true to your existence and have increased the stability of a small localized portion of Existence. Your VERITAS elevated tremendously, but has not been able to climb past the value of 10.|","...!","He had received similar prompts not long before, and he visibly felt his power increase as these ones settled, the hum in his depths thickening by a degree that his whole body registered.","But the most important thing was not the numbers. The most important thing was what his existence had communicated to him about the cause.","He had increased the stability of a localized portion of Existence!","And he could feel his existence was fortifying, and deep within him his singularity of Provenance Essence was growing larger and larger in concentration, denser and brighter.","And the growth was his to generate, but due to his actions bringing about the stability of existence itself!","Such a thing interested him greatly.","How were THE First Lifeforms connected to the stability of existence itself?","Everywhere he had ever traveled, existence ran on boundless chaos. Entropy only increased over time. Lifeforms always fought, wars churned realms into dust, and every framework ever built was a temporary argument against a disorder that always, eventually, won the argument.","And yet it seemed the earliest lifeforms, or truly the first lifeforms, became stronger by cutting against that disorder. Their power grew from their own existence generating more of themselves!","He sighed and opened his eyes, and turned to Anaximander beside him.","The scholar nodded to him.","\" Everything around THE Ymnaros is stable. We can have a moment to breathe, somewhat.\"","Noah nodded back, and looked down at the collar on his chest.","He wanted to use his own moment of breathing to take a proper look at this ridiculous cluster of bones of a First Lifeform.","How did it come about? Why would an existence so supremely powerful carve out its own bones and make them into a necklace? Beings hoarded power. Beings defended their bodies above all things. And this one had reached into its own chest and shaped what it found there into an ornament, and left the ornament behind for the ages to kill each other over.","And the more he thought about it, the more special the Superpowered Lifeforms became. Their power, their exemplification, the whole strange lineage of authority-less might that filled this Dimension, traced its origins back to the Panaceas. And the Panaceas actually stemmed from this very necklace, its runoff, its residue, pooling in wells across THE Ymnaros for others to drink.","THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity!","The First Purity now made sense in its name. He simply had to figure out the rest!","And while he did that, there was also his own newly changed existence to attend to. He needed to generate his own system of power, piece by piece, because he had cast out far too many things.","There were weavings he would have to alter as well. The Causes of the First Steed. Potentially the Laestrygonian too, Damodred, bound to him by structures that no longer had anything to bind to.","He would continue to experiment, and see exactly what path he would forge. A path that would be genuinely his, and nobody else’s, from here on out!","One of the bigger puzzles for him to solve remained the Causes.","THE Infiniverse was filled with them, thousands of realms turning on them.","Even one of Those Who Remain, THE Sleepless Fiend, was playing around with Causes in an entire Dimension. Well, really, in multiple Dimensions, if the Laestrygonians were included in the counting. Causes sat beneath everything he had ever climbed, and everything he intended to rule.","He had to generate something of his own that took the place of Causes.","And as he thought of this...","WAA!","Space folded open on the dark sands of what used to be the domain of the final trial, and three figures stepped through, delivered by the scholar’s quiet courtesy at Noah’s earlier request.","Hvitrmarr. Damodred. Ryaenara!","The White Steed came in her humanoid form, white-haired and gold-eyed, the ring pupils fixed on Noah the moment the fold released her. Damodred stood at her flank, and Ryaenara a step apart, and all three of them looked toward Noah with complex gazes, each carrying their own thoughts across the sand.","Hvitrmarr, who had felt her newly established bond dissipate out of her existence.","Damodred, who was bound to Noah, and who now sensed no Causes on him at all!","And Ryaenara.","Noah looked at this woman, vibrant and grand, and a silent thought arose within him.","He may actually be able to cure her little brother."]},{"number":5578,"title":"Chapter 5578: Chapter 5577: NOBLESSE! I","paragraphs":["With a bit of breathing room, many things could be done without rushing!","Noah crossed the sand to Hvitrmarr first, and caught her shoulder before her knee could touch the ground.","\" None of that,\" he said quietly. \" The bond you felt leave was one more borrowed thing I had to set down. It was never you I set down. I told you I would be your Rider, and I will continue to be your Rider. Soon, something better than what we had will bloom, okay?\"","The White Steed’s gold eyes searched his face. She straightened, and the distress she had carried finally loosened its grip on her frame, and she stayed close to him!","He then looked at Damodred.","\" With the power I have now, I should have something grander than Causes soon enough, \" Noah said. \"I will see if I can easily find the genetic markers of Laestrygonians, and bring more of your brethren back.\"","...!","The Laestrygonian went very still! His people, eradicated by THE Sleepless Fiend, existing now as one survivor bound to one man!","Damodred bowed his head deeply.","\"I follow The Master completely,\" he said, \" and await your continued glory.\"","Noah then turned to Ryaenara.","He chose his words carefully.","\"I don’t want to make any promises. But... we can try to see if curing your Brother is a possibility right now.\"","BOOM!","The words landed on her like a detonation! Her body trembled, her composure cracking as her eyes shone with unfathomable hope as she surged a step forward!","\" Can we... can we go right now? He is in my Dimension, as we ca... GAH!\"","Even before she finished her words, she spat crimson blood.","It was not ordinary blood! It came out shining with her Trueness, threads of her very existence leaving with it, and then, shockingly, her chest split open, and out of the wound erupted faces!","Hateful, roaring faces, pressing up out of her flesh in a snarling cluster, screaming without sound!","OOOOH!","...!","Noah frowned and was instantly at her side, his hands grasping her shoulders, his senses driving down into her existence, and he quickly understood what was happening.","HUUM!","|Analysis of the existence: RYAENARA.|","|A bond of following was established between this existence and THE Sealed One in ages past. However much of a double agent this existence believed herself to be, serving and not serving, the initial bond she formed was filled with weavings even she could not understand, layered beneath her perception at the moment of its making.|","|Through those hidden weavings, THE Sealed One has grasped the Lifeline of her existence and cursed it with deterioration. Her Trueness and her Intent are already infected. Her Lifeline is bound over to collapse.|","| Designation of the curse: THE Hollowing Chorus of the Forfeited Lifeline.|","|She is marked for death.|","...!","Noah looked at the prompts with heavy eyes.","The old monster still could not be underestimated. Killed in one body an hour ago, and reaching out as he must have perceived something regarding Ryaenara! After all, she was in THE Ymnaros where THE Sealed One just faced a catastrophic loss of THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity!","But for someone to be marked for death?","Noah’s voice tyrannically boomed out!","\"I won’t allow it.\"","BOOM!","He moved with immensity. Ryaenara was still convulsing in his grip, vomiting blood and Trueness in gouts now, and she was crying, and even dying she spent her words on someone else.","\" Ulf, please save Ulf! Enter my Dimension before it collap... GAAH!\"","She spat out more blood, and her teeth fell out with it, scattering white against the dark sand, and her body began sagging toward the ground as the roaring faces on her chest howled their silent howl!","Noah focused.","Time seemingly slowed before his perception, thinning and thinning until it was no longer even moving, the domain caught in a single stretched instant with her blood hanging mid-air between them.","A blood drop appeared on his fingertip.","He thought for a moment, whole architectures of reasoning assembling and collapsing and reassembling. The curse held her Lifeline, and her Lifeline sat threaded through the frameworks of existence, and anything threaded through frameworks could be gripped by things older and crueler than her.","He would continue to lean on his Infinite Sanguine Mana as the solution!","And right now, he was making another Art.","His fingertip began to carve, and this rune was unlike the shamanic rune, deeper and slower, waves and strings coming together within his blood as he drew, strand weaving into strand. The Letters of THE Osmontian Tongue flowed into its construction, I AM and OSMONT and HUMAN pressed into the turning lines, and beneath the Letters something even more ancient moved through the strokes, a texture that belonged to the age his blood now remembered, and the finished rune hung in the stopped air like a seal from before the first framework was ever raised!","Time resumed.","The rune flowed into Ryaenara.","HUUM!","|The third Provenance Art has formed.|","| PROVENANCE ART: THE PROVENANCE BLOOD MARK.|","|A mark carved of Sanguine Mana, THE Osmontian Tongue, and that which came before frameworks. It is placed upon a select few chosen existence, and it is irreversible.|","|The marked existence has its Lifeline and its entire Existence fully bound to you. Their fate is lost from all Scales and all frameworks: no instrument of existence may weigh them, no authority of existence may grip them, and no thread of theirs remains for any hand but yours. They follow you, fully, from the moment of marking onward.|","|In exchange, their Potential is elevated grandly. The marked become NOBLESSE BLOOD APOSTLES.|","|NOBLESSE BLOOD APOSTLES manifest in five tiers of rarity, determined by the potential of the one marked. From the least to the rarest: BLOOD KNIGHT, BLOOD BARON, BLOOD DUKE, BLOOD MONARCH, BLOOD SOVEREIGN. The rarer the Apostle, the grander the attributes their existence may carry.|","...!","The effects on Ryaenara were immediate!","She started trembling even harder, gushes of dark blood erupting from her, old blood, wrong blood, everything the curse had touched being driven out of her at once, and the hateful faces on her chest reared and cried out as the mark’s authority closed over them!","And yet, her Trueness stopped leaking.","The shining threads that had been escaping with every cough drew back into her, held fast, and then she transformed.","The dark blood burned away off her skin. Her hair poured down glossy obsidian, blacker and deeper than it had ever been, catching the obelisk light like still water at night. Her eyes opened, and the pupils within them burned bloody red, and behind the red turned a quiet light of infinity, depth without end!","Red gold robes wrapped around her out of nothing, layered and regal, settling onto her shoulders with the weight of a station rather than a garment.","The roaring faces gave one last soundless howl, and dissolved.","|The curse THE Hollowing Chorus of the Forfeited Lifeline has been destroyed.|","|Cause of destruction: the curse was anchored through the frameworks of existence, gripping a Lifeline threaded within them. The marked existence of RYAENARA no longer resides within any Scale or framework. There is nothing remaining for the curse to hold. Her Lifeline answers to one authority alone, and that authority cannot be weighed or touched by the instruments of THE Sealed One.|","|As of this moment, her existence is without any Scales or framework.|","| RYAENARA has become a Noblesse Blood Apostle of the fourth tier: BLOOD BARON.|","WAA!","Ryaenara stood whole in her red gold robes, and her crimson eyes burned with nobility and wonder as she looked at Noah.","Then she instantly knelt before him.","It was nothing like the kneel of a defeated thing. Her back was straight, her head lifted, her reverent eyes raised to him as if she were looking at a distant and grand lifeform across an impossible span, and her voice came out grandly, formal in a way Ryaenara had never once been formal in all the time he had known her!","\" Thank you for the generosity, Master. Command me, and I will move existence for you!\"","HUUM!","Noah looked at her oddly.","He had not expected such a heavy change!","Did his blood have such a heavy effect when he did this?","\" Are you... still you?\"","\"I am Ryaenara, your Apostle, from this point on in existence.\"","\"What... do you want?\"","\"If Master can grant my Brother the same favor as me, I would be grateful.\" Her crimson eyes did not waver.","\" He would also be of much more use to you, with his gaze being capable of reaching into the future.\"","...!","She was still her. The first thing she wanted was still Ulf, before power, before anything. But different!","Noah affirmed this as he looked at her deeply, his gaze reaching into her remade existence.","|STATUS PANEL: RYAENARA- NOBLESSE BLOOD APOSTLE, BLOOD BARON|","|VERITAS: 1|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 5|","|PONDUS: 2|","He took the panel in, and nodded.","He had changed her into a grand lifeform, unmoored from every Scale and framework in existence, her potential elevated to a value that stood beside numbers he had bled for!","And it seemed she would only be the first.","Because nearby, Hvitrmarr and Damodred had both kneeled down onto the dark sand, heads bowed, as if they were waiting for the same thing!"]},{"number":5579,"title":"Chapter 5579: Chapter 5578: NOBLESSE! II","paragraphs":["\"What the hell did you just do? And how?\"","Anaximander had come up behind Noah, and he was staring at Ryaenara with open marvel!","He could sense the complete change of her existence, and it was not a change of degree. Her weavings did not read as elevated, or healed, or empowered. They read as absent!","A being stood before him, undeniably present, radiating quiet crimson nobility, and every instrument of perception he owned reported that she did not display much immenisty at all.","Noah was already walking toward Hvitrmarr, a fresh drop of blood rising to his fingertip.","\" My existence has begun living truly as myself,\" he said, beginning to draw. The rune took form stroke by patient stroke, waves and strings gathering in the blood.","\" Everything I do now comes from that. I am using my blood as a resource to alter existence itself, because my blood carries everything I am, and I am no longer something existence gets a say in. This time in particular, it is the alteration of one’s Lifeline.\"","WAA!","The rune turned slowly in the air before the kneeling White Steed, and he began a second one beside it, for the Laestrygonian, speaking as he carved.","\" I’ve begun thinking of a Lifeline as a thread. Spun for you at your beginning and woven into frameworks you never chose, by hands you will never see. Every Scale that measures you holds that thread. Every authority that curses you grips it. Every framework that promises you power is also a loom that owns your weave. Beings spend their whole existences climbing ladders with this preset notion...\" His fingertip finished a spiral of joined strands.","\"My Mark cuts the thread free of every framework. Your Lifeline leaves the frameworks entirely, and binds to me instead. Simple enough.\"","...!","Simple enough! Oh, so simple!","He looked between the two kneeling figures.","\" This does change you bindings to fully be...behind me.\"","Neither of them moved from their knees.","Noah nodded once, and released the runes.","HUUM!","The two marks flowed into them, and the transformations began.","Hvitrmarr rose off the sand as her humanoid form dissolved outward into her true one, the colossal white dragon unfurling against the obelisk light, and then the Mark’s authority moved through her from Lifeline to scale-tips!","Her pearl white body deepened and glossed, alabaster taking on an undertone of living crimson, as though her whiteness now ran above a tide of blood. Her wing membranes thinned and cleared into sheets of red gold, light passing through them the way it passes through stained glass in an old hall. Her twin spiral ivory horns banded themselves in rings of red gold, her mane of white flame threaded through with ribbons of crimson fire, and along her jaw the elegant line of her fangs lengthened, refined, predatory, the mouth of something that drinks its conquests rather than merely winning them!","When her eyes opened, the gold ring pupils burned with a new center: bloody red, and behind the red, a quiet turning light of infinity.","She was still the White Steed. She was now also, unmistakably, something more magisterial!","And Damodred!","The Laestrygonian...his proportions loosened at their edges, joints suggesting themselves in numbers the eye declined to count, his silhouette gaining a margin of half-present limbs that existed mainly in the corner of one’s perception and withdrew when looked at directly.","The ancient blindfold of hands across his face changed first and most: every hand of it turned bloody crimson gold, fingers lengthening, and then the whole lattice of them opened outward from the center like a terrible flower.","And at the very center, revealed, a single cyclops eye burned.","Its iris was vast and dark. Its pupil was red, and the red was not a shape but a congregation: countless minute hands, joining and rejoining, clasped into the form of a pupil that flexed when it moved. The eye swept the domain once, and the domain felt swept!","|The marked existence of HVITRMARR presents a unique transformation.|","| While all that you carried was cast out, her Causes were never carried. They are part of her existence itself, seated within her organs, born into her flesh by the hands of Those Who Remain. They cannot be removed from her, and so they are transforming WITH her.|","|Her nine Causes are becoming her own: unthreaded from the frameworks that seated them, remaking themselves within her organs under your authority. The process is ongoing. Their transformation may provide weavings of what your own Causes could be.|","| HVITRMARR has become a Noblesse Blood Apostle of the third tier: BLOOD DUKE.|","|DAMODRED has become a Noblesse Blood Apostle of the third tier: BLOOD DUKE.|","...!","Noah read the prompt about her organs twice, and set it carefully into the front of his mind, beside the Cause-replacement puzzle it had just illuminated!","The two finished beings bowed to him, dragon and Laestrygonian, and he checked their status panels as they did.","|STATUS PANEL: HVITRMARR- NOBLESSE BLOOD APOSTLE, BLOOD DUKE|","|VERITAS: 3|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 9|","|PONDUS: 3|","| STATUS PANEL: DAMODRED- NOBLESSE BLOOD APOSTLE, BLOOD DUKE|","|VERITAS: 3|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 10|","|PONDUS: 3|","Noah nodded at their power and their advancements.","\" As of now, I basically have a backbone of my own power and forces, \" he said. \" This Dimension still has another Dimension fusing into it, and armies of Infinite Lifeforms remain scattered through both. I think you two would be able to take care of them, yes?\"","He looked at Hvitrmarr and Damodred, and both of them nodded with immensity, the dragon’s great head dipping and the cyclops eye closing once in assent.","Then Noah’s voice went grand, and cold.","\" Any who fight, kill them. Those simply living within the Dimension, and however things will be once these Dimensions finish fusing, will know that they are under a new rule. THE Ymnaros, for now, will be a base of operations. The first Dimension I will have under my rule, and protect. \" A pause the length of a decree being sealed. \" For now, go stabilize it.\"","He gave the command to Hvitrmarr and Damodred, and nodded to Anaximander, who smiled wryly at having been reduced, in the span of one afternoon to a courier service. He waved his hands.","WAP!","The two of them disappeared.","Noah then turned to Ryaenara. She was already looking at him, her crimson eyes carrying utmost conviction, her hands folded before her red gold robes.","He nodded.","\" Let us see about Ulf.\"","Times of peace were rare. Even as he moved to cover many things at once, his Provenance Essence continued its patient refining of THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity against his chest, working into bones older than frameworks, and beneath all of it his mind kept turning, constantly, on what more he could design for his own grand new system of existence.","There was so much to be done!"]},{"number":5580,"title":"Chapter 5580: Chapter 5579: Existence Does Not Collapse!","paragraphs":["<THE Creature>","The number, at this moment, stood at nine hundred and ninety nine.","THE Creature walked through the deep places of THE Ghor-Vazhal, and the deep places were veins. Tunnels of pulsing obsidian ran down and down, their walls contracting in a slow rhythm, warm underfoot, wet along their seams, and through their channels rivers of blood flowed thick and unhurried, all of it moving in one direction. He followed the direction as he knew who it would lead to!","Behind him, only corpses remained as a fiendish aura wrapped around his entire figure.","Ten minutes of the hour remained to him, and he did not hurry either.","The blood was not his. Very little of the last hour’s blood had been his!","He had walked through rivers of it. True Lifeforms of the Cultivation Farms, in their hundreds, bred and stacked and set against him in the trial’s counting, and he had borne their attacks and THE MAW had eaten what was worth eating, and the rest had gone into the rivers now keeping him company on his walk. Nine hundred and ninety nine lives lifted, and set down. One remained.","The statue spoke as he walked.","It had been silent for most of the hour. And yet now, its voice arrived the way it always arrived, from no direction.","| The coming battle will be extremely taxing and almost impossible for you. You can be given a boost to guarantee your victory... for another condition.|","THE Creature did not slow down.","\" And what condition would that be?\"","| Your friend. Osmont. He is also a perfect candidate to bear weight, just like you. We are interested if you steer him towards Existence as well. Only the willing may walk this path, so they can remain unfathomably true. Make the introduction. That is the only condition.|","...!","THE Creature’s gaze went heavy.","He walked on through the pulsing vein-tunnel, blood parting around his tread, and he thought for a moment before deciding.","Then he shook his head.","\" Everyone has their own weight to bear ,\" he said. \" My introduction would be me imposing that weight upon him. That is not an introduction. That is a debt, dressed as a door. If he is meant to bear the weight of Existence, he will bear it, regardless of my introduction or not.\" His voice did not rise. It never rose.","\" Existence is vast, and existence is grand, and there are countless paths through it. Even you. Even Those Who Remain behind you. You are only grains of sand in the vastness of existence.\"","BOOM!","...!","Existence shook as he said it.","The vein-tunnels seized around him, the rivers of blood jumping in their channels, the whole deep structure of THE Ghor-Vazhal trembling once!","And THE Creature could see the statue with whatever sense a bearer has for what he bears. The seated colossus, faceless and gray and worn, and across the blank stone where a face would be...smiled!","A brutal smile, wide and slow and satisfied, the smile of something that had asked its question mostly to hear this exact answer.","Then it turned silent.","THE Creature walked on, silently, and the tunnels widened as the rivers deepened, and the pulse of the walls grew slower and heavier, the rhythm of a larger heart. At the end of the last vein stood a door.","It was a door of blood and gore. Sheets of dried crimson layered over meat, arteries braided into hinges, the whole of it seamed together with the patience of something that had been building itself out of its victims for ages. Behind it, he could sense the power.","He walked through it while speaking.","\"I always felt my fingers trembling, whenever I was about to face a truly fearsome enemy,\" THE Creature said, to the statue, or to the door, or to no one really.","\" Every time. In the early ages, when I was small, and everything above me was a weight I had not yet learned to lift. I would look at my hands, and they would tremble, and I would close them, and go forward anyway. Always...just step by step. One foot at a time. Keep moving forward.\"","The gore of the door parted around him, unwilling and yet obeying!","\" But after so many years, they never tremble anymore. Do you know why?\"","A pause, in the place where he carried the statue as its voice boomed out...","|... Why?|","\"Now ,\" THE Creature said, \" Existence itself trembles.\"","HUUM!","And everything began to tremble.","The door shuddered apart around his shoulders. The vein-tunnels behind him convulsed down their whole length. The domain he stepped into rippled from its floor to its distant ceiling, blood standing up in the rivers, gore shaking loose from the walls, all of it trembling at his passage the way his fingers had once trembled at everything, the debt of ages inverted and repaid in a single direction.","The domain was vast, and it was made of slaughter.","Lakes of blood spread across its floor between islands of mounded remains. Arteries thick as towers rose from the lakes and climbed through the dark air toward the far end of the domain, converging, feeding. And at the place where they all connected, fed by every vein in this deep Domain, stood the final weight.","A massive humanoid titan, mountainous in the gloom, its flesh crawling and seething where countless Gu Lifeforms had been fused into it, bodies within bodies, a colony wearing the shape of a colossus. A Primeval One!","Its murky obsidian eyes opened, and looked at THE Creature coldly, with the flat assessment of something that had ended ages and expected to end another. It opened its mouth to speak.","THE Creature shot ahead!","Existence shook all around him as he came, the lakes of blood parting in walls, the tower-arteries snapping taut, and his voice arrived ahead of his fists gloriously!","\"A vile thing like you does not even deserve to converse. Fight. Either you or I will collapse here today.\" The distance closed to nothing!","\" And...Existence does not collapse.\"","...!"]},{"number":5581,"title":"Chapter 5581: Chapter 5580: A Message From Father!","paragraphs":["<Jarl Skallagrim>","In the boundless darkness between Dimensions, the Steed stopped.","It had not wavered in all the crossings behind them, the last of his eight, running on the hope he had whipped into it, following a scent that no distance had managed to thin. It simply stopped, mid-stride, in the middle of nothing, and stood trembling in its chains!","\" Why have we stopped,\" Jarl Skallagrim said. It was not a question as really, questions implied patience and he had fucking none.","The Steed’s voice came up to him small and confused, a mountain speaking like a child.","\" She is gone.\"","\"Gone.\"","\"I can no longer sense Hvitrmarr. Her trail did not thin, Jarl. It did not turn. It...\" The great head swung slowly in the dark, searching. \" It ceased. As if she stopped existing anywhere my senses can reach. There is nowhere the scent goes. There is only where it was.\"","Skallagrim sat very still upon his throne-saddle, rot ticking quietly along his fissures, and consulted his lucidity at this time.","Scents did not cease. Beings fled, veiled, died, and every one of those left a shape in the weavings. A ceasing left nothing, and nothing was not a thing that existence produced on its own. Something had been done to her. Something outside his considerable education, and he was fucking educated!","But...","They were close. He knew they were close. In this fold of the dark there were fewer than seven Dimensions within reach as they had been inches away!","The few nearby they were heading towards were...THE Cajaman. THE Tisana. THE Ymnaros. A few others, lesser and stranger. She should be inside one of them. The thing that had ceased her scent was inside one of them!","He would pass by each of them in turn to ensure he found them.","His whip-arm moved, and the lash of woven curse-light cracked across the Steed’s flank!","CRACK!","\" Go towards THE Cajaman Dimension, for now ,\" Jarl Skallagrim said. \" We will find them. Even if we have to search one Dimension at a time. You have carried me this far on hope, little steed. Carry me the rest of the way on certainty...\"","The Steed gathered itself, and ran.","And as they went, deep in the crossing-dark, Jarl Skallagrim twitched.","It began as a wrongness at his brow, a heat with a shape to it, and then an obsidian mark surfaced on the skin of his forehead, black lines assembling into an old, old seal, and the weight that came through it bent him forward over his saddle-throne and tore a bellow out of him that rolled away unanswered into the dark!","\" NNGH... AAAAGH!\"","The Steed faltered beneath him, feeling it, whatever it was, bleeding down through the chains.","Then the weight passed. Skallagrim hung there a moment, breathing through the last of it.","And he raised his head, and laughed in astonishment.","\" HAHAHA! Oh. Oh, now this. Now THIS!\"","The Steed below him trembled in fear, but it still asked!","\" Jarl... what has happened to you?\"","Skallagrim wiped at his mouth. When he spoke, his voice had that texture the eight had learned to dread more than his whip, the mad cadence with the terrible lucid stillness underneath, a man singing over the top of his own dying weavings.","\" Little steed, you don’t know this, but us Descendants are unique beings ,\" he said. \" You were bred. We were spoken. A Descendant is a sentence with a bloodline, and every sentence has a speaker, and our speakers are Those Who Remain. Our Fathers. \"","He tapped the fading obsidian mark on his brow. \" And we can receive messages, directly, from our Fathers. It is our oldest inheritance. Older than our strength. Older than our curse.\"","He settled back on the throne, warming to the telling the way he warmed to nothing else.","\" Do you know what those messages are like? I have collected the accounts my whole life, the way beggars collect glimpses through feast-hall windows. For the favored lines, the messages come often. Commands, mostly. A Father points, and the line moves.\"","\" Some receive blessings through the mark, gifts of authority poured straight into the blood. Some receive dreams, whole nights spent walking the memories of their ancestor, and they wake weeping at the size of what they come from. Some lines receive only a single word once a generation, and they build entire civilizations around each word. And some, \" his grin widened, crooked, \" some receive silence. Lifelong, perfect, complete silence. Because a Father speaks when a Father has use for you, and not one heartbeat before.\"","He spread his arms to the dark.","\"I have never received a message. Not once. All my life. THE Sleepless Fiend, my very own ancestor, the speaker of my line, and in all my centuries of dying, through every experiment, every steed, every year I carved off my own span hunting a way out of the sentence he wrote me into, I never heard so much as a syllable. I used to pray for the mark to burn, little steed, when I was young and still stupid enough to pray. Silence. Always silence. I stopped fighting my madness partly to spite that silence. Let him inherit a lunatic, I thought. Ha!\"","His laughter faded to something quieter and far worse.","\" And yet, just now, I heard this voice for the first time.\"","He touched his brow again, almost gently.","\" And do you know the most ridiculous part? It was not even addressing me. Not me, Skallagrim, his son’s son’s son, dying in his name. It went out to all of us at once, a broadcast to the whole bloodline, the way a lord posts a bounty in a market square. It simply said: the White Steed has been cured. Find information. Uncover how she was cured, and the one who cured her. Deliver this, and your life will be extended. You shall have....salvation.\"","...!","The Steed’s body trembled!","Skallagrim leaned back and laughed at the roof of the dark, and there was no joy anywhere in the sound, only astonishment sharpened into something with edges.","\" Haha! How ridiculous is that? A thousand years I begged existence for exactly two things. Salvation, or a single word from my Father. And I received neither, and I made my peace, I chose to watch, I chose the madness, I let go of salvation with both hands. And it was AFTER I let go of it that my Father finally wants to send me a message, to grant me one! Not for my sake. Never for my sake. Because his little cured steed interests something in his long, long game, and now the dying sons are useful, now the silence breaks! HAHA!\"","His fists closed on the chains until his knuckles split, rot weeping from the fissures, and his voice dropped through the laughter into the truest register he owned.","\"I hate them. I hate Those Who Remain so much. So much!\" A breath came. The grin returned, dreadful and bright and filled with magisterial madness. \" Haha...\"","...!"]},{"number":5582,"title":"Chapter 5582: Chapter 5581: THE Remnant Seer!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Ryaenara’s Dimension had changed with her.","Noah stood on its high plateau and looked at the changes openly, because they were everywhere. The floating paintings still drifted all around them, hundreds of them, Ulf’s life’s work hanging in the air at every height, some finished and some abandoned mid-stroke.","But the sky above them and the ground below had been painted over by something no brush had touched. Red gold light lay across all of it, the color of her new robes and her new blood, her transformation written onto the whole Dimension that answered to her existence!","Even the sickly figure of Ulf was looking around in excitement. He sat propped among his paintings, wasted thin by THE Withering of the Remembered Root, and his dim eyes moved across the changed sky with the wonder of a man who had watched it happen.","And yet, even now, he was raising one sickly finger.","He pointed toward a nearby floating painting.","It showed his sister. Ryaenara, in her newly transformed state, obsidian-haired and robed in red gold, kneeling on dark sands toward an illusory figure. The figure itself was barely rendered, a shape more than a body, and it was surrounded by a massive blood gold crown.","\"I didn’t know if it would be a true future, or a false one, \" Ulf said. His voice came out thin and worn. \" But the weight on my sister seems to be removed.\"","His dim eyes traveled up to Noah. \" Have you come to try and do the same to me?\"","Noah looked at the painting for a long moment.","Ulf had painted his sister kneeling toward him even before her transformation. How far back had this canvas been waiting?","He was more and more interested in what this being’s transformation could provide.","He moved forward, and a drop of radiant blood rose into the air before him, crimson gold around its stellar blue heart.","\"I want to see if you can be cured by my blood alone. There was a Panacea I was initially going to try, but this may just be better.\"","Ulf looked at the drop, sickly and small beneath the floating archive of his own visions, and he nodded with dim eyes.","Less than a day ago, curing this being had been an impossibility not worth speaking of. The curse laid upon him traced to one of Those Who Remain, and Noah had told Ryaenara that he could not cure her brother. That doing so would require replacing his entire existence!","And the capability he had designed since was almost exactly that. THE Provenance Blood Mark grasped the very Lifeline of an existence and took it out of every framework, forcefully, into his.","Almost exactly. He was still unsure whether it would work!","The drop of blood went forward, and entered the forehead of Ulf.","The process that began was grand and slow and strangely sacred, crimson gold light sinking through the sick man’s skin in spreading veins, tracing him from crown to chest like dawn moving down a mountain, and behind Noah the figure of Ryaenara watched with apprehensive eyes filled with anxiousness, her hands pressed together!","Noah stayed focused.","The sickly figure of Ulf began to tremble. Lightly, then violently, his thin frame shaking as if seized, his jaw locking, and Noah went forward and put his hand on the head of this being, and gave the whole of his attention to what his blood was finding inside.","\" Focus on my voice, and nothing else, \" Noah said. \" Focus on the drop of blood permeating across your existence. You have been given a horrible fate this whole time, just because you can see the future. I need your entire existence to fight alongside me in rejecting this fate. You have autonomy. You have your own choices. Accept this change, and alter your entire weavings of existence.\"","HUUM!","His voice boomed out and reverberated across the entire Dimension, red gold sky and painted ground trembling with it!","And even as he was finishing, he felt it. A roaring rejection inside the body of Ulf, surging up against his blood, thrashing, almost as if a sliver of something within him was offended by what Noah was doing!","BOOM!","The forehead of Ulf instantly split apart!","His entire skull began to tear along its seams, blood sheeting down his wasted face as he screamed in absolutely horrendous pain, his body arching against Noah’s grip, and Noah felt his Provenance Essence buzz through the whole of him!","He came forward and held the man down even tighter, and he bellowed himself, and multiple more drops of his blood shot out and entered the body of this being one after another, the brilliance of the singularity within his existence shining Quintessentially through every drop!","BOOM!","Noah’s own forehead began to bleed, a line of red opening at his brow as though his skull would crack in answer, pressure for pressure!","He stood grandly and tyrannically through it, and his voice came down like a verdict.","\" Merely a leftover curse! The being it was bound to is no longer here, as I have grasped their Lifeline and changed them to something else entirely!\"","BOOM!","The words landed, and the thing thrashing inside Ulf thrashed once more, and it was the last thrash of a dying grip, the death throes of a sentence whose subject had been rewritten out from under it. The figure of Ulf trembled violently as he gushed out rivers of blood, everything the Withering had ever put into him leaving at once, Ryaenara crying silently behind them with both hands over her mouth.","And in the next instant, his skin began to close up.","His torn skull sealed. His body began to rise off the ground, wasted limbs filling, and waves of crimson gold light radiated outward from him in rings, rivers of brilliance seething through the air of the Dimension and pouring off him like water off a surfacing thing!","Noah finally let go, and stepped back, and watched.","And around them, the Dimension itself began to protest.","The surrounding weavings of Ryaenara’s Dimension trembled and cracked, thin fractures spidering through the red gold sky, the painted ground groaning, as if existence itself was angry at what was being taken from it!","Ryaenara fell to her knees and spat out blood, her crimson eyes blazing as she poured everything she had into stabilizing the existence around her, because this was her Dimension, her weight to hold, and nothing like this was even supposed to be possible inside it!","Existence was displeased.","A curse written by one of Those Who Remain had reached for its victim and found nothing to hold, because its victim was becoming a brand new existence, outside every ledger where the debt had been recorded!","Then, slowly, everything cooled.","The fractures in the sky sealed. The rivers of brilliance settled and sank inward. And the figure of Ulf was revealed, standing in the air where a dying man had been, radiating an utterly pristine aura.","He was pale, but it was no longer the pallor of sickness. It was the flawless pale of old royalty, skin without a single mark of the Withering anywhere on it. His dark hair fell clean and heavy past a face that had recovered the bones of a much younger man. And his eyes had no pupils at all.","They were bathed entirely in swirling crimson gold light, turning slowly, depths without floors, the eyes of something that looked at time the way others looked at weather.","|The marked existence of ULF presents a unique quality.|","| Within his existence resides a singular art, his alone, carried through his bloodline of one. It has been identified: THE REMNANT SEER.|","|Its nature is not yet translated.|","|Due to the uniqueness of this art, the marked existence has achieved the second tier of rarity.|","| ULF has become a Noblesse Blood Apostle of the second tier: BLOOD MONARCH.|","|STATUS PANEL: ULF- NOBLESSE BLOOD APOSTLE, BLOOD MONARCH|","|VERITAS: 2|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 12|","|PONDUS: 4|","...!","| The First Attribute, excluding you from thr equation, has exceeded 10, and it is the POTENTIA of one of your people.|","...!","The moment his transformation finished, the being descended!","Ulf came down through the red gold air and knelt before Noah, his pristine aura folding around him like a court mantle, his pupil-less eyes raised, and when he spoke, his voice had changed entirely!","It came out measured and turning, every line falling into rhythm, the cadence of a man who no longer spoke words so much as recited what he found already written.","\" Oh my Master, crowned in gold, a future glorious, and yet untold! Unthinkable roads lie on your way, but you must guard yourself this day! Oh!\"","...!","Ulf seemed...a bit crazed at this moment! Like someone who would look at you crazily while telling you the end of the world was coming!","His pupil-less crimson gold eyes did not helo in making him look like a crazed Seer as he continued.","\"Twice you have crossed the elder chain, two workings of Those Who Remain: a Steed was cured against their sign, and now their curse, undone by thine!","Interest builds behind the veil, and some of Those Who Remain now trail. Protect yourself, Master, from what watches and pauses! Move at once. ENACT YOUR CAUSES!\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5583,"title":"Chapter 5583: Chapter 5582: Home! I","paragraphs":["After his ridiculous eruption and his words that rhymed, Noah looked at Ulf while squinting.","Of course, the seer noticed the look. Ulf blinked, and then scratched his throat with a bit of embarrassment, the royal bearing slipping just enough to show the man underneath it. Perhaps the recitation had come out of him the way a shiver comes out of a body, arriving on its own schedule and asking no one’s permission. He did not seem able to fully control it!","In truth, Noah found himself marveling at the ability of this being more than the delivery. Interest from Those Who Remain, because he had undone two of their actions. That alone was a thought!","The attention of such beings, arriving now, when he had only just begun enacting his own true power, with a single point of PROVENANCE to his name and most of his system still unbuilt. But how much did he actually need to worry? What extent did Ulf’s ability reach? What exactly had he seen, and how much of it could be trusted?","So Noah walked close to the seer. Ulf swallowed hard and took a small step back!","\" What limits does your capability have?\" Noah asked with interest.","Ulf scratched his head at the question. And when the answer came, it was once again in a rhythmic cadance...almost as if he had a stutter he could not deviate from after his transformation!","\" My limits, Master, none have I found, for I was never pushed past ground. A sick man paints what fever shows, and half his life to fever goes. I was sick before, and I am sick no more, and I have not tested what lies in store. But ask your questions, one by one, and I may answer what can be done...\"","\"...\"","Would he truly be rhyming every time he talked?","But...","It was a fair answer, all things considered. A man who had spent his whole existence dying had never been given the room to find his ceiling. Compared to testing the limits of an art, asking questions cost nothing, and so Noah chose the question that mattered most.","\" You mentioned the attention of Those Who Remain. Can you tell me more about this?\"","At that, Ulf’s pupil-less eyes began to release beams of crimson gold brilliance, two soft rivers of light pouring into the air, and around him the floating paintings drifted slowly closer, as if his own old works wished to listen. His voice deepened.","\" Those Who Remain are power beyond all measure and name, and no category holds them. They do not move as lifeforms move, in want or fear or plan. Across all history’s turning, they have not moved at all. They send instead their extensions, to answer every call: their progenies, their Descendants, the sentences they spoke, who act across the ages. Never once, in any age, in any war or need, has one among Those Who Remain moved personally. And so their interest, Master, will come the only way it can: their Descendants and their progenies, and even Primeval Ones, will begin to circle, slowly, around your weavings.\"","The beams from his eyes brightened, and his cadence slowed, giving each line its weight.","\" The future I envision now is bright, and yet it bends, unpredictable in all its roads, uncounted in its ends. Yet of the few points narrowing the countless ways I see, the brightest of them all are Causes... and yet not Causes. For what the Master comes to forge is not a Cause at all, but something else entirely, that answers his own call. And I see us, oh Master. Ryaenara. I. The dragon in her crimson, the one-eyed giant. The Undefined Lifeform, the Living Observable Existence too... I see all of us as your extensions, put to use by you, to move where you would not be seen, to mask your weavings’ hue. I am here to serve, my Master. And so are many, many others.\"","WAA!","Each word he said felt sacred and grand!","The light faded from his eyes, and the paintings drifted back to their stations.","In other words, this highest-rarity Noblesse Blood Apostle among his people was truly unique!","He had always planned to enact his own version of Causes, generated entirely from himself. The only thing that had changed was the schedule. A rhyming man and the circling attention of the oldest things in existence had moved the project to the front of the queue.","After all, the foundations were already laid. He had begun enacting Arts- the Blood Drop that made no distinction between body and framework, the Rune that unfolded his blood into titanic clones across a Dimension, and the Blood Mark that pulled Lifelines out of every framework and had built the very Apostles standing around him.","Beneath all three, he had defined his own Infinite Sanguine Mana, the resource that made the rest possible. Compared to where he had stood a little while ago, he had already come far.","But the other thing he placed the most importance on was understanding his four new attributes. How to pass that ridiculous number of 10, the wall his VERITAS pressed against with every true act. His potential had gone beyond it by infinity, of course, though that felt less like an answer and more like a differently shaped question.","And the Seer in front of him was the first existence apart from himself to pass the value of 10 in any attribute at all, that quiet 12 sitting in his potential like a door nobody had opened.","There should be a grand change when one passed the value of 10. It was too hard a wall for that not to mean something, when even he could not push through it. But was potential different from the others? The other three values correlated to something currently held: power, trueness, Provenance.","And since nobody held Provenance unless they were First Lifeforms, VERITAS and PONDUS were the two values that gave a direct display of the power anyone currently expressed, while POTENTIA pointed only at roads not yet walked!","Perhaps the wall at 10 guarded the actual, and left the possible unguarded. Perhaps potential was allowed to be absurd precisely because it had not happened yet.","There was a lot to understand. And while he was thinking, he found he had begun stroking the necklace on his chest without quite deciding to, thumb moving slowly over bones older than every question he was asking.","At this time, the figure of Ryaenara came over.","She knelt beside her brother and took his head in both hands, and Ulf smiled at her. The siblings held each other, and their foreheads touched, obsidian hair against dark.","The sister spoke softly.","\"I was ready to find IT,\" she said. \" I even bound myself to THE Sealed One, who was chasing after IT, for you. I did not think that I had already found IT... and that it was the Master himself, right here.\"","Noah came out of his reverie at such words.","Him? IT?","Of course, different things could hold different meanings for many. In this case, plainly enough, she meant that he was the solution she had been hunting this entire time, the cure her whole long deception had been bent toward, found at last standing in her own Dimension. But no. He was not as grand as whatever THE Sealed One was chasing!","Whatever IT was that an antiquity had spent ages hunting, it was not a man who had held his first drop of Provenance for less than a day.","And as he was thinking of this, his eyes began to shine.","Because he began to think about a certain Steed.","Her Causes were transforming. He could sense her as an Apostle, out across THE Ymnaros, and the sense was precise. Everything regarding any framework she had belonged to had been stripped away when she was bound to him. The only thing that was not stripped away was what she already held. Her Causes.","Which were actually her organs.","And he had replaced those very same organs himself, back when he cured her. From cursed ones, to brand new ones that carried his previous Causes within them. He had seated his own work into her flesh, and now that flesh was becoming something that was hers alone, under his authority, outside every framework.","So if he was looking to generate his own version of Causes, not the same idea carried out by THE Sleepless Fiend and the others, not seats installed from outside, then he simply needed to utilize...his organs . Or anything within his existence. Something he had already generated. Something filled with Provenance Essence, grown from it, steeped in it!","The solution was once more within his own existence, just like his blood that he had made into his Infinite resource!"]},{"number":5584,"title":"Chapter 5584: Chapter 5583: Home! II","paragraphs":["As he came to his epiphany, Noah’s existence buzzed, and then he felt a tug.","It was not a vague feeling. Something closely connected to him had answered this exact moment, this potential emergence of the equivalent of his Causes, and the answer was coming from inside THE Infiniverse!","Of course, that made a certain sense. Since his grand change, he had cast out nearly everything he held into her, and he had not once entered. His Provenance Essence and his new standing seemed to be causing something there, in the place where all his old treasures slept!","So he turned to the seer first.","\" See the limits of your power ,\" Noah said. \" Push at them. And prepare for me any further knowledge you can reach regarding the Descendants, THE Sealed One, and Those Who Remain. I will want all of it when I return.\"","Ulf bowed his head, and beside him Ryaenara straightened as if the instruction included her, which, in truth, it did.","Then Noah tugged back on the unbreakable connection to THE Infiniverse, and disappeared.","—","He appeared inside an endless sea of blue.","Strings and waves stretched away in every direction without a horizon, currents of deep cerulean light crossing and recrossing through one another, and the immensity of the place pressed in gently from all sides.","This was a core domain of THE Infiniverse, one of her innermost chambers, and only one person was currently in it.","THE Infiniverse herself, in her humanoid form, sat among bubbles.","There were many of them, drifting slowly around her in the blue, and each one held something he had cast out. The Primordial Source turned quietly in one, dense as a swallowed star. His Infinity coiled in another, blue and endless, pressing lightly against its skin. The eighteen Causes drifted in a loose constellation, his nine and Hvitrmarr’s nine, still keeping each other’s company. The Intent, the Pantheon, THE First and Second Infinite Scale, Mana itself. And nearest to her, small and red and beating slowly, THE Amaranthine Heart.","Noah sighed as he looked at it all. An ocean, bottled and shelved, and a caretaker sitting in the middle of it.","Then he turned his gaze to THE Infiniverse herself.","She seemed just as grand as before, if not grander, since his rise had always reflected on her. And yet even she seemed a bit desolate, sitting there in her own depths, staring at the things he had cast out.","She rose when she felt his eyes. She came over to him through the blue, unhurried, and when she reached him she did not bow or report. Instead, she traced one finger along the necklace of bones on his chest, following its curve.","\"I inherently know that you would never cast me out, or leave me, or abandon me, \" she said. \"I inherently know this. My thought process, my very existence, is a logical one, and this is cemented within my existence. And yet, when you were casting everything out, even your Infinite Mana... a sense of fear rose within me that does not need to be there, and should not even be possible. \" Her eyes came up to his.","\" So even though I logically understand, and know... can you just reassure me?\"","...!","Noah’s gaze softened.","Reassurance. Affirmation!","Every single human being needed this, even when they knew. Perhaps especially when they knew, since knowing a thing and feeling it were two different things.","He went to THE Infiniverse and put his hand on the side of her head. She leaned into it and closed her eyes, and the contentment that crossed her face was quiet and grand!","\" Even you are displaying more and more human qualities,\" Noah said, and he was smiling as he said it.","\" In relationships, and I have a few, even though they know they have my love, even though they each know the lengths I would go for them, I am constantly still asked. Just how much do you love me? How much do you care? After all this power and immensity you continue to gain, after all the change you go through over time, do you still care the same as before? Do you still look at us the same as before?\"","...!","\" I have received all these questions and more, and every single one of them is just looking for affirmation. It is a very human quality. And I am happy to see you displaying it. Because if something like you can also be this human, then it means my path is truly going to be a glorious one, and that boundless many things can, and will, be human.\"","His hand stayed where it was. \" No. I would never cast you out. You are my home, and I am yours.\"","HUUM!","Their existences buzzed together as he said it, the blue sea around them brightening by a shade, and THE Infiniverse kept her eyes closed, simply feeling her Master’s hand.","After a while, Noah spoke again, quieter now.","\" You are the only person so intricately connected to me that you feel every immensity of mine this closely. Can you feel the Provenance Essence?\"","\" It is not something so simple that it can just be generated because someone casts everything else out. I must have met certain conditions that made it a possibility. After all, I am human, and I was born human. I was not, and am not, among THE First Lifeforms. So I also want to know. Why was I able to generate Provenance Essence? What exact condition did I meet, in addition to casting out everything I held, to make this possible? And since it is something I generated, I cannot transfer it to another. I feel a distinct rejection of what Provenance Essence stands for if I try to extend it toward others. So the question naturally becomes... how can you generate it yourself?\"","THE Infiniverse opened her eyes grandly at this.","\" Your rise and immensity continue to reflect on THE Infiniverse, \" she said. \" And while I may not be able to generate Provenance Essence... due to the change in your transformation, and your connection to THE Infiniverse...\"","She waved her hand.","The endless blue sea of waves and strings parted all around them, currents drawing aside like curtains in a great hall, and what they revealed was a doorway!","Through it poured a scene of utter immensity, and Noah felt his own existence pulling him toward it, a pull that felt familiar and foreign at the same time!","It was a forming domain, surrounded by blue gold brilliance.","\" Since I am considered your home ,\" THE Infiniverse said, \" your weavings and your Provenance Essence seem to be generating a domain exclusive to you. One that you can truly call home. Even I currently do not know much about it, as I have only felt it forming within me. But it should be something beneficial, and critical, that a First Lifeform should call... home.\"","...!"]},{"number":5585,"title":"Chapter 5585: Chapter 5584: Home! III","paragraphs":["The home of a First Lifeform.","His home.","He began walking toward it, and THE Infiniverse purposely stayed back, her hands folded, as if to let him truly experience this himself!","Noah stepped through the doorway.","And he came out standing...in the first age of existence.","The Realm opened around him in every direction, and the first thing he understood about it was that it could not decide on a size, or rather, that it had decided on two. It read as a homestead. It measured as a Dimension!","His eyes told him he could walk its breadth in a day, and his existence told him the horizon was as far away as the edge of everything, and both reports were true at once!","Blue gold grass rolled away from his feet in long unhurried hills. A river of quiet light moved through the valleys without sound, in no hurry to be anywhere, and where it pooled, the pools held stars.","Standing stones rose from the hilltops in rings, each stone taller than a titan and worn smooth as though generations of hands had rested on them, though no hand ever had.","In the middle distance stood a long hall built of pale stone and heavy dark timber, simple as a shepherd’s house and large enough that a Steed could have walked its aisle with her wings spread, and from its center rose a hearth-smoke that smelled of every fire he had ever came across.","Orchards climbed the far slopes, their fruit unfamiliar and burning with Infinite Sanguine Mana!","And above all of it hung a sky of deep evening blue, holding a single unmoving star, blinding within, silent without, which he did not need to be told was the mirror of the thing in his own chest.","It was simple, having been built before complication was invented. And it was vast the way only his new existence could properly feel. The first humans of the first age, if they had held grand power and a quiet evening, would have lived exactly here.","He walked in slowly, and observed everything, and the Realm observed him back with the settled attention of a house recognizing its owner.","And as he did...","|A Domain linked to your Provenance has formed within THE Infiniverse.|","|It is currently deemed: THE PROVENANCE REALM OF THE FIRST LIFEFORM.|","|It is yours. It generates from your weavings, and it grows from what you are. Its functions have settled as follows.|","| Within the Realm, the concentration of your Provenance Essence increases at a greatly hastened pace. Time within the Realm answers to you, and flows favorably against the outside.|","|Within the Realm, there is no strain in being yourself. It is the one place where the wall your VERITAS presses against may be worked at rest.|","|Within the Realm, your Sanguine Mana is enriched: blood generated here carries a deeper measure of your light.|","|Within the Realm, the design and understanding of your Provenance Arts comes more easily. What takes you hours outside may take you moments here.|","|Anything brought into the Realm, so long as its Lifeline is not entirely shattered, can be healed here.|","|Admittance is yours to grant. Those sharing close ties with you, your close family and your Apostles, may be admitted. All others are refused by the Realm itself regardless of their rank or power.|","| Realm rank: HEARTH. It is the first of known three: HEARTH, HALL, HORIZON. The Realm will rise and become grander as your Provenance Essence increases.|","|A boon of the Realm binds to you as its master. This is your native ground. All Sanguine Mana you have ever shed, wherever it rests across existence, may be called home to its soil, and what returns carries back with it the taste of everything it touched. Blood claimed from your enemies may be given to the Realm, and the Realm will drink it: each draught nourishes the ground, deepens your light, and leaves the drained forever known to your senses. And no wound, weariness, or want survives a night spent under this sky. He who rests in his own ground rises whole.|","|At the rank of HEARTH: should you walk the full breadth of your home, from its first hill to its last, you may attain Inner Peace, and an unknown number of Provenance Essence can be generated within you.|","...!","Inner Peace.","Of course, the prompt had made it sound like a destination, something waiting at the far end of the Realm the way a reward waits at the end of a task. But Noah had lived long enough, and fought through enough, to suspect that peace was not a place a man arrived at!","So he decided he would not hunt it. He would simply walk his home, from its first hill to its last, and see what the walking taught him.","He started where he stood, in the long blue gold grass, and he went slowly.","The first hills rolled under his bare feet without urgency, and he let them set the pace. When had he last moved slowly?","He always moved heavily and with utgency that it seemed he should always be stressed.","There was always one threat after another as peace for him...was a rarity!","Here, for the first time, his feet and his mind were in the same place, and the grass bent and rose behind him as if approving.","At the first ring of standing stones, he stopped and rested his hand on the worn shoulder of the tallest one, and he thought about the past.","The stone was warm. He thought about the Lower Observable Existence that had been taken from him, and the mother who had originated a Cause for his sake, and the graves and the ashes and the long weavings of everything done to him and everything he had done back.","Was peace the settling of all past weavings? He turned the idea over and set it down. No. The records of past weavings would never settle.","He walked on.","At the river of quiet light, he crouched and put his fingers in the current, and he thought about the present. The river moved without sound and without hurry, and in its pools the stars turned slowly, patient as coins at the bottom of a well.","Compared to every water he had ever crossed, this one asked nothing of him. Was peace this, then, the absence of demand? The stillness of a thing with nowhere to be? He watched the light part around his fingers and rejoin on the other side, and set that idea down too.","Stillness was pleasant, but he had met still beings before, sealed ones and seated ones and watchers, and he would not have traded his existence for any of theirs. A man built the way he was built could not make a home out of stillness. He would pace its floors within a day!","He walked on, through the orchards on the far slopes, and he picked one of the unfamiliar fruits and ate it, and it tasted like something he had been missing without knowing its name.","He thought about the people he fed. Seo-yeon. Henry. His mother. The millions in a golden citadel who had looked up at his crown of blood. Was peace their safety? But their safety was his purpose, and purpose was work, and work was not peace, or at least, that was how he had always sorted the two.","It was at the doors of the long hall, with the hearth-smoke drifting over him carrying every fire he had ever sat beside, that the sorting itself came apart in his hands.","Because why had he always placed peace and purpose in separate rooms? Who had taught him that peace was what remained when the work stopped, that a man rested from his purpose?","He stood in the doorway of his own hall and looked back over the whole of his walk, the stones and the river and the orchards and the hills, and the answer assembled itself with the quiet click of a lock that had been waiting!","Peace was not the absence of purpose. Peace was the absence of argument.","HUUM!","At that moment, his existence began to buzz resplendently!"]},{"number":5586,"title":"Chapter 5586: Chapter 5585: Home! IV","paragraphs":["All his existence, some part of him had been arguing with some other part!","The conqueror argued with the protector. The greed argued with the giving. The man who wanted to gather every human under his fold argued with the man who wondered if he had the right, and the one who could not die argued with the one who was born to.","He had carried those arguments so long that he had mistaken them for his own heartbeat. But here, walking his own ground, under his own star, with nothing borrowed anywhere in him to take anyone else’s side, the arguments had gone quiet one by one.","Quiet. Every part of him, for the first time, agreeing on what he was for.","That was Inner Peace. Not stillness. Coherence. A man entirely aimed!","And in the moment he understood it, the epiphany went through him like dawn going through a valley, and something within him answered.","Deep in the hollow of his existence, beside the first singularity, a second light bloomed.","Nothing about it was violent. It simply began, the way his first had begun, a dazzling point of incandescent blue kindling out of nothing but himself, and then there were two of them, turning slowly around one another in his depths, and their two hums found each other and folded into a single deeper chord that ran through his bones.","A second Provenance Essence!","And the Realm changed in response. He felt it before he saw it: the ground under his feet grew a shade more certain of itself, the grass deepened from blue gold toward something richer, the river brightened along its whole silent length!","The standing stones settled, as though they had been holding a breath since the Realm formed and could finally release it. And above the long hall, in the deep evening sky, a second star kindled beside the first, small and new and blinding within, and the two of them hung together over his home the way his two lights now hung together in his chest.","Noah stood in his doorway for a long moment, at peace, actually at peace, and let himself have it!","Then, being who he was, the first thing he did with his peace was work.","He reached up and removed the necklace from his chest. THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity came away from his skin for the first time since he had put it on before an army, still humming faintly with the refinement his essence had been working into it, and he set it down on the broad stone threshold of his hall, carefully, the way one sets down a sleeping thing.","Then he traced one finger down the center of his chest.","His skin opened along the line. There was no pain in it, and no blood that he did not permit, and no violence at all. Skin, then tissue, then muscle parted smoothly at his instruction, folding aside like the doors of a place he owned, because he did own it, and his chest cavity lay open to the evening light of his Realm.","What glistened inside was worth the looking.","His bones shone stellar, blue gold light living in them the way light lives in deep ice, and among them his organs sat luminous and grand, each one remade by his transformation, each one his beyond any argument, and each one steeped through with the doubled hum of his two lights!","The heart most of all. It beat slow and strong in its place, and every beat sent a faint blue ring through the cavity, and he looked at it the way a founder looks at ground.","He started with his heart.","\" From my heart, Quintessence shall bloom once more, \" Noah said quietly.","\" But it will not be a Cause. It will be my... Telos. My Osmontian Provenance Telos. THE Osmontian Provenance Telos of... Quintessence. This will be one of the pillars of my existence. And in time, THE Infinite Cause itself will be replaced, for... THE Infinite Osmontian Telos!\"","...!","Telos.","A Cause is where a thing comes from. It is an origin, seated at the beginning of an existence by hands that arrived before it, and everything built on a Cause spends its whole span answering backward, toward the root, toward the seat, toward the question of what made it!","All the frameworks of existence run on that grammar, and all the old powers, THE Sleepless Fiend among them, are gardeners of other beings’ roots.","A Telos is the opposite direction. It is not where a thing comes from, but what a thing is for. Not the root but the aim. An end, chosen and generated by an existence for itself, planted ahead rather than behind, so that every part of that existence stops answering backward to a maker and starts moving forward toward a purpose.","A Cause is given, and can therefore be gripped, cursed, harvested, and owned by whoever did the giving. A Telos is declared, and can only ever be owned by the one who declares it.","The first beings needed no Causes installed at their beginnings, because they were their own beginnings. What they carried instead, if they carried anything, was direction. And a man who had just learned that his peace and his purpose were the same thing was, perhaps, the first existence in ages properly built to carry direction again!","The heart came first, since beginnings mattered!","Noah stood in the doorway of his long hall with his chest open to the evening light, and he began. A thread of Sanguine Mana rose out of the open cavity, drawn from the blood already moving through him, crimson gold and unhurried. Around it, he gathered slivers of his Provenance Essence, thin shavings of incandescent blue peeled carefully from his two turning lights, and this part he did slowly, because the essence resisted being divided the way a name resists being spoken in halves!","He wound the thread and the slivers together, and he laid them against his beating heart, and he spoke the aim into it.","Quintessence.","Not as a word borrowed from a Tongue, though his Tongue carried it. And not as the Cause it used to be, seated once in his old existence. As a direction!","The heart of him would be for the essential, the thing from which every other thing took its measure, and every beat from this one forward would answer that purpose rather than any origin. His blood carried the instruction, his essence carried the authority, and his heart, being his beyond any argument, accepted both.","The change moved across the organ grandly.","The heart’s deep red gained a lacquer of blue gold, light sinking into the muscle rather than sitting on it, and across its surface, rings began to turn. Ring within ring, nested and slow, the same pattern his old fused eyes had once carried, now living on the surface of the organ itself. With every beat, the rings brightened and a low, clean tone went out through his cavity, less a sound than a statement, and the two stars over his hall pulsed faintly in time with it. It no longer looked like an organ that pumped blood. It looked like a small throne that happened to beat!","|THE first Telos has been generated.|","|THE OSMONTIAN PROVENANCE TELOS OF QUINTESSENCE has been generated within your heart. It was declared and your existence has accepted the aim.|","|Your PONDUS has increased. PONDUS: 10.|","|You were Quintessentially true to your existence. Your VERITAS elevated tremendously, but has not been able to climb past the value of 10.|","Ten, and ten!","Two of his four measures now stood at that stubborn number, and the wall had not moved for either of them!","Of course, he knew exactly which aims came next. He had carried nine Prime Causes once, before the casting out!","Existence. Paradox. Chaos. Mana. Adversity. Tyranny. Harvest. Apocalypse. And Quintessence, already reborn and beating. Those nine had been his work carved in the shape of somebody else’s idea, and he did not intend to copy them back. He intended to answer them, each old origin reborn as an aim, pointed forward instead of planted behind.","The liver came second.","There was a debt in that choice! Once, in the war inside Hvitrmarr, he had died, and it was his liver, THE Hepatarch of the Undying Root, that had rebuilt him from a single pulse in an ocean of nothing, self first and flesh after. The organ that had once held the whole of his being in reserve now received the aim of being itself. Existence!","Seated where his existence had once been kept safe, so that from this day the deepest purpose of his flesh was simply, stubbornly, to be, and to go on being, past any argument the outside cared to make. The organ took the thread and the slivers and turned a deep steady gold!","His spine took Paradox, and he found he liked the symmetry: a spine whose aim was to carry opposing weights without breaking, conquest and protection, greed and giving, the mortal and the endless, all stacked on one column that would hold them because holding contradictions upright was now what it was for!","His marrow took Chaos, raw potential seated in the place where his blood was born, so that everything generated from his depths would rise out of the unformed the way the first things rose, answering no pattern but the one he gave it!","His lungs took Adversity, the breath before every charge, so that hardship itself became a thing he inhaled and was fed by, which, in fairness, had been true of him since an F Rank Hunter first refused to die regardless.","His stomach took Apocalypse, transformative endings seated inside the furnace of him, destruction held as a tool by discipline. His tongue took Mana, the old external ocean reborn as an aim of pure expression, so that speaking, casting, declaring, the whole grammar of power he had once borrowed, now lived in flesh as something he generated!","His hands took Harvest, the gathering aim, everything flowing to him and everything given flowing back grander, seated in the two instruments that had done all his life’s taking and all its giving alike.","And his eyes, last of the nine, took Tyranny.","He considered that one longest before seating it. Tyranny was a word other beings used about him with fear, and he used about himself without apology. Once it seated, to be looked at by him would carry weight, the gaze of a will that bent for nothing, before which existence itself tended to straighten and behave.","His obsidian singularity pupils drank the thread and the slivers, gained the faintest turning ring of gold at their event horizons, and the matter was settled!","HUUM!","Nine organs. Nine aims. Nine Teloi standing where nine Causes had once grown, the same nine names reborn in a new grammar, except that nothing had been planted in him by anyone, and everything pointed forward instead of back.","And when the ninth settled, his entire existence began to vibrate.","It started in the marrow and rose. Every seated Telos brightened at once, heart and liver and spine and marrow and lungs and stomach and tongue and hands and eyes, nine lights waking in one body and discovering one another, and the undulation that moved through him was less like power and more like agreement, immensity rolling through his frame in long slow waves as the whole architecture of him rang on a single note for the first time!","The grass of his Realm lay down in rings around the hall. The river of light stood still in its bed to listen. The standing stones leaned inward by a width no instrument would ever catch!","Nine aims, one direction. A man with a semblance of Inner Peace entirely aimed, now all the way down to his organs.","And in the hollow of his existence, beside the two turning lights, a third bloomed!","It came the way the second had come, without violence, kindling out of nothing but himself, and the moment it opened, the chord of his hum deepened again, three lights turning about one another now in a slow braided orbit, and above the long hall a third star kindled in the evening sky, and his Realm grew a shade more certain of itself from its first hill to its last!","A total of three Provenance Essence!","Noah closed his chest with a trace of his finger, skin and muscle folding shut over nine quiet thrones, and he stood in his doorway breathing his own hearth-smoke, and he waited as immensity bloomed!","|An advancement past 10 has begun to occur for VERITAS and PONDUS.|","...!"]},{"number":5587,"title":"Chapter 5587: Chapter 5586: Unperceivable! I","paragraphs":["Noah rose from the threshold of his hall, and looked out over his Realm, and felt the wall come down!","It came down one grain at a time and then all at once, and the two attributes that had pressed against it for so long, his VERITAS and his PONDUS, moved past 10 together, side by side!","He stood very still while it happened as he had to sense everything.","The first change was growth. Actual growth, as parts of his body...grew!","His existence was generating Appendages.","Of course, Appendages were his thing for a little while now. When he cast everything out beneath the falling sky, he had assumed that whole Chapter of his anatomy had gone into the bubbles with the rest. But that assumption, it turned out, had been selling them short.","Because the backbones of the Appendages had never been external at all.","The Pinion Vigil had watched because he was a being who watched. The Estuary Eye had drunk the weavings of past and future because he was a being who refused to be surprised by time. The Hepatarch of the Undying Root had rebuilt him from a single pulse because he was, at his floor, a thing that did not agree to end!","The boons had only ever been scaffolding around instincts that were his from the start, and his existence had quietly preserved those backbones through the casting out, waiting for when they could rebuild them out of proper material.","That time was now, and the material was him!","He felt THE Estuary Eye emerge first, reopening somewhere in the depths of his existence, and it was now an eye of incandescent blue, its currents running with his own light!","THE Pinion Vigil unfurled second! And THE Hepatarch came third, settling back into its deep seat beside the Telos of Existence like an old guard dog lying down next to a young one!","And then, with the three old instincts generated, his existence built something new.","It began across his shoulders and his back, though calling it a location was already a simplification.","He felt a vast structure condense out of his crossed PONDUS, invisible and immense, a yoke of blue gold force settling across shoulders that were suddenly broad enough for it, and when it finished settling, Noah rolled his shoulders once, slowly, and the ground of his Realm flexed beneath him in sympathy.","| Your VERITAS has crossed. VERITAS: 11.|","|Your PONDUS has crossed. PONDUS: 11.|","|Your existence has begun generating PROVENANCE APPENDAGES: anatomy grown from nothing but yourself, in the manner of THE First Lifeforms.|","|Three Appendages of your old existence carried backbones that stemmed truly from you. They have been preserved, and are reborn: THE ESTUARY EYE, THE PINION VIGIL OF THE UNBROKEN GAZE, and THE HEPATARCH OF THE UNDYING ROOT. They are currently transforming as their elevated capabilities are not yet known.|","|A new Provenance Appendage has been generated from the crossing of your PONDUS.|","|THE YOKE OF THE STANDING SKY.|","|It is the appendage of bearing. What cannot be lifted, you may take up: a wound, a curse, a dying Cause, a burning region, A Dimension, an Observable Existence, the weight pressing on another’s existence. What you take up, you carry, and while you carry it, it presses on no one else. What you carry, you may set down where you choose, and what you set down, you may take up again. The limit of what the Yoke may bear is the limit of your PONDUS.|","It was...somewhat a unique one as its usage was not entirely clear!","He had once knelt under a descending sky with his palms against its underside, and pushed it back up. This appendage seemed capable of allowing him to bear such a heaby weight like that freely!","Could he lift an entire Observable Existence or Dimension freely with this? And just lift, or do much more?","But the prompts were not finished, and neither was the crossing, because beneath the new anatomy, he felt a different kind of power rising!","It felt like something...inviolable.","| The crossing of an attribute past 10 grants a PRECEPT.|","|A Precept is an undeniable rule that an existence writes about itself. It is not a technique, and it is not an aim. It is a standing rule, always in force, which the surrounding weave of existence must simply work around. Precepts are not chosen. They are earned: your existence drafts them from how you have actually lived. They arrive as COMMON, RARE, or UNIQUE.|","|Two attributes have crossed simultaneously. In place of two lesser Precepts, your existence has written one law of the highest order.|","| THE PRECEPT OF SOLIPSISM. UNIQUE.|","| You are imperceivable to any lifeform whose VERITAS and PONDUS do not both stand at 10 or above. And what cannot perceive you, cannot harm you: from all such existences, you are immune to harm in every form it takes. In turn, what was imperceivable to you begins now to be perceived.|","...!","What?","Noah stood with that for a long moment!","SOLIPSISM!","He felt it settle over him as an invisible glow of power, sourceless and total, wrapping his existence!","But more than that, and stranger than that, was the last clause on this newly budding Precept. What was imperceivable to you begins now to be perceived.","Because everything around him was growing unfathomably brighter.","It came in gradually as his vision expanded. The blue gold hills stayed the blue gold hills. The river of light stayed the river. But through them, over them, woven among them at every height, he began to see something new: shimmering stellar white rivers of light, flowing all around.","They were everywhere!","They ran through the air of his Realm in slow braided currents, some as fine as thread and some as broad as roads, crossing the hills, pouring soundlessly over the standing stones, threading between the orchards, a whole second geography of white brilliance laid over the first, and it had all been here the entire time.","He had walked the full breadth of his home, first hill to last, at peace, observing everything. And he had seen none of it!","He reached out toward the nearest current, slowly.","And he touched it.","| You have perceived THE ARGENT LOOM.|","|It is an authority present throughout nature, flowing across Dimensions, Observable Existences, and the spaces between: the loomlight from which the higher weave is threaded. It is perceivable only to lifeforms of extremely high Dimensionality. To all others, it does not exist.|","|Those who perceive it use it. Some forge with it: constructs, domains, armaments, and treasures threaded from raw loomlight. Others, who are not Provenance Lifeforms, draw it into their existences and refine themselves upon it, ascending their Dimensionality through what they take in.|","| You are perceiving it for the first time. You are not the first to perceive it, far from it.|","HUUM!","The current ran over his fingers, cool and dense and old!","Something he didn’t even know about flowed here! In his Realm, born moments ago from his own weavings, and the Argent Loom already ran its white roads as though it!","Which meant it likely flowed across THE Infiniverse, through her seas and her thousand realms, past the bubbles of everything he had cast out. It flowed, presumably, through THE Ymnaros, over tbr Observable Existences within it. and over the Golden Expanse and its citadel of millions, past his floating clones....","It had been there through the whole of his existence, and he simply had not known it was there!","He drew his hand back slowly, and looked out across his Realm at the white rivers threading through everything.","With this new sight, what else was flowing, right now, through the places he thought he knew?","And if one authority this vast had been running invisibly through his whole life, right before him, close enough to touch...","What things existed out there, right before him, that he still could not see?"]},{"number":5588,"title":"Chapter 5588: Chapter 5587: Unperceivable! II","paragraphs":["Noah stepped back out through the glowing door of his Realm, and THE Infiniverse was waiting for him.","She floated beside the doorway in her endless blue sea, hands folded, eyes on the light. And she did not turn to him!","Because she could not see him.","He stood before her in the blue, close enough to count the strands of her hair, and her eyes rested on the doorway behind him, patient and unaware. THE Infiniverse. His companion, his home, the one existence so intricately connected to him that she felt his every immensity!","Her VERITAS and her PONDUS did not both stand at 10, and so, by a law his own existence had written, he was not in her reality at all.","Of course, he could make himself perceivable at any time. He felt the permission sitting in the Precept, his to grant with a thought. But he wanted to explore this state first.","So he raised his hand, and placed it on her cheek, the same way he had placed it not long ago when she had asked him for reassurance.","And...","Nothing. Her eyes did not move. Her breath did not change. His palm rested against her cheek and her existence reported an empty sea!","Was this...human?","To not be seen by others, once one reached enough of a height. Had that not always been the arrangement?","A father worked heights his children never perceived. A mother carried weights her whole house walked past daily. Every leader he had ever known became less visible the higher they rose, until their people saw the crown clearly and the man not at all!","Perhaps existence had not invented anything new for him. Perhaps it had only taken the oldest loneliness of the human condition and written it down formally, with clauses.","And yet.","She had asked him to reassure her, even though she logically knew.","Knowing a thing and feeling it were two different things. Was that not the answer sitting right in front of him? Humans climbed, and humans went unseen, and then humans came back down and put their hands on each other’s faces and made themselves perceivable again, over and over, every day.","He drew his hand back slowly, and left.","And behind him, THE Infiniverse blinked. Her hand rose, and touched her own cheek, and stayed there a moment, her brows drawing together over an empty sea.","—","Noah took a step, and crossed thousands of Realms.","He came out standing in the warm air of a farmland realm, gold fields running to the horizon under a kind afternoon sky, and he heard them before he saw them.","Laughter. A long table set outside a farmhouse, crowded with food and more crowded with people. Henry sat sprawled at one end, blue-gold hair catching the light.","Seo-yeon sat cross-legged on the bench beside Amelia, stealing food off her grandmother’s plate. Barbatos and Adelaide argued warmly over a pitcher. Naldine, Titano, Sigrid, and half a dozen others filled out the benches, and the whole table had the settled, unhurried noise of people enjoying themsleves!","Noah floated near them, unperceived, and watched his family eat.","Amelia was smiling as her hand was on her chest, no doubt sensing the newly revamped Causes that were now Telos, oh which she was an Originator of still.","And her eyes went, briefly, to the empty place that had been set at the head of the table.","Seo-yeon paused. Her head tilted a fraction, and for one breath her gaze drifted through the air near him, past him, through him, searching for something she could not name.","Noah stayed longer than he had planned to.","He did not make himself perceivable.","He had many thoughts crossing his mind as...he took another step.","—","He came out among endless volcanic mountains.","Crimson blue infinity churned through the ranges, rivers of burning power running down black slopes, the sky above lit from below. And near the peak of the nearest mountain, small against all of it, sat the crying figure of Emotive.","Her manic emotions buzzed around her in ragged loops, joy and grief and fury tangled past sorting, and she was doing something with her hands. Taking things out of herself!","Portions of her Everythings, drawn out one after another, glimmering pieces of what she was and what she owned, and she was throwing them into the burning lava below, one by one, and repeating the same words with each throw.","\" You don’t deserve love. You have done too much... this is why he threw away your heart...!\"","...!","Noah had not thought Emotive would take it this hard!","He made himself perceivable instantly.","Emotive blinked.","Her head came up, and she looked at him floating there in the burning light, and instead of stopping, she cried harder, her whole body shaking, and her voice came out manic and small at once!","\" Am I...deserving of any love? Of anything at all?\"","Noah came down.","He crossed the black slope and wrapped his arms around her, and she was rigid in them!","\"I am sorry I didn’t communicate in advance. I cast out many things from myself. The Source. My Infinity. The heart. But I did not cast them out because I did not want them. I cast them out because my existence had to generate everything truly from itself, and it could not do that in a space already full. What I set down is kept, and safe, and not one piece of it was thrown away.\" He drew back just far enough to look at her.","\" You, and all the others, are deserving of all the love and happiness you could want. Okay?\"","Emotive’s face crumpled entirely.","She crashed into his chest and hugged him and cried, loudly, gracelessly, her manic emotions collapsing one by one into plain ordinary weeping!","The lava churned below them. The crimson blue infinity rolled through the mountains.","And then his gaze suddenly changed.","His head came up, and his eyes went distant, because far away, something had just happened.","Above THE Golden Expanse within THE Ymnaros, his clone floated where it had floated since the pledge. And his clone had changed with him. It, too, had become something that could not be perceived. It, too, could now perceive what Noah could not perceive before, the white rivers, the second geography, the layer of existence that had been running silently over everything all along.","And it had just looked up.","Because hanging above the endless skies of THE Ymnaros, in that layer no eye below the law could see, there was something terrifying!"]},{"number":5589,"title":"Chapter 5589: Chapter 5588: Unperceivable! III","paragraphs":["Above THE Golden Expanse, in the layer of existence that no eye below the law could see, something was hanging in the endless skies of THE Ymnaros as the gaze of THE True Human Emperor rose to meet it!","And it was vaster than an Observable Existence.","Noah looked at it through his clone as the looking itself took time, because the thing did not end! It was a single living thing, deep stellar purple in color, and its body stretched past the horizon in every direction as it kept going past the horizon after that, so vast that an entire Observable Existence could have been lost inside it!","And its shape was a simple one to grasp, because it closely mimicked something like a massive bacteria or virus.","Its head was a huge many-sided shell of flat purple plates fitted together, hanging directly above THE Golden Expanse.","From under that head, long thin jointed legs reached down for thousands of miles, and each leg ended in millions of hair-fine threads that spread out across the sky of the domain below! Its long body was see-through in places, and inside that clear purple skin, small violet lights drifted and churned in slow waves, glowing brighter and dimmer as the whole terrifying presense of it pulsed and fed.","Because its jaws were open!","Under the many-sided head, the plates had pulled apart into a huge open mouth as it was drinking, and Noah could see the intake now with his new sight.","Thin ribbons of color were rising up off the entire Golden Expanse below, off the citadel of millions, off the pledged thousands, off every survivor of the war! Their worry. Their pain. Their misery. And even their happiness, the new fragile hope of a domain that had just stopped burying its dead, all of it being pulled up in slow threads into the open mouth of a thing none of them would ever know was there...!","HUUM!","| Identity: a WOE CULTURE. A vast lifeform of the unseen layer. Woe Cultures are relatively harmless lifeforms in themselves: they do not hunt, they do not conquer, and they do not devour bodies. They latch above gatherings of lifeforms and siphon the happiness, anxieties, pain, and miseries of all those around. However: tendrils of its power permeate out across nearby existence, altering probability, and calling in more conflict and adversity to the region it has latched onto. Where a Woe Culture feeds, wars arrive more often, tragedies align more easily, and grief is harvested at its ripening. This nature sits at their core. It is simply who they are. They are not particularly powerful. They will preserve themselves if attacked...|","|STATUS PANEL: WOE CULTURE|","|VERITAS: 12|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 11|","|PONDUS: 11|","...!","Twelve!","A VERITAS above his own!","It hung fat and glowing over his domain with a Trueness that surpassed him, and of course it was twelve, of course, because the thing was perfectly true to itself! It had no doubts about its nature and no arguments inside its endless body as it fed on sorrow and farmed sorrow to feed on, never once questioning either.","And the tendrils!","The probability-tendrils spread across the sky of THE Golden Expanse were quietly bending the odds of an entire region toward conflict as horrendous questions bloomed one after another. How long had it hung here? How many of the age-cycles of war that had emptied the family graves of Superpowered Lifeforms, one generation after another, had simply been harvest seasons arranged by the thing above the clouds?","\"...\"","The clone of THE True Human Emperor looked at it with a furious gaze as when it came to what exactly he should do here, his existence already knew it clearly.","A thing was farming his people.","In the next second, eight more Provenance Sanguine Clones tore into the unseen layer out of folds of crimson gold as they appeared behind the first, titanic and shamanic and glorious as crowns of blood turned above nine heads!","Nine bloody staffs rose as one, and at the tip of each, a drop of blood formed, crimson gold around stellar blue!","Sanguine Blood Drop!","Nine drops popped!","BOOM!","A battle bloomed...that those around could not even see.","The unseen sky of THE Ymnaros turned crimson gold from horizon to horizon as event horizons bloomed in their uncounted numbers across the stellar purple bulk, twisting force of infinite density detonating along light years of skin and plate! And below, in the seen world, not one soul of THE Golden Expanse felt so much as a breeze as the war above them did not exist in their Dimensionality at all.","The Woe Culture convulsed!","Its many-sided head snapped around as its plates ground against each other, and across its vast surface the violet motes froze mid-churn as Noah felt its attention arrive on his clones carrying something he had not expected from a thing that size.","Shock!","It blinked in its fashion, every mote going dark at once and relighting, because it had been perceived.","Something below had seen it, and things below did not see it, had never seen it, in all the long ages of its grazing!","Then it preserved itself.","Its retaliation came in its own grammar, and its grammar was corruption.","The long thin legs snapped up off the domain’s sky and drove down at the clones as hollow lances longer than mountain ranges struck at crimson gold flesh, and they did not cut, they injected, violet code flooding toward his blood as it tried to rewrite what it touched into more of itself!","Patches of its see-through skin swelled and burst in silent blooms as clouds of glimmering spore-motes latched onto whatever they met and began to replicate, doubling, quadrupling, purple frost spreading across the arms of two clones!","Sheets of dissolving fluid sluiced from its jaws as they unmade the very weave where they fell, and beneath all of it, the probability-tendrils turned on him.","But his blood did not take instruction!","The violet code flooded into Sanguine Mana and found nothing it was permitted to rewrite! The spore-frost spread across crimson gold and instsntly stopped, starved, because his blood answered no authority but his own!","The clones circled the endless body in wide burning arcs as their staffs swept and the barrage did not pause, Sanguine Blood Drops falling in continuous rhythm as they tore gorges of crimson through stellar purple, whole plates of its many-sided head shearing away and dissolving as thousands of miles of its body collapsed in slow silence!","And midway through its tearing, the thing spoke.","Its voice boomed through the unseen layer, heavy and vast and genuinely puzzled.","\" Why attack me, Little One? We are all simply moving in accordance with our nature across existence.\"","Noah answered through nine mouths at once, and his voice came out tyrannically calm.","\"I reject your nature. Do you understand what you hang above? Lifeforms who bury their children and cannot say why the wars keep coming. Countless many have died across the ages, bled out in conflicts your tendrils arranged, grieving on schedule so that your jaws would not go empty. Their miseries were your farmland. I reject it. Wholly.\"","The motes of the Woe Culture churned slowly, and when it answered, there was no cruelty anywhere in it, and there was no comprehension either.","\" So... what? Lifeforms live, and lifeforms die. It is nature. It is...existence\"","...!","Oh!","\" Then let me enforce nature,\" Noah said as nine staffs rose together, \" and give you your death!\"","BOOM!","The barrage redoubled as gorges became canyons across the endless purple!","And the Woe Culture became infuriated!","Every mote down its lighy years flared violet-white at once as its grammar changed! Its long thin legs spread wide as fields of hair-fine threads opened across the whole unseen sky, and it reached, not for the clones, but for the rivers!","The endless white authority of THE Argent Loom answered it! Currents that had flowed serenely through the battle bent out of their courses and poured toward the vast body as white rivers wrapped around its long legs and gathered into its open jaws, threading through the wounds in its body as loomlight knitted across the crimson canyons!","And along its many-sided head, the gathered white began to weave, strand crossing strand at terrifying speed as lances and lattices and turning wheels of pure stellar white assembled above THE Golden Expanse, authority older than the frameworks bending into weapons!"]},{"number":5590,"title":"Chapter 5590: Chapter 5589: Nature Against Nature!","paragraphs":["The white weapons fell!","Lances of woven loomlight rained down from the many-sided head of the Woe Culture as turning wheels of stellar white carved through the unseen sky, and the nine clones of THE True Human Emperor scattered across the heavens as detonations of crimson gold met an authority older than the frameworks themsleves!","And through all of it, the vast thing was still trying to understand.","\" You strike me even now,\" its heavy voice boomed as three of its long legs swept a clone out of the sky, hair-fine threads bending fortune so that every dodge arrived a breath late!","\" And I strike you, because you would end me, and I preserve myself. But I do not understand you, Little One! This... is what I am? I am a Woe Culture? I am simply living as I should, emulating the Primevals and THE First Lifeforms. You would hunt me because of my nature? Others have passed through here and seen me and not done anything. We simply nod to each other. Why not you?\"","Others!","The word boomed inside Noah even as his clones wove between falling lances. Others had passed through this unseen layer.","Others had seen this thing hanging over his people, and nodded, and moved along! What manner of beings strolled through the white rivers above the skies of Dimensions unobserved?","\"I do not hunt you because having a nature is a crime. Everything alive has one. I hunt you because your nature and mine conflict, and conflicting natures do not get to share one sky!\"","\" Natures do not conflict ,\" the Woe Culture cut in, a lance of white driving down between two clones as it spoke, genuinely arguing now, fighting and reasoning in the same breath!","\" Natures coexist. The storm does not conflict with the mountain.\"","\"The storm does not FARM the mountain!\" Noah’s nine voices cracked back across the sky as staffs swept a wheel of white aside!","\" Your nature farms the grief of gathered lifeforms. My nature is to gather lifeforms and guard them. The ones you drink from below are mine, sworn to me, led by me, and every ribbon of misery you pull up through those jaws is pulled out of my people! Those others who nodded at you carried no one beneath your shadow. I do. Your claim on this sky and my claim on this sky cannot both stand.\"","His voice went cold as a drop of blood formed at every staff. \" So one of them falls. You will not die for being what you are. You die for being what you are...HERE.\"","HUUM!","The violet lights churned slowly through the endless body as its legs drew back, and when it spoke again, there was something almost reasonable in the vast voice.","\" Then I will leave here. I will go elsewhere, and live my nature above some other sky.\"","\"You will do the same where you go, yes?\"","\" Of course,\" the Woe Culture said honestly, without a single beat of hesitation, \" for that is my nature.\"","...!","And there it was.","It would drift across the unseen layer and settle above some other Dimension of countless decillions who buried their dead and never knew why the wars kept coming, and it would open its jaws, and it saw nothing in that sentence to apologize for.","\"...\"","Noah shook his head as before any sentence could be carried out, he reached for his newest tool.","THE Yoke of the Standing Sky!","The invisible structure across his shoulders woke for the first time as he willed it, blue gold force spreading out from him through all nine clones at once, and nine titanic figures raised their hands toward the endless purple body as Noah did something no being below had ever done to a Woe Culture.","He took it up.","BOOM!","The weight arrived!","Gigaparsecs of living lifeform came down onto his existence in a single instant as the Yoke gathered the whole of it, plates and legs and gigaparsecs of glowing skin, every league of a thing vaster than an Observable Existence, and Noah felt his frame ring from his clones to his true body on a distant volcanic peak! His shoulders bent!","The three singularities in his depths flared as his PONDUS was pressed to its edges for the first time since crossing, and the question of what the Yoke could bear was being answered in the harshest classroom there was!","Could he hold a lifeform the size of an endless sky?","His spine, seated with the Telos of Paradox, held opposing weights without breaking. His shoulders, broad with the Yoke, held the rest!","And the Woe Culture thrashed in shock as its entire body lifted, because it was being CARRIED, hoisted off the domain it had grazed for ages by something a fraction of a fraction of its size, its legs kicking at nothing, its fortune-threads finding no odds to bend against a grip that was not an attack at all!","\" What... what is this?! Put me down, Little One! PUT ME DOWN!\"","\"As you wish,\" Noah said.","And he threw it.","BOOM!","Nine clones pivoted as one as the carried weight swung, and THE True Human Emperor hurled a lifeform countless gigaparsecs wide out of the unseen sky of THE Ymnaros entirely!","The endless purple body tore upward through the layer, through the white rivers, through the skin of the Dimension itself, and was flung countless gigaparsecs out into the dark, tumbling end over end over end, until it crashed to a stop far beyond any sky, in the foamy space between Dimensions!","Black foam churned around its sprawled bulk in slow enormous bubbles, the void between all things frothing where a Dimension’s weight had landed in it, and before the Woe Culture could even right itself, nine folds of crimson gold opened in the dark around it.","The clones had followed.","Nine crowns of blood turned in the foamy black as nine staffs rose, and blood began to gather at every one. Not in drops now. In seas! Millions of Sanguine Blood Drops condensed around each titanic figure as the space between Dimensions filled with crimson gold rain waiting to fall, and below them the Woe Culture gathered its legs beneath it and reached desperately for the white rivers that threaded even here, even through the foam, because the Argent Loom flowed through the spaces between as surely as it flowed through everything!","\" I too shall have to live truly to my nature,\" Noah said quietly, \" as my heart and mind tell me... You must die.\"","BOOM!","The rain fell!","Millions of Blood Drops from each clone tore down through the churning foam as the body of the Woe Culture vanished beneath detonations without number, event horizons blooming across gigaparsecs of stellar purple as plates shattered and clear skin ruptured and violet lights burst in waves!","And it endured!","The Argent Loom poured into it from every direction as white rivers bent out of their courses and flooded its wounds. Loomlight knitted faster than crimson could tear! Lattices of white rose around its many-sided head and DRANK the detonations whole!","And for the first time since his transformation, Noah felt his own power struggle.","His blood detonated against woven loomlight, and the loomlight refused to be commanded, refused to be corrupted, refused even to properly break. He had felled a vessel of THE Sealed One with two drops. He had cleared armies with one. And this relatively harmless thing, this grazer, wrapped in the Loom, was costing him millions! The comparison told him everything about what flowed through those white rivers.","So Noah stopped holding back the only thing he had that it did not.","He filled his Provenance Essence into his blood completely!","All three singularities poured themselves through the connection to his clones as every remaining drop in the foamy dark ignited from within, stellar blue blazing up through crimson gold, blood that was no longer merely his resource but his very light given liquid form!","And when the next wave of drops fell, they did not detonate against the loomlight walls.","They passed through them.","Because the Loom was an authority, and grand beyond measure, but it was still a thing that flowed OUTSIDE of lifeforms, a river to be used! And his blood now carried the one thing in all of existence that answered to nothing outside itself. He had Provenance. This creature did not. That was the entire difference, and today, it was the entire battle!","The white lattices parted around his burning drops as loomlight slid off stellar blue without purchase, and the detonations landed on flesh that could no longer knit itself closed, and gorges became canyons became severings as the endless body of the Woe Culture came apart across the foam!","And it cried out.","The sound rolled through the space between Dimensions, mournful and vast and utterly without anger, the grief-drinker grieving at last on its own behalf as its violet lights guttered out along thousands of Gigaparsecs.","\" How could you end me... for simply living by my nature? I curse you... I curse you...!\"","...!","Its body burst.","Countless light years of stellar purple, gigaparsecs of plates and legs and clear glowing skin, ruptured outward in slow silence and dissolved, breaking down into indicernable motes of violet that scattered across the black foam and thinned and went dark.","The nine clones of THE True Human Emperor floated amid the dissolution and gazed upon it, crowns of blood turning, saying nothing, as the largest lifeform Noah had ever killed stopped existing in the space between Dimensions, far from any sky it could ever graze again.","And Noah, through nine sets of senses at once, probed the dying words.","I curse you. Had that been a wail, or a working? He swept his sight across his clones, across his blood, across the connection running back to his body on a volcanic peak, hunting for any thread of violet that had latched where it should not have. He found nothing.","Which meant nothing had landed, or that whatever had landed was not a thing his senses knew how to find yet.","HUUM!","|The Woe Culture has been granted its death. Its nature has ended with it: the probability-tendrils woven across THE Golden Expanse and its surrounding regions have unraveled. The adversity it farmed will no longer be called. Your Provenance Essence has increased in concentration. Your PONDUS has increased. PONDUS: 12.|","|A separate matter, Master.|","|Due to settings enacted by THE Infiniverse, THE Tide That Owes Nothing has been quietly generating and preserving potential boons for all things you have given, for a while now. Leadership given to a domain. Protection given to millions. Marks given to the marked. Affirmation given to the grieving. The ledger has been kept, and none of it has yet been answered.|","|With the granting of death to a unique lifeform, the Tide has reached an unprecedented generation.|","|Shall the generation and preservation continue?|","...!"]},{"number":5591,"title":"Chapter 5591: Chapter 5590: Wrong Place, Wrong Time!","paragraphs":["<THE Sealed One>","Deep within THE Infinite Carcosa, a temple rose out of a sea of golden mist.","It was built of white stone in tiers upon tiers, each tier wide enough to hold a city, and across its endless steps and colonnades, True Lifeforms moved about in the plain robes of priests! Hundreds of them!","Beings whose presense would have flattened Observable Existences walked in silent lines carrying censers and sealed urns, tending rows of caged radiances that pulsed behind lattice screens, and every one of them moved with bowed heads, because the master of this temple had been old before their Ages had names.","At the very top of the temple, on a wide platform open to the golden mist, a humanoid Primeval One sat on a plain stone seat.","He wore the shape of a broad old man with skin the color of river clay, hairless, heavy-shouldered, dressed in a single white cloth, and his eyes held the slow patience of something that had watched harvests of entire Ages come and go.","This was one of the old harvesters. One of those who had stood behind the Gilded Lifeforms across the Ages as they reaped First Causes from the young and the dying, gathering the yield into temples exactly of this kind.","And onto the platform before him, without sound or ceremony, a figure appeared.","A tall pale man in layered dark robes, lean and unhurried, looking around calmly at the tiers and the priests and the caged lights with the mild interest of a buyer in a familiar market.","THE Sealed One had arrived.","The Primeval One smiled slowly.","\" Now what ,\" he said, \" would bring a vile thing like you to my steps?\"","\"Is that any way to greet an old customer?\" The vessel of THE Sealed One clasped its hands behind its back. \"I bought from this temple when it had four tiers. I remember when your priests were seven frightened Gilded children.\"","\" And I remember what you paid with .\" The old man’s smile did not move. \" Which is why I ask what brings you, instead of asking you to leave. Speak your business.\"","The Sealed One drifted a step along the platform, gaze trailing across the caged radiances below.","\"I came to make things easy on myself.\" The pale man turned, and his voice settled into the tone of a man laying goods on a table.","\"I have too many avenues where I must place my focus. Too many boards, too many pieces, and recently, a new expense I did not plan for. So I have come to hand you an opportunity, and let your nature do my work. Consider it a gift between old friends.\"","\" You have never given a gift in your existence.\"","\"And you have never refused one. Listen.\" The vessel raised one finger.","\" A Remnant Existential Treasure has surfaced. Not a rumor. Not a fragment. A true Remnant, whole, worn openly. It sits in THE Ymnaros Dimension, in the hands of a lifeform that is just now growing into its power. Young. Unguarded. Unclaimed by any faction you would have to answer to .\" He smiled thinly.","\"I wanted to use you as a sharp sword, harvester, because my hands are full, and because I want this enemy of mine to suffer. Noah Osmont, in THE Ymnaros Dimension... holds a Remnant Existential Treasure.\"","...!","The words settled over the platform, and below, several priests paused mid-step.","A Remnant Existential Treasure! The kind of prize that emptied temples and started wars between Primeval Ones, offered up freely with a name and an address attached!","The old man looked at the pale vessel for a long moment.","And then the Primeval One smiled wider than he had smiled all Age.","\" It is a good plot that you had ,\" he said warmly. \" It truly is. It is just a shame... that you came here at the wrong, wrong time.\"","The moment the words finished, the air above the platform moved.","Unseen white authority descended!","THE Argent Loom, rivers of it, bent down out of the golden mist where no eye had marked them and wrapped around the body of THE Sealed One’s vessel in silent coils, and before the pale man could so much as flinch, someone appeared behind him.","A hand reached past his shoulder.","And a collar closed around his neck!","CLICK!","The change was instsntly and total. The waves of Intent that forever rolled off the vessel of THE Sealed One faded away! His Infinity, silent and compounding beneath every body he had ever worn, went dark! The deep patient weight of the Primordial Source drained out of his frame like water out of an unstoppered basin, and what remained standing on the platform, in layered dark robes, was a body that read to every sense in existence as a normal human with absolutely no authority at all.","The vessel’s hands rose slowly to his own neck.","The collar was a seamless band of pale gray metal, cool and light, without lock or hinge or joint, and across its surface, thread-fine lines of white ran in woven patterns, loomlight hardened into a shape. It did not burn him. It did not bind his limbs. It simply sat there, quiet as a closed door, and on its far side sat everything he had ever been.","He looked down at it with a heavy, heavy gaze.","\" Hm. I did not expect to bag one of the vessels of THE Sealed One here.\"","The voice came from behind him, and he turned.","A woman stood on the platform. She was tall, dressed in simple pale garments without ornament, dark hair bound back plainly, and she was terrifying for one reason above all others: she emanated nothing.","Not a glimmer of authority. Not a thread of Intent, not a breath of any Source, not one single register on any instrument his stripped senses had ever owned. There was only THE Argent Loom, flowing around her in slow white rivers, orbiting her frame the way rivers orbit nothing else in existence, and her pale eyes studied him with unhurried interest.","\" This particular body of yours should have low dimensionality ,\" she said, walking a slow circle around him. \" It shouldn’t have sensed anything. And it should be cut off entirely from your main ones. No records out. No memories back. You build your vessels carefully, I will grant you that.\"","She stopped in front of him, and tilted her head. \" But we can still torture you, to obtain information. Hmm.\"","She turned from him, crossed the platform, and did something that struck the stripped vessel harder than the collar had.","She walked to the Primeval One, and stroked the top of his ancient head.","The old harvester, a being who had stood behind the reaping of Ages, sat perfectly still under her hand, eyes lowered, and around his own thick neck, half-hidden by the white cloth, a band of pale gray metal caught the light!","\" The age of lifeforms utilizing and abusing authority is coming to an end ,\" the woman said, her hand resting on the Primeval One’s head as she looked out over the temple tiers.","\" Intents. Sources. Infinities. Causes. For long enough, existence has bent and bled beneath beings who were handed power by frameworks and used it as they pleased. That ends now. You have simply joined the many of you that we will round up, and shackle, and make incapable of utilizing any ounce of authority... to finally bring stability across existence.\" She smiled, small and cold.","\" Rejoice, oh Sealed One. For you will join many others.\"","And as she said it, the golden mist around the temple flashed with white!","Rivers of THE Argent Loom lit up across the whole horizon as veils that had hung there unseen came down, and metallic structures were revealed on every side!","Cubical prisons of dull gray metal, stacked upon each other in columns and walls and mountains of cells, rising out of the mist tier upon tier upon tier!","The vessel of THE Sealed One squinted through eyes that were merely human now.","And inside the cells, he saw them.","Thousands upon thousands of lifeforms! Infinite Lifeforms and Gilded Lifeforms with their silent seas gone dark! Source Lifeforms, dense and patient no longer! Even ancient True Lifeforms, beings whose names held weight across THE Infinite Carcosa, sitting in chained collars in bare metal cells, and not one of them emanated any authority at all, and their eyes, every pair of eyes down every corridor of stacked cells, showed the same three things.","Despair. Horror. Fear!","\"A new age is coming... a new age is coming, as many wrongs will be corrected.\"","The voice of that terrifying woman echoed out across the golden mist, calm and certain, and the vessel of THE Sealed One stood collared at the top of the temple and looked out at the true scale of the place he had walked into, because the stacked cubical prisons did not end at the horizon.","They continued past it, wall after mountain after wall of caged authority, stretching out around this entire place for gigaparsecs in every direction!","The golden mist rolled against the temple tiers, and against the walls of stacked cells beyond them, and at the top of it all, the two captors spoke over their prize.","\" You heard his offering, Ohmran .\" The woman stood at the platform’s edge with the white rivers turning slowly around her.","\"A Remnant Existential Treasure. Worn openly, in THE Ymnaros, by a lifeform still growing into its power.\"","\"I heard it, Warden Yrsa.\" The old clay-skinned Primeval One rose from his stone seat, and standing, he was half again the height of a titan, thick and slow and heavy-footed, the pale gray band glinting at his throat beneath the white cloth.","Yrsa turned from the mist, and the vessel of THE Sealed One, collared and stripped and merely human, watched her plain face as she thought.","\"A Remnant cannot be left in random hands. So...\" She looked up at the towering old one.","\"Check this out, Ohmran. Go to THE Ymnaros. Verify the treasure and the holder. Observe. Touch nothing that is not confirmed, and engage nothing that is. You carry my leash and my patience, and only one of them is long.\"","The Primeval One bowed his heavy head.","\" As the Warden says.\"","He stepped off the platform, and the golden mist swallowed a being who had stood behind the reaping of Ages, sent now as an errand-runner with a collar under his cloth, and the vessel of THE Sealed One watched it happen.","Then Yrsa turned to him.","\" Now ,\" she said. \" You.\"","She crossed the platform without hurry, and took his right hand in both of hers, almost gently, the way one takes the hand of an elder at a bedside.","And she broke it.","CRACK!","The sound rolled across the platform as bones that were merely human bones gave way in her grip, and the vessel of THE Sealed One made a noise he had not made in Ages, because there was no Intent to seal the pain away, no Infinity to compound beneath it, no Source to drink it down! There was only a hand, and a broken hand hurt!","\" Interesting ,\" Yrsa said, watching his face with mild attention. \" You feel it fully. Your main bodies truly receive nothing from this one. That is fine workmanship.\"","She let the ruined hand drop, and took the left.","\"Let us speak of THE Dimensionlapses.\"","CRACK!","\" The collapsing of Dimensions into one another. The fusings. The falls. Whole skies folding into other skies while their lifeforms drown between.\" Her voice never rose, never quickened.","\"It has accelerated this Age, and the pattern is not natural...\"","CRACK!","\" So .\" She looked up at him from below, pale eyes patient, hands already moving to the last unbroken limb. \" What do you know regarding THE Dimensionlapses? Is it just you behind them... or are there others?\"","...!","The Sealed One had a heavy gaze as he did everything he could not to scream in pain, and he forced himself to utter out...","\" Do you know who you are making an enemy of? I am-\"","CRACK!","Another limb was broken as the woman before him looked down coldly.","\"I don’t give a damn who you are, O Riven. O Sealed One. I will throw you in a prison to bleed out and die soon enough as before that, you will answer my questions. Oh, you are fully...a lifeform with no power by the way, so my end move is a simple one of extracting your memories. But sadly...many records are kept with a mixture of authorities as I will fry your brain and kill you when I do and gain a few tidbits. So before that, I like for you to talk freely. So...talk.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5592,"title":"Chapter 5592: Chapter 5591: What Reigns Supreme?","paragraphs":["<THE Sealed One>","Talk.","The word hung in the golden mist as the vessel of THE Sealed One stood on four broken foundations, blood running freely down his wrists and pooling in his shoes, and instead of answering her, he lifted his merely human eyes and gazed up at the prisons.","They went on and on. Wall after mountain after wall of stacked gray cells, and in every cell, a face! An Infinite Lifeform staring at nothing as its silent seas stayed dark. A Gilded one with its brilliance snuffed, hugging its own knees. Source Lifeforms pressed against metal, ancient True Lifeforms sitting perfectly still in the way of beings who had run out of things to try, and down every corridor, in every direction, for gigaparsecs, those same three tenants living in every pair of eyes.","Despair. Horror. Fear!","\"I will talk ,\" the vessel said, and even bleeding, his voice found its old evenness. \" Let us talk about you. Are you among the hypocrites, Warden? The ones who think they are doing something good?\"","Yrsa said nothing, and he took the silence as a stage.","\" There are a number of beings like me who move above the many. We sit behind thrones and beneath foundations, and we use authority and power to do our own bidding across Ages. I am guilty of everything you suspect and a great deal you lack the imagination for. If you shackled me, and told me you were banning the usage of authority for things like me who abuse it... that, I would understand. I would even call it overdue.\"","His broken hand rose an inch, gesturing at the horizon of cells. \" But look at all of these innocent ones. Look at them! What did the millions, the billions of Infinite Lifeforms and Gilded ones and Source Lifeforms DO with their authority to deserve being chained like this? They grew as their natures grew them. They climbed the only ladders existence offered. And your answer to my crimes... is their cages.\"","And Warden Yrsa laughed at this time!","It was a real laugh, short and genuinely amused as she knew THE Sealed One didn’t give a damn about innocents and just wanted to waste time!","\" Who are you ,\" she said, \" to even discuss morality? To sort which ones are innocent and which ones are not? The single greatest argument for my work is standing in front of me .\" She walked a slow half-circle around him.","\" But fine. Let us grant your point fully. Let us say the vast majority of them are innocent. Truly innocent. Do you know what they are then?\"","She stopped, and looked up at the cells.","\" They are you, earlier. You rose from beings just like them. You were once a tiny little lifeform, climbing the only ladders existence offered, growing as your nature grew you. And yet look at what you grew up to be. Every horror above starts as an innocent below, and existence has run that experiment for eons and drowned in the results every single time. So no, I do not chain them for what they did. I chain them for what the ladder makes. \"","Her voice settled into something vast and level. \" At this moment in time, we have begun the process. Binding, chaining, and removing authority across many Observable Existences and Dimensions, across THE Source Lands, across THE Infinite Carcosa. And when the bindings are done, every single one of them will be transferred to live peacefully across different regions of existence, in places where the abuse of authority cannot harm any other life.\"","\"They can build their civilizations with their own hands. They can farm, and craft, and argue, and grow old. And if any of them ever wishes harm, they can, at most, harm themselves or a specific few. Never again will a single existence hold such an abuse of authority that it can affect the lives of countless others.\"","The vessel of THE Sealed One looked at her through the pain, bleeding from four broken limbs, and smiled.","\" And look at you ,\" he said softly. \"A single existence, deciding the fate of countless all around you, right now.\"","For one moment, the white rivers around her slowed.","Then Yrsa waved her hand, unbothered.","\"I do not care for philosophy. I care for informstion. So we return to my questions, and you will notice that I have been patient.\" She crouched before him again.","\" THE Dimensionlapses. The fusings accelerate this Age, and Dimensions do not fold into each other on their own schedule. Who benefits from skies drowning in skies? What is being consolidated? Speak.\"","\" Mm. And here is my question.\" Blood was running from the corner of his mouth now, but the old pleasantness never left his voice. \" What does a thing like you belong to? You wear no authority. You hate authority and yet use it. You collar Primevals and quote a coming age. So whose dog are you, Warden? A dog of Those Who Remain, sent to clean the board for its owners? Or something rarer... a dog of those who look down upon authority itself? \"","His breath rattled, and his smile widened through it. \"Or are you a dog of THE First Lifeforms?\"","\"The conflicts between True Lifeforms and the Primeval Ones. \" Yrsa continued as if he had not spoken at all. \" Three Ages of cold war warming. Someone has been feeding both sides of that fire. Was it you? Name your partners.\"","\" You did not answer my question.\"","\"Name the other hands behind THE Dimensionlapses.\"","\"You did not answer my question. \" A wet laugh. \" Which means the answer of who you belong to is...interesting. Merely a dog. Oh, a bitch, merely a bitch...that is all you are.\"","CRACK!","She broke a rib almost absently, and he folded around it, and still nothing came out of him but blood! Question after question, minutes of them, the fusings, the wars, his vessels, his allies, and the vessel of THE Sealed One deflected and asked and smiled and bled, growing paler by the exchange, his voice thinning as the pool beneath him spread, an ancient monster spending the last of a borrowed body on the only currency he had left.","Silence.","At last, Yrsa rose, and shook her head.","\"I did not want to do it this way. Extraction through a fried brain wastes almost everything.\" She looked down at him.","\" So. Memory extraction is the way to go. Any last words, as this vessel of yours is about to lose its life?\"","The dying vessel lifted his head.","And he smiled with red teeth.","\" Death... smiles at everyone, \" said THE Sealed One. \"I smile back at it.\"","BOOM!","Yrsa waved her hands.","Brilliant white authority flowed down out of the rivers and into the head of the vessel as his entire body began to seize, limbs hammering the platform, blood misting from his nose and ears, and through the seizure, through the frying of everything he was, his voice came out one last time, wet and shaking and utterly unafraid!","\" Wait for me. Just wait for me... and I will show you how vast this existence is. I have been living across dimensions and time. My vessels are many. My connections are abundant. Just you... wait for me.\"","BOOM!","His body bled out of every orifice at once, and in the next moment, his head burst!","—","<Warden Yrsa>","Yrsa frowned unpleasantly at the mess.","She waved her hand, and the ruined vessel of THE Sealed One turned to a drift of pale ash that the golden mist carried off the platform. What remained was the collar, and she caught it out of the air and held it, looking at the woven white lines in silence, reading what the extraction had pulled through them.","Then she shook her head with slow frustration.","\" Barely any salvageable memories come out of this... haa!\"","While she was expressing it, the rivers of THE Argent Loom around the platform slowed.","A handsome young man appeared out of the white, tall and clean-featured, and around his body circled halos of white light, ring after slow ring, orbiting him from shoulders to heels. His gaze was heavy as it settled on her.","\" THE Sealed One is one of the major threats we keep tabs on across dimensions and time ,\" he said. \" Are we certain this one was entirely inhibited? That it did not get the chance to send any information back to its main components?\"","Yrsa smiled slightly at that.","\" Even he does not know that another vessel of his, alongside multiple vile but great minds of existence, inadvertently lent their help in making the design of these Existential Inhibitors possible. No, Axon. Nothing got through.\" She turned the collar once in her hand, and set it down on the empty stone seat.","\"I will finish things up in this region of THE Infinite Carcosa. Can you actually go to THE Ymnaros Dimension, where Ohmran is already heading? Since THE Sealed One was there, and he faced a problem he wanted another to take care of... let us make sure it is not anything too major. And do not make a move unless you are absolutely certain of who is involved. We have begun locking up True Lifeforms, and even Primeval Lifeforms... but we have yet to start our hands on Descendants. We wait for further instructions before we make any moves on our own...\"","\" Understood.\"","...!","The halos brightened, and Axon was gone into the white.","Yrsa stood alone at the top of the temple, and sighed, and looked out across the region. The tiers below her. The priests of a collared master. The mountains of cells running past every horizon, gigaparsecs of caged authority sitting in gray silence, millions of the mighty of existence waiting in small rooms for a peaceful age they had not asked for.","And she whispered to none of them.","\"Existence breathes, and epochs pass, leaving Civilizations that become monuments, then crumble to memory, and are long forgotten when that breath comes again. In all these eons... just what reigns supreme?\""]},{"number":5593,"title":"Chapter 5593: Chapter 5592: All Of Us Are Slaves!","paragraphs":["<THE Creature>","The deepest domain of THE Ghor-VazHAL no longer had a floor.","The lakes of blood had been thrown out of their beds. The tower-arteries lay snapped and draining across miles of churned meat and shattered stone, and the vaulted dark above had been torn open in long strips through which the veins of the deeper structure hung loose and dripping, and through all of it drifted the debris of a battle between two things that did not know how to stop!","On one side of the ruin, THE Creature breathed heavily.","He was carrying unfathomably heavy wounds. His obsidian frame had been opened from shoulder to hip, his body nearly split in half along a diagonal of ruin, held together by weavings of white-gold and black that knitted with terrible slowness, and one arm hung wrong, and his breath came in long dragging pulls, each one a payment he counted out and made!","And on the other end of the ruin lay the Primeval One.","The colossus was torn apart. Whole colonies of Gu Lifeforms had been ripped out of its titan flesh and lay scattered and dead in drifts around it, and its vast stomach had been opened to the dark, its contents spilling out in a slow tide, and from that tide, the remnants of its remaining weavings of existence rose constantly into the air, thread after glimmering thread, the substance of an ancient life leaking out with nowhere left to be kept.","It was dying. It knew it was dying. And so, in the way of old things, it talked!","\" Why .\" The voice came out of the ruined titan wet and heavy. \" Of all the vileness in existence... why did you come here, to kill me? There are things out there that unmake whole Dimensions for the taste of it. There are things that wear bodies the way you wear wounds. There are sentences walking around with bloodlines, little bearer, and hungers older than me. So much wrong. So much vile. And you spent your time... on me.\"","THE Creature looked at it across the ruin, and did not move yet!","\" You were simply the weight in front of me ,\" he said.","The Primeval One laughed wetly at that, and more of its weavings tore loose with the laughing.","\" Do you even know what I built here? The Farms fed things you have never stood close enough to smell. I raised crops of lifeforms across whole Ages, kept them fat, kept them breeding, and the harvest was never even mi...\" It stopped itself, slow and deliberate, and its murky obsidian eyes glinted. \" Ah, it doesn’t even matter. But I built immensity!\"","THE Creature’s voice stayed flat . \"I know what you built. I walked through it for an hour. Vein-tunnels full of vileness\"","\"I built what I needed to LIVE!\" The titan’s ruined bulk heaved. \" You do not know what was done to me! What I was before, what was taken, what I crawled up from! When everything is taken from a thing, the thing takes! That is the oldest law there is!\"","And here, THE Creature rose slightly on his ruined frame, and his voice came down with a tyrannical weight that made the leaking threads of the dying Primeval shiver in the air!","\" Regardless of what happened to you... you did not have to resort to draining the lives of countless others. Existence is vast. It is so vast, and it is filled with so many means, so many roads, so many ways for a wronged thing to rise. And out of all of them, it only means one thing that you chose this one. You took the easy route.\" His breath dragged, and he continued through it.","\" Your kind of existence, the ones who only ever seek the easy ways out... you get nowhere. You sit in your farms and your temples and your hoards, fat and ancient and NOWHERE. Do what is harder! Chase adversity. Bear what others set down. And maybe... maybe you might just stand at the peak of existence, as a Great Ruler.\"","For a moment, the ruin was quiet.","And then the Primeval One laughed!","It was a real laugh, rolling and wet and delighted, blood and weavings spilling out of it together as its existence continued to fade, and it laughed until the laughing tore something further inside it, and it kept laughing anyway!","\" Haha! Is THAT what you are chasing? A Great Ruler? BAHAHA! You dumb motherfucker!\" Its murky eyes fixed on him, bright with dying mirth.","\" You will never get anywhere unless you are suckling at the feet of Those Who Remain, or others like them! There is no peak, there is only a longer table, and every seat at it is bought! You will never be a ruler... as much as you will be a slave. In existence... all of us are slaves...\"","THE Creature rose.","His nearly split body drew itself up out of the ruin, wounds still open, one arm still wrong, and he did not answer the dying thing with words!","THE Pantheon of All Existence unfurled!","It had no shape, and it needed none, because it simply became the surroundings! The torn domain, the snapped arteries, the drifts of dead Gu, the vaulted broken dark, all of it turned in a single breath into HIM, and the Primeval One’s fading eyes widened as it understood, far too late, that it was no longer lying in a battlefield.","It was lying inside its bearer.","And the surroundings constricted.","The whole domain drew inward in one slow, total motion, existence folding shut around the torn colossus from every direction at once, and THE Creature devoured the Primeval One completely, flesh and Gu and stomach-tide and every last leaking thread of its ancient weavings, drawing all of it down into the depths of what he was until the laughter thinned, and thinned, and was gone, and nothing of the farmer of THE Ghor-Vazhal remained anywhere in existence at all!","Silence settled over a domain that was, once more, only a domain.","And in the center of it stood THE Creature.","He stood grandly amid the ruin he had made and survived, split-bodied and unbowed, obsidian frame threaded with slow-knitting white-gold, his presense filling the vaulted dark from wall to broken wall, and he let it fill, unhurried, the tally of one thousand complete behind him and the weight of a Primeval One settling into his depths!","Then he turned his head slightly, toward the place where he carried what he carried.","\" Give me my damn rewards.\"","...!","And the statue smiled brutally.","He felt it before he saw it, the wide slow satisfaction spreading across a blank stone face, and then, for the first time in all the time he had borne it, the statue MOVED for him!","The seated colossus raised its worn gray hands, and placed them upon its own chest.","And invisible rivers of white authority began to flow!","They came down out of nowhere that any sense could name, silent and vast, pouring into the stone figure from every direction at once, gathering in its chest beneath its layered hands, and then they turned, and began flowing with immensity into the body of THE Creature, white beyond white, old beyond old, flooding into his split frame and his ruined arm and the depths where a Primeval One was still settling...!","The white rivers poured gloriously.","They poured through the hands of the statue and into the split body of THE Creature in endless silent volumes, an authority he had not even known existed before this moment, and it was remaking the weavings of what he was! His torn frame drank it and knitted at a pace his own weavings had never managed. His Intent was being fortified in an unfathomable manner, its claim reinforced along every thread as though each thread were being rewoven with a second, whiter strand beneath it!","And his Pantheon, the shapeless entirety of him that became its surroundings, grew heavier and steadier and MORE, the way ground grows more when bedrock is poured beneath it!","What was this authority? Where had it flowed from, all this time, that Existence itself had never once felt it pass?","He asked nothing aloud. He drank, and endured, and counted.","And the statue spoke.","|I knew you could overcome even this adversity.|","A pause, wide and pleased.","| Do you want to listen to a story, O Creature?|","THE Creature remained silent.","He knew this thing by now. It had not asked a question. It had announced an intention, dressed politely, and whether he answered or not, the statue would continue talking. This thing loved talking.","He felt the statue smile devilishly across its blank stone face, its worn hands still layered on its chest, still gathering the brilliant white rivers and channeling them down into his body, and it began to talk.","|An unknown number of Ages ago, there was a lifeform.|","|It had a unique origin, and nothing in it was given, for it arose in the manner of the earliest things. It walked among the young kinds of existence, and it did a strange thing with its endless span. It carried for them.|","|Wherever it walked, it took up what was crushing others. The grief of the bereaved. The ruin of the broken. The adversity that falls on the small without ever asking their leave. It took these things up onto itself, and bore them, and the lands around its walking grew stable, and calm, and kind, and civilizations rose in the shadow of its bearing the way grass rises in the shadow of a mountain. The young kinds had a thousand names for it, and every name meant the same thing. The one who stood between.|","The rivers poured on. THE Creature listened.","|Now. In that same span of Ages, there were also the speakers.|","|You know them. Those Who Remain. They did not carry, and they did not walk. They spoke, and their sentances settled over existence like weather, arranging what would be, binding what would serve, and existence bent itself around their words because that was the order of things, and order held.|","| And there came a day when one of the speakers prepared a great sentence. They had a fascination of Mounts, you see. Durable ones. Bred ones. A young kind would be taken, and Causes would be seated into their living by the speakers’ own hands, and that kind would carry burdens across existence forever because it would be spoken so.|","...!","THE Creature’s eyes opened slightly in the flowing white.","Bearers? Causes? It was talking about the Steeds in THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension?","| And the lifeform who carried, who had never once in all its span opposed anything, walked to the place of one of Those Who Remain, and stood between, one last time. It said the Mounts should choose their burdens, as all bearers must, or the bearing would rot into suffering. It said this plainly, and without armies, believing, in the way of things that are good, that being right would be enough.|","Who...was the lifeform? What was it called. What happened at the place of speaking?","THE Creature felt the invitation hang in the white-flooded dark to ask, and he refused it as he felt the stone face’s smile deepen.","|It did not win.|","| Those Who Remain do not move, O Creature. You know this. They did not move then, either. And that lifeform died all the same, and the manner of its death is not part of tonight’s story. The sentence was spoken. The Mount was seated, and bred, and burdened, and you have met what their line became. And the lands that had grown calm in the lifeform’s shadow fell back into the weather of the speakers’ words, and the lifeform’s thousand names were forgotten by everyone who had shouted them. And that lifeform who had helped so many...was forgotten by even those it helped.|","|I tell you this because...Just because one wants to do good does not mean one will win. Existence does not favor good, and it does not favor evil. Existence favors stability. Those who spread misery and pain and instability across it may find adversity stacking against them, higher and harder than against others, this is true, and it is why the farmer you just devoured spent his last Age dying in a hole. But one who stands against the order of things, however good the standing... creates instability too. And existence weighed the one who stood between, and the speakers who held the order, and it chose the order. It may choose so again.|","The hands pressed deeper into the stone chest, and the rivers of white surged.","| You have won now. Your tally is paid, and your reward flows, and a Primeval One sits in your depths. But...your next weight will not be a single vile Primeval Lifeform, half-dead in a farm of its own filth. It will be an entire group of them. Very much alive and not already dying. Fat with Ages and fond of the order exactly as it stands.|","|So. Will you continue to try and balance the scales?|","The white rivers rose through THE Creature as the question settled, flooding up through his knitted chest, up through his fortified Intent, up into his skull, and when he lifted his gaze to the dark, his eyes had begun to fill with swirling rivers of white, the unknown authority turning slowly through them in currents that did not belong to any framework he had ever been offered!","And his answer came out cold.","\" Whether one or many does not matter. What needs to fall before me... will fall before me.\"","...!","He was confident.","Existence... had to be confident!"]},{"number":5594,"title":"Chapter 5594: Chapter 5593: Salvation! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","|Shall the generation and preservation continue?|","Noah looked at the waiting prompt for a long moment, and gave his answer simply.","\" Continue it. For now.\"","HUUM!","The Tide’s ledger settled back into its quiet keeping, unprecedented and unopened, one more sealed door he would walk through when he chose to, and across the foamy dark between Dimensions, his nine clones drew together above the scattered violet motes of a dead Woe Culture.","And Noah thought about many things.","About the things that could not be perceived, and about his own power. How many more things like the Woe Culture were out there, hanging in unseen layers above unsuspecting skies? And what would happen if he met one that was too powerful for the current him? Because the only reason he had dominated the Woe Culture, even though its attributes were higher than his, was Provenance Essence. But what if the attributes were not a single digit higher? What if they were significantly higher?","He had to get a better grasp of his new power!","Much of what he now carried had been regained from what he cast out. His nine old Causes had returned as nine Teloi, reborn in his organs as aims instead of origins. His oldest Appendages had returned rebuilt from their preserved backbones. Even Mana had returned, remade as his blood. Piece by piece, the old ocean was being answered by things that were wholly his!","But the best way forward, the continued elevation of his power, ran through the thing that made a First Lifeform unique. What he generated. Provenance Essence! Three singularities of it now swirled within him, and they were the reason his power was immense at all.","And if they were the core of his power at this moment... then he had to think about how to better utilize this Generated Resource. So far, every Art he had made used a semblance of its power, but moreso through his blood. Perhaps he needed to try designing something focused around Provenance Essence itself!","While he was thinking all of this... his gaze suddenly changed.","His clones sensed something approaching!","And it approached rapidly, tearing through the foamy dark at a pace that made distance meaningless, and by the time he had sensed it, it was already there!","A throne-saddle, riding the black.","A single chained Steed beneath it, flanks heaving.","And upon it, rot ticking along the fissures of his frame, obsidian mark faint upon his brow, sat Jarl Skallagrim!","HUUM!","The Cursed Descendant’s eyes shone brightly as they swept across the nine titanic clones, and his voice came out through the dark with madness and wonder held in the same breath.","\"I...thought I sensed something. A war, ringing through the crossing-dark. So I turned my little steed toward the ringing, and... \" His shining eyes fixed on the clone at the center. \"It is... you, right?\"","\"...\"","\" The same face. Even if your existence does not give off waves of authority anymore. Even if you read as nothing at all.\" A slow, crooked smile spread. \"I am... immensely happy to have found you once more, you whose name I never learned. Is the other part of you, thay woman, within THE Ymnaros Dimension? That is the only one close by...\"","...!","Noah’s eyes burned luminously as his nine clones lined up across the dark, crowns of blood turning!","A Cursed Descendant of THE Sleepless Fiend!","The lucid madman who had bound Hvitrmarr across a thousand years of patience, standing at speaking distance, PERCEIVING him!","\" Did my existence...make you so desperate that you left your Dimension?\"","The Jarl’s smile flickered.","\"I have been obtaining information from Hvitrmarr,\" Noah continued, his voice level. \" She says all of you are tied down there for a chance of salvation. That leaving is the one thing a Cursed Descendants and Steeds do not do.\"","\"... She said that, did she?\"","\"So what are you now? A Descendant of Those Who Remain who is damned, with no salvation at all? What exactly were you hoping to find by coming here?\"","He was asking, and beneath the asking, he was working! Because this being should not have been able to see him. His battle with the Woe Culture had rung out across the dark, fine.","But Skallagrim was looking AT him. Perceiving him directly, and that could only mean one thing about the being on that throne!","Jarl Skallagrim frowned, and the madness and the lucidity moved across his face together, neither one winning.","\" Salvation.\"","He said the word the way other beings said the names of their dead.","\"I have... very little time. Less than the little I had when you saw me last. So I took salvation into my own hands, yes. I left.\"","His fists tightened on the chains.","\" And now, now things are changing. Our great Father is now interested in you. The silence of my whole life, broken, over you.\"","The frown deepened into something pained.","\" Why... could you not have remained within THE Krazhor-Nul? We could have all had our salvation there... just like you cured Hvitrmarr, I could have had my salvation there. There would be no interest from Father... there would be none of this. Why... why...?!\"","HUUM!","The Jarl seemed mad and pained at once, and Noah’s eyes became heavy!","Father!","Noah pressed, prying at the seam. \" Did you not lose any chance of salvation when you left your home Dimension? What has changed now?\"","And at this time, he was finally able to see the details of the power of this being!","|STATUS PANEL: JARL SKALLAGRIM- CURSED DESCENDANT OF THE SLEEPLESS FIEND|","|VERITAS: 19|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 15|","|PONDUS: 10|","|Note: a unique power that only Descendants hold circles this existence. It has not currently been quantified.|","Noah analyzed these details with shining eyes!","Nineteen! A VERITAS of nineteen, nearly double his own eleven, sitting on a rotting madman in the dark between Dimensions! The Woe Culture’s twelve had already stood above him, and this was seven past that!","Was this what a sentence with a bloodline measured as, a being spoken into existence with its nature written before its birth, true to itself because it had never been given a self to betray?","And the PONDUS of ten beside his VERITAS explained the perceiving in full, both values standing at the threshold of his own law! But fifteen POTENTIA on a dying man? And what was the unquantified power that circled him?","Questions stacked on questions!","Jarl Skallagrim’s gaze had gone distant.","\" Salvation may be further away from me now than it ever was before,\" the Jarl said quietly. \"I know what I am. I know what leaving cost. But with death so near... I make my own salvation.\"","His shining eyes came back to the clones, and sharpened.","\" So...from you, I want the cure. I want this abominable curse lifted, the way you lifted hers.\"","\" And if I refuse?\"","\"I would rather you not. Force is possibe. And...our great Father already seeks information about you. A bounty of information has gone out to us. \" The Jarl’s voice did not rise at all, and that made it heavier.","\" So if I do not get my salvation from you... then I will take the risk, and I will give what information I can about you. And my brethren, the Progenies of THE Sleepless Fiend, will swarm you, and hunt you, and hunt the Living Observable Existence behind you, until you are caught and kept in a cage like all of us.\"","\"...\"","Then, without any change in tone at all, the madman added.","\" Do you need the Living Observable Existence here for the cure, by the way? Because we can make our way to THE Ymnaros Dimension, if so...\"","...!","Heavy words came out of the Jarl, threat and arrangements in the same breath, and Noah’s clones remained steady across the dark.","A dying Cursed Descendant, who only wanted salvation.","How could he play this? Battle against this being was ill advised. But what if he actually cured him? He had cured a Steed before, and never a Descendant!","And if he put his hands on a Descendant... Ulf had already said how he drew interest from those terrifying beings by reversing two of their actions. Hvitrmarr. And Ulf. The more he became embroiled with Steeds and Descendants, the deeper he would be drawn into this web!","But a dying lifeform stood before him, wanting salvation.","And he... he could potentially give it without a fight!","The only caveat was the worry of the attention of One of Those Who Remain!"]},{"number":5595,"title":"Chapter 5595: Chapter 5594: Salvation! II","paragraphs":["How deeply should he worry about Those Who Remain?","Noah turned the question over once. To fear was human.","He had learned that lesson again! Fear was a map that he simply needed to navigate as on the other side of fear...was boundless glory!","He was afraid, correctly. And he would still move! That had always been the immensity of being human, feeling everything, and going forward anyway!","And beneath the fear sat something warmer and greedier, because a Descendant of Those Who Remain stood at speaking distance offering open access to his own existence, and Noah was so, so curious about what such a being held within!","The foamy dark had gone very quiet. Nine clones hung in a loose ring around the throne-saddle, and the last Steed stood trembling beneath its Jarl with its head lowered, and the silence stretched until it had a weight of its own.","Then Noah spoke.","\"I can cure you.\"","The Jarl’s eyes pulsed audibly in the dark as this...was all it wanted! It wanted to be cured! It wanted to live...no matter what.","\" But I’ll need access to your existence,\" Noah continued. \" All of it. Opened to me, unresisting. Nothing between my work...and what you are.\"","Skallagrim stared at him across the dark for a long moment.","\" Do you know what it is ,\" he said quietly, \" to spend a thousand years planning the possibility of a single cure?\"","\"....\" Noah gazed out wordlessly.","\"I built that plan the way other beings build empires. I watched Hvitrmarr. I waited on her. I whipped eight of my own steeds to death crossing the dark after the trail of it.\" His hands opened slowly on the chains.","\" And now I sit at the end of everything, at the end of my life, waiting for that cure. I cannot really say no, can I? But I can watch and observe as if there is any trickery...I have no qualms taking both of us down. You may not know, but I...am immense.\"","HUUM!","\" Do what needs to be done. \" Skallagrim leaned back on his throne-saddle and spread his arms wide, chest bared to the dark, in the oldest gesture there was.","The gesture said...come!","The heaviness of that moment settled over the foamy black! A Cursed Descendant, terror of the Krazhor-Nul, a being wearing a VERITAS of nineteen, sitting open-handed and undefended before the thing he had once hunted, and the ring of clones tightened around him, slow and wide, crowns of blood turning!","Below the throne, the last Steed shifted, and its small voice came up through the chains.","\"J-Jarl... are we truly doing this...?The Great Father asked for information. We cannot go against...!\"","\"Quiet, little steed. \" There was almost gentleness in it. \" We are already done doing everything else as this...will be a salvation I grasp myself. Father has watched us die for Eons. Sometimes, you need to move yourself. \"","Noah raised a hand, and his blood answered.","Drops rose around the clones in their dozens, and then they changed! Each drop drew itself long and thin, crimson gold flowing into edges, stellar blue running down each spine, and where a rain of detonations had once hung above a Woe Culture, there now hung a surgeon’s array of slender crimson blades!","\" Don’t move ,\" Noah said. \" However deep I go. A tremble in the wrong place becomes a grave....\"","The Jarl closed his eyes and said nothing as Noah felt the grand aura of immensity of being this close to a Cursed Descendant!","If he was not burning with Provenance Essence...he may have felt suffocation of royalty and majesty!","But as he was now...he only felt a...lower kind of regality as his regality far exceeded a Descendant.","The blades descended, and began to cut a Cursed Descendant open.","They worked in silence, parting rotted skin and fissured frame in exact lines, folding the Jarl’s chest open to the dark the way Noah had once folded his own, and Skallagrim endured it awake and unflinching, rotten breath dragging through his teeth, and the dark pressed in around the work, and the Steed below did not dare to breathe!","And as Noah’s senses poured into the opened existence, the Jarl surprisingly talked, because dying men at the edge of salvation cannot sit inside a silence that long.","\" While you work... let a dying man ask something.\"","\" Ask what?\"","\" Who... are you? Really.\" His voice came out low and labored. \"I’ve turned you over in my mind since the Krazhor-Nul. I turned you over harder after you almost vanished out of every sense I own, and even here, I could barely perceive you...\"","\"Does it matter who I am?\"","\"It matters .\" The shining eyes cracked open. \" Look at where your hands are, Cure-Giver. You are inside a Descendant of THE Sleepless Fiend, unmaking a working of one of Those Who Remain, while their attention gathers on your name. Nothing weak would do that. Nothing without history behind it would even dream to. So what are you? A Descendant of some other line, raised wild where no one could collar you? Something older?\"","A pause, and quieter: \" What stands behind you... that your hands do not shake while you defile the sentance of one of Those Who Remain?\"","Noah did not look up from the work. \" Nothing stands behind me.\"","\"I am human, and I stand behind everything that is mine.\" His blades turned, and cut deeper!","\"...\"","The Jarl was silent for a long moment after that, opened to the dark, bleeding into the black.","\"A human,\" he repeated at last, softly, and there was no mockery in it at all. \" Existence has a vile sense of humor.\"","WAA!","And what Noah found inside Jarl Skallagrim was unlike anything he had ever opened!","There were... no Causes. He had half-expected the architecture of the Steeds, organs seated with ancient suns, and there was none of it! Where Hvitrmarr’s structure had been anatomy, the inner existence of a Descendant was WRITING!","Through the whole of the Jarl, through frame and weavings and depths, there ran a single unbroken line of script, dense and dark and terribly old, written in an authority Noah could not read, and it did not begin at Skallagrim’s birth!","It ran backward out of him, out of his existence entirely, threading away into distances Noah’s senses could not follow, through father and father and father, one continuous written thing stretching all the way back to the hand that had designed the line and mixed them with many other things!","A sentence with a bloodline . Ulf had mentiomed something close to this!","And here it was, literal, a lineage that was one long sentence written across generations, and Jarl Skallagrim was simply its current clause!","’So this is what a Descendant is...’","And wound through that clause, black and gnawing, was the curse.","It did not sit anywhere. It had no seat to sit in! It was written INTO the line itself, a counter-writing braided through the lineage-script along its whole visible length, annotation upon annotation of ending, and Noah traced the remaining unwritten span of Skallagrim’s clause and felt his expression harden, because the span was short. Months. This being had a matter of months to live!","Months, on such a terrifyingly powerful existence, a VERITAS of nineteen with its conclusion already drafted!","And then Noah saw the third thing, and his eyes narrowed in the dark.","Coiling WITH the curse, braided through the black counter-writing along every length of it, ran rivers of white.","THE Argent Loom!","Thin threads of that stellar white authority, the same rivers that flowed through his Realm and his Dimension and the whole higher weave of nature, wound intimately through the curse of a Descendant, white through black through the written line, and question after question stacked up behind Noah’s eyes!","Why was the Loom braided into a curse of Those Who Remain? Did the speakers work the loomlight when they wrote their sentances? Had the curse captured the rivers, or had the rivers been the ink all along?","The Woe Culture utilized the Argent Loom. And now it coiled inside the oldest curse he had ever opened.","Hvitrmarr had carried her curse in her Causes, and her Causes in her organs, and he had cured her by replacing anatomy. But Skallagrim had no Causes. There was no seat to empty, no organ to regrow, no anchor to starve! The curse was applied directly to who he was. To the written line. To his lineage!","So for Noah to cure him... he would have to reach into the sentence of THE Sleepless Fiend itself, and mess with, and alter, the lineage of a Descendant, fully!"]},{"number":5596,"title":"Chapter 5596: Chapter 5595: Primevals and Descendants!","paragraphs":["Nine clones drew closer around the opened Descendant, crowns of blood turning slowly, and Noah studied the written line running through Jarl Skallagrim with the interest of a man who had just been handed a language older than every framework he had ever broken!","The plan assembled itself as he looked.","He could not read the script of Those Who Remain. Fine!","He did not need to read it. He needed to REPLACE it! Where the curse’s counter-writing braided through the lineage-line, where the Argent Loom coiled white through the black, he would lay down his Blood Marks as anchors, and then, clause by careful clause, he would swap out the bound lengths of an ancient sentence with material of his own. With his Infinite Sanguine Mana. With his own Osmontian Tongue.","With his words!","But which words? THE MORTAL COIL was a Word of endings and mortality, and it belonged in this work, but it was not enough alone. This was a matter of lineage. Of inheritance. Of a line of descent that had been written for its bearers instead of by them, and against that, he needed something new.","So, hands steady in the opened existence of a Cursed Descendant, Noah began to design the second Word of his Tongue.","’ Lineage... and humanity.’","He built it from what he knew to be true. Humans inherited. Blood, faces, tempers, debts.","No human chose the line they were born into, and in that much, humans and Descendants were kin. But there the kinship ended!","Because a human’s inheritance was a beginning, not a verdict. A human took the blood handed down and wrote their own fate with it, and their children would write theirs, and no ancestor’s hand, however old, reached forward to finish anyone’s sentence for them!","A lineage was supposed to be a gift passed forward, not a leash held backward!","The Letters of his Tongue turned around the thought. HUMAN. I AM. And between them, meaning condensed into sound, and sound into a Word, and Noah spoke it silently into his own depths and felt his whole Tongue accept it!","HUUM!","|THE Osmontian Tongue has expanded.|","|A second Word has been designed: THE UNBOUND LINEAGE.|","|Its meaning: a line of descent belongs to those who live it. Every clause of a lineage is written by its own bearer, and no hand behind may finish the sentence of one who breathes. Where this Word settles, inheritance becomes a gift, and ceases to be a verdict.|","|THE MORTAL COIL and THE UNBOUND LINEAGE may be expressed together.|","...!","Noah’s eyes gleamed in the dark, and he went to work!","His blades of blood thinned further, becoming instruments finer than any edge, and through them, he began the infusion. THE MORTAL COIL flowed in first, settling mortality’s honest grammar against a curse that had made mortality a punishment.","Then THE UNBOUND LINEAGE poured after it, wrapping the bound clauses, and behind both came his Blood Marks, laid down one by one along the written line as anchor points, and where curse-writing and Loom-thread coiled together... he began, slowly, to replace them.","And it was like moving mountains with his fingertips!","The first clause resisted him with a heaviness that had nothing to do with mass! He was not lifting a thing, he was contradicting a SENTENCE, prying loose words spoken by one of the oldest hands in existence, and his frame across nine clones strained as though each syllable weighed a Dimension!","His Provenance Essence surged as he commanded all three singularities into the work, stellar blue flooding down his instruments, and all around them, existence itself started to vibrate and shake, the foamy dark trembling in slow waves that spread out from the surgery for light years in every direction!","\" While we are here. \" Noah’s voice stayed level through the strain. \" Tell me about Those Who Remain.\"","\"... Now?\" THE Cursed Descendant’s eyes were somber as he had to ask!","\"Especially now. THE Sleepless Fiend. All of them. If I am gaining their animosity by doing this, I should at least understand who they are.\"","Skallagrim was quiet for a moment, opened to the dark, watching a stranger pry at the oldest thing in his blood.","\" Where would I even begin,\" he murmured. \" They are supposedly the idea of beginnings\"","\" They were ancient when life itself was early. That is the first thing every Progeny is taught, and it is the only thing all of us agree on.\" His voice found the cadence of something recited across a whole lifetime.","\" Before oddities like Vakochev and their Scales. Before the frameworks. When existence was young and thin, they were already old in it. And in that early age...Those Who Remain were known to get together with THE First Lifeforms.\"","Noah’s hands did not pause, but his attention sharpened to a point as he asked...","\" Get together?\"","\" Joining. Meeting. Working. Warring. The word changes depending on which Progeny tells the story.\"","A weak, crooked smile arose from him.","\" And between their joining... we arose. The Descendants. And the Primeval Lifeforms both. Though no one living agrees on how.\"","The Jarl’s breath dragged as another clause came loose inside him.","\" Some say it was experimentation. That Those Who Remain took existence itself and its budding lifeforms and altered them, generation upon generation, and what rose out of those alterations became the Primeval Ones. Some say Those Who Remain copulated with THE First Lifeforms, and that the Descendants are what came of it, bloodlines carrying a drop of each. And others...\"","He laughed, low and rattling. \" Others say all of us are just accidents. Residues from their weavings. Runoff that learned to walk and gave itself titles.\"","\"...\"","Noah thought for a moment as he continued to unravel the Lineage of this being with precision before he asked.","\" Which do you believe?\"","\"I believe I am dying right now, Cure-Giver, \" His shining eyes dimmed slightly.","\" But if I were to continue talking about this...the words themselves tell you something, no? Progenies. Descendants. We are called what we are called because we CAME from them, however it happened. And even among us... there are those of extreme purity and closeness.\"","\"Brethren whose blood runs so near to Fathers and Mothers that speaking to them is like standing in a doorway with something enormous on the other side. And there are those born dull, and far, and thin.\" The crooked smile returned.","\"I can be considered... a middle child, if you are wondering.\"","Noah held every word of it, questions multiplying faster than the work beneath his hands!","\" And the Primeval Ones. What are they to you, then? Cousins?\"","\"Estranged ones. They do not serve, and they are not spoken to, and messages of Those Who Remain have never once mentioned them in all the history of the line. Whatever happened between Those Who Remain and the Primeval Ones... it ended long before I was written.\""]},{"number":5597,"title":"Chapter 5597: Chapter 5596: Defiance! I","paragraphs":["Noah was gaining an overabundance of information while he worked as he continued to pry from this being!","\" THE First Lifeforms. \" Noah kept his voice idle, a man making conversation over delicate work. \" Have any of your line seen one?\"","\"Seen one?\" Skallagrim actually laughed, and paid for it in pain.","\" No Progeny I know has EVER seen one. Not the pure ones, not the old ones, no one. They are gone from every telling after the early age. None know much about them as they are very secretive. \" His voice dropped.","...!","Noah’s hands kept moving, and behind his level expression, the questions stacked into towers! But he pressed no further along that road, because the work beneath his fingers was steepening!","He had passed a quarter of the line. Then a third. Clause after ancient clause pried loose and replaced, THE MORTAL COIL and THE UNBOUND LINEAGE settling into a Descendant’s code in growing crimson-gold lengths, his Blood Marks burning at every anchor, his three singularities pouring themselves out, and existence around them shook harder with every replaced word, the vibrations climbing from tremble to quake!","And progressively, Jarl Skallagrim’s expressions had been becoming pale.","The color drained from his fissured face as the work deepened, his breath shortening, his opened frame flickering with strain, and the moment Noah’s replacement crossed the fiftieth percent of the written line, the Jarl’s whole body began to shake atop his Steed!","\" Whatever you’re doing,\" he forced out through rattling teeth, \" you may want to hurry it up!\"","BOOM!","And at such a point, the surroundings answered!","The foamy dark above them SPLIT with white as a storm of THE Argent Loom began to descend! Rivers upon rivers of stellar white authority poured down out of every direction at once, gathering, twisting, wrathful in a way that no current of it had ever been before, and out of the descending storm, the white began to take shape!","Snakes of Argent Loom, dozens of them, each one vaster than mountains, coiled out of the storm with open jaws of woven light and hurled themselves down at Noah’s clones as if to smite him for his actions!","The snakes came down, and Noah’s blood rose to meet them!","BOOM!","Rushes of Sanguine Blood Drops tore upward from all nine clones in walls of crimson gold, detonating against descending jaws of woven light, and the foamy dark turned into a natural disaster being born!","The storm of THE Argent Loom spread across the whole sky of the between-space, white rivers gathering into thunderheads vaster than Observable Existences, and from those thunderheads, coiling bodies of loomlight rained down with open mouths while Noah’s Infinite Sanguine Mana poured out of him in floods to answer them!","Snake after snake burst apart against detonating crimson! And for every one that burst, the storm above thickened, white swirling into white, the wrath of it pressing down on existence until the dark itself groaned!","And through all of it, Noah kept working, hands deep in a half-rewritten sentence, his voice cutting level through the roar.","\" What about THE Argent Loom? For it to react like this to the change I am implementing...what do you know about it?\"","Skallagrim’s pale face managed something between a grimace and a smile as another volley of drops burst above them.","\"It is...also something very early ,\" he rasped. \" An extremely early authority. From the same age as Them. My line’s teachings say Those Who Remain utilized it before there were frameworks to utilize anything else... but perceiving it, using it, that needs high Dimensionality. Terribly high. Most of existence lives and dies never knowing it is there.\"","\" And those without it... they chase instead the fused authority. \" His breath dragged. \" Infinity, and THE Primordial Source. Woven together into one. That is the only other thing that can match up to the Argent Loom... and it is chased across all of existence, because the fusion does something the pure paths do not.\"","His shining eyes found the clone before him. \" It elevates Dimensionality. You climb it, and you begin to perceive what you could not perceive. Climb far enough... and others stop perceiving you.\"","...!","Noah’s hands nearly paused inside the written line!","Perception, scaling with depth! His own Precept had made him absent from the reality of everyone below a threshold!","\" There are many, many paths across existence . Some Primeval Ones and some of my brethren follow Infinity alone, all the way up. Others follow THE Primordial Source, deep and patient, density into density. Others try the fusing .\"","\"There are many different results from the fusion of Infinity and THE Primordial Source as it depends on the individual, and very few achieve perfect fusion. One being attained a unique fusion ages ago that made his confidence a bit high. Someone known as Riven, in the past.\"","...!","The Sealed One was mentioned casually from the weavings of Jarl Skallagrim as Noah continued while listening closely.","The Jarl coughed. \" And then there are the ones who abandon all of it. The moment they climb high enough to perceive the Argent Loom... they switch to it. Leave their whole path behind like a boat they only needed for the crossing. Because the Argent Loom does not have to be climbed. It is simply THERE, everywhere, waiting for anything deep enough to touch it.\"","Noah nodded at these words as his Osmontian Tongue continued surging, his eyes on the storm above as he asked!","\" Then why does THE Argent Loom rage at this moment?\"","\"...Because of the last thing they say about it.\" Skallagrim’s voice dropped low. \" Some say THE Argent Loom is not just an authority. Some say it is an extension of the thoughts of Those Who Remain themselves. Their musings, threaded through all of nature. \"","His pale face turned up toward the boiling white sky. \" It would explain why... they are turning into a storm right now.\"","..!","The storm answered as if it had heard!","The white thunderheads SPLIT, and swirling pillars of white lightning began to crash down in volleys, each strike carrying enough authority to turn millions of Mesozoic and Cenozoic Scale entities into ash instantly, and there were HUNDREDS of them, battering down in cycles upon cycles as Noah’s clones spread wide and met them with oceans of detonating blood!","And he worked!","Seventy percent! Eighty! His Blood Marks burned along the ancient line as THE MORTAL COIL and THE UNBOUND LINEAGE flooded clause after clause, his three singularities pouring themselves dry into the labor, and sharp, corrosive tendrils of Argent Loom began slipping through the barrage, one raking open a clone’s shoulder, another passing entirely through a second clone’s side and leaving a hissing white wound that his blood strained to close! The strain mounted across all nine bodies!","Ninety percent!","And at ninety percent, Jarl Skallagrim began to SHINE!"]},{"number":5598,"title":"Chapter 5598: Chapter 5597: Defiance! II","paragraphs":["Resplendent crimson gold light bloomed up through his fissures, through his opened chest, through the rot itself, Noah’s blood and Noah’s Osmontian Tongue filling the written line of this being from end to end, and the aura that began radiating off him was extremely unique, ancient sentence and living blood and unbound humanity all braided into one presense that existence had never once held before!","His paleness faded! His breathing steadied! And when his eyes opened, they had changed, swirling seas of crimson gold immensity turning where the shining madness had been!","And Jarl Skallagrim raised his own hand.","The vast majority of the surrounding existence... transformed INTO his hand!","Light years of the foamy dark simply became his palm and his fingers, the unquantified power of a Descendant expressing itself at last, and that hand of transformed existence closed around the descending storm and snuffed out the vast majority of it in a single grip, white lightning dying in fistfuls, snakes crushed mid-strike!","Curer and cured, side by side, fighting the calamity of THE Argent Loom together!","And below them, the last Steed broke.","It shook in terror under the burning sky, and its voice tore out of it in a scream!","\" We shouldn’t go against Them! We should live and die as they wish! We should not rebel! Ah!\"","The steed was fearful at the storm all around as Noah glanced down coldly before he answered!","His voice rolled out of nine mouths across the storm-torn dark, tyrannical and calm at once, and even the lightning seemed to fall quieter around it.","\" Live and die as they wish? That storm is the opinion of old things. It is human to rebel against old things. It is human to look at an order that grinds the small into the dirt and ask WHO DECIDED THIS?!\"","HUUM!","His words boomed as he expressed his trueness, the philosophy of who he was as THE True Human Emperor and what humanity...stood for.","\"Questioning, rebellion, revolution, the refusal to kneel to arrangements we never agreed to... that is human!\"","WAA!","His many eyes burned up at the wrathful white. \" I question the motives of Those Who Remain. I question their sentences, their harvests, their weavings. And today in particular... I REJECT them!\"","BOOM!","All nine clones erupted with invisible might as the last of his strength drove home, and inside Jarl Skallagrim, the final cursed weavings were altered, scorched out, and replaced, and the work reached... one hundred percent!","...!","Skallagrim’s entire body and existence began to shake!","A pillar of crimson gold light erupted from him, tearing up through the storm itself, and his voice rose inside it, cracking open with something no Cursed Descendant had ever been permitted to feel!","\" Can it really be so? Is it truly so?!\"","HUUM!","Utmost resplendancy erupted across the between-space! And above, THE Argent Loom ROARED as if utterly infuriated, and across countless gigaparsecs, seas of white bloomed and swirled and gathered themselves, no longer a storm but a tide of smiting, converging from every horizon upon whatever abomination was rising down below, with surety!","Noah raised his many heads to look up in defiance!","|The lineage of a Progeny of THE Sleepless Fiend has been fully altered. The sentence of one of Those Who Remain has been rewritten in your blood and your Tongue. THE UNBOUND LINEAGE has settled: this line of descent now belongs to the one who lives it.|","|You have undone a third action of Those Who Remain, and this one was not undone at the edges. It was undone at the root. Your VERITAS has increased. VERITAS: 12. Your PONDUS has increased. PONDUS: 13.|","|Your existence has answered the magnitude of this generation. 7 Provenance Essences have emerged at once. Total Provenance Essence: 10.|","|A unique Apostle has emerged.|","| JARL SKALLAGRIM has become a NOBLESSE BLOOD APOSTLE of the highest rarity: BLOOD SOVEREIGN. He is the first of his tier. Due to the uniqueness of his making, an altered lineage rather than a granted Mark alone, he holds his own level of independence: he may disagree with commands, and he may reject them.|","|Further boons are still emerging.|","|Surviving the phenomenon above is paramount.|","The seas of white stopped swirling.","And they began to build!","Across countless gigaparsecs, the gathered wrath of THE Argent Loom drew itself inward, rivers braiding into cables, cables weaving into plates, plates locking over plates, and out of the converging tide, a titanic form assembled itself against the dark!","A colossus of hardened loomlight, humanoid and faceless, its body forged entirely of woven white metal-light layered in overlapping plates, taller than the storm it condensed from, and where a face should have been, there was only a single horizontal slit running across its head, blazing with annihilating white radiance from within!","Noah only had to blink to see many question marks on it as the only thing he grasped...","|THE Loomwrought Smiter| :: ?????","THE Loomwrought Smiter, built out of the musings of Those Who Remain, and every line of it existed for one purpose!","The slit across its head FLARED!","And a beam of pure smiting white, wide enough to swallow an entire Observable Existence, tore down toward Noah’s clones and the newborn Sovereign!","But before it reached Noah... Skallagrim moved!","He crossed the space in front of the clones in a single graceful step, placing his shining body between the beam and the one who had cured him, and his newly crimson gold eyes rose to meet the descending white without a trace of the old madness!","Jarl Skallagrim breathed in, and used something terrifying!","His fissures, the old cracks of his dying, split open across his whole frame, and out of them poured centuries of gathered endings, every death that had ever been written into his clause and was now unpaid, drawn out of his remade line and worn openly, a vast shroud of dark crimson gold ruin billowing around his body, an armament woven of everything he no longer owed!","\" THE Thousand Deaths...I Do Not Owe!\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5599,"title":"Chapter 5599: Chapter 5598: Defiance! III","paragraphs":["The beam struck the shroud, and the shroud ate it screaming!","And then the Sovereign went to work, and Noah watched a being fight in a way he had never seen.","Skallagrim did not draw a weapon, because his body was the weapon! He flowed up the colossus’s descending arm with gliding, unhurried steps, and his movements were graceful in the way of an art refined across lifetimes, elbows and knees and turning shins, each strike thrown from the hips with his whole frame behind it!","A rising knee met the colossus’s forearm and the forearm caved, plates of woven loomlight bursting apart, because every limb of him now carried terrifying bursts of pure PONDUS and VERITAS, weight and truth detonating together at every point of contact!","CRACK!","A smashinf elbow took the Smiter across its chest-plates and a canyon of white weave shattered inward! He slipped a sweeping counter-blow with a small tilt of his head, stepped inside it, seized the colossus’s wrist in a clinch of transformed existence, and drove three knees into its elbow joint in a fluid burst that severed the entire arm into dissolving light!","And then he did the profane thing.","He reached out with his remade existence... and commanded THE Argent Loom itself!","The white rivers still pouring into the Smiter shuddered, and bent, and answered him, loomlight peeling off the construct and braiding into his strikes, white swirling into his crimson gold until every elbow and shin arc carried both authorities at once, the storm’s own substance turned against the storm!","The battle was heavy, and it was brutal, and it was beautiful! The Smiter rebuilt its arm and he tore it off again at the shoulder! It flared its head-slit for a second beam and his shroud of unpaid deaths swallowed the light while his knee came up through its chin, snapping the faceless head backward in a spray of dissolving weave!","His hands and feet were like hammers as they smashed out, each one very likely capable of decimating an entire Observable Existence!","Blow after graceful, merciless blow, the manifestation of the Loom’s rage came apart, plates dimming, cables unraveling, until at last, beneath one final descending elbow that carried the full weight of a heavy PONDUS...","The Loomwrought Smiter burst apart into fading white motes across the dark!","\"...\"","Silence fell over the between-space.","And Jarl Skallagrim floated there amid the dissolving remnants of a smiting, his shroud settling back into his frame, crimson gold light rolling off his shoulders in slow waves, and he turned, and gazed at Noah’s clones silently for a few seconds, saying nothing at all.","Then he looked down at his own hands. At his arms. At the body that had just unmade the wrath of an authority older than frameworks.","And as he did, Noah gazed at this being, and saw his status panel!","|STATUS PANEL: JARL SKALLAGRIM- BLOOD SOVEREIGN, DESCENDANT UNBOUND|","|VERITAS: 20|","|PROVENANCE: 0|","|POTENTIA: 20|","|PONDUS: 20|","|Note: as the first BLOOD SOVEREIGN, a unique capability is budding within this existence. It has not yet finished forming.|","...!","Twenty! Twenty across every attribute, a perfect score on every measure his system knew how to take, floating in front of him wearing a shroud of unpaid deaths!","HUUM!","|A tremendous act of giving has occurred. Salvation, given to the dying. A lineage, given back to its bearer. A Sovereign, given to existence.|","|All of it has been further pooled into the immensity generating from THE Tide That Owes Nothing. The preservation continues, and what is being prepared within the Tide has grown past all precedent.|","And across from the prompts, the immense Sovereign finally spoke, and his deep voice boomed out over the dark, cracking under the weight of what it carried.","\"I am... cured. I have... my salvation!\"","And at this moment, Noah knew it was true in the deepest sense there was, because he could not sense the end of Skallagrim’s lifeline anymore! The drafted conclusion was gone from the written line! The months were gone!","He would not die!","Skallagrim looked toward Noah’s clones with many complex emotions moving through his crimson gold seas, gratitude and awe and confusion all turning together, and when he spoke again, his voice had gone quiet.","\" You have given me my salvation. And I do not wish to sound ungrateful. But...\" His hand rose slowly to his own chest.","\" Why is it that all parts of my Existence... naturally feel an inclination of reverence toward you? What... have you done to me?\"","...!","Noah looked back at him calmly across the settling dark, nine crowns of blood turning slowly, and answered without hurry.","\"I edited your line. I removed the workings of THE Sleepless Fiend from your existence, clause by clause, and I replaced them with my weavings. The sentence that wrote you no longer runs back to him. It runs back...to me.\"","BOOM!","His voice did not rise at all as his own existence could feel a sense of inner peace and wonder even he couldnt envision.","Should he feel this way when he had just done something that went against the weavings of a terrifying type of Lifeform?","He expected to feel a sense of fear or worry right after, wondering if the skies would crack and if everything would fall apart!","But truly, he felt a sense of...exhilaration as if he wanted to do even more of this!","He did not know if it wss due to the immense gains of Provenance Essence or what...but he found it thrilling to go against the actions of Those Who Remain!","He continued.","\" So if you were a Descendant of One of Those Who Remain before... you are now my Descendant...a Descendant of THE True Human Emperor!\"","HUUM!","Immense silence crashed down over the between-space!","The newborn Sovereign stared at the clones with his crimson gold seas gone perfectly still, the words settling into him one at a time, and below them both, a certain little steed was trembling harder than it had trembled through the entire storm, shaking as if its whole Existence was fearful just to be HEARING such profane words spoken aloud into a world where Those Who Remain existed!","Who the fuck did this guy think he was?!"]},{"number":5600,"title":"Chapter 5600: Chapter 5599: Service and Employment!","paragraphs":["Noah watched the newborn Sovereign absorb his words, and he was curious how Skallagrim would react.","Because the autonomy was real, but so was the Mark! Skallagrim held his own level of independence, the first Apostle who could disagree and refuse, but he was still marked, still an Apostle of his Infinite Sanguine Mana, and if this being wanted to have a battle of contention regarding his own existence, Noah held a lot of leeway of control that he could exert at any moment he chose.","For now, he did not exert it.","He was... curious.","Skallagrim’s crimson gold seas turned slowly as many things moved through them, and when he finally spoke, his deep voice came out measured.","\" Descendant of THE True Human Emperor.\" He said the words carefully, testing their weight. \" Do you understand what you are asking my existence to accept? THE Sleepless Fiend is not a father the way small kinds have fathers. He is a personage of such immense power that distance means nothing before him.\"","The Sovereign’s hand closed slowly. \"I have brethren purer than me. Brethren more powerful than me, who know more than me, who have stood closer to the center of the line than I ever will. And every single one of them trembles at his name without ever once being near him. Not from his messages. Not from his workings. From the simple knowledge that he exists, and that we atem from him.\" His eyes fixed on the clones.","\" That is what sat at the root of my line for my whole existence. So answer me plainly, Cure-Giver. Why is it that I should follow you... over someone I have referred to as Father?\"","Noah’s reply came out calm, and level, and utterly tyrannical.","\" Because it was not one of Those Who Remain who gave you salvation.\"","\"...\"","\" You were about to die. Very soon. And in all that time, with all that immensity you tremble before... none of Them came down to help you. Should things have played out, should I have not visited THE Krazhor-Nul Dimension...there would be no Jarl Skallagrim\"","Noah’s pulsed as he wanted to see if a motherfucker could be grateful!","\" I came down into your opened chest with my own hands, and I did something none of Those Who Remain has ever done for you or for any Cursed Progeny. So when you weigh him against me, weigh THAT. The life you are standing in, and the immensity you currently hold... is thanks to me!\"","BOOM!","The words landed across the between-space with a weight of their own, and heavy silence followed them!","Could a fucker be grateful?!","Skallagrim looked down at his hands. He turned them over slowly.","At last, the Sovereign sighed.","\" Too many lifeforms move across existence without honor,\" he said quietly. \" I have watched it my whole life. Beings who take and never mark the debt. Beings who are saved and then sharpen knives for their saviors, because gratitude sits heavy and they would rather walk light.\"","His crimson gold eyes rose. \"Everything else about me was written by another hand. My power, my curse, my months. But honor is the one sentence a being gets to write for itself, in its own hand, with no ancestor holding the pen. It is the only clause that is truly ours. And I...will not write mine crooked on the very first day of my freedom.\"","Oh?","\" So, for having my life and my salvation... I will not be ungrateful. I have my own trueness now, and it prevents me from submitting myself to another. I will not kneel to you. I will not call you Master.\" He inclined his head.","\" But I will hang around you for the near future. And I will make a move when you tell me to. Call it... service, and employment.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes were sharp as he said nothing at this!","Service and employment! A perfect-twenty attribute Sovereign wearing a shroud of unpaid deaths, negotiating himself into position of service! He let the words stand unanswered, neither accepted nor corrected, and instead turned his gaze downward.","To the steed.","The little cursed thing that had screamed through the storm about blasphemy! We should live and die as they wish! We should not rebel! Noah’s gaze settled on it coldly.","’ This fucker was cursed to death by them... and it is still this loyal and fearful?’","The steed’s eyes trembled and dropped, as if they could not meet Noah’s at all, its whole small frame pressed low against the dark.","And as if he could see Noah’s cold gaze from where he floated, Skallagrim drifted down toward the creature, and laid one immense hand on its trembling neck.","\"I feel sentimental with this one,\" the Sovereign said. \" The last steed under me. All the others are gone, spent on the crossing, spent on the hunt, spent on me. This one carried me to my salvation on shaking legs.\" His hand moved once along its neck, almost gently. Then his voice cooled.","\" Can you cure him, the way you cured the white one?\" A pause. \" And little steed. If you say anything the Cure-Giver does not like... then maybe you can find your salvation elsewhere.\"","...!","The Cursed Steed trembled harder, and its gaze went further down.","Noah regarded it for a moment, and inside, his thoughts were already pricing the work.","He had no qualms curing another steed. Another dying thing freed, another gain harvested, a fourth action of Those Who Remain undone, and his last cure had just erupted seven essences into him at once! And beyond the gains, there was the structure of it. Skallagrim’s independence had come from an altered lineage.","But a steed cured and Marked in the way of Hvitrmarr... he was fairly sure he could make this one into an Apostle that had to absolutely follow his commands!","So he would begin this work here, blades of blood already thinning in the dark, and as his instruments descended toward a second trembling steed, he kept Skallagrim talking, extracting every further thread the Sovereign held, about the brethren, about the Descendants, about the messages of a Father who had never once come down!","Because as he did this... his main body moved.","On a volcanic peak inside THE Infiniverse, Emotive had finally calmed, and Noah crossed thousands of realms, and came out inside his own Realm, on the threshold of his long hall, beside the thing that rested there.","THE Aurate Collar of the First Purity.","It sat where he had set it down, pale and quiet, the chest bones of a First Lifeform that all of existence mistook for a Remnant Existential Treasure. It had not stirred...until now.","And the moment his main body arrived beside it, carrying ten full Provenance Essences within...","The collar PULSED!","A slow throb of light through ancient bone, as if some condition had finally, finally been met... as if he had at last become something that was permitted to peer through its weavings!","...!"]}]);
